window.ZGCLAB_DETAILS["news-48"]=[{"id":"news-1716","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"参议员蒂利斯等人呼吁国土安全部长诺姆辞职","title_en":"Senator Tillis among those calling for Kristi Noem to resign as DHS secretary","summary_cn":"北卡罗来纳州联邦参议员汤姆·蒂利斯加入呼吁国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆辞职的行列，阿拉斯加州参议员丽莎·穆尔科斯基也发出同样呼声，成为首批要求其下台的共和党国会议员。蒂利斯表示对诺姆毫无信心，批评其行为如同业余助理经理。此番言论发生在明尼阿波利斯联邦执法人员枪杀亚历克斯·普雷蒂、以及本月一名移民官员枪杀蕾妮·古德之后。","summary_en":"North Carolina US Senator Thom Tillis has joined calls for Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem to resign, with Alaska Senator Lisa Murkowski also doing so, making them the first Republicans in Congress to say she should step down. Tillis said he has no confidence in Noem at all, calling her actions amateurish. The comments come days after federal officers shot and killed Alex Pretti in Minneapolis and an immigration officer killed Renee Good this month.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:20:24.619499+00:00","url":"https://www.witn.com/2026/01/28/senator-tillis-among-those-calling-kristi-noem-resign-dhs-secretary","content":"Senator Tillis among those calling for Kristi Noem to resign as DHS secretarySenator Tillis among those calling for Kristi Noem to resign as DHS secretaryBy WITN Web TeamPublished: Jan. 27, 2026 at 7:50 PM ESTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON, D.C. (WITN/NBC) - North Carolina U.S. Senator Thom Tillis is among those calling for Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem to resign. NBC News also reports that Alaska Senator Lisa Murkowski has, making them the first Republicans in Congress to say she should step down.Asked whether he had confidence in Noem, Tillis told reporters on Capitol Hill: “No, not at all. I think she should go.”Tillis is not running for reelection and said some of Noem’s actions reflected “amateurish assistant-manager-sort of thought processes,” calling them “unacceptable” for someone in a Cabinet-level position.Murkowski, whose term runs until January 2029, said Noem should not be running DHS.Their comments come days after federal officers shot and killed Alex Pretti in Minneapolis, where an immigration officer killed Renee Good this month.A spokesperson for DHS did not immediately respond to a request for comment.Numerous congressional Democrats have already said Noem should resign. Copyright 2026 WITN. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"蒂利斯参议员等人呼吁克里斯蒂·诺姆辞去国土安全部长职务\n蒂利斯参议员等人呼吁克里斯蒂·诺姆辞去国土安全部长职务\nWITN新闻团队\n发表于2026年1月27日美国东部时间晚上7:50\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n华盛顿特区（WITN/NBC）——北卡罗来纳州联邦参议员汤姆·蒂利斯是呼吁国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆辞职的人之一。NBC新闻还报道称，阿拉斯加州参议员丽莎·穆尔科斯基也提出了这一要求，这使她们成为国会中首批表示诺姆应该下台的共和党人。\n当被问及是否信任诺姆时，蒂利斯在国会山告诉记者：“不，一点也不。我认为她应该离职。”\n蒂利斯不参加连任竞选，并表示诺姆的一些行为体现出“业余的、类似助理经理式的思维过程”，称对于一名内阁级官员而言，这些行为“不可接受”。\n任期将持续至2029年1月的穆尔科斯基表示，诺姆不应继续领导国土安全部。\n他们发表上述言论的几天前，联邦官员在明尼阿波利斯开枪打死了亚历克斯·普雷蒂；本月早些时候，一名移民官员在那里杀死了蕾妮·古德。\n国土安全部发言人未立即回应置评请求。\n许多国会民主党人此前已经表示诺姆应该辞职。\n版权所有 2026 WITN。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"witn.com","publish_time":"2026-01-28T00:50:04.790000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1656","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"警长办公室证实FBI正调查伦敦警察局","title_en":"FBI investigating London Police Department, sheriff’s office confirms","summary_cn":"肯塔基州劳雷尔县警长约翰·鲁特证实，FBI正在调查伦敦警察局，NCIC系统控制权已从该局移交至县警长办公室。前伦敦市长候选人汉德利称，调查涉及NCIC信息被滥用的指控，肯塔基州警建议移交控制权。FBI按长期政策拒绝确认或否认具体调查的存在。","summary_en":"Laurel County Sheriff John Root confirmed that the FBI is investigating the London Police Department in Kentucky, and that control of the NCIC system was transferred from the department to the sheriff's office. Former mayor Tracie Handley said the probe involves alleged misuse of NCIC information, with Kentucky State Police advising the transfer. The FBI declined to confirm or deny any specific investigation per longstanding policy.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:25:09.893514+00:00","url":"https://www.wkyt.com/2026/02/04/fbi-investigating-london-police-department-sheriffs-office-confirms","content":"FBI investigating London Police Department, sheriff’s office confirmsFBI investigating London Police Department, sheriff’s office confirmsBy Samantha ValentinoPublished: Feb. 4, 2026 at 10:27 AM EST|Updated: Feb. 4, 2026 at 4:25 PM ESTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLAUREL COUNTY, Ky. (WKYT) - The FBI is currently investigating the London Police Department, according to the Laurel County Sheriff’s Office.Laurel County Sheriff John Root confirmed the city and county’s control of the FBI’s National Crime Information Center (NCIC) was transferred from the London Police Department to the Laurel County Sheriff’s Office.Former London Mayor and current mayoral candidate Tracie Handley says the investigation was revealed in a special called meeting of the London-Laurel County Communications Center Board Tuesday night. The only item on the meeting’s agenda was “CJIS Management Control.”London-Laurel County Communications Center Board Meeting Agenda(London-Laurel County Communications Center Board)The FBI’s Criminal Justice Information Services Division (CJIS) manages and operates several national crime information systems used by the public safety community for both criminal and civil purposes. Among these systems is the National Crime Information Center (NCIC). The U.S. Department of Justice describes the NCIC as “a criminal records database allowing criminal justice agencies to enter or search for information about stolen property, missing or wanted persons, and domestic violence protection orders; to get criminal histories; and to access the National Sex Offender Registry.”“We don’t know what the complaint said or who made it, but we know that it held the gravitas to make the FBI step up and contact the state police and explain that they believe there’s been a misuse of the NCIC information and that control of that information needed to be transferred immediately,” Handley said.WKYT’s Samantha Valentino asked Sheriff Root whether the London-Laurel County Communications Center Board approved transferring control of NCIC usage from the London Police Department to the Laurel County Sheriff’s Office. Additionally, Samantha asked Root whether the decision came at the request of Kentucky State Police due to an ongoing investigation by the FBI regarding LPD’s NCIC usage.In response to Samantha’s questions, Sheriff Root said, “Yes it was changed and we were advised by KSP to change from London PD to LCSO. There is in fact a on going investigation by the FBI into the matter.”The FBI said as a matter of longstanding policy, they can neither confirm nor deny the existence of any specific investigation.WKYT has reached out to Kentucky State Police, the London Police Department, London Mayor Randall Weddle, and the London-Laurel County Communications Center Board for comment.London-Laurel County 911 Director Larry Walls said, “At this time I can’t comment on the investigation.”Copyright 2026 WKYT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI调查伦敦警察局，警长办公室证实\nFBI调查伦敦警察局，警长办公室证实\n作者：Samantha Valentino\n发表于：2026年2月4日，美国东部时间上午10:27\n更新：2026年2月4日，美国东部时间下午4:25\n分享\n将我们添加到Google\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n肯塔基州劳雷尔县（WKYT）——劳雷尔县警长办公室称，FBI目前正在调查伦敦警察局。\n劳雷尔县警长约翰·鲁特证实，FBI国家犯罪信息中心（NCIC）由伦敦警察局负责的市县管理权限已转移至劳雷尔县警长办公室。\n前伦敦市长、现任市长候选人特蕾西·汉德利表示，这项调查是在周二晚间召开的伦敦-劳雷尔县通信中心委员会特别会议上披露的。会议议程中唯一的项目是“CJIS管理控制”。\n伦敦-劳雷尔县通信中心委员会会议议程\n（伦敦-劳雷尔县通信中心委员会）\nFBI刑事司法信息服务部门（CJIS）管理和运营多个全国性犯罪信息系统，供公共安全部门用于刑事和民事用途。其中包括国家犯罪信息中心（NCIC）。美国司法部将NCIC描述为：“一个犯罪记录数据库，允许刑事司法机构录入或查询有关被盗财产、失踪人员或被通缉人员以及家庭暴力保护令的信息；获取犯罪记录；并访问全国性犯罪者登记册。”\n“我们不知道投诉写了什么，也不知道是谁提出的，但我们知道其分量足以让FBI采取行动，联系州警察并解释，他们认为NCIC信息遭到了滥用，需要立即转移该信息的控制权，”汉德利说。\nWKYT的Samantha Valentino询问警长鲁特，伦敦-劳雷尔县通信中心委员会是否批准将NCIC使用控制权从伦敦警察局转移至劳雷尔县警长办公室。此外，Samantha还询问鲁特，这一决定是否应肯塔基州警察的要求作出，原因是FBI正在对伦敦警察局使用NCIC一事展开调查。\n针对Samantha的问题，警长鲁特说：“是的，控制权已经变更，我们接到肯塔基州警察的通知，要求从伦敦警察局改为劳雷尔县警长办公室。FBI确实正在对此事进行调查。”\nFBI表示，按照长期以来的政策，他们既不能确认也不能否认任何具体调查是否存在。\nWKYT已联系肯塔基州警察、伦敦警察局、伦敦市长Randall Weddle以及伦敦-劳雷尔县通信中心委员会寻求置评。\n伦敦-劳雷尔县911中心主任Larry Walls说：“目前我无法对调查发表评论。”\n版权所有2026 WKYT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wkyt.com","publish_time":"2026-02-04T15:27:04.617000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1221","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"列克星敦警方协助国土安全部开展本地调查","title_en":"Lexington Police assist Department of Homeland Security with local investigation","summary_cn":"据WKYT报道，列克星敦警方表示本周协助美国国土安全部及国土安全调查局（HSI）在列克星敦多地执行了数份搜查令，涉及Dennis Drive一处商业地点。警方未说明搜查令执行地点及是否有人被捕，称列克星敦警方仅为协助方，后续问题应转交HSI。WKYT已联系国土安全部寻求更多信息，尚未获回复。","summary_en":"According to WKYT, Lexington Police said they assisted the Department of Homeland Security and Homeland Security Investigations (HSI) this week in executing several search warrants at multiple locations, including a business on Dennis Drive in Lexington. Police did not specify where the warrants were executed or whether any arrests were made, saying LexPD is only an assisting partner and further inquiries should go to HSI. WKYT reached out to DHS for more information and has not yet heard back.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:34:54.387088+00:00","url":"https://www.wkyt.com/2026/04/04/lexington-police-assist-department-homeland-security-with-local-investigation","content":"Lexington Police assist Department of Homeland Security with local investigationLexington Police assist Department of Homeland Security with local investigationBy WKYT News StaffPublished: Apr. 4, 2026 at 7:07 PM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLEXINGTON, Ky. (WKYT) - Lexington Police say they assisted the Department of Homeland Security with a local investigation this week. WKYT reached out to Lexington Police to ask about a possible investigation at a business on Dennis Drive in Lexington. In response to our questions, police said they “assisted DHS / Homeland Security Investigations (HSI) with the execution of several search warrants at multiple locations” on Tuesday. Officers did not specify where those search warrants were executed, or whether any arrests were made. “LexPD is an assisting law enforcement partner with this investigation and further inquiries should be directed to HSI,” the department wrote. WKYT has reached out to the Department of Homeland Security for more information about this investigation. We have not yet heard back. Copyright 2026 WKYT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"列克星敦警方协助国土安全部开展当地调查\n列克星敦警方协助国土安全部开展当地调查\n作者：WKYT新闻工作人员\n发布时间：2026年4月4日，美国东部时间晚上7:07\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n肯塔基州列克星敦（WKYT）——列克星敦警方表示，他们本周协助国土安全部开展了一项当地调查。WKYT联系列克星敦警方，询问有关列克星敦丹尼斯大道一家企业可能遭到调查的情况。警方在回应我们的问题时表示，他们“于周二协助国土安全部/国土安全调查局（HSI）在多个地点执行了数份搜查令”。警方没有具体说明这些搜查令在哪里执行，也没有说明是否有人被捕。\n该部门写道：“列克星敦警察局是此次调查的协助执法伙伴，进一步询问应直接联系HSI。”\nWKYT已联系国土安全部，以获取有关此次调查的更多信息。截至目前，我们尚未收到回复。\n版权2026 WKYT。版权所有。","publish_source":"wkyt.com","publish_time":"2026-04-04T23:07:28.222000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-499","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"贝希尔加入多州诉讼，质疑FEMA与DHS拨款附加条件","title_en":"Beshear joins multistate lawsuit over FEMA, DHS grant conditions","summary_cn":"据WKYT报道，肯塔基州州长安迪·贝希尔与25个州及华盛顿特区共同起诉联邦紧急事务管理署（FEMA）和国土安全部（DHS），指控其对数亿美元防灾与国土安全拨款附加条件，要求各州采纳与特朗普政府一致的选举和移民政策。诉讼称相关条件涉及用“有缺陷”的联邦系统核验选民公民身份、改用读取手写选票的设备等，并称FEMA可依“机构优先事项”随时终止资金。","summary_en":"According to WKYT, Kentucky Gov. Andy Beshear joined 25 states and Washington, D.C. in suing FEMA and the Department of Homeland Security, alleging the agencies attached conditions to millions of dollars in disaster-preparedness and homeland security grants requiring states to adopt election and immigration policies aligned with the Trump administration. The suit cites conditions involving verifying voter citizenship through a 'faulty' federal system and transitioning to equipment reading hand-marked paper ballots, and says FEMA could terminate funds at any time based on 'agency priorities.'","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:00:08.745608+00:00","url":"https://www.wkyt.com/2026/07/24/beshear-joins-multistate-lawsuit-over-fema-dhs-grant-conditions","content":"Beshear joins multistate lawsuit over FEMA, DHS grant conditionsGov. Andy Beshear joined 25 states and Washington, D.C. in a lawsuit against the Federal Emergency Management Agency and Department of Homeland Security.By WKYT News Staff and Samantha ValentinoPublished: Jul. 24, 2026 at 7:25 AM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleFRANKFORT, Ky. (WKYT) - Gov. Andy Beshear joined 25 states and Washington, D.C. in a lawsuit against the Federal Emergency Management Agency and Department of Homeland Security.The lawsuit alleges the agencies have set conditions on millions of dollars in disaster-preparedness and homeland security grants that would require states to adopt election and immigration policies aligned with the Trump Administration.[READ FULL LAWSUIT BELOW]The conditions for the Homeland Security Grant Program would require states to verify the citizenship of all individuals in state voter databases using a “faulty” federal system, transition to equipment that reads hand-marked paper ballots and more, the lawsuit says.The lawsuit says the Constitution gives states the power to administer and set rules governing federal elections, and that states have adopted a range of systems to count votes fairly and accurately.“Defendants, however, seek to upend those laws and policies and—using hundreds of millions of dollars in federal funds as a cudgel—impose the current Administration’s preferred policies in their place,\" the lawsuit reads.DHS has included a set of conditions regarding immigration, according to the lawsuit. DHS and FEMA also reportedly imposed new terms that grant FEMA the authority to terminate funds to states at any time based on alignment with “agency priorities.”Last year, the lawsuit claims FEMA and DHS attempted to leverage billions in federal funding “to coerce States into adopting the Administration’s preferred policies.”A federal court previously vacated immigration conditions set forth by the agencies, calling it unconstitutional “economic dragooning,” the lawsuit says. “Frustrated by the court’s judgment, DHS and FEMA simply cut millions of dollars in funding from jurisdictions they viewed as hostile to the President’s immigration agenda,” the lawsuit reads. “This Court enjoined that action, too, explaining that ‘[t]o hold hostage funding for programs like these based solely on what appear to be [d]efendants’ political whims is unconscionable and, at least here, unlawful.’” Beshear joins multistate lawsuit over FEMA, DHS grant conditions by WKYT Copyright 2026 WKYT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"Beshear加入针对FEMA、DHS拨款条件的多州诉讼州长Andy Beshear与25个州及华盛顿哥伦比亚特区一道，对联邦紧急事务管理局和国土安全部提起诉讼。作者：WKYT新闻团队及Samantha Valentino发布时间：2026年7月24日美国东部夏令时间上午7:25分享在Google上添加我们将我们添加为Google首选来源肯塔基州法兰克福（WKYT）——州长Andy Beshear与25个州及华盛顿哥伦比亚特区一道，对联邦紧急事务管理局和国土安全部提起诉讼。该诉讼指控，这些机构为数亿美元的灾害准备和国土安全拨款设定条件，要求各州采纳与特朗普政府一致的选举和移民政策。[请在下方阅读完整诉状]诉讼称，国土安全拨款计划的条件将要求各州使用一个“有缺陷的”联邦系统核验州选民数据库中所有个人的公民身份，改用能够读取手工标记纸质选票的设备，等等。诉讼称，宪法赋予各州管理联邦选举并制定相关规则的权力，各州已采取多种制度来公平、准确地计票。诉状写道：“然而，被告试图颠覆这些法律和政策，并且——将数亿美元联邦资金用作大棒——以本届政府偏好的政策取而代之。”根据诉讼，DHS纳入了一套与移民有关的条件。据报道，DHS和FEMA还施加了新条款，授权FEMA可随时依据是否符合“机构优先事项”终止向各州提供资金。诉讼称，去年，FEMA和DHS试图利用数十亿美元的联邦资金“胁迫各州采纳本届政府偏好的政策”。诉讼称，联邦法院此前撤销了这些机构规定的移民条件，称其为违宪的“经济胁迫”。诉状写道：“因对法院判决感到沮丧，DHS和FEMA干脆从他们认为对总统移民议程抱有敌意的辖区削减了数百万美元的资金。”“本院也禁止了该行动，并解释称，‘仅仅基于看似是被告政治任性的原因，就把此类项目的资金扣为人质，是不合良心的，而且至少在此处是不合法的。’”WKYT报道：Beshear加入针对FEMA、DHS拨款条件的多州诉讼。版权所有2026 WKYT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wkyt.com","publish_time":"2026-07-24T11:25:35.560000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-364","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"与列克星敦有关联的FBI“十大通缉犯”在密西西比州被捕","title_en":"FBI ‘Ten Most Wanted’ Fugitive with ties to Lexington arrested in Mississippi","summary_cn":"据WKYT报道，FBI“十大通缉犯”之一、46岁的印第安纳波利斯居民格雷戈里·亨德森二世在密西西比州卢因镇被无冲突逮捕，距其被列入名单仅一天。他自2023年8月起在逃，联邦逮捕令源于印第安纳南区对国际贩毒和非法斗狗活动的多辖区调查。当局指控他领导暴力帮派、经营由锡那罗亚贩毒集团供货的贩毒网络，并称其与列克星敦、路易斯维尔等地有关联。","summary_en":"According to WKYT, one of the FBI's 'Ten Most Wanted' fugitives, 46-year-old Gregory Henderson Jr. of Indianapolis, was apprehended without incident in Louin, Mississippi, one day after being added to the list. He had been evading law enforcement since August 2023, with a federal warrant issued in the Southern District of Indiana following a multi-jurisdictional investigation into international drug trafficking and illegal animal fighting. Authorities allege he led a violent gang and ran a drug network supplied by the Sinaloa Cartel, with ties to Lexington and Louisville.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:49:28.854733+00:00","url":"https://www.wkyt.com/2026/08/16/fbi-ten-most-wanted-fugitive-with-ties-lexington-arrested-mississippi","content":"FBI ‘Ten Most Wanted’ Fugitive with ties to Lexington arrested in MississippiGregory Henderson, Jr., 46, of Indianapolis, Indiana, was apprehended without incident on WednesdayBy WKYT News StaffPublished: Aug. 16, 2026 at 6:19 PM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLEXINGTON, Ky. (WKYT) - One of the FBI’s “Ten Most Wanted” fugitives is in federal custody after being captured in Mississippi, just one day after being added to the high-profile list.Gregory Henderson, Jr.(FBI)Gregory Henderson, Jr., 46, of Indianapolis, Indiana, was apprehended without incident on Wednesday, August 12, at 1:55 p.m. in the small town of Louin, Mississippi, according to federal authorities.Henderson had been evading law enforcement since August 2023. A federal arrest warrant was originally issued against him in the Southern District of Indiana following a multi-jurisdictional investigation into international drug trafficking and an illegal animal fighting enterprise.PREVIOUS (Aug. 11, 2026): Authorities allege Henderson led a violent neighborhood-based gang in Indianapolis and ran a drug trafficking network supplied by the Sinaloa Cartel. The network allegedly distributed methamphetamine, cocaine, and fentanyl across central Indiana and the surrounding Midwest region. He is also accused of operating a dog-fighting enterprise that caused the abuse and death of numerous dogs.In addition to Indiana, the FBI says Henderson has ties to several cities, including Louisville and Lexington, Kentucky, as well as Chicago, Detroit, Dayton, Cincinnati, and St. Louis.Federal officials say that Gregory Henderson Jr. was the 542nd addition to the “Ten Most Wanted Fugitives” list.Copyright 2026 WKYT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"与列克星敦有关联的联邦调查局“十大通缉犯”在密西西比州被捕\n来自印第安纳州印第安纳波利斯的46岁格雷戈里·亨德森二世于周三被顺利逮捕\n作者：WKYT新闻工作人员\n发布时间：2026年8月16日美国东部夏令时间下午6时19分\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n将我们添加为 Google 首选来源\n肯塔基州列克星敦（WKYT）——联邦调查局一名“十大通缉逃犯”在密西西比州落网，目前已被联邦拘押；他被列入这一知名名单仅一天后即被捕。\n格雷戈里·亨德森二世\n（联邦调查局）\n据联邦当局称，来自印第安纳州印第安纳波利斯的46岁格雷戈里·亨德森二世，于8月12日周三下午1时55分在密西西比州小镇卢因被顺利逮捕。\n亨德森自2023年8月起一直躲避执法部门。此前，在对国际贩毒和非法动物斗殴活动进行跨辖区调查后，印第安纳州南区联邦地区法院曾对他签发联邦逮捕令。\n此前报道（2026年8月11日）：当局指控亨德森领导印第安纳波利斯一个以社区为基础的暴力帮派，并经营一个由锡那罗亚贩毒集团供货的贩毒网络。该网络据称向印第安纳州中部及周边中西部地区分销甲基苯丙胺、可卡因和芬太尼。他还被控经营斗狗活动，导致大量犬只遭受虐待和死亡。\n联邦调查局称，除印第安纳州外，亨德森还与多座城市有关联，包括肯塔基州的路易斯维尔和列克星敦，以及芝加哥、底特律、代顿、辛辛那提和圣路易斯。\n联邦官员表示，格雷戈里·亨德森二世是第542名被列入“十大通缉逃犯”名单的人。\n版权所有 © 2026 WKYT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wkyt.com","publish_time":"2026-08-16T22:19:08.501000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2191","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"“做好你们的本职工作”：三角洲居民回应FBI涉毒逮捕行动","title_en":"‘Just do your job’: Delta residents react to FBI drug-related arrests","summary_cn":"FBI在密西西比三角洲地区展开大规模逮捕行动，多名现任及前任执法人员因涉嫌毒品共谋被拘留，向日葵县首席副警长弗劳尔斯在列。警长海伍德承认三角洲执法腐败历史，居民卡尔弗特呼吁彻查并追究涉案人员责任，希望执法者以诚信服务社区。","summary_en":"The FBI conducted widespread arrests across the Mississippi Delta, detaining several current and former law enforcement officers in a drug conspiracy takedown, including Sunflower County Chief Deputy Marvin Flowers. Sheriff James Haywood acknowledged the Delta's history of police corruption, while resident Tammy Calvert urged a thorough investigation and accountability, calling on officers to serve the community with integrity.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:56:13.306238+00:00","url":"https://www.wlbt.com/2025/10/30/just-do-your-job-delta-residents-react-fbi-drug-related-arrests","content":"‘Just do your job’: Delta residents react to FBI drug-related arrests By Teddy ReidyPublished: Oct. 30, 2025 at 6:53 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleSUNFLOWER CO., Miss. (WLBT) - On Thursday morning, the Federal Bureau of Investigation conducted widespread arrests across the Delta region, which ended with several current and former law enforcement officers being taken into custody in what is being called a drug conspiracy takedown.The Sunflower County Sheriff’s Office is just one of the numerous departments across the Delta affected by this massive law enforcement shakedown. Sunflower County Chief Deputy Marvin Flowers was one of the many officers taken away in handcuffs early on Oct. 30. According to Sunflower County Sheriff James Haywood, the Mississippi Delta has a history of corruption. “The Delta has always had a reputation for corruption in police work. There are a lot of many good, dedicated people working in law enforcement,” Haywood explained. “When something like this happens, it taints all of us and we have to go out again to establish public trust again.” Tammy Calvert, an Indianola native, said she hopes justice is served. “Me being from the Delta, there is so much more going on, and the police and sheriffs out here involved with the same thing they’re doing,” Calvert said. “They need to investigate and, whoever all is into it, they need to get them and lock them up like they do the rest of the criminals - so that’s what they are.” Calvert shared how she wants the law enforcement officers representing her hometown to serve the community with integrity. “Just do your job. Put them in the handcuffs and put them on where they’re supposed to be, and get us some good, hard-earning, working people to be in the office and do what they’re supposed to do to help and protect us,” said Calvert.Several residents who spoke with 3 On Your Side said they are not surprised by these allegations and arrests, and they hope those responsible are held accountable for their actions. Want more WLBT news in your inbox? Click here to subscribe to our newsletter.See a spelling or grammar error in our story? Please click here to report it and include the headline of the story in your email.Copyright 2025 WLBT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"“做好你们的工作”：三角洲地区居民回应FBI与毒品有关的逮捕行动\n作者：Teddy Reidy\n发布：2025年10月30日 CDT 下午6:53\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n密西西比州向日葵县（WLBT）——周四上午，联邦调查局在三角洲地区开展了大范围逮捕行动，多名现任及前任执法人员被拘押，此次行动被称为打击毒品共谋的行动。\n向日葵县警长办公室只是三角洲地区众多受到这场大规模执法震荡影响的部门之一。10月30日早些时候，向日葵县首席副警长 Marvin Flowers 是多名戴着手铐被带走的警员之一。向日葵县警长 James Haywood 表示，密西西比三角洲地区有腐败的历史。\nHaywood 解释说：“三角洲地区的警务工作一直有腐败的名声。有许多优秀、敬业的人在执法部门工作。当这样的事发生时，它会玷污我们所有人，我们必须再次努力重建公众信任。”\nIndianola 本地人 Tammy Calvert 表示，她希望正义得到伸张。\nCalvert 说：“作为来自三角洲地区的人，这里还有太多事情在发生，警察和警长也参与了他们正在做的同样事情。他们需要调查，凡是涉入其中的人，都应当像对待其他罪犯一样抓住并关进监狱——因为他们就是罪犯。”\nCalvert 表示，她希望代表其家乡的执法人员能以正直的方式服务社区。\nCalvert 说：“做好你们的工作。给他们戴上手铐，把他们送到该去的地方，并让一些优秀、靠辛勤劳动谋生的人进入办公室，做他们该做的事，帮助和保护我们。”\n多位接受《3 On Your Side》采访的居民表示，他们对这些指控和逮捕并不感到意外，并希望责任人对其行为承担责任。\n想在收件箱中获得更多 WLBT 新闻？点击此处订阅我们的通讯。\n发现我们报道中的拼写或语法错误？请点击此处报告，并在电子邮件中附上报道标题。\n版权所有 2025 WLBT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wlbt.com","publish_time":"2025-10-30T23:53:13.718000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2782","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI杰克逊分局与国土安全部在长滩逮捕7名非法移民","title_en":"FBI Jackson, Department of Homeland Security arrest 7 illegal immigrants in Long Beach","summary_cn":"周四下午，FBI杰克逊分局与国土安全部在密西西比州长滩逮捕了7名非法移民。联邦官员未透露逮捕的具体时间和地点，但一名执法消息人士称行动发生在长滩一处建筑工地。此次逮捕正值美国众议员本尼·汤普森带领84名众议院民主党人向国土安全部发出监督信，质疑ICE近期执法策略，称其并非针对犯罪分子，而是针对守法者。目前细节有限，报道将持续更新。","summary_en":"On Thursday afternoon, officials with FBI Jackson, along with the Department of Homeland Security, arrested seven illegal immigrants in Long Beach, Mississippi. Federal officials did not specify when or where the arrests occurred, but a law enforcement source said it happened at a construction site. The arrests came as U.S. Rep. Bennie Thompson led 84 House Democrats in sending an oversight letter to DHS questioning ICE tactics, saying recent arrests target those following the rules rather than criminals. Details remain limited.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:39:09.329436+00:00","url":"https://www.wlox.com/2025/06/05/fbi-jackson-department-homeland-security-arrest-7-illegal-immigrants-long-beach","content":"FBI Jackson, Department of Homeland Security arrest 7 illegal immigrants in Long BeachThe Department of Homeland Security and FBI Jackson arrested seven illegal immigrants in Long Beach on Thursday.By WLOX StaffPublished: Jun. 5, 2025 at 6:44 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLONG BEACH, Miss. (WLOX) - Thursday afternoon, officials with FBI Jackson, along with the Department of Homeland Security, arrested seven illegal immigrants in Long Beach.Federal officials did not say exactly when or where the arrests were made, but one law enforcement source told WLOX News that it happened at a construction site in Long Beach.The arrests come as US Representative Bennie Thompson led 84 House Democrats today, sending an oversight letter to DHS regarding the rise in what they say are “questionable” ICE tactics, adding that recent arrests are not targeting criminals, but rather those who are “doing it the right way.”This new policy, designed to meet an arbitrary quota of deportations, is not targeting criminals...but instead is surreptitiously and deceptively aimed at those who are following the rules, voluntarily appearing in court, and doing it the right way. This policy neither targets criminals nor makes the public safer.Details are limited at this time. We will update this story as new information becomes available.See a spelling or grammar error in this story? Report it to our team HERE.Copyright 2025 WLOX. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局杰克逊分局与国土安全部在长滩逮捕7名非法移民\n国土安全部和联邦调查局杰克逊分局周四在长滩逮捕了7名非法移民。\nWLOX工作人员\n发布时间：2025年6月5日下午6:44（美国中部时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n密西西比州长滩（WLOX）——周四下午，联邦调查局杰克逊分局与国土安全部官员在长滩逮捕了7名非法移民。\n联邦官员没有说明逮捕具体是在何时何地进行的，但一名执法部门消息人士告诉WLOX新闻，逮捕发生在长滩的一处建筑工地。\n这些逮捕行动发生之际，美国众议员本尼·汤普森今天率领84名众议院民主党议员向国土安全部发出监督信，针对他们所称日益增加的“可疑”移民与海关执法局（ICE）行动，并补充说，近期的逮捕行动并未针对罪犯，而是针对那些“以正确方式行事”的人。\n这项旨在达到任意驱逐配额的新政策，并未针对罪犯……相反，它在暗中且具有欺骗性地针对那些遵守规则、自愿出庭并以正确方式行事的人。这项政策既不针对罪犯，也不会让公众更安全。\n目前细节有限。随着新信息出现，我们将更新此报道。\n在这篇报道中发现拼写或语法错误？请在此处向我们的团队报告。\n版权所有2025年WLOX。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wlox.com","publish_time":"2025-06-05T23:44:55.195000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-583","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"诺兰·韦尔斯案调查公布FBI介入情况及调度录音","title_en":"FBI involvement, dispatch audio released in Nolan Wells investigation","summary_cn":"据WLOX报道，杰克逊县警长莱德贝特证实FBI正协助检查诺兰·韦尔斯案已收集的数字证据，称因霍恩岛属联邦土地，警长办公室常与FBI合作。FBI向ABC新闻表示正处理与该案相关人员收到的跨州威胁。韦尔斯遗体于7月6日在霍恩岛附近水域被发现，此前7月4日晚被报失踪。报道还公布了其朋友所乘船只的私人拖车公司调度录音，录音中有人请求救援。","summary_en":"According to WLOX, Jackson County Sheriff John Ledbetter confirmed the FBI is helping examine digital evidence in the Nolan Wells investigation, noting Horn Island is federal land and the sheriff's office frequently works with the FBI. The FBI told ABC News it is 'working to address interstate threats' received by individuals related to the matter. Wells' body was found July 6 in water off Horn Island after he was reported missing the night of July 4. Dispatch audio from a private towing company for the boat his friends used was also released, with a caller heard requesting help.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:01:05.314632+00:00","url":"https://www.wlox.com/2026/07/16/fbi-involvement-dispatch-audio-released-nolan-wells-investigation","content":"FBI involvement, dispatch audio released in Nolan Wells investigationDispatch audio has been released from the boat Wells' friends took home, where a person is heard requesting help.By WLOX StaffPublished: Jul. 16, 2026 at 11:22 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleOCEAN SPRINGS, Miss. (WLOX) — New details have been released on the Federal Bureau of Investigation’s (FBI) involvement in the Nolan Wells investigation, along with dispatch audio.Wells’ body was found in the water off Horn Island on the morning of July 6. Wells was reported missing the night of July 4 after he did not return from a boating trip with friends.FBI assistingJackson County Sheriff John Ledbetter confirmed with WLOX that the FBI is helping examine digital evidence collected so far. He said the involvement is not out of the ordinary, as Horn Island is on federal land and the sheriff’s office frequently works with the FBI.The FBI confirmed with ABC News that the agency is “working to address interstate threats that were received by individuals related to this matter.” The agency did not identify any of the recipients, but some people have stated publicly that they have received threats.Jackson County Chancery Judge Ashlee Cole shared a Facebook post addressing death threats made to her family amid the investigation. Cole is the stepmother of one of three teens who made the trip to Horn Island with Wells.One of Wells’ friends, Tracestin Shepherd, told ABC News that he and other friends of Wells’ who were with him on the island have also received threats.“It worries me for my friends. It worries me for my family,” Shepherd told ABC News. Dispatch audioAccording to reports, dispatch audio from a private towing company has been released in connection with the boat Wells’ friends used.In the call, a person is heard requesting help.CALLER: We’re sinking, can y’all please come?DISPATCH: And is everyone on board and in good health otherwise? CALLER: Yeah, yeah everybody is on board. Ledbetter confirmed that the three friends who were on the boat with Wells have been interviewed. He said his office has interviewed more than 60 witnesses.See a spelling or grammar error in this story? Report it to our team HERE. Copyright 2026 WLOX. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI介入，Nolan Wells调查中发布调度录音\nWells的朋友们驾船回家时使用的船只上的调度录音已经发布，录音中可以听到有人请求帮助。\nWLOX工作人员\n发布于2026年7月16日上午11:22（CDT）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n美国密西西比州奥申斯普林斯（WLOX）——联邦调查局（FBI）参与Nolan Wells调查的新细节已经公布，同时发布了调度录音。\n7月6日上午，Wells的遗体在Horn Island附近水域被发现。7月4日晚，Wells与朋友乘船出行后未归，随后被报告失踪。\nFBI提供协助\nJackson县警长John Ledbetter向WLOX证实，FBI正在协助审查迄今收集到的数字证据。他说，这种参与并不罕见，因为Horn Island属于联邦土地，警长办公室经常与FBI合作。\nFBI向ABC新闻证实，该机构“正努力处理与此事有关人员收到的州际威胁”。该机构没有指明收到威胁者的身份，但一些人已公开表示他们收到过威胁。\n在调查期间，Jackson县衡平法院法官Ashlee Cole分享了一篇Facebook帖子，谈及针对其家人的死亡威胁。Cole是三名与Wells一同前往Horn Island的青少年中一人的继母。\nWells的一位朋友Tracestin Shepherd告诉ABC新闻，他和当时在岛上陪同Wells的其他朋友也收到了威胁。\n“这让我担心我的朋友，也让我担心我的家人，”Shepherd告诉ABC新闻。\n调度录音\n据报道，一家私人拖船公司的调度录音已经发布，相关船只正是Wells的朋友们所使用的那艘船。\n在通话中，可以听到有人请求帮助。\n呼叫者：我们正在下沉，你们能来吗？\n调度员：那么船上每个人都在船上，并且其他方面都健康吗？\n呼叫者：是的，是的，所有人都在船上。\nLedbetter证实，与Wells一同在船上的三名朋友已经接受问询。他说，其办公室已经询问了60多名证人。\n在这篇报道中发现拼写或语法错误？请在此处向我们的团队报告。\n版权所有2026 WLOX。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wlox.com","publish_time":"2026-07-16T16:22:02.777000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3429","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI搜查与米卡·米勒案有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所","title_en":"FBI searches home of Myrtle Beach pastor linked to Mica Miller investigation","summary_cn":"FBI发言人向WMBF新闻证实，联邦探员对默特尔比奇牧师约翰-保罗·米勒位于冷水圈的住所执行了授权搜查。记者在现场看到探员进出并携带证据袋，搜查持续数小时，约下午6点结束。米勒的妻子米卡今年早些时候在北卡罗来纳州被裁定死于自杀，其死亡因婚姻相关指控引发全国关注。目前尚不清楚此次搜查是否与其死亡有关，米勒本人不在家中。","summary_en":"An FBI spokesperson confirmed to WMBF News that agents conducted an authorized search at the home of Myrtle Beach pastor John-Paul Miller on Coldwater Circle. Reporters saw agents going in and out carrying evidence bags; the search lasted hours and ended around 6 pm. Miller's wife Mica was ruled to have died by suicide in North Carolina earlier this year, and her death gained national attention amid allegations surrounding their marriage. It is unclear whether the search is related to her death, and Miller was not at home.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:42:21.362681+00:00","url":"https://www.wmbfnews.com/2024/11/01/fbi-home-myrtle-beach-pastor-linked-mica-miller-investigation","content":"FBI searches home of Myrtle Beach pastor linked to Mica Miller investigationFederal authorities were at the home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to an investigation that gained national attention.By Ale Espinosa, Michael Owens, Julia Richardson and Ashley BolesPublished: Nov. 1, 2024 at 1:17 PM EDT|Updated: Nov. 1, 2024 at 7:28 PM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleMYRTLE BEACH, S.C. (WMBF) - Federal authorities were at the home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to an investigation that gained national attention. FBI spokesperson Kevin Wheeler confirmed to WMBF News that they are doing an authorized search at the home of John-Paul Miller on Coldwater Circle. No further information was provided.WMBF News Reporters Ale Espinosa and Ashley Boles were both at the scene throughout the afternoon and saw FBI agents at the home. They also saw agents going in and out of the home and carrying evidence bags. As of around 4 p.m., neighbors told WMBF News the agents had been at Miller’s home for hours. By around 6 p.m., the FBI had cleared out. “It‘s just one of those things that you don’t think would ever happen where you live,” said Butch, a neighbor of Miller’s. The FBI was at home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to the investigation into Mica Miller's death earlier this year.(WMBF)The FBI was at home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to the investigation into Mica Miller's death earlier this year.The FBI was at home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to the investigation into Mica Miller's death earlier this year.The FBI was at home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to the investigation into Mica Miller's death earlier this year.Earlier this year authorities ruled Miller’s wife, Mica, died by suicide in Robeson County, North Carolina. Mica Miller’s death gained national attention due to allegations surrounding her marriage to John-Paul Miller. At that time, John-Paul Miller was the pastor of Solid Rock Church in Myrtle Beach.It‘s unclear if the FBI’s search was related to her death. John-Paul Miller, meanwhile, was not found at the home and his whereabouts were unknown Friday afternoon. Butch said while he didn’t really know John-Paul Miller personally, one particular clue makes him think Miller had not been home for the past few days. “He walks the dogs and basically goes back inside. That’s basically it,” he said. “It’s been a couple of days. His truck is gone. His truck was there yesterday, but it’s gone today.”The search also brought up emotions for the community and neighbors - as well as those who have followed the case since it first gained national attention. “I’ve been following it since the day after it happened,” said Gina Whittington. “I watched the pastor announce Mica’s passing from inside the church, and followed it quickly. I was working today, and actually was on a TikTok live and it was announced that the FBI was at the pastor’s house. And it just went from there.”This story will be updated as more details are released. Stay with WMBF News for updates. Copyright 2024 WMBF. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局搜查与Mica Miller调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所联邦当局搜查了一名与一项引发全国关注的调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所。作者：Ale Espinosa、Michael Owens、Julia Richardson和Ashley Boles发表于2024年11月1日美国东部时间下午1:17｜更新于2024年11月1日美国东部时间下午7:28分享在Google上添加我们将其添加为Google上的首选来源默特尔比奇，南卡罗来纳州（WMBF）——联邦当局正在搜查一名与一项引发全国关注的调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所。联邦调查局发言人Kevin Wheeler向WMBF News证实，他们正在Coldwater Circle的John-Paul Miller住所进行经授权的搜查。未提供更多信息。WMBF News记者Ale Espinosa和Ashley Boles整个下午都在现场，并看到联邦调查局特工在该住所。他们还看到特工进出住所并携带证物袋。大约下午4点，邻居告诉WMBF News，特工已经在Miller家中待了数小时。大约下午6点，联邦调查局人员撤离。“这只是那种你从没想过会发生在自己居住地的事情，”Miller的邻居Butch说。联邦调查局正在搜查一名与今年早些时候Mica Miller死亡调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所。（WMBF）联邦调查局正在搜查一名与今年早些时候Mica Miller死亡调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所。联邦调查局正在搜查一名与今年早些时候Mica Miller死亡调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所。联邦调查局正在搜查一名与今年早些时候Mica Miller死亡调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师住所。今年早些时候，当局裁定Miller的妻子Mica在北卡罗来纳州罗伯逊县自杀身亡。由于围绕她与John-Paul Miller婚姻的指控，Mica Miller的死亡引发全国关注。当时，John-Paul Miller是默特尔比奇Solid Rock Church的牧师。目前不清楚联邦调查局的搜查是否与她的死亡有关。与此同时，John-Paul Miller并未在住所内被发现，截至周五下午其下落不明。Butch说，虽然他并不真正认识John-Paul Miller，但有一个特别线索让他认为Miller过去几天一直不在家。“他遛狗，然后基本上就回到屋里。基本就是这样，”他说。“已经有几天了。他的卡车不见了。昨天他的卡车还在，但今天不见了。”这次搜查也引发了社区和邻居的情绪，也触动了那些自案件首次引发全国关注以来一直关注此案的人。“从事情发生后的第二天起我就一直在关注，”Gina Whittington说。“我看到牧师在教堂里宣布Mica去世的消息，并迅速跟进此事。我今天在工作，当时正在TikTok直播，直播中有人宣布联邦调查局正在牧师家里。事情就这样发展下去。”随着更多细节公布，本报道将持续更新。请继续关注WMBF News获取最新消息。版权所有2024 WMBF。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wmbfnews.com","publish_time":"2024-11-01T17:17:52.244000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-250","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前国土安全部领导人回顾该部门9·11后的起源","title_en":"Former DHS leaders revisit department’s post-9/11 origins","summary_cn":"9·11恐怖袭击促使联邦政府保护国家的方式发生重大变化，核心举措是成立国土安全部。布什总统在袭击后不久设立白宫国土安全办公室，任命汤姆·里奇领导；国会2002年通过《国土安全法》，2003年1月国土安全部开始运作，合并22个机构，是历史上最大规模的政府重组之一。前官员阿萨·哈钦森和迈克尔·切尔托夫回顾了整合机构、打破情报共享壁垒及应对卡特里娜飓风的挑战，并指出网络安全和人工智能是日益增长的国家安全关切。","summary_en":"The Sept. 11 attacks led to sweeping changes in federal protection, centered on creating the Department of Homeland Security. President Bush established the White House Office of Homeland Security, appointing Tom Ridge to lead it; Congress passed the Homeland Security Act in 2002, and DHS began operations in January 2003, merging 22 agencies in one of history's largest government reorganizations. Former officials Asa Hutchinson and Michael Chertoff recalled integrating agencies, breaking intelligence-sharing barriers, and responding to Hurricane Katrina, noting cyberattacks and AI as growing national security concerns.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:39:30.959522+00:00","url":"https://www.wmtv15news.com/2026/09/08/former-dhs-leaders-revisit-departments-post-911-origins","content":"Former DHS leaders revisit department’s post-9/11 originsBy Stephen GoinPublished: Sep. 8, 2026 at 8:19 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON (Gray DC) - The Sept. 11 terrorist attacks led to sweeping changes in how the federal government protects the nation. At the center of those efforts, was the creation of the Department of Homeland Security. President George W. Bush created the White House Office of Homeland Security shortly after the attacks, appointing former Pennsylvania Gov. Tom Ridge to lead it. Congress later passed the Homeland Security Act in 2002, creating the Department of Homeland Security as a new Cabinet-level department. DHS began operations in January 2003, with most of its agencies transferred into the department that March. It was the largest government reorganizations in history, bringing together 22 agencies different agencies under one roof.Former Arkansas Gov. Asa Hutchinson served as the first DHS undersecretary for border and transportation security. He told Gray’s Washington Bureau that the possibility of another terrorist attack weighed heavily on officials working to stand up the new department.“Every day we woke up thinking, is this going to be the day we’re going to get hit again?” Hutchinson said.Hutchinson said establishing DHS also required bringing together agencies that had previously operated in different parts of the federal government.For example, Customs and the Border Patrol had been housed in separate federal departments. Customs was part of the Treasury Department, while the Border Patrol was part of the Justice Department. “All of a sudden, two different departments are having to work together seamlessly,” Hutchinson said.DHS was further tasked with helping address gaps in intelligence sharing exposed by the Sept. 11 attacks.Michael Chertoff had seen those barriers firsthand from inside the Justice Department. On 9/11, Chertoff was the assistant attorney general in charge of the department’s Criminal Division and later helped lead the federal investigation into the attacks.After serving as a federal appeals court judge, Chertoff became the nation’s second homeland security secretary in 2005.“One of the critical things when we first began was the process of removing the walls and creating a much more efficient intelligence-sharing mechanism,” Chertoff said.Months after Chertoff took office, Hurricane Katrina exposed additional problems with the federal government’s response to catastrophic disasters.“We had to change the model, and we had to be prepared to have the federal government step in and actually take the leadership role,” Chertoff said.Congress later overhauled the Federal Emergency Management Agency, now within DHS, strengthening its authority and making changes to the federal government’s approach to disaster preparedness.In the years since, DHS has taken on a wide-ranging mission that includes counterterrorism, cybersecurity, disaster response, border security and immigration enforcement. Immigration enforcement has become one of the most politically contentious parts of that mission.“I think the department and their image has suffered because of the enforcement tactics, some of those that have been used,” Hutchinson said.Speaking to Gray Media, both Hutchinson and Chertoff said they believed the country was safer today with DHS. However, Chertoff pointed to cyberattacks and artificial intelligence as growing national security concerns.“We’ve avoided a repeat of 9/11,” Chertoff said. “But now we can’t lose sight of the fact there will be other kinds of challenges that are multiplying day by day.”The legal proceedings stemming from the Sept. 11 attacks also remain unresolved. Khalid Sheikh Mohammed, the accused mastermind of the attacks, is scheduled to face a military trial at Guantanamo Bay in June 2028.Copyright 2026 Gray DC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"前国土安全部领导人回顾该部门“9·11”后的起源\nStephen Goin\n发布时间：2026年9月8日上午8:19（中部夏令时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n华盛顿（Gray DC）——“9·11”恐怖袭击导致联邦政府保护国家的方式发生了广泛变化。这些努力的核心，是创建国土安全部。袭击发生后不久，乔治·W·布什总统创建了白宫国土安全办公室，并任命前宾夕法尼亚州州长Tom Ridge领导该办公室。国会随后通过了2002年《国土安全法》，创建国土安全部这一新的内阁级部门。国土安全部于2003年1月开始运作，同年3月大多数机构转入该部门。这是历史上规模最大的政府重组之一，将22个不同机构整合到同一部门之下。\n前阿肯色州州长Asa Hutchinson曾担任国土安全部首任边境与运输安全副部长。他告诉Gray新闻网华盛顿分社，另一次恐怖袭击的可能性给负责组建新部门的官员带来了沉重压力。\n“我们每天醒来都会想：今天会不会再次遭到袭击？”Hutchinson说。\nHutchinson表示，建立国土安全部还需要整合此前在联邦政府不同部门运作的机构。\n例如，海关和边境巡逻队此前隶属于不同的联邦部门。海关属于财政部，而边境巡逻队属于司法部。“突然之间，两个不同的部门必须无缝协作，”Hutchinson说。\n国土安全部还被赋予填补“9·11”袭击暴露出的情报共享漏洞的任务。\nMichael Chertoff在司法部任职期间亲眼见过这些障碍。2001年9月11日，Chertoff担任司法部刑事司助理司法部长，后来还参与领导了对袭击事件的联邦调查。\n在担任联邦上诉法院法官后，Chertoff于2005年成为美国第二任国土安全部长。\n“我们刚开始时，关键事项之一就是拆除壁垒，建立更加高效的情报共享机制，”Chertoff说。\nChertoff上任数月后，卡特里娜飓风暴露了联邦政府应对灾难性灾害的更多问题。\n“我们必须改变模式，必须做好准备，让联邦政府介入并真正发挥领导作用，”Chertoff说。\n国会后来对如今隶属于国土安全部的联邦紧急事务管理局进行了改革，加强其权力，并改变联邦政府应对灾害准备工作的方式。\n此后多年，国土安全部承担了范围广泛的任务，包括反恐、网络安全、灾害响应、边境安全和移民执法。移民执法已成为该部门使命中政治争议最激烈的部分之一。\n“我认为，由于执法策略以及其中一些被采用的做法，该部门及其形象受到了损害，”Hutchinson说。\n在接受Gray Media采访时，Hutchinson和Chertoff都表示，他们相信如今有了国土安全部，美国比过去更安全。不过，Chertoff指出，网络攻击和人工智能正成为日益严重的国家安全问题。\n“我们避免了‘9·11’重演，”Chertoff说。“但现在我们不能忽视这样一个事实：还会有其他类型的挑战，而且这些挑战正日复一日地增加。”\n源自“9·11”袭击的法律程序仍未解决。被指控为袭击幕后主谋的Khalid Sheikh Mohammed计划于2028年6月在关塔那摩湾接受军事审判。\n版权2026 Gray DC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wmtv15news.com","publish_time":"2026-09-08T13:19:52.797000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-139","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"威斯康星州麻疹疫情持续扩大，DHS调查新病例是否与疫情相关","title_en":"DHS investigates if current Measles cases are connected","summary_cn":"威斯康星州弗农县新确诊两例麻疹病例，州卫生官员称全州今年确诊病例已达166例，约45%为学龄儿童。DHS传染病局局长韦斯特加德表示，每出现一例病例都会增加病毒传播机会，尤其在疫苗接种率低的社区，呼吁民众接种疫苗。卫生部门建议居民通过免疫登记系统核查接种记录，出现高烧或红疹症状应居家并先致电诊所。","summary_en":"Two new measles cases were confirmed in Vernon County, Wisconsin, as the state's outbreak grows to 166 cases this year, about 45% of them school-aged children. Dr. Ryan Westergaard, chief medical officer for the DHS Bureau of Communicable Diseases, said each case creates an opportunity for the virus to spread, especially where vaccination coverage is low, and urged residents to get vaccinated. Officials advised checking immunization records and staying home while calling a clinic if symptoms appear.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T19:53:40.756053+00:00","url":"https://www.wmtv15news.com/2026/09/17/dhs-investigates-if-current-measles-cases-are-connected","content":"DHS investigates if current Measles cases are connected Two new measles cases have been confirmed in Vernon County, state health officials said, as Wisconsin’s measles outbreak continues to grow.By Kennedy DuPontPublished: Sep. 16, 2026 at 8:25 PM CDT|Updated: Sep. 16, 2026 at 9:49 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleMADISON, Wis. (WMTV) - Two new measles cases have been confirmed in Vernon County, state health officials said, as Wisconsin’s measles outbreak continues to grow. State health officials confirmed the two cases through testing at the Wisconsin State Lab of Hygiene. Contact tracing is underway. There are no known public exposure sites in Vernon County. Investigators are working to determine whether the new infections are linked to the larger outbreak clustering in nearby counties. Statewide, confirmed measles cases have reached 166 this year. About 45% of those cases are school-aged children, according to health officials. Officials say unvaccinated children face the highest risk of severe illness. Health officials urge vaccination Dr. Ryan Westergaard, chief medical officer for the DHS Bureau of Communicable Diseases, said the virus can spread further each time a case occurs in a community. “Every time a case of measles occurs in a community, it creates an opportunity for the virus to spread. Especially so in communities where vaccination coverage is low. Our message to the people of Wisconsin today is to make sure you and your family are protected against measles by being vaccinated,” Westergaard said. Dr. Stephanie Schauer, Wisconsin immunization program manager, urged residents to check their vaccination records as students return to school. “Really recommending that, you know, people check records, and avail themselves a vaccine as they head back to school, so that this is one less thing that they have to worry about,” Schauer said. The Department of Health Services urges residents to check their vaccination status through the Wisconsin Immunization Registry or their health care provider. Anyone experiencing symptoms, such as a high fever or red rash, is urged to stay home and call a clinic before visiting. For more information, visit the DHS website at www.dhs.wisconsin.gov/ Click here to download the WMTV15 News app or our WMTV15 First Alert weather app.Copyright 2026 WMTV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"DHS调查当前麻疹病例是否有关联\n州卫生官员表示，弗农县已确认新增两例麻疹病例，随着威斯康星州麻疹疫情持续扩大。由Kennedy DuPont报道。发表于2026年9月16日中部夏令时间晚上8:25 | 更新于2026年9月16日中部夏令时间晚上9:49\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n威斯康星州麦迪逊（WMTV）——州卫生官员表示，弗农县已确认新增两例麻疹病例，随着威斯康星州麻疹疫情持续扩大。州卫生官员通过威斯康星州卫生实验室的检测确认了这两例病例。目前正在进行接触者追踪。弗农县没有已知的公共暴露地点。调查人员正在确定这些新感染病例是否与邻近县聚集的大规模疫情有关。\n今年全州确诊麻疹病例已达166例。卫生官员称，其中约45%为学龄儿童。官员表示，未接种疫苗的儿童面临重症的最高风险。\n卫生官员敦促接种疫苗\n卫生服务部传染病司首席医疗官Ryan Westergaard医生表示，每当一个病例在社区出现，病毒就可能进一步传播。“每当一个社区出现麻疹病例，就为病毒传播创造了机会。在疫苗接种覆盖率较低的社区尤其如此。我们今天对威斯康星州民众的讯息是：务必通过接种疫苗，确保您和家人受到麻疹保护，”Westergaard说。\n威斯康星州免疫项目负责人Stephanie Schauer医生敦促居民在学生返校之际查看自己的疫苗接种记录。“我们确实建议大家查看记录，并在返校时接种疫苗，这样就少了一件需要担心的事情，”Schauer说。\n卫生服务部敦促居民通过威斯康星州免疫登记系统或其医疗服务提供者核查自己的疫苗接种状态。任何出现高烧或红疹等症状的人，都应留在家中，并在前往诊所前先致电诊所。\n更多信息请访问卫生服务部网站：www.dhs.wisconsin.gov/\n点击此处下载WMTV15新闻应用，或下载我们的WMTV15第一预警天气应用。\n版权所有 2026 WMTV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wmtv15news.com","publish_time":"2026-09-17T01:25:11.411000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1371","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI路易斯维尔分局警告针对肯塔基人的各类诈骗","title_en":"FBI Louisville warns of various scams targeting Kentuckians - WNKY News 40 Television","summary_cn":"FBI路易斯维尔分局警告针对肯塔基州民众的诈骗增多，骗子冒充执法或政府官员，以未出庭或逮捕令为由施压要求付款。2025年IC3收到475起相关投诉，损失超315万美元。FBI强调执法机构不会电话索款或威胁逮捕，并建议民众“缓一缓”、勿提供个人信息或转账。","summary_en":"The FBI Louisville Field Office warned of rising scams targeting Kentuckians, with fraudsters impersonating law enforcement or government officials and pressuring victims over missed jury duty or arrest warrants. In 2025, IC3 received 475 complaints in Kentucky with losses exceeding $3.15 million. The FBI stressed that agencies will not call to demand payment or threaten arrest, advising the public to pause, avoid sharing personal information and never send money.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:18:01.038649+00:00","url":"https://www.wnky.com/fbi-louisville-warns-of-various-scams-targeting-kentuckians","content":"1 / 0\nFBI Louisville warns of various scams targeting Kentuckians\nMarch 18, 2026\nWNKY Staff,\nShare This StoryFacebookTwitteremailPrintLinkedinRedditLOUISVILLE, Ky. – The Federal Bureau of Investigation Louisville Field Office is warning the public about an increase in scams targeting Kentuckians.\nOfficials say these scams include unsolicited phone calls where scammers impersonate law enforcement or government officials to gain money or to steal personal information.\nAccording to the FBI Louisville Field Office, scammers contact victims using spoofed phone numbers and other tactics to appear trustworthy.\nCurrently, the FBI Louisville states the most prevalent type of scam it has seen is a scammer impersonating a local sheriff’s office. During these scams, officials say the caller accuses a victim of failing to show for jury duty or missing a court date and may claim an arrest warrant is active against that victim.\nAuthorities say scammers pressure victims to immediately pay a fine to avoid an arrest or other consequences.\nIn addition, officials say scammers may use Artificial Intelligence, provide official looking court documents or may have personal information about the victim.\nThese scams can also be seen in emails, officials say.\nSigns of these scams include an urgent and aggressive tone, refusal to speak or to leave a message with anyone other than the victim and urging victims not to tell anyone about what is happening.\nPayment is demanded in several forms, with the most common being cash deposited into cryptocurrency ATMs, prepaid cards and wire transfers, officials say.\nThe FBI Louisville Field Office says law enforcement and FBI agencies will not call the public to demand payment or to threaten arrest, nor will they request or accept payment using cryptocurrency ATMs.\nLast year, the FBI states its Internet Crime Complaint Center received over 39,949 complaints regarding government impersonation scams, with victim losses surpassing $833 million nationwide.\nIn Kentucky, officials say 475 complaints were received through IC3 in 2025, and victim losses exceeded $3.15 million.\nTo avoid being scammed, the FBI advises to:\n“Take a beat” before acting\nResist pressure tactics and take time to asses if the situation is real\nTo not provide or verify personally identifiable information to someone they have only met online, over the phone or through unsolicited contact.\nTo not send money, gift cards, cryptocurrency or other assets to individuals they have not met in person.\nLearn more about scam prevention at www.fbi.gov/takeabeat\nIf you believe you are a victim of this scam, or any other online fraud scheme, timely reporting is key. Cease all contact with the scammers immediately, notify your financial institution and safeguard all financial accounts, contact your local law enforcement, and file a complaint with the IC3 at www.ic3.gov.\nGUIDE: How to Watch WNKY News 40 Broadcasts >\nDownload WNKY News 40 Apps\nThe Latest\nTrio of Hilltoppers Score as WKU Defeats SEMO to Remain Unbeaten\nGame of the Week Preview: Bowling Green vs. Barren County\nHilltoppers Fall to Sooners in Five Sets\nThe American Red Cross is still under urgent blood supply crisis: Donors needed\nSevere Weather\n2 active weather alerts\nView Alert Details »\nPopular Articles\n1 dead, 1 flown after two-vehicle crash in Barren County2 arrested in Bowling Green on child abuse charges after welfare checkBowling Green preteen fighting for her life against a one-of-a-kind brain cancerBowling Green man charged with vehicle theft2 Smiths Grove residents indicted on Medicaid fraud charges12 Sumner County residents indicted in alleged cocaine trafficking ring\nno iframe support!","content_cn":"1 / 0\nFBI路易斯维尔分局警告针对肯塔基州居民的各种诈骗\n2026年3月18日\nWNKY工作人员\n分享此故事 Facebook Twitter 电子邮件 打印 LinkedIn Reddit\n路易斯维尔，肯塔基州——联邦调查局路易斯维尔外勤办公室警告公众，针对肯塔基州居民的诈骗有所增加。\n官员表示，这些诈骗包括未经请求的电话，诈骗者冒充执法人员或政府官员，以骗取钱财或窃取个人信息。\n据FBI路易斯维尔外勤办公室称，诈骗者使用伪造的电话号码和其他手段联系受害者，使自己看起来值得信任。\n目前，FBI路易斯维尔分局表示，其见到的最常见诈骗类型是诈骗者冒充当地警长办公室。在这些诈骗中，官员说，来电者指责受害者未参加陪审团义务或错过开庭日期，并可能声称受害者已有逮捕令。\n当局表示，诈骗者向受害者施压，要求其立即支付罚款，以避免被捕或遭受其他后果。\n此外，官员表示，诈骗者可能使用人工智能，提供看似官方的法庭文件，或掌握受害者的个人信息。\n官员说，这些诈骗也可能通过电子邮件进行。\n这些诈骗的迹象包括紧迫且咄咄逼人的语气，拒绝与受害者以外的任何人交谈或留言，以及敦促受害者不要告诉任何人正在发生的事情。\n官员表示，诈骗者会要求以多种形式付款，其中最常见的是将现金存入加密货币自动取款机、预付卡和电汇。\nFBI路易斯维尔外勤办公室表示，执法部门和FBI机构不会致电公众要求付款或威胁逮捕，也不会要求或接受通过加密货币自动取款机支付的款项。\nFBI表示，去年，其互联网犯罪投诉中心（IC3）收到超过39,949起有关冒充政府机构诈骗的投诉，全国受害者损失超过8.33亿美元。\n官员表示，在肯塔基州，2025年通过IC3收到475起投诉，受害者损失超过315万美元。\n为避免受骗，FBI建议：\n“停一下再行动”\n抵制施压手段，花时间评估情况是否属实\n不要向仅通过网络、电话或未经请求的联系认识的人提供或核实个人身份信息。\n不要向从未当面见过的人发送金钱、礼品卡、加密货币或其他资产。\n在www.fbi.gov/takeabeat了解更多防诈骗信息\n如果您认为自己是此次诈骗或任何其他网络欺诈计划的受害者，及时报告至关重要。立即停止与诈骗者的一切联系，通知您的金融机构并保护所有金融账户，联系当地执法部门，并在www.ic3.gov向IC3提交投诉。\n指南：如何观看WNKY News 40广播 >\n下载WNKY News 40应用\n最新消息\n三名Hilltoppers得分，WKU击败SEMO保持不败\n本周比赛预告：Bowling Green对阵Barren County\nHilltoppers五盘不敌Sooners\n美国红十字会仍处于紧急血液供应危机：需要献血者\n恶劣天气\n2个正在生效的天气警报\n查看警报详情 »\n热门文章\n巴伦县两车相撞事故造成1人死亡、1人被送医\n福利检查后，Bowling Green两人因虐待儿童罪被捕\nBowling Green一名学龄前少年与罕见脑癌抗争，生命垂危\nBowling Green男子被控盗窃车辆\nSmiths Grove两名居民因医疗补助欺诈罪被起诉\nSumner县12名居民因涉嫌可卡因贩运团伙被起诉\n不支持iframe！","publish_source":"wnky.com","publish_time":"2026-03-18T22:43:27+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2074","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"格拉斯哥警方接到冒充FBI诈骗的报案","title_en":"Glasgow Police Department receives reports of FBI scam - WNKY News 40 Television","summary_cn":"肯塔基州格拉斯哥警察局警告公众，当地出现冒充美国联邦调查局特工的诈骗，已接到多起投诉。诈骗者致电民众，要求提取现金当面交付或电汇转账以“摆平麻烦”。警方强调，FBI绝不会致电或电邮私人公民索要付款或威胁逮捕，也不会要求汇款以免被捕，并建议受害者向当地执法部门和FBI互联网犯罪投诉中心举报。","summary_en":"The Glasgow Police Department in Kentucky warned the public about a scam in which someone impersonates a Federal Bureau of Investigation agent, saying it has received several complaints. The caller asks people to withdraw cash and meet them or wire money to \"pay off their trouble.\" Police stressed the FBI will never call or email a private citizen to demand payment or threaten arrest, nor ask for a settlement wire to avoid arrest, and urged victims to report to local law enforcement and the FBI's Internet Crime Complaint Center.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:29:30.191559+00:00","url":"https://www.wnky.com/glasgow-police-department-receives-reports-of-fbi-scam","content":"1 / 0\nGlasgow Police Department receives reports of FBI scam\nNovember 21, 2025\nWNKY Staff,\nShare This StoryFacebookTwitteremailPrintLinkedinRedditGLASGOW, Ky. – The Glasgow Police Department says it is warning the public about a scam in the community involving someone impersonating an agent with the Federal Bureau of Investigation.\nPolice say they have received several complaints about the scam circulating in the Glasgow area.\nAuthorities say it involves someone calling around while impersonating an FBI agent. The caller then asks people to withdraw cash and meet them or wire transfer money to “pay off their trouble.”\nThe Glasgow Police Department says the FBI will never call or email a private citizen to demand payment or threaten arrest. Authorities say the FBI will also not ask to wire a settlement to avoid an arrest.\nIf you think you may be a victim of this scam or any other online scam, file a report with your local law enforcement agency and the FBI’s Internet Crime Complaint Center at ic3.gov.\nGUIDE: How to Watch WNKY News 40 Broadcasts >\nDownload WNKY News 40 Apps\nThe Latest\nEdmonton police seek information on individual, vehicle in connection with investigation\nNew National Corvette Museum Collections Facility opens for tours on Jan. 13\nDriver's license pop-up events scheduled in Edmonson County\nSeven unclaimed veterans laid to rest at Kentucky Veterans Cemetery West\nPopular Articles\nGlasgow man formally charged with third-degree rape of minorPedestrian dies after being struck by vehicle in RussellvilleButler County man pleads guilty in case of son's deathRecording device allegedly found in Grayson County High School bathroomMorgantown man arrested after reported vehicle pursuit ends in wreckKentucky State Treasurer looking to return more than $2 billion back to residents\nno iframe support!","content_cn":"1 / 0\n格拉斯哥警察局收到冒充 FBI 的诈骗报告\n2025 年 11 月 21 日\nWNKY 员工，\n分享此报道 Facebook Twitter 电子邮件 打印 LinkedIn Reddit\n肯塔基州格拉斯哥——格拉斯哥警察局表示，他们正在提醒公众注意社区内的一起诈骗案，有人冒充联邦调查局特工。\n警方称，他们已收到多起关于该诈骗在格拉斯哥地区传播的投诉。\n当局称，诈骗者会冒充 FBI 特工四处打电话。随后，来电者要求人们取出现金并与其见面，或向其电汇款项，以“解决他们的麻烦”。\n格拉斯哥警察局表示，FBI 绝不会致电或发送电子邮件给私人公民，要求付款或威胁逮捕。当局称，FBI 也不会要求通过电汇支付和解金来避免被捕。\n如果你认为自己可能是这起诈骗或任何其他网络诈骗的受害者，请向当地执法机构以及 FBI 的互联网犯罪投诉中心 ic3.gov 报案。\n指南：如何观看 WNKY News 40 的广播节目 >\n下载 WNKY News 40 应用\n最新消息\n埃德蒙顿警方寻求有关与调查相关人员和车辆的信息\n新的国家 Corvette 博物馆藏品设施将于 1 月 13 日开放参观\n埃德蒙森县安排驾照临时办理活动\n七名无人认领的退伍军人在肯塔基州西部退伍军人公墓下葬\n热门文章\n格拉斯哥男子被正式控以三级强奸未成年人罪\n行人在拉塞尔维尔被车辆撞击后死亡\n巴特勒县男子在儿子死亡案件中认罪\n据称在格雷森县高中卫生间发现录音设备\n莫尔甘敦男子在据报发生的车辆追逐以车祸结束后被捕\n肯塔基州财政部长寻求将超过 20 亿美元返还居民\n不支持 iframe！","publish_source":"wnky.com","publish_time":"2025-11-21T16:19:25+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3529","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"独家：FBI奥马哈分局随政策变化开始佩戴执法记录仪","title_en":"EXCLUSIVE: FBI Omaha to begin wearing bodycams as protocol changes","summary_cn":"WOWT独家报道，FBI奥马哈分局约100名内布拉斯加和艾奥瓦的探员已完成培训，将按FBI政策在预先计划的逮捕、行动和搜查令中使用执法记录仪，但不会全程佩戴，以保护调查机密与敏感线人手段。负责人称此举增加透明度与问责。报道提及奥马哈警方此前执法记录仪被盾牌遮挡引发讨论。","summary_en":"WOWT reports exclusively that about 100 FBI agents in Nebraska and Iowa have been trained and will begin using body-worn cameras under FBI policy for pre-planned arrests, operations, and search warrants, but not at all times, to protect confidential investigations and sensitive sources. The special agent in charge says it adds transparency and accountability. The story notes a recent Omaha police case where a shield blocked a chest camera.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:47:11.911084+00:00","url":"https://www.wowt.com/2024/09/19/exclusive-fbi-omaha-begin-wearing-bodycams-protocol-changes","content":"EXCLUSIVE: FBI Omaha to begin wearing bodycams as protocol changesBodycams are now required in some situations by FBI policy.By Brian MastrePublished: Sep. 19, 2024 at 5:39 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleOMAHA, Neb. (WOWT) - When something goes wrong, the public expects to see footage via a bodycam released in the name of transparency and accountability.For most police departments, the body-worn camera has become just another piece of their uniform and the tools of their job. Like handcuffs, a gun, or a police radio.But as more and more local agencies added bodycams to the budget, the FBI, DEA and ATF did not mandate them. It wasn’t until five years ago that the Department of Justice started a pilot program for cameras to be used by federal agents in task forces where local officers and deputies take part in the investigations.The cameras are now FBI policy.“This month, we’ve now received the equipment here at FBI Omaha,” said Special Agent in Charge Eugene Kowel.Kowel says that 100 or so agents in Nebraska and Iowa have now been trained and will begin using the cameras — but not for everything they do.“These will be used for pre-planned arrests, pre-planned operations and pre-planned search warrants,” Kowel said. “They won’t be used for everything. We won’t wear them all the time. There are many situations where we want to protect the confidential nature of an investigation or sensitive sources and techniques.”The FBI is often at the forefront when it comes to using technology in investigations such as cybercrime and crimes against children. In this case, they’re adding what has become a best-practices element in law enforcement.“We hope to never have an agent involved in a shooting or use of force, but sometimes it does occur,” Kowel said. “We think that by wearing body-worn cameras in these operations, it’s an extra layer of transparency and accountability to the community.”Bodycams have been a topic of discussion in Omaha recently after the shield blocked the chest camera worn by Omaha Police during a search warrant that resulted in a shooting. OPD is testing whether it would be best to put a second camera on the shield or the helmet for the SWAT team. Copyright 2024 WOWT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"独家：随着规程变化，FBI奥马哈分局将开始佩戴执法记录仪\n根据FBI政策，在某些情况下现在必须使用执法记录仪。\n记者：布莱恩·马斯特雷\n发表于：2024年9月19日下午5:39（中部夏令时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上设为首选来源\n内布拉斯加州奥马哈（WOWT）——当出现问题时，公众希望看到以透明和问责为名公开的执法记录仪画面。\n对于大多数警察部门来说，执法记录仪已经成为制服和工作工具中的又一件装备，就像手铐、枪支或警用无线电一样。\n但随着越来越多的地方机构将执法记录仪列入预算，FBI、缉毒局和烟酒枪炮及爆炸物管理局并未强制要求使用。直到五年前，司法部才启动试点项目，让联邦特工在地方警员和警长办公室副警长参与调查的联合工作组中使用摄像机。\n如今，摄像机已成为FBI政策的一部分。\n“本月，我们终于在FBI奥马哈分局收到了设备，”主管特工尤金·科韦尔说。\n科韦尔表示，内布拉斯加州和爱荷华州约有100名特工现已接受培训，并将开始使用摄像机——但并非用于他们所做的一切工作。\n“这些摄像机将用于预先计划的逮捕、预先计划的行动以及预先计划的搜查令执行，”科韦尔说。“它们不会用于所有事情。我们不会一直佩戴。有许多情况下，我们希望保护调查的机密性质，或保护敏感来源和技术。”\n在网络犯罪和侵害儿童等调查中，FBI往往处于技术应用的前沿。在此情况下，他们正在加入执法部门已形成最佳实践的一项措施。\n“我们希望永远不会有特工卷入枪击或使用武力，但有时确实会发生，”科韦尔说。“我们认为，在这些行动中佩戴执法记录仪，可以为社区的透明度和问责增加一层保障。”\n最近，执法记录仪在奥马哈成为讨论话题。此前，奥马哈警察局在执行一份最终导致枪击事件的搜查令时，防弹盾牌挡住了警员佩戴的胸前摄像机。奥马哈警察局正在测试，对于特警队而言，最好是在盾牌上还是头盔上加装第二台摄像机。\n版权所有2024 WOWT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wowt.com","publish_time":"2024-09-19T22:39:17.787000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2267","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"道格拉斯县警长办公室与国土安全部调查南奥马哈和贝尔维尤的劳工贩运案","title_en":"DCSO, Homeland Security investigate human trafficking in South Omaha, Bellevue","summary_cn":"道格拉斯县警长办公室与美国国土安全部于周四在南奥马哈和贝尔维尤执行九份搜查令，调查一起劳工贩运案。据称一名雇主涉嫌将劳工偷运入社区，支付低于最低工资的报酬，并强迫他们住在雇主拥有的住房中，费用等于其工资。多个地方、县、州及联邦执法机构协助执行。案件仍在调查中，已移交美国检察官办公室。","summary_en":"The Douglas County Sheriff's Office and U.S. Homeland Security served nine warrants Thursday in South Omaha and Bellevue as part of a joint labor trafficking investigation. An employer is alleged to have smuggled laborers into the community, paid them below minimum wage, and forced them to live in employer-owned housing at a cost equal to their pay. Multiple local, county, state, and federal agencies assisted. The case remains under investigation and is pending with the U.S. Attorney's Office.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:18:52.301739+00:00","url":"https://www.wowt.com/2025/10/10/dcso-homeland-security-investigate-human-trafficking-south-omaha-bellevue","content":"DCSO, Homeland Security investigate human trafficking in South Omaha, BellevueSmuggled workers allegedly paid scarce wages, forced to live in employer’s homesAuthorities served nine warrants Thursday in South Omaha and Bellevue as part of a joint investigation into labor trafficking in the area.By Gina DvorakPublished: Oct. 9, 2025 at 8:29 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleOMAHA, Neb. (WOWT) - Douglas County Sheriff’s deputies and U.S. Homeland Security served nine warrants Thursday in South Omaha and Bellevue as part of a joint investigation into labor trafficking in the area. “The investigation centers on an employer alleged to have smuggled laborers into the community. The employer is further accused of paying employees below minimum wage and forcing them to live in housing owned by the employer at a cost equal to their rate of pay,“ the Douglas County Sheriff’s Office stated in a news release Thursday night.DCSO shared four approximate locations where the warrants were served, stating that multiple locations in Bellevue were also included in the search and arrest warrants served Thursday.Several local, county and state law enforcement personnel had assisted in executing the warrants, including DCSO SWAT, Nebraska State Patrol, and Omaha and Bellevue police. Multiple federal agencies were also involved, including the Drug Enforcement Agency, the Internal Revenue Service, FBI, and the U.S. Bureau of Alcohol Tobacco Firearms and Explosives.DCSO SWAT also served a federal search warrant near 157th and Lincoln they said was related to an ongoing firearms investigation, according to the release.“Both cases remain under investigation and are pending with the U.S. Attorney’s Office,” the release states. —Get a first alert to breaking news delivered to your inbox. Sign up for First Alert 6 email alerts.Copyright 2025 WOWT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"道格拉斯县警长办公室、国土安全部调查南奥马哈和贝尔维尤的人口贩运\n据称被偷运来的工人获得微薄工资，被迫住在雇主家中\n周四，当局在南奥马哈和贝尔维尤执行了9份搜查令，这是该地区联合调查劳工贩运行动的一部分。\n作者：吉娜·德沃拉克\n发表于：2025年10月9日美国中部夏令时间晚上8:29\n分享\n在谷歌上添加我们\n在谷歌上添加为首选来源\n内布拉斯加州奥马哈（WOWT）——道格拉斯县警长办公室副警长和美国国土安全部周四在南奥马哈和贝尔维尤执行了9份搜查令，这是对该地区劳工贩运进行联合调查的一部分。\n道格拉斯县警长办公室周四晚间在一份新闻稿中表示：“调查围绕一名据称将劳工偷运进社区的雇主展开。该雇主还被指控向员工支付低于最低工资的薪酬，并强迫他们住在雇主拥有的住房中，住房费用等于他们的工资。”\n道格拉斯县警长办公室公布了执行搜查令的大致4个地点，并表示周四执行的搜查和逮捕令还涉及贝尔维尤的多个地点。\n包括道格拉斯县警长办公室特警队、内布拉斯加州巡警以及奥马哈和贝尔维尤警方在内的多个地方、县和州执法机构人员协助执行了搜查令。多个联邦机构也参与其中，包括缉毒局、国税局、联邦调查局以及美国烟酒枪械及爆炸物管理局。\n根据新闻稿，道格拉斯县警长办公室特警队还在第157街与林肯街附近执行了一份联邦搜查令，据称该搜查令与一项正在进行的枪支调查有关。\n新闻稿称：“两起案件仍在调查中，目前由美国检察官办公室处理。”\n—第一时间获取突发新闻，直接发送到您的收件箱。注册“第一警报6”电子邮件提醒。\n版权所有2025 WOWT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wowt.com","publish_time":"2025-10-10T01:29:56.786000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1401","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"ATM劫持案嫌疑人因奥马哈发出的逮捕令被列入FBI头号通缉名单","title_en":"ATM jackpotting suspect added to FBI most wanted list after warrant issued from Omaha","summary_cn":"联邦当局周四将49岁的阿尼巴尔·亚历山大·卡内隆·阿吉雷列入FBI“十大通缉犯”名单，并因奥马哈发出的联邦逮捕令悬赏高达100万美元。他涉嫌参与ATM劫持阴谋，为外国恐怖组织提供资金。FBI认为他携带武器且危险，与委内瑞拉和墨西哥有联系。此案由联合特遣部队火神调查，与奥马哈性贩运案有关联。","summary_en":"Federal authorities on Thursday added Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre, 49, to the FBI's Ten Most Wanted Fugitives list, issuing a federal warrant out of Omaha and offering up to $1 million for information leading to his arrest. He is wanted in an ATM jackpotting conspiracy that authorities say funds a foreign terrorist organization. The FBI believes he is armed and dangerous and has ties to Venezuela and Mexico. The case is investigated by Joint Task Force Vulcan and is linked to an Omaha sex trafficking case.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:18:18.714107+00:00","url":"https://www.wowt.com/2026/03/12/atm-jackpotting-suspect-added-fbi-most-wanted-list-after-warrant-issued-omaha","content":"ATM jackpotting suspect added to FBI most wanted list after warrant issued from Omaha Federal authorities say Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre funds foreign terrorists, is armed and dangerousAnibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre, 49, is wanted in an ATM jackpotting conspiracy investigation.By John Chapman and Gina DvorakPublished: Mar. 12, 2026 at 2:00 PM CDT|Updated: Mar. 12, 2026 at 8:00 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleOMAHA, Neb. (WOWT) - Federal authorities on Thursday added a name to its “Ten Most Wanted Fugitives” list, issuing a federal warrant for his arrest out of Omaha and offering a reward of up to $1 million for information leading directly to his arrest.Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre, 49, is wanted in an ATM jackpotting conspiracy investigation that federal authorities say provides a revenue stream to a foreign terrorist organization, according to information FBI Omaha and U.S. Attorney’s Office for the District of Nebraska shared at a news conference Thursday afternoon. Authorities believe he is armed and dangerous.Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre(FBI Omaha)Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre stands about 5-feet-5 and 5-feet-7 tall, weighs approximately 190 pounds, and has black and gray hair. He has ties to Venezuela and Mexico and is known to speak Spanish. He also goes by the names “Prometheus” and “The Engineer.”Anyone with information about this case is urged to call the FBI’s Toll-Free tipline at 1-800-CALL-FBI (225-5324). They can also reach out to FBI Omaha or the FBI office nearest them, or contact the nearest American Embassy or Consulate. Tips can also be submitted online at tips.fbi.gov.“Canelon Aguirre led a vast conspiracy to commit cyber attacks against financial institutions in communities across our country on behalf of Tren de Aragua,” Kowel said in the release.Groundbreaking investigationSpecial Agent Kowel said Canelon Aguirre is the first person accused of cybercrimes to be added to the “Ten Most Wanted” list. The FBI believes he is funding TdA by installing malware on ATMs that provides unauthorized withdrawal of cash; then funneling that stolen cash through a complex money laundering network.The unique crime has prompted federal officials to file unique charges.“In this case, this individual — Mr. Aguirre — was charged with an offense that, to my knowledge, has not been charged anywhere nationally before — and specifically with material support based on a computer access crime that is unique to the facts of this case,\" U.S. Attorney Lesley Woods said. Canelon Aguirre is facing the following charges: conspiracy to commit bank fraud; conspiracy to commit bank burglary and intentionally camage a protected Computer System; Conspiracy to Commit Money Laundering; and Conspiracy to Provide Material Support to Terrorists, the FBI Omaha’s news release states. “Canelon Aguirre is the alleged mastermind behind the malware that Tren de Aragua deployed against federally insured banks across the United States of America to raise millions of dollars for the terrorist organization. Without the malware, these crimes would not have been possible.”U.S. Attorney Lesley Woods“Canelon Aguirre is a threat to national security, and information leading to his arrest would make Nebraska and the rest of the country safer. Arresting Canelon Aguirre would financially devastate TdA, one of the most violent and most active terrorist organizations operating within the United States today,” Woods said in the news release. The FBI said Thursday that they think Canelon Aguirre has committed some of the crimes here in the Omaha metro while he was in South America.“Canelon Aguirre did all of his work remotely from Venezuela utilizing remote access, remote control software to install the malware on ATMs, with assistance from his crews on the ground here,” Kowel said. “...Once the cyber intrusion had been completed, the ATM could be directed to dispense all the cash in the machine.”Joint Task Force Vulcan, launched in August 2019 as a coordinated federal effort to take down MS-13, is investigating the case in conjunction with the Computer Crime and Intellectual Property Section, part of the U.S. Department of Justice.Links to Omaha sex trafficking caseThe alleged crimes are believed to have cost banks across the country tens of millions of dollars, all to fund TdA’s terrorist activities. And there have been arrests made. The latest information from the U.S. Attorney’s Office in the Nebraska district shows that 250 TdA individuals have been charged with various federal crimes across the country — 113 of them in the District of Nebraska. The Omaha metro area has been witness to some of the crimes allegedly connected to money stolen from ATMs, including the case involving the sex trafficking of minors at area motels. “We filed that one in the spring of last year, and then that case was brought later. But that is financially related to the TdA sex-trafficking case. So the FBI actually did excellent work in that case — to ‘follow the money,’ so to speak — on the human trafficking angle. And then that led the search warrant that we executed against those area hotels,\" Woods said.—Watch breaking news unfold on our livestream. Download the First Alert 6 streaming app to your TV or find us in your favorite streaming platform.Copyright 2026 WOWT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"ATM取款机“爆破”案嫌疑人在签发逮捕令后被列入 FBI 最通缉名单\n联邦当局称，Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre 为外国恐怖分子提供资金，持有武器且十分危险\n49岁的 Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre 因参与 ATM 取款机“爆破”阴谋调查而被通缉。\n\n作者：John Chapman 和 Gina Dvorak\n发布于：2026年3月12日下午2:00 CDT|更新于：2026年3月12日晚上8:00 CDT\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n\n内布拉斯加州奥马哈（WOWT）——联邦当局周四将一名嫌疑人的姓名加入“十大通缉逃犯”名单，并从奥马哈签发联邦逮捕令，同时悬赏最高100万美元，征集能够直接促成其被捕的信息。\n\n据 FBI 奥马哈办事处和内布拉斯加州地区联邦检察官办公室周四下午在新闻发布会上公布的信息，49岁的 Anibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre 因参与一项 ATM 取款机“爆破”阴谋调查而被通缉。联邦当局称，这一阴谋为一个外国恐怖组织提供了收入来源。当局认为他持有武器且十分危险。\n\nAnibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre\n（FBI 奥马哈办事处）\n\nAnibal Alexander Canelon Aguirre 身高约5英尺5英寸至5英尺7英寸，体重约190磅，头发黑白相间。他与委内瑞拉和墨西哥有联系，会说西班牙语。他还使用“普罗米修斯”和“工程师”的名字。\n\n任何掌握此案信息的人都请拨打 FBI 免费举报热线 1-800-CALL-FBI（225-5324）。也可以联系 FBI 奥马哈办事处或离自己最近的 FBI 办公室，或者联系最近的美国大使馆或领事馆。还可以通过 tips.fbi.gov 在线提交线索。\n\n“Canelon Aguirre 代表 Tren de Aragua，在我们全国各地的社区策划了针对金融机构的大规模网络攻击阴谋，”Kowel 在新闻稿中说。\n\n开创性调查\n\n特别探员 Kowel 表示，Canelon Aguirre 是首名因涉嫌网络犯罪而被列入“十大通缉”名单的人。FBI 认为，他通过在 ATM 上安装恶意软件，使其能够未经授权提取现金，从而为 TdA 提供资金；随后再通过复杂的洗钱网络转移这些赃款。\n\n这种独特的犯罪促使联邦官员提出了独特的指控。\n\n“在本案中，这名个人——Aguirre 先生——被指控犯有一种据我所知此前在全国任何地方都未曾以此罪名起诉过的罪行，具体来说，是基于一种计算机访问犯罪而提出的实质性支持指控，而这种计算机访问犯罪是本案事实所独有的，”美国检察官 Lesley Woods 说。FBI 奥马哈办事处的新闻稿称，Canelon Aguirre 面临以下指控：共谋实施银行欺诈；共谋实施银行盗窃并故意损坏受保护的计算机系统；共谋洗钱；以及共谋向恐怖分子提供实质性支持。“Canelon Aguirre 是 Tren de Aragua 部署恶意软件、攻击美国各地联邦保险银行，以便为该恐怖组织筹集数百万美元的幕后主谋。没有这些恶意软件，这些犯罪就不可能发生。”\n\n美国检察官 Lesley Woods\n\n“Canelon Aguirre 对国家安全构成威胁，任何能够促成其被捕的信息都将使内布拉斯加州及全国其他地区更加安全。逮捕 Canelon Aguirre 将在财务上摧毁 TdA——这是当前在美国境内活动的最暴力、最活跃的恐怖组织之一，”Woods 在其\n新闻稿。联邦调查局周四表示，他们认为卡内隆·阿吉雷在南美期间，在奥马哈都会区实施了这里的一些犯罪。“卡内隆·阿吉雷在委内瑞拉远程完成了所有操作，利用远程访问和远程控制软件将恶意软件安装到自动取款机上，同时得到他在这里的地面团队协助，”科韦尔说。“……网络入侵完成后，就可以指示自动取款机吐出机器内的全部现金。”\n\n“火神联合特遣部队”于2019年8月启动，是一项旨在协调联邦力量取缔MS-13的行动。该部队正与美国司法部下属的计算机犯罪与知识产权科合作调查此案。\n\n与奥马哈性贩运案件的联系\n\n据信，这些涉嫌犯罪使全国各地的银行损失了数千万美元，而这些资金全部用于资助TdA的恐怖活动。此外，已有人员被捕。内布拉斯加地区联邦检察官办公室的最新信息显示，全国共有250名TdA人员被控犯有各种联邦罪行，其中113人在内布拉斯加地区。奥马哈都会区也见证了一些据称与从自动取款机盗取的钱有关的犯罪，包括当地汽车旅馆涉及未成年人性贩运的案件。“我们在去年春天提起了那起案件，之后该案又有了进展。但那在财务上与TdA性贩运案件有关。因此，联邦调查局实际上在那起案件中做得非常出色——可以说，是沿着资金流向追查——从人口贩运角度展开调查。随后，这就促成了我们对当地那些酒店执行的搜查令，”伍兹说。\n\n—在我们的直播中观看突发新闻的进展。将First Alert 6流媒体应用下载到电视上，或在你最喜欢的流媒体平台上找到我们。\n\n版权归2026年WOWT所有。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wowt.com","publish_time":"2026-03-12T19:00:24.687000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-793","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部长在奥马哈全国警长协会年会上发表讲话","title_en":"Homeland Security secretary addresses sheriffs at Omaha convention","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部长马克韦恩·穆林在奥马哈CHI健康中心举行的全国警长协会年会上向数千名警长发表讲话，表示其首要任务是重建美国民众对国土安全部的信任，并称希望该部门在执法中“重新变得不引人注目”。道格拉斯县警长汉森及肯塔基州警长皮涅罗伊表示，此次会议为全国警长提供了交流与协作机会。会议为期四天。","summary_en":"U.S. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin addressed thousands of sheriffs at the National Sheriffs' Association annual conference in Omaha, saying his top priority is restoring public trust in the department and that he wants DHS to become \"invisible again\" in law enforcement. Douglas County Sheriff Aaron Hanson and Kentucky Sheriff Ramon Pineiroa said the four-day gathering offers valuable networking and collaboration opportunities for sheriffs nationwide.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:21:44.741336+00:00","url":"https://www.wowt.com/2026/06/09/homeland-security-secretary-addresses-sheriffs-omaha-convention","content":"Homeland Security secretary addresses sheriffs at Omaha conventionThousands of law enforcement officials gather for National Sheriffs’ Association annual conferenceHomeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin addressed sheriffs Monday, saying he wants to regain the public’s trust.By Andrew PfeiferPublished: Jun. 8, 2026 at 10:26 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleOMAHA, Neb. (WOWT) - The National Sheriffs’ Association opened its annual conference Monday at the CHI Health Center, drawing thousands of sheriffs from across the country and a member of President Donald Trump’s cabinet.Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin addressed sheriffs Monday, saying he wants to regain the public’s trust.“I think the biggest priorities that we have is restoring confidence back in the American people. We have been demonized so much,” Mullin said.With the DHS’ recent involvement in ICE operations nationwide, Mullin said he wants the DHS to stay out of the spotlight.“I simply want to enforce the laws that congress passed, and the only way we can do that is to become invisible again,” Mullin said.Douglas County Sheriff Aaron Hanson said Omaha went through a thorough selection process to be chosen for this year’s convention.“Not only is this a great opportunity to showcase our county, our city, but it’s an awesome opportunity for sheriffs all across the country to come collaborate and network with a goal of keeping our community safe,” Hanson said.Sheriff Ramon Pineiroa from Nelson County, Kentucky, said learning from other communities has been valuable.“The comradery, the networking, seeing how it’s done in other towns whether small or larger,” Pineiroa said.Pineiroa said the networking opportunities extend beyond the conference.“You can call somebody from 1000 miles away or 5-6 states away and they’ll answer and give you guidance,” he said.Hanson said Omaha is making an impression on visiting sheriffs.“I think what’s coming across loud and clear to these Sheriffs is that Omaha is a hidden gem,” Hanson said.The NSA has over 14,000 active members. The conference lasts four days and will wrap up on Thursday.Copyright 2026 WOWT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"国土安全部长在奥马哈会议上向治安官发表讲话\n数千名执法官员齐聚全国治安官协会年度会议\n国土安全部长Markwayne Mullin周一向治安官们发表讲话，称他希望重新赢得公众信任。\n作者：Andrew Pfeifer\n发布于：2026年6月8日晚上10:26（CDT）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n内布拉斯加州奥马哈（WOWT）——全国治安官协会周一在CHI Health Center举行年度会议开幕式，吸引了来自全国各地的数千名治安官以及总统Donald Trump内阁的一名成员。\n国土安全部长Markwayne Mullin周一向治安官们发表讲话，称他希望重新赢得公众信任。\nMullin说：“我认为我们最重要的优先事项是恢复美国人民的信心。我们一直被妖魔化得太厉害了。”\n鉴于国土安全部近期参与了全国范围内的ICE行动，Mullin表示，他希望国土安全部远离聚光灯。\nMullin说：“我只想执行国会通过的法律，而我们做到这一点的唯一方式，就是再次变得不引人注目。”\n道格拉斯县治安官Aaron Hanson表示，奥马哈经过了严格的遴选程序才被选为今年大会的举办地。\nHanson说：“这不仅是展示我们县和我们城市的绝佳机会，也是全国各地治安官前来合作和交流、以维护社区安全这一目标的绝佳机会。”\n肯塔基州尼尔森县治安官Ramon Pineiroa表示，向其他社区学习非常有价值。\nPineiroa说：“这种同志情谊、交流，以及了解其他城镇——无论规模较小还是较大——是如何开展工作的。”\nPineiroa表示，这些交流机会延伸至会议之外。\n他说：“你可以给1,000英里外或相隔5至6个州的人打电话，他们会接听并给你指导。”\nHanson表示，奥马哈给来访治安官留下了深刻印象。\nHanson说：“我认为这些治安官清楚地感受到，奥马哈是一颗隐藏的宝石。”\n全国治安官协会拥有超过14,000名活跃会员。会议为期四天，将于周四结束。\n版权所有2026 WOWT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wowt.com","publish_time":"2026-06-09T03:26:04.699000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-525","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI在南奥马哈枪支贩运调查中缴获71支枪及逾4万美元现金","title_en":"FBI seizes 71 guns, more than $40K in cash in South Omaha gun trafficking investigation","summary_cn":"奥马哈FBI办公室宣布，在枪支贩运调查中缴获70多支枪和逾4万美元现金，并逮捕36岁的Jose Gerardo Ruiz-Alonso，其被控枪支罪名，据称2012年旅游签证逾期后非法滞留美国。法庭记录显示，一家银行因其生意出现洗钱迹象而通报调查人员，随后FBI派线人向其购买枪支，并在突袭其住所和商铺时查获71支枪及数千美元现金。","summary_en":"Omaha's FBI office announced agents seized more than 70 guns and over $40,000 in cash in a gun trafficking investigation and arrested 36-year-old Jose Gerardo Ruiz-Alonso on gun charges; he is allegedly in the country illegally after overstaying a tourist visa in 2012. Court records show a bank tipped off investigators over signs of money laundering at his business, leading agents to send a confidential informant to buy guns before raiding his home and business, where 71 guns and thousands in cash were found.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:21:57.483726+00:00","url":"https://www.wowt.com/2026/07/22/fbi-seizes-71-guns-more-than-40k-cash-south-omaha-gun-trafficking-investigation","content":"FBI seizes 71 guns, more than $40K in cash in South Omaha gun trafficking investigationOmaha’s FBI office announced agents seized more than 70 guns and over $40,000 in cash in a gun trafficking investigation.By Mike BellPublished: Jul. 22, 2026 at 5:30 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleOMAHA, Neb. (WOWT) - Omaha’s FBI office announced agents seized more than 70 guns and over $40,000 in cash in a gun trafficking investigation.Agents arrested Jose Gerardo Ruiz-Alonso, 36, on gun charges. He is allegedly in the country illegally after overstaying a tourist visa in 2012.FBI Omaha gun bust(Courtesy FBI Omaha)Court records reveal a bank tipped off investigators after Ruiz-Alonso’s business showed signs of money laundering. That led investigators to discover his alleged side business dealing firearms.Agents sent a confidential informant to Ruiz-Alonso’s business in South Omaha to buy a gun. Investigators say Ruiz-Alonso took the informant to a side room in his warehouse where at least 15 guns were on the counter. Ruiz-Alonso allegedly sold three guns to the informant.FBI Omaha gun bust(Courtesy FBI Omaha)When the FBI raided his home and business this week, agents found 71 guns and thousands of dollars in cash.Investigators say Ruiz-Alonso obtained most of the guns through parking lot deals at gun shows where he did not have to show identification.Copyright 2026 WOWT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局在南奥马哈枪支贩运调查中查获71支枪和超过4万美元现金\n奥马哈联邦调查局办公室宣布，特工在一项枪支贩运调查中查获了70多支枪和超过4万美元现金。\n作者：Mike Bell\n发布于：2026年7月22日，中部夏令时间下午5:30\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n内布拉斯加州奥马哈（WOWT）——奥马哈联邦调查局办公室宣布，特工在一项枪支贩运调查中查获了70多支枪和超过4万美元现金。\n特工以枪支相关罪名逮捕了36岁的Jose Gerardo Ruiz-Alonso。据称，他在2012年旅游签证逾期后非法滞留在美国。\n奥马哈联邦调查局枪支突袭行动（图片由奥马哈联邦调查局提供）\n法院记录显示，一家银行在Ruiz-Alonso的企业出现洗钱迹象后向调查人员通报了情况。这使调查人员发现了他涉嫌经营的枪支交易副业。\n特工派遣一名机密线人前往Ruiz-Alonso在南奥马哈的企业购买枪支。调查人员称，Ruiz-Alonso将线人带到其仓库的一个侧室，柜台上至少摆放着15支枪。据称，Ruiz-Alonso向线人出售了三支枪。\n奥马哈联邦调查局枪支突袭行动（图片由奥马哈联邦调查局提供）\n本周联邦调查局突袭他的住宅和企业时，特工发现了71支枪和数千美元现金。\n调查人员称，Ruiz-Alonso获得的大多数枪支来自枪展停车场交易，在那里他无需出示身份证明。\n版权2026 WOWT。版权所有。","publish_source":"wowt.com","publish_time":"2026-07-22T22:30:10.798000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-327","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"调查发现：FBI在客户损失更多钱之前已知晓奥马哈旅行社问题","title_en":"FBI was aware of Omaha travel agent concerns before clients lost more money, investigation finds","summary_cn":"美国内布拉斯加州奥马哈旅行社Captivating Travels by Connie取消客户预付行程，客户称损失惨重，其中一场目的地婚礼涉及约20万美元。报道称，早在2025年6月18日，一家旅行管理公司终止其合同并向FBI报告，但FBI表示知晓相关指控，不评论是否已立案调查。","summary_en":"Clients of Omaha travel agency Captivating Travels by Connie lost prepaid trips after cancellations, with one destination wedding involving about $200,000. A travel management company terminated her contract and reported her to the FBI on June 18, 2025. The FBI said it is aware of the allegations but does not comment on whether an investigation is underway.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:11:19.958579+00:00","url":"https://www.wowt.com/2026/08/25/fbi-was-aware-omaha-travel-agent-concerns-before-clients-lost-more-money-investigation-finds","content":"FBI was aware of Omaha travel agent concerns before clients lost more money, investigation findsClients who paid upfront for trips got a message from the travel agent who left them with canceled reservations.By Mike McKnightPublished: Aug. 24, 2026 at 10:28 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleOMAHA, Neb. (WOWT) - Clients who paid upfront for trips got a message from the travel agent who left them with canceled reservations.A First Alert 6 investigation first brought this case to light last week. Tonight, new information adds to the clients’ frustration.The cancellation emailClients of Captivating Travels by Connie received an email informing them their trips were canceled.“Saying they are no longer in business, and all our reservations have been canceled,” said Stacy Russ, a client.The email promised refunds would be issued through the proper channels.“Also, it’s not so much about the money — it’s about the memories she has taken away from our families and our kids, really,” Russ said.A Facebook page titled “Connie Seastedt Victims” has 242 members. Traci Lutt says about 100 guests to her daughter’s Dominican Republic destination wedding paid upfront for bookings through Captivating Travels by Connie.“It’s not just a little bit here and there. No money has been received by the resort,” Lutt said. When asked how much money was involved, Lutt said, “Two hundred thousand — we’re not quite sure.”Where clients can turnDonna Dutcher of Celebrate Travel says clients of Connie Seastedt may have another avenue to pursue.“They can maybe go back to the host agency who she worked under and see if they have any insurance that would cover fraud. In order to even operate as a travel agent, she’s under someone,” Dutcher said.Captivating Travels by Connie has issued refunds to several clients, but five checks written to one couple all bounced.FBI involvement predates recent lossesFirst Alert 6 has learned that up to eight months before dozens of clients lost thousands of dollars in prepaid trips canceled by Captivating Travels by Connie, a travel management company had terminated her contract and reported her to the FBI.Neither the company nor its attorney wanted to be named while the investigation is ongoing, but the attorney sent an email stating the FBI became involved shortly after concerns about Seastedt were reported on June 18, 2025.More than eight months later, Heidi Gatling sent Connie Seastedt a $13,000 wire transfer for a trip that was later canceled.“My money could have been saved if this had been handled a year ago — over a year ago when they found out about this. And a lot of our money, actually, a lot of us,” Gatling said.A Federal Bureau of Investigation spokesperson said the FBI is aware of the allegations. However, the FBI does not comment on whether an investigation is underway.s at this time.”Copyright 2026 WOWT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"调查发现：在客户损失更多钱之前，FBI已知悉奥马哈旅行社相关担忧\n提前支付旅行费用的客户收到该旅行社发来的消息；该旅行社让他们的预订被取消。\n作者：Mike McKnight\n发布时间：2026年8月24日晚上10:28（CDT）\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n\n内布拉斯加州奥马哈（WOWT）——提前支付旅行费用的客户收到该旅行社发来的消息；该旅行社让他们的预订被取消。\n\nFirst Alert 6的一项调查上周首次披露了此案。今晚，新信息加剧了客户们的沮丧。\n\n取消邮件\n\nCaptivating Travels by Connie的客户收到一封电子邮件，通知他们旅行已被取消。\n\n“邮件说他们已不再营业，我们所有的预订都已被取消，”客户Stacy Russ说。\n\n该邮件承诺将通过适当渠道发放退款。\n\n“而且，这不完全是钱的问题——实际上，是她夺走了我们家人和孩子们的回忆，”Russ说。\n\n一个名为“Connie Seastedt Victims”的Facebook页面有242名成员。Traci Lutt说，约有100名参加其女儿在多米尼加共和国举办的目的地婚礼的宾客，通过Captivating Travels by Connie提前支付了预订费用。\n\n“这不是零星的一点钱。度假村没有收到任何款项，”Lutt说。当被问及涉及多少钱时，Lutt说：“二十万美元——我们还不太确定。”\n\n客户可以求助的途径\n\nCelebrate Travel的Donna Dutcher表示，Connie Seastedt的客户或许还有另一条途径可以追究。\n\n“他们或许可以回头联系她所隶属的主办旅行社，看看该机构是否有能够覆盖欺诈的保险。要想以旅行代理人的身份经营，她必须挂靠在某个机构之下，”Dutcher说。\n\nCaptivating Travels by Connie已向数名客户退款，但开给一对夫妇的五张支票均遭退票。\n\nFBI介入早于近期损失\n\nFirst Alert 6获悉，在数十名客户因Captivating Travels by Connie取消了已预付的旅行而损失数千美元之前最多八个月，一家旅行管理公司已终止了她的合同，并向FBI举报了她。\n\n在调查仍在进行期间，该公司及其律师均不愿具名，但该律师发送了一封电子邮件，表示在2025年6月18日报告有关Seastedt的担忧后不久，FBI便介入了。\n\n八个多月后，Heidi Gatling向Connie Seastedt电汇了13,000美元，用于一趟后来被取消的旅行。\n\n“如果这一问题在一年前——在他们发现这件事时的一年多以前——就得到处理，我的钱本可以保住。事实上，我们很多人的钱都本可以保住，”Gatling说。\n\n一名联邦调查局发言人表示，FBI知悉这些指控。不过，FBI不对是否正在进行调查发表评论。目前。”\n\n版权所有2026 WOWT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wowt.com","publish_time":"2026-08-25T03:28:28.747000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3427","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI搜查默特尔比奇牧师住宅，其妻死亡案受关注","title_en":"FBI searches home of Myrtle Beach pastor after wife's death :: WRAL.com","summary_cn":"据WMBF报道，美国联邦调查局（FBI）探员于周五搜查了默特尔比奇牧师约翰-保罗·米勒位于Coldwater Circle的住宅。FBI发言人凯文·惠勒证实这是一次授权搜查。米勒的妻子米卡今年在罗伯逊县被裁定死于自杀，其死亡因婚姻相关指控引发全国关注。搜查时米勒本人不在家，其去向不明。目前尚不清楚搜查是否与其妻死亡有关。","summary_en":"Federal Bureau of Investigation agents searched the Myrtle Beach home of pastor John-Paul Miller on Coldwater Circle on Friday, FBI spokesperson Kevin Wheeler confirmed as an authorized search. Miller's wife, Mica, was ruled to have died by suicide in Robeson County earlier this year, and her death drew national attention over allegations surrounding their marriage. Miller was not at the home and his whereabouts were unknown. It remains unclear whether the search is related to her death.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:42:14.205649+00:00","url":"https://www.wral.com/archive/21702936","content":"FBI searches home of Myrtle Beach pastor after wife's death\nFederal authorities on Friday were at the home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to an investigation that gained national attention, WMBF reports.\nPosted\n11/2/2024, 1:22:44 PM\nUpdated\n11/7/2024, 3:37:56 PM\nRelated\nsuicide\nFBI\nFederal Bureau of Investigation\nMyrtle Beach\nInvestigators say 30-year-old Mica Miller called 911 in Robeson County and told them she was about to take her own life. The circumstances surrounding her death made national headlines. (© WRAL)\nBy WMBF staff\nFederal authorities on Friday were at the home of a Myrtle Beach pastor linked to an investigation that gained national attention.\nFBI spokesperson Kevin Wheeler confirmed to WMBF News they were doing an authorized search at the home of John-Paul Miller on Coldwater Circle. No further information was provided.\nOther WRAL Top Stories\nWMBF News reporters Ale Espinosa and Ashley Boles were both at the scene throughout the afternoon and saw FBI agents at the home. They also saw agents going in and out of the home and carrying evidence bags.\nAs of around 4 p.m., neighbors told WMBF News the agents had been at Miller’s home for hours. By around 6 p.m., the FBI had cleared out.\n\"It‘s just one of those things that you don’t think would ever happen where you live,\" said Butch, a neighbor of Miller’s.\nEarlier this year authorities ruled Miller’s wife, Mica, died by suicide in Robeson County, North Carolina.\nMica Miller’s death gained national attention due to allegations surrounding her marriage to John-Paul Miller. At that time, John-Paul Miller was the pastor of Solid Rock Church in Myrtle Beach.\nIt‘s unclear if the FBI’s search was related to her death.\nJohn-Paul Miller, meanwhile, was not found at the home and his whereabouts were unknown Friday afternoon.\nButch said while he didn’t really know John-Paul Miller personally, one particular clue makes him think Miller had not been home for the past few days.\n\"He walks the dogs and basically goes back inside. That’s basically it,\" he said. \"It’s been a couple of days. His truck is gone. His truck was there yesterday, but it’s gone today.\"\nThe search also brought up emotions for the community and neighbors - as well as those who have followed the case since it first gained national attention.\n\"I’ve been following it since the day after it happened,\" said Gina Whittington. \"I watched the pastor announce Mica’s passing from inside the church, and followed it quickly. I was working today, and actually was on a TikTok live and it was announced that the FBI was at the pastor’s house. And it just went from there.\"\nCredits\nJessica Patrick\nweb_editor\nWMBF","content_cn":"FBI在妻子去世后搜查默特尔比奇牧师的住所\n据WMBF报道，联邦当局周五出现在一名与一项曾引起全国关注的调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师家中。\n发布于\n2024年11月2日，下午1:22:44\n更新于\n2024年11月7日，下午3:37:56\n相关\n自杀\nFBI\n联邦调查局\n默特尔比奇\n调查人员称，30岁的米卡·米勒在罗布森县拨打911，告诉他们她即将结束自己的生命。围绕其死亡的情形登上全国新闻头条。（© WRAL）\n作者：WMBF工作人员\n联邦当局周五出现在一名与一项曾引起全国关注的调查有关的默特尔比奇牧师家中。\nFBI发言人凯文·惠勒向WMBF新闻证实，他们正在科尔德沃特环路约翰-保罗·米勒的住所执行经授权的搜查。未提供进一步信息。\nWRAL其他头条新闻\nWMBF新闻记者阿莱·埃斯皮诺萨和阿什利·博尔斯整个下午都在现场，看到FBI探员在该住所内。他们还看到探员进出住所，并携带证物袋。\n截至下午约4点，邻居告诉WMBF新闻，探员已在米勒家中待了数小时。到晚上约6点，FBI已撤离。\n“这就是那种你不会认为会发生在自己居住地的事情，”米勒的一名邻居布奇说。\n今年早些时候，当局裁定米勒的妻子米卡在北卡罗来纳州罗布森县死于自杀。\n由于围绕米卡·米勒与约翰-保罗·米勒婚姻的指控，她的死亡引起全国关注。当时，约翰-保罗·米勒是默特尔比奇坚石教堂的牧师。\n目前尚不清楚FBI的搜查是否与她的死亡有关。\n与此同时，未在住所内找到约翰-保罗·米勒，周五下午其下落不明。\n布奇说，虽然他并不真正认识约翰-保罗·米勒本人，但有一条特别的线索让他认为米勒过去几天不在家。\n“他遛狗，然后基本上就回屋里。基本就是这样，”他说。“已经有几天了。他的卡车不见了。他的卡车昨天还在，但今天不见了。”\n这次搜查也激起了社区和邻居的情绪——以及自该案件首次引起全国关注以来一直关注此案的人们的情绪。\n“从事件发生的第二天起我就一直在关注，”吉娜·惠廷顿说。“我看到牧师在教堂内宣布米卡去世，随后很快就持续关注此事。我今天在工作，实际上当时正在TikTok直播中，直播里宣布FBI在牧师家中。然后事情就这样发展下去。”\n鸣谢\n杰西卡·帕特里克\n网络编辑\nWMBF","publish_source":"wral.com","publish_time":"2024-11-02T13:22:44+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3416","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI搜查住宅数日后，默特尔比奇牧师被捕","title_en":"Myrtle Beach pastor arrested days after FBI searches home following wife's death :: WRAL.com","summary_cn":"默特尔比奇Solid Rock Church牧师、45岁的约翰-保罗·米勒于周三被捕并被控袭击罪。数日前，美国联邦调查局（FBI）曾搜查其住宅，此前其分居妻子米卡于四月死亡。米卡之死因婚姻相关指控引发全国关注。周日，抗议者聚集在教堂对面，举着“为米卡讨公道”的标语。报道由WRAL员工撰写，WMBF亦有贡献。","summary_en":"John-Paul Miller, 45, a pastor at Solid Rock Church in Myrtle Beach, was arrested Wednesday and charged with assault, days after the Federal Bureau of Investigation searched his home following the April death of his estranged wife, Mica. Her death gained national attention over allegations surrounding their marriage. On Sunday, protesters lined up across from the church holding signs reading \"Justice for Mica.\" The report was by WRAL staff, with WMBF contributing.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:41:59.925599+00:00","url":"https://www.wral.com/archive/21711712","content":"Myrtle Beach pastor arrested days after FBI searches home following wife's death\n45-year-old John-Paul Miller, a pastor at Solid Rock Church, was arrested and charged with assault on Wednesday.\nPosted\n11/7/2024, 3:38:45 PM\nUpdated\n11/7/2024, 4:45:32 PM\nRelated\nMyrtle Beach\npastor\ncrime\narrest\nassault\nFBI\nFederal Bureau of Investigation\nsuicide\nA Myrtle Beach pastor is facing an assault charge. This comes just days after the FBI searched the pastor's home following the death of his wife. (© WRAL)\nBy WRAL staff\nA Myrtle Beach pastor has been arrested just days after the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) searched his home following the death of his estranged wife in April.\n45-year-old John-Paul Miller, a pastor at Solid Rock Church, was arrested and charged with assault on Wednesday.\nOther WRAL Top Stories\nJohn-Paul Miller (© WRAL)\nAuthorities said his wife, Mica Miller, died by suicide in April; her death gained national attention due to allegations surrounding her marriage to John-Paul.\nWMBF reported that federal authorities searched the pastor's home on Friday.\nOn Sunday, protesters were lined up across the street from Solid Rock Church, holding up signs that read \"Justice for Mica.\"\nWMBF contributed to this story.\nIf you're having suicidal thoughts or a mental health crisis, call or text 988 or call the National Suicide Prevention Lifeline at 800-273-8255. Veterans can press “1” after dialing 988 to connect directly to the Veterans Crisis Lifeline. For texts, veterans should continue to text the Veterans Crisis Lifeline short code: 838255.\nCredits\nDelaney Eyermann\nweb_editor\nWRAL","content_cn":"迈尔特尔比奇牧师在妻子去世后联邦调查局搜查其住所数日后被捕\n45岁的约翰-保罗·米勒是坚石教会的牧师，于周三被捕并被控袭击罪。\n发布\n2024年11月7日，下午3:38:45\n更新\n2024年11月7日，下午4:45:32\n相关\n迈尔特尔比奇\n牧师\n犯罪\n逮捕\n袭击\n联邦调查局\n联邦调查局\n自杀\n一名迈尔特尔比奇牧师面临袭击指控。就在几天前，联邦调查局在其妻子去世后搜查了这名牧师的住所。（© WRAL）\nWRAL工作人员\n一名迈尔特尔比奇牧师在其分居妻子于4月去世后，联邦调查局（FBI）搜查其住所数日后被捕。\n45岁的约翰-保罗·米勒是坚石教会的牧师，于周三被捕并被控袭击罪。\nWRAL其他热门报道\n约翰-保罗·米勒（© WRAL）\n当局称，他的妻子米卡·米勒于4月自杀身亡；由于围绕她与约翰-保罗婚姻的指控，她的死亡引起了全国关注。\nWMBF报道称，联邦当局于周五搜查了这名牧师的住所。\n周日，抗议者在坚石教会对面的街道上列队，举着写有“为米卡伸张正义”的标语。\nWMBF为本报道提供了素材。\n如果你有自杀念头或正经历心理健康危机，请拨打或短信联系988，或拨打全国自杀预防生命线800-273-8255。退伍军人在拨打988后可按“1”，直接接通退伍军人危机生命线。短信联系时，退伍军人应继续发送至退伍军人危机生命线短码：838255。\n署名\n德莱尼·艾尔曼\n网页编辑\nWRAL","publish_source":"wral.com","publish_time":"2024-11-07T15:38:45+00:00"}},{"id":"news-170","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"新娘称FBI就婚礼照片缺失问题询问Holly Christina摄影公司","title_en":"Bride claims FBI asking about Holly Christina Photography over missing wedding photos :: WRAL.com","summary_cn":"一名聘请Holly Christina Photography的新娘称，FBI探员致电她收集信息，以判断此事是否构成联邦犯罪。FBI以司法部政策为由拒绝确认或否认。该摄影公司被指收取数百对北卡新人费用后未提供服务或交付照片，公司两名负责人各面临一项重罪指控，北卡总检察长办公室已提起诉讼并寻求近60万美元赔偿及逾110万美元民事罚款。","summary_en":"A bride who hired Holly Christina Photography said an FBI agent called her to gather information and determine whether the matter could be a federal crime. The FBI declined to confirm or deny the inquiry, citing DOJ policy. The company is accused of taking money from hundreds of North Carolina couples without providing services or photos; its two owners each face a felony charge, and the state attorney general has sued, seeking nearly $600,000 in restitution and over $1.1 million in civil penalties.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:31:24.976338+00:00","url":"https://www.wral.com/consumer/5onyourside/bride-claims-fbi-investigating-holly-christina-photography-over-missing-wedding-photos-september-2026","content":"Bride claims FBI asking about Holly Christina Photography over missing wedding photos\nAccording to a bride who hired the photography company, an agent from the FBI called her to gather more information and determine if it should be considered a federal crime or not. The FBI declined to comment when asked by WRAL if it was looking into the case.\nPosted\n9/16/2026, 2:02:52 AM\nUpdated\n9/16/2026, 8:23:01 AM\nRelated\nconsumer\nscams\nattorney general\nfraud\n5 on Your Side\nFBI\nBy WRAL staff\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation could be the next agency to investigate Holly Christina Photography.\nAccording to a bride who hired the photography company, an agent from the FBI called her to gather more information and determine if it should be considered a federal crime or not.\nOther WRAL Top Stories\nWRAL reached out to the FBI for comment, but the agency said it could neither confirm nor deny the call, citing a Department of Justice policy.\nHundreds of North Carolina couples are out thousands of dollars after Holly Christina Photography took their money but never provided their services or never released the photos already taken.\nHolly Scott Ayscue and her husband Christopher Owen Ayscue, the co-owners of Holly Christina Photography, are each facing one count of felony obtaining property by false pretenses. The charges stem from a bride who said she paid the couple a $5,600 deposit that was never returned after the business closed.\nNorth Carolina’s Attorney General Jeff Jackson’s office also sued the company in February after receiving complaints from more than 220 people. The lawsuit alleged that the defendants misled and defrauded couples and their families by not providing the photographs and videos they were promised.\nIn May, a judge issued a preliminary injunction ordering the company to turn over all edited and unedited photos and videos within 30 days. The order also required the company to stop doing business and prohibited its owners from moving company assets while the case proceeded.\nJackson’s office says the company did not comply.\nThe attorney general is now seeking a final judgment requiring the delivery of every remaining photo and video, nearly $600,000 in restitution for affected consumers and more than $1.1 million in civil penalties. The requested judgment would also permanently prohibit the company and its owners from engaging in similar conduct.\nBoth owners of the company told reporters outside a Winston-Salem courthouse in August that they were doing \"everything\" in their power to make things right.\nA judge has not yet ruled on the attorney general’s request.\nA judge ordered that a Raleigh-based photography company that failed to deliver for Triangle couples on their wedding day turn over the photos and videos they are owed.\n© 2026 Copyright Capitol Broadcasting Company","content_cn":"新娘称，FBI就丢失婚礼照片一事询问 Holly Christina Photography\n据一名雇用该摄影公司的新娘称，一名FBI探员致电她，以收集更多信息并确定此事是否应被视为联邦犯罪。WRAL询问FBI是否正在调查此案时，FBI拒绝置评。\n发布于\n2026年9月16日，凌晨2:02:52\n更新于\n2026年9月16日，上午8:23:01\n相关\n消费者\n诈骗\n总检察长\n欺诈\n5 On Your Side\nFBI\n作者：WRAL工作人员\n联邦调查局可能成为下一个调查 Holly Christina Photography 的机构。\n据一名雇用该摄影公司的新娘称，一名FBI探员致电她，以收集更多信息并确定此事是否应被视为联邦犯罪。\n其他 WRAL 热门报道\nWRAL联系FBI寻求评论，但该机构援引司法部政策表示，既不能确认也不能否认这通电话。\n数百对北卡罗来纳州夫妇损失了数千美元，因为 Holly Christina Photography 收了他们的钱，却从未提供服务，或从未交付已拍摄的照片。\nHolly Christina Photography 的共同所有人 Holly Scott Ayscue 及其丈夫 Christopher Owen Ayscue 各面临一项以虚假借口取得财产的重罪指控。这些指控源于一名新娘的说法：她向这对夫妇支付了5,600美元订金，但该企业关闭后订金从未退还。\n北卡罗来纳州总检察长 Jeff Jackson 的办公室在收到220多人投诉后，也于2月起诉了该公司。诉讼指控被告未提供承诺的照片和视频，误导并欺诈了夫妇及其家人。\n5月，一名法官发布初步禁令，命令该公司在30天内交出所有已编辑和未编辑的照片及视频。该命令还要求该公司停止营业，并禁止其所有人在案件审理期间转移公司资产。\nJackson的办公室称，该公司未遵守命令。\n总检察长目前正寻求终审判决，要求交付每一份剩余的照片和视频，向受影响消费者支付近60万美元赔偿，并处以超过110万美元的民事罚款。所请求的判决还将永久禁止该公司及其所有人从事类似行为。\n该公司的两名所有人8月在温斯顿-塞勒姆法院外对记者表示，他们正在竭尽“全力”纠正问题。\n法官尚未就总检察长的请求作出裁决。\n一名法官命令一家总部位于罗利、未能在婚礼当天向三角地区夫妇提供服务的摄影公司，交出他们应得的照片和视频。\n© 2026 Capitol Broadcasting Company 版权所有","publish_source":"wral.com","publish_time":"2026-09-16T02:02:52+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1075","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI局长科米在弗吉尼亚被捕并短暂出庭","title_en":"Former FBI Director James Comey arrested in Virginia, appears briefly in court :: WRAL.com","summary_cn":"前美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长詹姆斯·科米在弗吉尼亚州向执法部门自首，并就一项指控短暂出庭。他被控在社交媒体发布含“86 47”字样的贝壳照片，构成对总统的威胁及跨州传递威胁。科米称自己“仍然无辜”，其律师表示将以“报复性和选择性起诉”抗辩。这是特朗普政府司法部第二次对科米提出指控。","summary_en":"Former FBI Director James Comey surrendered to authorities in Virginia and was briefly arraigned on charges of making and transmitting a threat against the president, tied to a social media post of seashells reading \"86 47.\" Comey said he is \"still innocent,\" and his attorney said they would challenge the case as a \"vindictive and selective prosecution.\" It is the second time Trump's Justice Department has charged Comey.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:40:15.587509+00:00","url":"https://www.wral.com/news/ap/comey-indicted-surrender-federal-courthouse-april-2026","content":"Former FBI Director James Comey arrested in Virginia, appears briefly in court\nFormer FBI Director James Comey surrendered to authorities in Virginia and was briefly arraigned on charges of making and transmitting a threat against the president, tied to a social media post reading “86 47.” Comey said he is “still innocent.”\nPosted\n4/29/2026, 12:47:45 PM\nUpdated\n4/29/2026, 11:48:12 PM\nRelated\nCNN\nTrump\ncrime\nFBI\nJames Comey appears in court after being indicted in North Carolina\nBy Hannah Rabinowitz, Kristen Holmes, Holmes Lybrand, Tierney Sneed, CNN\nFormer FBI Director James Comey surrendered Wednesday to law enforcement at federal court in the Eastern District of Virginia, according to a person familiar.\nAuthorities arrested Comey ahead of his first appearance in court. Wednesdays' hearing lasted less than 10 minutes.\nOther WRAL Top Stories\nComey is charged with making a threat against the president and transmitting a threat in interstate commerce, according to court documents.\nThe New York Times reported that Comey did not speak before the magistrate judge, William E. Fitzpatrick, but nodded along as he was reminded of his rights and the charges against him. The judge addressed mainly administrative matters, including the conditions of Comey’s release, during which he referred to the last time Comey appeared at the federal court in Alexandria, Virginia, over the first indictment the Justice Department brought against him.\n“I don’t think conditions of release are necessary,” Fitzpatrick said. “They weren’t necessary last time. They are not necessary this time.”\nFitzgerald was the only one who spoke for Comey, and told the court that they would be challenging the case by claiming a “vindictive and selective prosecution.”\nComey is expected to appear in court in North Carolina at a later date.\nIn a video message posted to Substack,  Comey said that he is “still innocent.”\nTuesday’s indictment is centered on a picture Comey posted on social media last May, of shells on a beach writing out the numbers “86 47.” He wrote in the caption, “Cool shell formation on my beach walk.”\nAlmost immediately following his post, Republicans and administration officials began criticizing Comey for what they said amounted to a death threat against President Donald Trump.\nWhen used as slang, the number 86 can refer to getting rid of or tossing something out. Trump is currently the 47th president.\nComey’s indictment comes as Blanche has picked up the pace in bringing cases that the president has publicly jockeyed for.\n“This is not going anywhere. This is clearly not a punishable threat,” Eugene Volokh, a senior fellow at the Hoover Institution at Stanford University who specializes in First Amendment law, told CNN Tuesday.\nThis is the second time that Trump’s Justice Department brought charges against Comey.\nIn September 2025, the Justice Department first brought charges against Comey, accusing him of lying to Congress over leaks to the press.\nThe case was dismissed late last year by a federal judge who found that the interim U.S. Attorney for the Eastern District of Virginia had been improperly appointed, having skirted approval from the Senate.\n© 2026 Copyright Capitol Broadcasting Company","content_cn":"前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米在弗吉尼亚州被捕，短暂出庭\n\n前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米向弗吉尼亚州当局自首，并因涉嫌制作和传播针对总统的威胁而短暂接受提审；相关指控与一则写有“86 47”的社交媒体帖子有关。科米说自己“仍然是无罪的”。\n\n发布于\n2026年4月29日，下午12:47:45\n\n更新于\n2026年4月29日，晚上11:48:12\n\n相关\nCNN\n特朗普\n犯罪\n联邦调查局\n\n詹姆斯·科米在北卡罗来纳州被起诉后出庭\n作者：Hannah Rabinowitz、Kristen Holmes、Holmes Lybrand、Tierney Sneed，CNN\n\n据知情人士称，前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米周三向执法部门自首，地点是弗吉尼亚东区联邦法院。\n\n当局在科米首次出庭前将其逮捕。周三的听证会持续不到10分钟。\n\nWRAL其他头条\n\n根据法庭文件，科米被控制作针对总统的威胁，并在州际商业中传播威胁。\n\n《纽约时报》报道称，科米没有在治安法官威廉·E·菲茨帕特里克面前发言，但在法官提醒其权利和所受指控时点头回应。法官主要处理行政事项，包括科米获释条件；期间法官提到科米上次在弗吉尼亚州亚历山德里亚联邦法院出庭的情况，那是司法部首次起诉他时。\n\n“我不认为有必要设置释放条件，”菲茨帕特里克说。“上次没有必要。这次也没有必要。”\n\n只有菲茨杰拉德代表科米发言，并告诉法庭，他们将以“报复性和选择性起诉”为由对案件提出质疑。\n\n预计科米稍后将在北卡罗来纳州出庭。\n\n科米在发布于Substack的视频消息中说，他“仍然是无罪的”。\n\n周二的起诉书围绕科米去年5月在社交媒体上发布的一张照片展开，照片中海滩上的贝壳摆出了“86 47”这几个数字。他在配文中写道：“在海滩散步时发现的酷炫贝壳造型。”\n\n他的帖子发布后几乎立刻，​​共和党人士和政府官员就开始批评科米，称其构成了对唐纳德·特朗普总统的死亡威胁。\n\n当作俚语使用时，数字86可以指摆脱或扔掉某物。特朗普目前是第47任总统。\n\n科米被起诉之际，布兰奇加快了办理总统公开推动的案件。\n\n“这不会有任何结果。这显然不是可惩罚的威胁，”斯坦福大学胡佛研究所高级研究员、专门研究第一修正案法律的尤金·沃洛克周二对CNN说。\n\n这是特朗普司法部第二次对科米提出指控。\n\n2025年9月，司法部首次起诉科米，指控他就向媒体泄密一事对国会撒谎。\n\n去年年底，一名联邦法官驳回了该案，理由是弗吉尼亚东区代理联邦检察官的任命程序不当，绕过了参议院批准。\n\n© 2026 Capitol Broadcasting Company版权所有","publish_source":"wral.com","publish_time":"2026-04-29T12:47:45+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2454","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"达勒姆被FBI突袭房屋的房主讲述租客异常行为","title_en":"Owner of Durham home raided by FBI details tenants' unusual behavior :: WRAL.com","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）突袭了达勒姆一处与“上帝全球国度教会”人口贩运和洗钱指控相关的住宅。房主吉姆·威尔方表示，他并不知晓针对租客的刑事指控，但注意到租客行为异常，包括加高围栏、封闭缝隙、安装大量摄像头等。联邦起诉书指控教会领袖强迫他人从事无薪工作并洗钱，涉案金额约5000万美元。多州相关房产也被突袭。","summary_en":"The FBI raided a Durham home tied to allegations of human trafficking and money laundering at Kingdom of God Global Church. Landlord Jim Wilfong said he was unaware of the criminal allegations against his tenants but noticed unusual behavior, including a heightened fence, sealed gaps and numerous cameras. A federal indictment accuses church leaders of forced unpaid labor and money laundering involving roughly $50 million. Properties in other states were also raided.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:50:37.016848+00:00","url":"https://www.wral.com/news/investigates/durham-fbi-raid-homeowner-tenants-unusual-behavior-august-2025","content":"Owner of Durham home raided by FBI details tenants' unusual behavior\nThe owner of a Durham home raided by the FBI said he was unaware of the criminal allegations against his tenant, who is connected to a church accused of human trafficking and money laundering.\nPosted\n8/28/2025, 9:53:09 PM\nUpdated\n8/29/2025, 1:02:27 PM\nRelated\nWRAL investigates\nWRAL specialists\ncrime\nDurham landlord discusses FBI raid on rental tied to investigation on self-proclaimed religious leader\nBy Sarah Krueger, WRAL investigative reporter\nThe man who owns the Durham home that FBI agents raided Wednesday says he noticed odd behavior from his tenants, but was stunned to learn of criminal allegations.\nWRAL News reported on the raid, tied to allegations of human trafficking at Kingdom of God Global Church. According to a federal indictment, church leaders forced people into unpaid work at call centers, soliciting money that was then used to buy luxury items like a boat and bulletproof cars.\nOther WRAL Top Stories\nProperties in other states, including Florida and Texas, were also raided. Charges were filed against David Taylor, of Durham, and Michelle Brannon, of Florida, related to forced labor and money laundering. The indictment says Taylor received roughly $50 million over the course of about 10 years.\nWRAL Investigates tracked down the owner of 2523 South Miami Blvd. through tax records, and spoke to him on the phone.\nJim Wilfong said he has been renting the property to a church for about 10 or 12 years. He said David Taylor is not the name on the lease.\n\"Like a lot of people in the neighborhood, [I was] unaware of what was going on,\" he said.\nOne thing that immediately stands out about the property is how fortified it is, with multiple cameras, \"no trespassing\" signs, covered windows, and a tall privacy fence. Wilfong says when the renters added the fence, he found it unusual.\n\"They raised the level of the fence higher than what normally is done,\" he said. \"They seamed all of the cracks between any of the uprights, which seemed odd.\"\nWilfong said that in his dealings with the man on the lease, he was polite yet private. WRAL Investigates is not naming him, as he has not been charged.\nWilfong says in the 10-plus years that the man rented the home, Wilfong went inside only once, early on, and noticed a lot of video equipment.\n\"Anytime there were any issues that normally I would be involved with as far as maintenance, they seemed to always go with some third party or some other maintenance organization,\" Wilfong said. \"They seemed to keep me at an arm's length.\"\nThe South Miami Boulevard home displays a large banner with the name Kingdom Restoration Church for All Nations. That is a different name from the church named in the federal indictment. State records show Kingdom Restoration Church for All Nations was founded in 2005 under a different name. The founder is the same man who Wilfong said is on the lease for the South Miami Boulevard home.\nWRAL Investigates has not found any connection in state documents between Kingdom Restoration Church for All Nations and David Taylor.\nA knock at the door of the home went unanswered Thursday, and the man who leases the home did not return WRAL Investigates' email or calls.\n© 2026 Copyright Capitol Broadcasting Company","content_cn":"达勒姆一处遭FBI突袭房屋的业主详述租户的异常行为\n达勒姆一处遭联邦调查局突袭房屋的业主表示，他不知道其租户面临的刑事指控；该租户与一所被控人口贩运和洗钱的教会有关联。\n发布于\n2025年8月28日，晚上9:53:09\n更新于\n2025年8月29日，下午1:02:27\n相关内容\nWRAL调查\nWRAL专家\n犯罪\n达勒姆房东谈及FBI突袭：出租房与针对一名自称宗教领袖的调查有关\n作者：WRAL调查记者Sarah Krueger\n拥有达勒姆这处周三遭FBI探员突袭房屋的男子表示，他注意到租户有异常行为，但得知存在刑事指控时仍感到震惊。\nWRAL新闻此前报道了此次突袭行动，该行动与Kingdom of God Global Church涉嫌人口贩运的指控有关。根据一份联邦起诉书，教会领导人强迫人们在呼叫中心无偿工作，募得的钱随后被用于购买游艇和防弹汽车等奢侈品。\n其他WRAL头条新闻\n佛罗里达州和得克萨斯州等其他州的房产也遭到突袭。来自达勒姆的David Taylor和来自佛罗里达州的Michelle Brannon因强迫劳动和洗钱相关罪名被起诉。起诉书称，Taylor在约10年间获得了大约5,000万美元。\nWRAL调查团队通过税务记录找到2523 South Miami Blvd.的业主，并与其进行了电话交谈。\nJim Wilfong表示，他已将该房产出租给一所教会约10或12年。他说，David Taylor并不是租约上的名字。\n“和社区里许多人一样，[我]不知道发生了什么事，”他说。\n该房产最显眼的特点之一是其防护严密：设有多个摄像头、“禁止擅入”标志、被遮挡的窗户以及高大的隐私围栏。Wilfong称，租户加装围栏时，他觉得很不寻常。\n“他们把围栏加高到了通常不会采用的高度，”他说。“他们把所有立柱之间的缝隙都封了起来，这看上去很奇怪。”\nWilfong表示，在与租约上的男子打交道时，对方礼貌但很注重隐私。由于此人尚未被起诉，WRAL调查团队没有公布其姓名。\nWilfong说，在该男子租住这所房子十余年间，他仅在早期进过屋一次，并注意到屋内有大量录像设备。\n“每当出现通常应由我参与处理的维修问题时，他们似乎总是找第三方或其他维修机构，”Wilfong说。“他们似乎一直让我保持距离。”\nSouth Miami Boulevard上的房屋挂着一幅大型横幅，上面写着Kingdom Restoration Church for All Nations。这个名称与联邦起诉书中所指的教会名称不同。州记录显示，Kingdom Restoration Church for All Nations于2005年以另一个名称成立。其创始人正是Wilfong所称列在South Miami Boulevard房屋租约上的那名男子。\nWRAL调查团队没有在州文件中发现Kingdom Restoration Church for All Nations与David Taylor之间的任何联系。\n周四，有人敲该房屋的门但无人应答，租住该房屋的男子也没有回复WRAL调查团队的电子邮件或电话。\n© 2026 Capitol Broadcasting Company版权所有","publish_source":"wral.com","publish_time":"2025-08-28T21:53:09+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1535","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI：罗利男子承认在联想中心附近持有机枪改装装置","title_en":"FBI: Raleigh man pleads guilty to having machine gun devices near Lenovo Center :: WRAL.com","summary_cn":"据美国联邦调查局（FBI）称，罗利男子路易斯·阿尔贝托·格拉-马丁内斯承认在2025年北卡罗来纳州博览会期间，于联想中心附近持有“机枪改装装置”。警方因其驾驶异常将其拦停，在其车中发现五支枪、两个可将半自动枪械改为全自动的装置，以及大麻、砍刀等物品。FBI罗利安全街道特别工作组等机构参与调查。他面临最高10年监禁，量刑听证定于5月5日。","summary_en":"According to the FBI, Raleigh man Luis Alberto Guerra-Martinez pleaded guilty to possessing \"machine gun conversion devices\" near the Lenovo Center during the 2025 North Carolina State Fair. Stopped for erratic driving, police found five guns, two drop-in sears that convert semi-automatic guns to fully automatic, marijuana, a machete and other items. The FBI Raleigh Safe Streets Taskforce and other agencies investigated. He faces up to 10 years in prison, with sentencing set for May 5.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:53:51.882209+00:00","url":"https://www.wral.com/news/local/raleigh-man-pleads-guilty-machine-gun-conversion-devices-lenovo-center-nc-state-fair-october-2025","content":"FBI: Raleigh man pleads guilty to having machine gun devices near Lenovo Center\nA Raleigh man has pleaded guilty to having \"machine gun conversion devices\" near the Lenovo Center during the North Carolina State Fair, according to the Federal Bureau of Investigation.\nPosted\n2/25/2026, 2:09:53 PM\nUpdated\n2/25/2026, 10:56:02 PM\nRelated\ncrime\nFBI\nLenovo Center\nNorth Carolina State Fairgrounds\nNorth Carolina State Fair\nFBI: Man had guns, machine gun devices near Raleigh concert and NC State Fair\nBy WRAL staff\nA Raleigh man has pleaded guilty to having \"machine gun conversion devices\" near Lenovo Center during the 2025 North Carolina State Fair, according to the Federal Bureau of Investigation.\nLuis Alberto Guerra-Martinez was charged in October 2025 with possession of a machine gun.\nOther WRAL Top Stories\nAccording to court documents, on Oct. 24, 2025, during the fair, Guerra-Martinez was stopped for driving erratically in the parking lot between the North Carolina State Fairgrounds and the Lenovo Center.\nEllis Boyle, U.S. Attorney for the Eastern District of North Carolina told WRAL News in a phone interview on Wednesday that a Dunn police officer working security had stopped Guerra-Martinez.\n\"I don't think they had any idea going into it that this was going to be a situation where they discover a whole arsenal of guns in the parking lot,\" Boyle said.\nGuerra-Martinez got out of his car and attempted to run away, officials said. According to documents, police found five guns and two drop-in sears in the car, which convert semi-automatic guns into fully automatic machine guns.\nOfficers also found marijuana, THC vape cartridges, a machete, a hunting knife and a Lenovo Center radio inside.\nA news release from the U.S. Attorney's Office says Guerra-Martinez had recently been fired Guerra-Martinez had recently been fired from Lenovo, where he had worked as a janitor for a third-party contractor.\nBoyle noted it's unclear why Guerra-Martinez was in the area that night.\n\"He was recently terminated from there, and you know, he was in the parking lot, he wasn't in going to the concert, he wasn't working, he wasn't at the State Fair, so it was certainly suspicious,\" he said.\nThere was an NBA Young Boy concert going on at Lenovo Center at the time, along with the thousands attending the fair.\n\"We needed to remove him from all this group of people, which, again, he didn't do anything like a mass shooting, but ... we were worried, and we had suspicions that we wanted to ensure that we protected the safety of the public,\" Boyle said.\nThe FBI Raleigh Safe Streets Taskforce, the Wake County Sheriff's Office, the Raleigh Police Department and the Dunn Police Department investigated the case, according to federal prosecutors.\n\"The FBI Safe Streets Violent Crime Initiative was designed to allow each FBI field office to address violent street gangs and drug-related violence through the establishment of FBI-sponsored, long-term, proactive task forces focusing on violent gangs, crimes of violence, and the apprehension of violent fugitives,\" said an FBI spokesperson in an email to WRAL.\nGuerra-Martinez faces up to 10\nyears in prison. He is scheduled for a sentencing hearing on May 5 in Wilmington.\n© 2026 Copyright Capitol Broadcasting Company","content_cn":"FBI：罗利男子承认在联想中心附近持有机枪装置\n据联邦调查局称，一名罗利男子承认在北卡罗来纳州博览会期间于联想中心附近持有“机枪转换装置”。\n发布时间\n2026年2月25日，下午2:09:53\n更新时间\n2026年2月25日，晚上10:56:02\n相关\n犯罪\nFBI\n联想中心\n北卡罗来纳州博览会场地\n北卡罗来纳州博览会\nFBI：男子在罗利音乐会和北卡罗来纳州博览会附近持有枪支及机枪装置\nWRAL工作人员报道\n据联邦调查局称，一名罗利男子承认在2025年北卡罗来纳州博览会期间于联想中心附近持有“机枪转换装置”。\n路易斯·阿尔贝托·格拉-马丁内斯于2025年10月被控持有机枪。\nWRAL其他头条新闻\n根据法庭文件，2025年10月24日博览会期间，格拉-马丁内斯因在北卡罗来纳州博览会场地与联想中心之间的停车场内危险驾驶而被拦下。\n东区北卡罗来纳州联邦检察官埃利斯·博伊尔周三在接受WRAL新闻电话采访时说，一名当时负责安保工作的邓恩警察拦下了格拉-马丁内斯。\n博伊尔说：“我不认为他们一开始会想到，这会变成在停车场发现整批枪支的情况。”\n官员称，格拉-马丁内斯下车后试图逃跑。根据文件，警方在车内发现了五支枪和两个插入式阻铁，这些装置可将半自动枪械改装成全自动机枪。\n警员还发现了大麻、含THC的电子烟弹匣、一把砍刀、一把猎刀和一台联想中心的对讲机。\n美国检察官办公室的一份新闻稿称，格拉-马丁内斯此前不久已被解雇格拉-马丁内斯此前不久已被解雇；他曾作为第三方承包商的清洁工在联想工作。\n博伊尔指出，目前尚不清楚格拉-马丁内斯当晚为何在该区域。\n他说：“他最近刚被那里解雇，而你知道，他当时在停车场，他不是要去参加音乐会，也没有在工作，也不在州博览会上，所以这确实很可疑。”\n当时联想中心正在举行NBA Young Boy的音乐会，同时还有数千人参加博览会。\n博伊尔说：“我们需要把他从这群人中带走；话虽如此，他并没有实施类似大规模枪击的行为，但……我们很担心，也怀疑可能存在风险，因此想确保保护公众安全。”\n据联邦检察官称，FBI罗利安全街道特别工作组、韦克县警长办公室、罗利警察局和邓恩警察局对该案进行了调查。\n一名FBI发言人在给WRAL的电子邮件中说：“FBI安全街道暴力犯罪倡议旨在通过建立由FBI支持的、长期主动开展工作的特别工作组，使每个FBI外地办事处能够应对暴力街头帮派和毒品相关暴力，重点打击暴力帮派、暴力犯罪，并抓捕暴力逃犯。”\n格拉-马丁内斯最高可被判处10\n年监禁。他定于5月5日在威尔明顿举行量刑听证会。\n© 2026 Capitol Broadcasting Company版权所有","publish_source":"wral.com","publish_time":"2026-02-25T14:09:53+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1052","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI局长下次出庭：5月11日在格林维尔","title_en":"Former FBI director's next court appearance: May 11 in Greenville :: WRAL.com","summary_cn":"前美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长詹姆斯·科米因被控对总统构成威胁，将于5月11日在北卡罗来纳州格林维尔联邦法院出庭。指控源于他在社交媒体发布贝壳拼出“8647”的照片，检方将其解读为对特朗普总统的威胁。科米此前已在弗吉尼亚州联邦法院自首并短暂出庭，其律师表示将以“报复性和选择性起诉”抗辩。这是司法部第二次对科米提出指控。","summary_en":"Former FBI Director James Comey, charged with making a threat against the president, is scheduled to appear May 11 at the federal courthouse in Greenville, North Carolina. The charge stems from a social media photo of seashells spelling \"8647,\" which prosecutors interpreted as a threat against President Trump. Comey previously surrendered and was briefly arraigned in Virginia, and his attorney said they would challenge the case as a \"vindictive and selective prosecution.\" It is the Justice Department's second case against Comey.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:39:34.571505+00:00","url":"https://www.wral.com/news/state/comey-court-appearance-set-nc-april-2026","content":"Former FBI director's next court appearance: May 11 in Greenville\nThe next court appearance for former FBI Director James Comey, charged with making a threat against the president, will take place in North Carolina.\nPosted\n4/30/2026, 7:05:12 PM\nUpdated\n4/30/2026, 7:12:32 PM\nRelated\nFBI\ncrime\nTrump\nAP Politics\nFILE - Former FBI Director James Comey testifies before the Senate Select Committee on Intelligence, on Capitol Hill in Washington, June 8, 2017. (AP Photo/J. Scott Applewhite, File)\nBy WRAL staff\nThe next court appearance for former FBI Director James Comey, charged with making a threat against the president, will take place in North Carolina.\nComey is scheduled for a May 11 appearance at the federal courthouse in Greenville, N.C., according to reports. Comey owns a property in Emerald Isle, and his charges stem from a photo posted to social media of seashells that spelled out \"8647,\" a message interpreted by prosecutors as a threat against President Trump.\nOther WRAL Top Stories\nWhen used as slang, the number 86 can refer to getting rid of or tossing something out. Trump is currently the 47th president.\nComey surrendered Wednesday to law enforcement at federal court in the Eastern District of Virginia.\nThe New York Times reported that Comey did not speak before the magistrate judge, William E. Fitzpatrick, but nodded along as he was reminded of his rights and the charges against him. The judge addressed mainly administrative matters, including the conditions of Comey’s release, during which he referred to the last time Comey appeared at the federal court in Alexandria, Virginia, over the first indictment the Justice Department brought against him.\n“I don’t think conditions of release are necessary,” Fitzpatrick said. “They weren’t necessary last time. They are not necessary this time.”\nFitzgerald was the only one who spoke for Comey, and told the court that they would be challenging the case by claiming a “vindictive and selective prosecution.”\n“This is not going anywhere. This is clearly not a punishable threat,” Eugene Volokh, a senior fellow at the Hoover Institution at Stanford University who specializes in First Amendment law, told CNN Tuesday.\nThis is the second time that Trump’s Justice Department brought charges against Comey.\nIn September 2025, the Justice Department first brought charges against Comey, accusing him of lying to Congress over leaks to the press.\nThe case was dismissed late last year by a federal judge who found that the interim U.S. Attorney for the Eastern District of Virginia had been improperly appointed, having skirted approval from the Senate.\nMore on this\nFormer FBI Director James Comey has appeared briefly in court, kick-starting a criminal case against him that legal experts say presents significant hurdles for the prosecution and will likely be a challenge for the Justice Department to win. Comey was indicted in North Carolina on Tuesday on cha...\nFormer FBI Director James Comey surrendered to authorities in Virginia and was briefly arraigned on charges of making and transmitting a threat against the president, tied to a social media post reading “86 47.” Comey said he is “still innocent.”\nFormer FBI Director James Comey has been indicted again, this time over a social media photo of seashells arranged on a North Carolina beach that officials say constituted a threat against President Donald Trump.\n© 2026 Copyright Capitol Broadcasting Company","content_cn":"前 FBI 局长下次出庭：5月11日在格林维尔\n被控威胁总统的前 FBI 局长 James Comey，将在北卡罗来纳州下次出庭。\n发布\n2026/4/30，晚上7:05:12\n更新\n2026/4/30，晚上7:12:32\n相关\nFBI\n犯罪\nTrump\nAP 政治\n资料图——前 FBI 局长 James Comey 于2017年6月8日在华盛顿国会山出席参议院情报特别委员会作证。（美联社照片/J. Scott Applewhite，资料图）\n作者：WRAL staff\n被控威胁总统的前 FBI 局长 James Comey，将在北卡罗来纳州下次出庭。\n据报道，Comey 定于5月11日在北卡罗来纳州格林维尔的联邦法院出庭。Comey 在 Emerald Isle 拥有一处房产；其所涉指控源于他在社交媒体上发布的一张照片，照片中的贝壳拼出了“8647”，检方将该信息解读为对 Trump 总统的威胁。\n其他 WRAL 热门报道\n作为俚语使用时，数字86可以指除掉或扔掉某物。Trump 目前是第47任总统。\nComey 周三在弗吉尼亚东区联邦法院向执法部门投案。\n《纽约时报》报道，Comey 在治安法官 William E. Fitzpatrick 面前没有发言，但在被告知其权利及所受指控时点头示意。法官主要处理行政事项，包括 Comey 的释放条件；期间，他提及 Comey 上次在弗吉尼亚州亚历山德里亚联邦法院出庭的情况，当时涉及司法部首次对他提出的起诉。\nFitzpatrick 表示：“我认为没有必要设定释放条件。上次不需要，这次也不需要。”\nFitzgerald 是唯一代表 Comey 发言的人，并向法庭表示，他们将以“报复性和选择性起诉”为由对案件提出质疑。\n“这案子不会有结果。这显然不是可处罚的威胁。”专门研究第一修正案法律的斯坦福大学胡佛研究所高级研究员 Eugene Volokh 周二对 CNN 表示。\n这是 Trump 的司法部第二次对 Comey 提出指控。\n2025年9月，司法部首次对 Comey 提出指控，指控他就向媒体泄密一事向国会作伪证。\n该案于去年年底被一名联邦法官驳回。该法官认定，弗吉尼亚东区代理联邦检察官的任命不当，因为其绕过了参议院批准。\n更多相关内容\n前 FBI 局长 James Comey 曾短暂出庭，由此启动针对他的刑事案件。法律专家称，该案给控方带来重大障碍，司法部可能难以胜诉。Comey 周二在北卡罗来纳州因……被起诉\n前 FBI 局长 James Comey 向弗吉尼亚州当局投案，并因发出和传递针对总统的威胁而被短暂提讯，该指控与一则写有“86 47”的社交媒体帖子有关。Comey 表示自己“仍然无罪”。\n前 FBI 局长 James Comey 再次被起诉，这次是因一张社交媒体照片：北卡罗来纳州海滩上的贝壳被排列成文字，官员称这构成对 Donald Trump 总统的威胁。\n© 2026 Capitol Broadcasting Company 版权所有","publish_source":"wral.com","publish_time":"2026-04-30T19:05:12+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2012","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"12名因在种族正义抗议中单膝跪地被解雇的FBI探员起诉要求复职","title_en":"12 FBI agents fired for kneeling during racial justice protest sue to get their jobs back","summary_cn":"12名前FBI探员因2020年华盛顿种族正义抗议中单膝跪地，于2025年9月被局长卡什·帕特尔解雇，现提起诉讼要求复职。诉状称下跪是为缓和局势的非政治战术行为，此前内部审查和司法部监察长均认定无政治动机。诉讼还寻求宣告解雇违宪、补发薪资及删除相关人事记录。FBI拒绝置评。","summary_en":"Twelve former FBI agents fired in September 2025 after kneeling during a 2020 racial justice protest in Washington sued Monday to get their jobs back, saying the gesture was an apolitical tactic to de-escalate a volatile situation. The lawsuit says prior internal reviews found no political motive. It seeks reinstatement, a ruling that the firings were unconstitutional, backpay and expungement of personnel files. The FBI declined to comment.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:00:49.898642+00:00","url":"https://www.wsaw.com/2025/12/08/12-fbi-agents-fired-kneeling-during-racial-justice-protest-sue-get-their-jobs-back","content":"12 FBI agents fired for kneeling during racial justice protest sue to get their jobs backFILE - Federal Bureau of Investigation officers take a knee with demonstrators as they march on Pennsylvania Ave during a protest over the death of George Floyd on June 4, 2020, in Washington.(Jose Luis Magana | AP Photo/Jose Luis Magana, File)By The Associated Press and ERIC TUCKER Associated PressPublished: Dec. 8, 2025 at 3:36 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON (AP) — Twelve former FBI agents fired after kneeling during a 2020 racial justice protest in Washington sued Monday to get their jobs back, saying their action had been intended to de-escalate a volatile situation and was not meant as a political gesture.The agents say in their lawsuit that they were fired in September by Director Kash Patel because they were perceived as not being politically affiliated with President Donald Trump. But they say their decision to take a knee on June 4, 2020, days after the death of George Floyd at the hands of Minneapolis police, has been misinterpreted as political expression.FILE - Federal Bureau of Investigation officers take a knee with demonstrators as they march on Pennsylvania Ave during a protest over the death of George Floyd on June 4, 2020, in Washington.(Jose Luis Magana | AP Photo/Jose Luis Magana, File)The lawsuit says the agents were assigned to patrol the nation’s capital during a period of civil unrest prompted by Floyd’s death. Lacking protective gear or extensive training in crowd control, the agents became outnumbered by hostile crowds they encountered and decided to kneel to the ground in hopes of defusing the tension, the lawsuit said. The tactic worked, the lawsuit asserts — the crowds dispersed, no shots were fired and the agents “saved American lives” that day.“Plaintiffs were performing their duties as FBI Special Agents, employing reasonable de-escalation to prevent a potentially deadly confrontation with American citizens: a Washington Massacre that could have rivaled the Boston Massacre in 1770,” says the lawsuit, which was filed by attorneys with the Washington Litigation Group.The FBI declined to comment Monday.The lawsuit in federal court in Washington represents the latest court challenge to a personnel purge that has roiled the FBI, targeting both top-ranking supervisors and line agents, as Patel has worked to reshape the nation’s premier law enforcement agency. Besides the kneeling agents, other employees pushed out in recent months have worked on investigations involving Trump or his allies and in one case displayed an LGBTQ+ flag in his workspace.After photographs emerged of the agents taking a knee, the FBI conducted an internal review, with the then-deputy director determining that the agents had no political motive and should not be punished. The Justice Department inspector general reached a similar conclusion and expressed concern that the department had put the agents in a precarious situation that day, the lawsuit says.It was only after Patel took over the bureau in February that the FBI took a different posture.Multiple kneeling agents were removed from supervisory positions last spring and a fresh disciplinary inquiry was launched that resulted in the agents being interviewed about their actions. That internal process was still pending when the agents in September received terse letters telling them they were being terminated because of “unprofessional conduct and a lack of impartiality in carrying out duties, leading to the political weaponization of government.”“Defendants dismissed Plaintiffs in a partisan effort to retaliate against FBI employees that they perceived to be sympathetic to President Trump’s political opponents,” the lawsuit states. “And Defendants acted summarily to avoid creating any further administrative record that would reveal their actions as vindictive and unjustified.”The plaintiffs are among roughly 22 agents from different squads across Washington who were deployed to downtown D.C. on June 4, 2020 to demonstrate a visible law enforcement process during a time of protests in the nation’s capital and across the country.The lawsuit asserts that the agents were thrust into a chaotic scene, saying that a crowd recognized them as being from the FBI and “intentionally” pushed toward them, becoming “increasingly agitated” and shouting and gesturing toward them. Some in the crowd began chanting “take a knee,” a gesture that at that point was widely recognized as a sign of solidarity with Floyd, who was pinned to the pavement by police with a knee on his neck, and the protest movement more generally.The agents closest to the crowd were the first to kneel. After the crowd’s attention turned to the other agents who remained standing, the other FBI employees followed suit, taking a knee in recognition that it was the “most tactically sound means to prevent violence and to maintain order.” The crowd moved on.“Plaintiffs demonstrated tactical intelligence in choosing between deadly force — the only force available to them as a practical matter, given their lack of adequate crowd control equipment — and a less-than-lethal response that would save lives and keep order,” the lawsuit says. “The Special Agents selected the option that prevented casualties while maintaining their law enforcement mission. Each Plaintiff kneeled for apolitical tactical reasons to defuse a volatile situation, not as an expressive political act.”In addition to seeking reinstatement, the lawsuit also asks for a court judgment declaring the firings unconstitutional, backpay and other monetary damages and an expungement of personnel files related to the terminations.Copyright 2025 The Associated Press. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"12名因在种族正义抗议期间下跪而被解雇的联邦调查局特工起诉，要求恢复工作\n\n资料照片——2020年6月4日，在华盛顿举行的抗议乔治·弗洛伊德之死的活动中，联邦调查局官员与示威者一起在宾夕法尼亚大道上行进时下跪。（Jose Luis Magana | 美联社照片/Jose Luis Magana，资料照片）\n\n美联社及美联社记者 ERIC TUCKER\n美联社\n发布时间：2025年12月8日下午3:36（中部标准时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n华盛顿（美联社）——12名前联邦调查局特工周一提起诉讼，要求恢复工作。他们此前因在2020年华盛顿举行的一场种族正义抗议活动中下跪而被解雇，并称他们的行为旨在缓和紧张局势，而非政治姿态。\n\n这些特工在诉讼中称，联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔于9月解雇了他们，因为他们被认为在政治上不与总统唐纳德·特朗普站在一边。但他们表示，自己于2020年6月4日下跪的决定——当时乔治·弗洛伊德在明尼阿波利斯警方手中死亡仅数日——被误解为政治表达。\n\n资料照片——2020年6月4日，在华盛顿举行的抗议乔治·弗洛伊德之死的活动中，联邦调查局官员与示威者一起在宾夕法尼亚大道上行进时下跪。（Jose Luis Magana | 美联社照片/Jose Luis Magana，资料照片）\n\n诉讼称，在弗洛伊德之死引发的社会动荡期间，这些特工被派往首都执行巡逻任务。诉讼称，由于缺乏防护装备和大规模人群控制方面的培训，这些特工在遭遇敌对人群时人数处于劣势，于是决定跪下，希望缓和紧张局势。诉讼主张，这一策略奏效了——人群散去，没有开枪，这些特工当天“挽救了美国人的生命”。\n\n诉讼由华盛顿诉讼集团的律师提起，其中写道：“原告作为联邦调查局特工履行职责，采取合理的降级措施，以防止与美国公民发生可能致命的对抗：一场本可能堪比1770年波士顿大屠杀的华盛顿大屠杀。”\n\n联邦调查局周一拒绝置评。\n\n这起在华盛顿联邦法院提起的诉讼，是针对一场令联邦调查局陷入动荡的人事清洗行动的最新司法挑战。帕特尔一直在努力重塑这个国家首要的执法机构，清洗对象包括高层主管和一线特工。除这些下跪特工外，近几个月被清退的其他雇员曾参与涉及特朗普或其盟友的调查，其中一人在办公空间展示了LGBTQ+旗帜。\n\n这些特工下跪的照片出现后，联邦调查局展开内部审查。当时的副局长认定，这些特工没有政治动机，不应受到惩罚。诉讼称，司法部监察长也得出了类似结论，并表示担忧，认为司法部当天将这些特工置于岌岌可危的境地。\n\n直到帕特尔于2月接管该局后，联邦调查局才采取了不同的立场。\n\n去年春季，多名下跪特工被免去主管职务，并启动了新的纪律调查，导致这些特工就其行为接受问询。9月，这一内部程序仍在进行时，这些特工收到措辞简短的信件，告知他们将因“缺乏专业行为以及缺乏\n在履行职责时保持公正，从而导致政府被政治武器化。”“诉讼称，被告以党派动机解雇了原告，意图报复那些他们认为同情特朗普总统政治对手的联邦调查局雇员。”“被告还草率行事，以避免制造任何可能进一步揭露其行为具有报复性且毫无正当理由的行政记录。”\n\n原告是来自华盛顿各地不同小组的大约22名特工中的一部分。他们于2020年6月4日被部署到华盛顿特区市中心，在美国首都及全国各地发生抗议期间，展示一种可见的执法过程。\n\n诉讼称，这些特工被推入混乱的现场，人群认出他们来自联邦调查局，并“故意”向他们逼近，变得“越来越激动”，对他们大喊并做出手势。人群中一些人开始高喊“单膝下跪”，当时这一姿势已被广泛视为与弗洛伊德以及更广泛抗议运动团结一致的象征；弗洛伊德曾被警察用膝盖压住脖子，按在地面上。\n\n最靠近人群的特工首先跪下。在人群的注意力转向其他仍站立的特工后，其他联邦调查局雇员也纷纷效仿，单膝跪地，因为他们认识到这是“防止暴力和维持秩序的最具战术合理性的手段”。人群继续向前移动。\n\n诉讼称：“原告在致命武力——鉴于他们缺乏足够的控制人群装备，实际上这是他们唯一可用的武力——与一种能挽救生命并维持秩序的非致命性应对方式之间作出选择时，展现了战术智慧。”“特别探员选择了在维持执法任务的同时避免人员伤亡的方案。每名原告单膝跪下都是出于与政治无关的战术原因，旨在缓和紧张局势，而不是一种表达政治立场的行为。”\n\n除要求复职外，诉讼还请求法院作出判决，宣布这些解雇违宪，并要求补发工资及其他金钱损害赔偿，同时清除与终止雇佣有关的人事档案。\n\n版权所有 2025 美联社。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsaw.com","publish_time":"2025-12-08T21:36:37.102000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1257","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI在蒙哥马利行动中逮捕63人","title_en":"63 arrested during FBI operation in Montgomery","summary_cn":"FBI联合州及地方执法部门在蒙哥马利开展为期两周的“南方之星行动”，共逮捕63人，缴获40批毒品、52支枪，执行7份搜查令，查获逾1万美元现金。FBI负责人表示不会放松打击暴力犯罪，该行动属于FBI的VIPER专项行动，旨在针对暴力犯罪明显的城市。阿拉巴马州总检察长对联邦、州与地方的合作表示赞赏。","summary_en":"A two-week FBI operation with state and local law enforcement in Montgomery, dubbed \"Operation Southern Star,\" led to 63 arrests, 40 drug seizures, 52 guns recovered, seven search warrants executed, and over $10,000 in cash seized. The FBI special agent in charge said the bureau is not letting up on violent crime. The operation falls under the FBI's VIPER surge initiative targeting cities with evident violent crime. Alabama's attorney general praised the federal, state and local collaboration.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:35:17.828713+00:00","url":"https://www.wsfa.com/2026/03/31/63-arrested-during-fbi-operation-montgomery","content":"63 arrested during FBI operation in MontgomeryA two-week operation led to more than 60 arrests in Montgomery after the FBI teamed up with state and local law enforcement for “Operation Southern Star.”By WSFA 12 News Staff and Ian AlvanoPublished: Mar. 30, 2026 at 1:46 PM CDT|Updated: Mar. 31, 2026 at 8:45 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleMONTGOMERY, Ala. (WSFA) - A two-week operation led to more than 60 arrests in Montgomery after the FBI teamed up with state and local law enforcement for “Operation Southern Star.” The group made 63 arrests, 40 drug seizures, recovered 52 guns, executed seven search warrants, and seized over $10,000 in cash.The FBI said it is not taking its foot off the gas when it comes to stopping violent crime in Montgomery.“None of our personnel are ceding the area. We have a presence here that we maintain and we have now formed the model of how we want to work together to greatly impact the community,” said Special Agent in Charge with the FBI, Sara J. Jones. “So, this is almost a kickstart to how we envision doing that. So, this will be again, as we said, not the conclusion, but really a demonstrated beginning of how we are now working side by side, effortlessly and tirelessly to make sure we are bringing safer communities to the area.”Alabama Attorney General Steve Marshall mentioned his pleasure with the involvement in “Operation Southern Star.”“Today is an example of when we are at our best in law enforcement,” Marshall said. “When you have collaboration and cooperation across federal, state and local officials, when you do not see jurisdictional boundaries limiting your participation, and when everybody is united behind a singular mission, and that is to be able to make this a safer city and this a safer community.” The operation falls under the FBI’s VIPER (Violence Intervention, Proactive Enforcement, and Response) surge initiative which is intended to target cities where evidence of violent crime is apparent and where the city has requested assistance. Special Agent Jones said that now steps fall to the community by calling in tips and keeping law enforcement informed if violent crime is seen. Not reading this story on the WSFA News App? Get news alerts FASTER and FREE in the Apple App Store and the Google Play Store! Copyright 2026 WSFA. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI在蒙哥马利行动中逮捕63人\nFBI与州和地方执法部门联手开展“南方之星行动”，为期两周的行动在蒙哥马利逮捕了60多人。\n作者：WSFA 12 News工作人员和Ian Alvano\n发布于：2026年3月30日中部时间下午1:46｜更新于：2026年3月31日中部时间上午8:45\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n阿拉巴马州蒙哥马利（WSFA）——FBI与州和地方执法部门联手开展“南方之星行动”，为期两周的行动在蒙哥马利逮捕了60多人。该团体逮捕63人，查获40批毒品，缴获52支枪，执行7份搜查令，并查扣超过10,000美元现金。\nFBI表示，在制止蒙哥马利暴力犯罪方面不会放松力度。\n“我们的任何人员都没有放弃这一地区。我们在这里保持着存在，并且现在已经形成了我们希望共同工作的模式，以极大地影响社区，”FBI负责特别探员Sara J. Jones说。“所以，这几乎是我们设想如何开展工作的一个启动点。正如我们所说，这再次不是终点，而是真正展示了我们现在如何并肩、毫不费力且不知疲倦地工作，以确保为该地区带来更安全的社区。”\n阿拉巴马州总检察长Steve Marshall提到，他很高兴参与“南方之星行动”。\n“今天是我们执法部门处于最佳状态的一个例子，”Marshall说。“当联邦、州和地方官员之间进行协作与合作，当你看不到管辖边界限制参与，当每个人都团结在一个单一使命之后时，那就是让这座城市和这个社区变得更加安全。”\n该行动属于FBI的VIPER（暴力干预、主动执法与响应）增援行动计划，旨在针对暴力犯罪证据明显且城市已请求援助的城市。特别探员Jones表示，下一步取决于社区：如果看到暴力犯罪，应提供线索并让执法部门了解情况。\n没有在WSFA新闻应用上阅读这篇报道？在Apple App Store和Google Play Store中获取新闻提醒，速度更快且免费！\n版权归2026年WSFA所有。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsfa.com","publish_time":"2026-03-30T18:46:55.838000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3555","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"田纳西州人类服务部称日托中心在业主恢复执照后可继续营业","title_en":"DHS says daycare can stay open after owner reinstates license","summary_cn":"田纳西州Chapel Hill的Franklin Springs Academy因未提交2023年度报告于8月10日被行政解散，WSMV 4告知田纳西州人类服务部（TDHS）后，该部门发出安全计划要求其在8月23日前恢复执照，否则立即关闭。TDHS确认该中心已满足要求可继续运营，但该中心将于9月底因无法续租而关闭。此前业主丈夫因强奸等指控被捕，另有教师曾因虐待学生被定罪。","summary_en":"Franklin Springs Academy in Chapel Hill, Tennessee, was administratively dissolved on August 10 after failing to file its 2023 annual report. After WSMV 4 notified the Tennessee Department of Human Services (TDHS), the department issued a safety plan requiring the center to reinstate its license by August 23 or close immediately. TDHS confirmed the center met requirements and can continue operating, though it will close at the end of September due to an inability to renew its building lease. The owner's husband was previously arrested on rape and incest charges, and a teacher had been convicted of abuse and neglect.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:34:39.588315+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2024/08/27/dhs-says-daycare-can-stay-open-after-owner-reinstates-license","content":"DHS says daycare can stay open after owner reinstates licenseThe daycare has been in the news multiple times, most recently because the owner’s husband was arrested on charges of rape. Franklin Springs Academy in Chapel Hill(WSMV)By Danica SauterPublished: Aug. 27, 2024 at 6:51 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleCHAPEL HILL, Tenn. (WSMV) - A Middle Tennessee daycare can stay open after WSMV 4 discovered it failed to file a 2023 annual report with the Tennessee Secretary of State office and was administratively dissolved on August 10th.One day after WSMV 4 notified the Tennessee Department of Human Services about the dissolution, DHS issued a safety plan for Franklin Springs Academy, requiring the center reinstate its license by August 23 or close immediately.DHS confirms the child care center met the requirements and can continue to operate.However, WSMV 4 has also uncovered that Franklin Springs Academy, owned by Rebekah Proctor, will close at the end of September.In a letter apparently sent to parents, the closure was blamed on an inability to renew the building lease.Franklin Springs Academy in Chapel Hill made headlines earlier in the month when Proctor’s husband, Corey Proctor, was arrested on two charges of rape and one charge of incest.PREVIOUS COVERAGE‘Kids are not in danger’ daycare owner says after husband arrested on rape chargeOwner says daycare closing due to expiring lease after husband’s arrest on rape chargesAuthorities in Bedford County said one rape occurred as he drove the victim from school back in May — the victim was reportedly underage. He’s also charged with aggravated sexual battery from 2018.Bedford County deputies say one of the rapes, incest, and sexual battery all happened at the home where Proctor lives with his wife Rebekah.Corey is being held on a $500,000 bond. Rebekah says when and if he’s released, he will not be allowed on the property of the Chapel Hill or Franklin locations of Franklin Springs Academy.In February, a WSMV 4 Investigation revealed that a worker at Franklin Springs Academy in Chapel Hill had been convicted of abuse and neglect of two separate students.“It’s sickening to know the teacher that has been her teacher for four years did this to her. This is a teacher I saw every morning, every afternoon smiled at me and to know she was mistreating my daughter was disheartening,” said Jessica Allison.However, the biggest blow came when the Allisons found out about another situation with that same teacher. An incident report from the school says it happened in 2021. That was 15 months before Luna was fired.“She had pulled my daughter off a table by the back of her hair,” said Jessica Allison. Her husband added, “We should have known about that right away.”The state should have known about it right away too. A Tennessee Department of Human Services inspection report shows personnel files were inspected at Franklin Springs Academy the month after this happened. Yet, when you visit the TDHS website that’s supposed to document these situations, there’s no mention of the first encounter from 2021.TDHS wouldn’t answer WSMV4′s questions about whether the department investigated the 2021 incident. When asked if Franklin Springs Academy contacted TDHS to report a child was pulled by their ponytail in November of 2021, a DHS spokesperson said no. When asked if the daycare was required to report such incidents, TDHS responded, “Yes.”Copyright 2024 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"国土安全部称，日托中心老板恢复执照后可以继续营业\n这家日托中心曾多次登上新闻，最近一次是因为其老板的丈夫因强奸指控被捕。田纳西州教堂山的富兰克林斯普林斯学院\n（WSMV）\n作者：Danica Sauter\n发布于：2024年8月27日上午6:51（CDT）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州教堂山（WSMV）——WSMV 4发现，中田纳西州一家日托中心未向田纳西州州务卿办公室提交2023年度报告，并于8月10日被行政解散，但如今可以继续营业。\n在WSMV 4通知田纳西州人类服务部该机构被解散的第二天，国土安全部为富兰克林斯普林斯学院发布了一项安全计划，要求该中心在8月23日前恢复执照，否则立即关闭。\n国土安全部确认，该托儿中心符合要求，可以继续运营。\n然而，WSMV 4还发现，由Rebekah Proctor拥有的富兰克林斯普林斯学院将在9月底关闭。\n一封显然发给家长的信称，关闭原因是无法续租大楼。\n本月早些时候，位于教堂山的富兰克林斯普林斯学院登上新闻头条，因为Proctor的丈夫Corey Proctor被控两项强奸罪和一项乱伦罪而被捕。\n此前报道\n“孩子没有危险”，日托中心老板在丈夫因强奸指控被捕后表示\n老板称，丈夫因强奸指控被捕后，日托中心将因租约到期而关闭\n贝德福德县当局称，其中一起强奸发生在他今年5月开车送受害者从学校回家途中——据报道，受害者未成年。他还被控2018年的加重性侵罪。\n贝德福德县警员称，其中一起强奸、乱伦和性侵均发生在Proctor与妻子Rebekah共同居住的家中。\nCorey目前被拘押，保释金为50万美元。Rebekah表示，无论他何时以及是否获释，他都不被允许进入富兰克林斯普林斯学院位于教堂山或富兰克林的校舍。\n2月，WSMV 4的一项调查披露，教堂山富兰克林斯普林斯学院的一名工作人员曾因虐待和忽视两名不同学生而被定罪。\n“想到教了她四年的老师竟对她做出这种事，令人作呕。这个老师我每天早上、每天下午都能看到，她还对我微笑；得知她虐待我的女儿，我非常心痛。”Jessica Allison说。\n然而，当Allison一家发现同一名教师的另一桩情况时，打击更大。学校的事件报告称，这起事件发生在2021年，也就是Luna被解雇前15个月。\n“她抓住我女儿后脑勺的头发，把她从桌子上拽了下来。”Jessica Allison说。她的丈夫补充道：“我们本应该马上知道这件事。”\n州政府也本应马上知道。田纳西州人类服务部的一份检查报告显示，事件发生后的次月，检查人员查看了富兰克林斯普林斯学院的人员档案。然而，当你访问田纳西州人类服务部网站——该网站本应记录这些情况——却没有提到2021年的第一次事件。\n田纳西州人类服务部拒绝回答WSMV4关于该部门是否调查2021年事件的问题。当被问及富兰克林斯普林斯学院是否联系田纳西州人类服务部，报告2021年11月一名儿童被拽马尾时，国土安全部发言人回答“没有”。当被问及日托中心是否必须报告此类事件时，田纳西州人类服务部回答：“是。”\n版权归2024 WSMV所有。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2024-08-27T11:51:04.346000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3221","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI称田纳西州青少年被控策划袭击纳什维尔清真寺","title_en":"TN teen charged with planning to attack Nashville mosque, FBI says","summary_cn":"据WSMV报道，田纳西州斯图尔特县18岁的冈纳·约瑟夫·费舍尔于2024年12月被捕，此前Meta向纳什维尔美国联邦调查局（FBI）举报其网络帖子。FBI调查发现，费舍尔自2024年6月起发布购买武器弹药及策划大规模伤亡袭击的帖子和信息，后于12月4日将袭击地点改为纳什维尔一座清真寺。他于12月18日被捕，被控威胁实施大规模暴力，目前仍被联邦拘留。","summary_en":"Gunner Joseph Fisher, 18, of Stewart County, Tennessee, was arrested in December 2024 after Meta alerted the FBI in Nashville to his online posts, WSMV reported. The FBI investigation found posts and messages dating to June 2024 about buying weapons and planning mass-casualty attacks, later shifting the target to a Nashville mosque on Dec. 4. He was arrested Dec. 18 on charges of threatening to commit mass violence and remains in federal custody.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:30:25.645905+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/01/27/tn-teen-charged-with-planning-attack-nashville-mosque-fbi-says","content":"TN teen charged with planning to attack Nashville mosque, FBI saysThe FBI investigation revealed the 18-year-old posted about plans to cause mass casualties at various locations before deciding on the mosque.Federal Bureau of Investigation.(FBI)By Tony GarciaPublished: Jan. 27, 2025 at 10:54 AM CST|Updated: Jan. 27, 2025 at 11:40 AM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleBIG ROCK, Tenn. (WSMV) - A teenager from Stewart County was arrested in December 2024 following an investigation into his online messages about plans to orchestrate multiple mass casualty events in Tennessee.On Dec. 14, 2024, Meta alerted the Federal Bureau of Investigation in Nashville about some alarming posts from 18-year-old Gunner Joseph Fisher. Fisher was discussing carrying out a mass shooting with another user through his Instagram and Facebook accounts, according to the criminal complaint document.The FBI investigation uncovered multiple concerning posts dating back to June 2024, including the purchasing of weapons, ammunition, a machete, and a tactical vest. The complaint included pictures of Fisher brandishing such items.The investigation discovered several posts and messages where Fisher claimed to be planning an attack:June 8, 2024 - Fisher messaged another user about attacking a furry conventionJune 12 - Fisher bragged about his manifesto, and compared himself to other mass shootersJune 16 - Fisher sent a message claiming he was “gonna go on a spree this year”June 19 - Fisher posted a photograph of himself wearing a camouflage tactical vest and holding a rifleFBI agents went to Fisher’s residence in Big Rock, Tennessee, on Dec. 14 to speak with the teenager. He admitted his fascination with school shootings and mass shootings to the agents, according to the complaint. He even admitted he had a “favorite mass shooter of all time,” during the interview.Fisher’s father gave the agents permission to search the boy’s room and seize his electronics. More plans with another person online were discovered, including a video rant on Nov. 1 showing Fisher railing against Jewish people and Muslims, the complaint detailed. The other person involved in the chats was traced to another state.A text from Fisher to the other individual on Dec. 4 described moving up his plans for a mass attack, and changing the location to a mosque, according to the document. The message included a screenshot of a Google Maps location, which was to a mosque in Nashville, Tennessee.The 17-year-old Antioch High School shooter, Solomon Henderson, wrote about Fisher in his online diary — saying that he was from his area after learning of his arrest connected to his mass attack plans.On Jan. 15, 2025, The American Muslim Advisory Council (AMAC) praised the U.S. Attorney’s Office in Middle Tennessee for thwarting the threat of potential mass violence against a local mosque.In the release, AMAC said the suspect had been apprehended and was in custody.“We are relieved to confirm that the suspect has been arrested and remains in custody as investigations continue,” AMAC’s director wrote. “This alarming incident highlights the critical importance of early intervention in preventing acts of violence and ensuring the safety of all.”Fisher was arrested on December 18 and remains in federal custody on threatening to commit an act of mass violence charges.His arraignment was scheduled for Monday, January 27, but his defense attorneys needed more time to prepare. The arrangement was moved to Tuesday, January 28.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"田纳西州青少年被控策划袭击纳什维尔清真寺，联邦调查局称\n联邦调查局的调查显示，这名18岁少年曾发布关于在不同地点造成大规模伤亡的计划，之后决定袭击清真寺。\n联邦调查局（FBI）\n作者：Tony Garcia\n发布：2025年1月27日上午10:54（CST）|更新：2025年1月27日上午11:40（CST）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州Big Rock（WSMV）——斯图尔特县一名青少年于2024年12月被捕，此前当局调查了他在网上发布的、有关策划田纳西州多起大规模伤亡事件的消息。\n2024年12月14日，Meta向纳什维尔的联邦调查局通报了18岁的Gunner Joseph Fisher发布的一些令人担忧的帖子。据刑事诉状文件称，Fisher通过自己的Instagram和Facebook账号与另一名用户讨论实施大规模枪击事件。\n联邦调查局的调查发现了多条可追溯至2024年6月的令人担忧的帖子，其中包括购买武器、弹药、砍刀和战术背心。诉状中还包括Fisher手持这些物品的照片。\n调查发现了多条帖子和消息，Fisher在其中声称正在计划发动袭击：\n2024年6月8日——Fisher给另一名用户发消息，谈论袭击一场兽迷大会\n6月12日——Fisher吹嘘自己的宣言，并将自己与其他大规模枪手相提并论\n6月16日——Fisher发送消息称他“今年要开始一场大开杀戒”\n6月19日——Fisher发布了一张自己穿着迷彩战术背心、手持步枪的照片\n12月14日，联邦调查局特工前往Fisher位于田纳西州Big Rock的住所，与这名青少年交谈。据诉状称，他向特工承认自己着迷于校园枪击和大规模枪击事件。他甚至在谈话中承认自己“有史以来最喜欢的大规模枪手”。\nFisher的父亲允许特工搜查男孩的房间并扣押其电子设备。诉状详细说明，调查人员还发现了他与网上另一人的更多计划，包括一段11月1日的视频 rant，视频中Fisher抨击犹太人和穆斯林。聊天中涉及的另一人后来被追查到另一个州。\n据文件称，Fisher于12月4日发给另一人的一条短信描述了提前实施大规模袭击计划，并将地点改为一座清真寺。消息中包含一张Google地图位置截图，指向田纳西州纳什维尔的一座清真寺。\n17岁的Antioch高中枪手Solomon Henderson在网上日记中写到了Fisher——他在得知Fisher因与大规模袭击计划有关而被捕后，称Fisher来自他所在的地区。\n2025年1月15日，美国穆斯林咨询委员会（AMAC）赞扬田纳西州中部地区美国检察官办公室挫败了针对当地清真寺的潜在大规模暴力威胁。\nAMAC在声明中表示，嫌疑人已被逮捕并处于拘押之中。\nAMAC主任写道：“我们很欣慰地确认，嫌疑人已经被捕并仍被拘押，调查仍在继续。这起令人震惊的事件凸显了及早干预对于预防暴力行为、确保所有人安全的重要性。”\nFisher于12月18日被捕，目前因被控威胁实施大规模暴力行为而被联邦拘押。\n他的提审原定于1月27日星期一进行，但辩护律师需要更多时间准备。提审改期至1月28日星期二。\n版权所有2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-01-27T16:54:33.089000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3096","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"逃犯在南纳什维尔住宅车库被FBI特警队发现死亡","title_en":"Fugitive found dead in garage by FBI SWAT team at South Nashville home","summary_cn":"田纳西州纳什维尔警方通报，30岁逃犯迈尔斯·欧文斯在FBI特警队进入南纳什维尔一处住宅后，被发现死于车库内一辆被盗轿车中，头部中枪，疑似自杀。欧文斯因联邦枪支和毒品指控被通缉，另有20项未出庭指控。警方在搜查中缴获70磅大麻、近5万美元现金、珠宝和两支枪械，并逮捕一名涉案同伙。","summary_en":"Metro Nashville Police reported that 30-year-old fugitive Myles Owens V was found dead from an apparent suicide inside a stolen sedan in the garage of a South Nashville home after an FBI SWAT team entered. Owens was wanted on federal firearms and drug charges and had 20 outstanding failure-to-appear warrants. The search yielded 70 pounds of marijuana, nearly $50,000 cash, jewelry and two firearms, and an associate was arrested.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:21:10.818112+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/03/05/fugitive-found-dead-garage-by-fbi-swat-team-south-nashville-home","content":"Fugitive found dead in garage by FBI SWAT team at South Nashville homeDetectives searched the home on Ben Hill Drive and found 70 pounds of marijuana, nearly $50,000 cash, jewelry, and two firearms.Fugitive found dead in stolen car by FBI SWAT team at South Nashville home(MNPD)By Caleb WethingtonPublished: Mar. 4, 2025 at 5:44 PM CST|Updated: Mar. 5, 2025 at 3:24 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - The Metro Nashville Police Department has released new information on Tuesday morning’s standoff at a home in South Nashville that ended in the death of a fugitive.MNPD reports that 30-year-old Myles Owens V was found dead by an apparent suicide at the home on Benn Hill Drive.An FBI SWAT team entered the home after making announcements for Owens to surrender and confirming he was inside. He was then found inside a stolen sedan in the garage with a gunshot wound to the head. MNPD said a gun was found on his right side.Owens was taken to Vanderbilt University Medical Center where he died.Previous Coverage: Gunfire sparks standoff in AntiochPolice said Owens was wanted on an outstanding federal criminal complaint charging him with possession of an unregistered firearm, possession of a firearm in furtherance of a drug trafficking crime, and possession of a controlled substance with intent to distribute. He also had 20 outstanding failure-to-appear-in-court charges in Davidson County and two in Williamson County.“MNPD Violent Crimes Division detectives had been working to locate Owens for the last few months after a search warrant was executed on October 25, 2024, at Extra Space Storage on Charlotte Pike, where Owens was known to frequent. Recovered during the search were 119 pounds of marijuana, three rifles, one handgun, six Glock switches (which unlawfully make firearms fully automatic), $81,000 in cash, cocaine, pills, and methamphetamine,” MNPD said.The search of the home on Ben Hill Drive on Tuesday resulted in the discovery of 70 pounds of marijuana, nearly $50,000 cash, jewelry and two firearms. As the search was taking place, MNPD said a known associate of Owens, 31-year-old Kenneth Strickland Jr. walked up to the scene.Police said Strickland had an outstanding warrant for identity theft and was taken into custody. As he was being arrested, officers found an aftermarket key fob on his person. Police said they used the fob to find a nearby stolen Infiniti Q60 which he arrived in.Police said inside the stolen car, detectives found two fake driver’s licenses, both with Strickland’s face on it, but using different names. One ID was from Texas and the other was from New Jersey.“Strickland was charged with motor vehicle theft, driving on a suspended license, and two additional counts of identity theft. He is currently being held on a $40,500 bond,” MNPD said.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"逃犯被联邦调查局特警队发现死于南纳什维尔住宅的车库内\n侦探搜查了本·希尔大道的住宅，发现70磅大麻、近5万美元现金、珠宝和两支枪支。逃犯被联邦调查局特警队发现死于南纳什维尔住宅的一辆被盗汽车内\n（MNPD）\n作者：Caleb Wethington\n发布：2025年3月4日下午5:44（中部标准时间）|更新：2025年3月5日下午3:24（中部标准时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——大都会纳什维尔警察局周二上午公布了有关南纳什维尔一处住宅对峙事件的新信息，该事件以一名逃犯死亡告终。\nMNPD报告称，30岁的Myles Owens V在本·希尔大道住宅内被发现，显然是自杀身亡。\n联邦调查局特警队在宣布要求Owens投降并确认他在屋内后进入住宅。随后，他在车库内一辆被盗轿车中被发现，头部中枪。MNPD表示，一把枪在他的右侧被发现。\nOwens被送往范德比尔特大学医疗中心，后在那里死亡。\n此前报道：枪声在安条克引发对峙\n警方称，Owens因一项未执行的联邦刑事控告被通缉，该控告指控他持有未注册枪支、为实施贩毒犯罪而持有枪支，以及持有意图分销的受管制物质。他还在戴维森县有20项未出庭指控，在威廉姆森县有两项。\n“MNPD暴力犯罪部门的侦探在2024年10月25日对夏洛特派克的Extra Space Storage执行搜查令后，过去几个月一直在设法找到Owens。已知Owens经常去那里。搜查中发现119磅大麻、三支步枪、一支手枪、六个Glock转换开关（可非法将枪支改为全自动）、8.1万美元现金、可卡因、药片和甲基苯丙胺，”MNPD表示。\n周二对本·希尔大道住宅的搜查发现了70磅大麻、近5万美元现金、珠宝和两支枪支。MNPD称，搜查进行期间，Owens的一名已知同伙、31岁的Kenneth Strickland Jr.走到现场。\n警方称，Strickland因身份盗窃被发出逮捕令，并被拘留。在逮捕他时，警员在其身上发现了一个改装后的钥匙扣。警方称，他们利用该钥匙扣找到了一辆附近被盗的英菲尼迪Q60，他就是乘坐这辆车到达的。\n警方称，在这辆被盗汽车内，侦探发现了两张假驾照，上面都是Strickland的脸，但使用了不同姓名。一张证件来自得克萨斯州，另一张来自新泽西州。\n“Strickland被控盗窃机动车、无证驾驶，以及另外两项身份盗窃罪。目前他以40,500美元保释金被羁押，”MNPD表示。\n版权所有2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-03-04T23:44:14.615000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2908","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI技术人员因与少女交换露骨图像被判刑","title_en":"Former FBI tech sentenced after being found guilty of exchanging ‘sexually explicit images’ with teen girls","summary_cn":"前美国联邦调查局电子技术员贾斯汀·卡罗尔因与三名14岁女孩进行露骨聊天并交换色情图像，被判处20年联邦监禁。案件因一名受害者向FBI办公室寄送情人节包裹而曝光。FBI纳什维尔办事处负责人和代理联邦检察官表示，执法人员犯罪将受到严惩，以恢复公众信任。卡罗尔获释后还将接受10年监督释放。","summary_en":"Former FBI electronics technician Justin Carroll was sentenced to 20 years in federal prison after being found guilty of engaging in sexually explicit chats and exchanging explicit images with three 14-year-old girls. The case came to light after a victim mailed a Valentine's Day package to the FBI office. The FBI Nashville field office and acting U.S. attorney said those in law enforcement who commit crimes will face serious penalties. Carroll will also serve 10 years of supervised release.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:32:26.151971+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/05/05/former-fbi-tech-sentenced-after-being-found-guilty-exchanging-sexually-explicit-images-with-teen-girls","content":"Former FBI tech sentenced after being found guilty of exchanging ‘sexually explicit images’ with teen girlsHe was convicted of engaging in sexually explicit chats and exchanging sexually explicit images with three 14-year-old girls.Cannot find custom embedBy Caleb WethingtonPublished: May 5, 2025 at 12:08 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - A former electronics technician for the Federal Bureau of Investigation has been sentenced more than a year after being found guilty of child sex crimes, according to the U.S. Attorney’s Office in the Middle District of Tennessee.The former FBI tech, Justin Carroll, was sentenced to 20 years in federal prison after being found guilty of engaging in sexually explicit chats and exchanging sexually explicit images with three 14-year-old girls across several social media platforms after connecting with them on chatting websites.“Today’s sentencing underscores that no matter who you are, you will be brought to justice if you are found guilty of such criminal behavior,” said Special Agent in Charge Joseph E. Carrico of the FBI Nashville Field Office. “The FBI will continue to work with our partners to protect children from exploitation and hold accountable those who exploit or endanger them.”The U.S. Attorney’s Office said that Carroll was charged with one count of sexual exploitation of a minor, one count of coercion and enticement of a minor to engage in unlawful sexual activity, two counts of receipt of child pornography, and three counts of transferring obscene material on an individual under the age of sixteen.Previous Coverage: FBI electronics technician found guilty of child sex crimesHere are instructions on how to watch WSMV4 live on various platforms.His actions were brought to light after one of the victims mailed a Valentine’s Day package to the FBI office.The U.S. Attorney’s Offices said there were sexually explicit images of the girls found in Carroll’s social media accounts and on his cell phone. Images of Carroll were also found in one of the girls’ social media accounts and on another girl’s phone.He continued to message the girl who sent the package, even after receiving an email from her mother advising him of her age and why the package was sent.“When someone in law enforcement dishonors their responsibilities by committing criminal acts, we will seek the most serious penalties in order to restore the public’s trust,” said Acting United States Attorney Robert E. McGuire. “Justin Carroll dishonored the men and women of the FBI by his deplorable actions and now, thanks to the prosecution team and our law enforcement partners, he faces the consequences of those actions.”Upon his release from incarceration, Carroll will be on supervised release for 10 years.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"前联邦调查局技术人员被判刑，此前被判定与未成年女孩交换“露骨色情图片”\n他被判定与三名14岁女孩进行露骨色情聊天并交换露骨色情图片。\n找不到自定义嵌入内容\n作者：Caleb Wethington\n发表于：2025年5月5日，中部夏令时间下午12:08\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——据田纳西州中区美国检察官办公室称，一名前联邦调查局电子技术员在被判犯有儿童性犯罪一年多后被判刑。\n这名前联邦调查局技术人员Justin Carroll在被判定有罪后，被判处20年联邦监禁。他曾在聊天网站上与三名14岁女孩建立联系，随后通过多个社交媒体平台与她们进行露骨色情聊天并交换露骨色情图片。\n“今天的判决再次表明，无论你是谁，只要被判定犯有此类犯罪行为，都将受到法律制裁，”联邦调查局纳什维尔外勤办事处特别探员主管Joseph E. Carrico说。“联邦调查局将继续与合作伙伴共同努力，保护儿童免受剥削，并追究那些剥削或危害儿童者的责任。”\n美国检察官办公室表示，Carroll被控一项剥削未成年人的罪名、一项胁迫和诱骗未成年人从事非法性活动的罪名、两项接收儿童色情制品的罪名，以及三项向16岁以下个人转移淫秽物品的罪名。\n此前报道：联邦调查局电子技术员被判犯有儿童性犯罪\n以下是如何在各种平台上观看WSMV4直播的说明。\n他的行为是在其中一名受害者向联邦调查局办公室寄送情人节包裹后曝光的。\n美国检察官办公室称，在Carroll的社交媒体账户和手机中发现了这些女孩的露骨色情图片。Carroll的照片也在其中一名女孩的社交媒体账户以及另一名女孩的手机中被发现。\n即使收到寄送包裹女孩的母亲发来的电子邮件，告知他女儿的年龄以及寄送包裹的原因后，他仍继续给这名女孩发消息。\n“当执法人员通过实施犯罪行为背弃职责时，我们将寻求最严厉的处罚，以恢复公众的信任，”代理美国检察官Robert E. McGuire说。“Justin Carroll以其令人发指的行为玷污了联邦调查局男女工作人员的声誉，如今多亏检方团队和执法合作伙伴的努力，他将为这些行为承担后果。”\nCarroll获释后将在监督释放状态下接受10年监管。\n版权所有2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-05-05T17:08:25.305000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2434","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI再次呼吁提供塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯失踪案线索","title_en":"FBI renews call for tips in Sebastian Rogers’ disappearance","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局再次呼吁公众提供自闭症少年塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯失踪案的线索。罗杰斯于2024年2月26日在田纳西州亨德森维尔母亲家中失踪，至今未寻获。FBI称搜救范围约4.5英里、覆盖约4.4万英亩，约2000名搜救人员参与，并已排除“手电筒理论”和“绿衣人”等传言。FBI悬赏最高5万美元征集线索。","summary_en":"The FBI has renewed its call for tips in the disappearance of Sebastian Rogers, a teen with autism who went missing from his mother's Hendersonville, Tennessee home on Feb. 26, 2024. The FBI said the search covered about a 4.5-mile radius and roughly 44,000 acres with about 2,000 searchers, and addressed two disproven rumors. A reward of up to $50,000 is offered for information.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:47:56.028185+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/09/06/fbi-renews-call-tips-sebastian-rogers-disappearance","content":"FBI renews call for tips in Sebastian Rogers’ disappearanceThe teen with autism went missing from his mother’s Hendersonville home on Feb. 26, 2024, and hasn’t been seen since. Cannot find custom embedBy Kassidy BrownPublished: Sep. 5, 2025 at 8:50 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleHENDERSONVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) is renewing its call for tips regarding the disappearance of Sebastian Rogers.The teen with autism went missing from his mother’s Hendersonville home on Feb. 26, 2024, and hasn’t been seen since. He was last seen on Stafford Court in Hendersonville.Related Coverage:‘My son is out there somewhere’: Sebastian Rogers’ mom, stepdad share struggles, hopes with WSMV4 year after son’s disappearancePrivate investigator says new video could be break in search for Sebastian RogersFact check: No credible leads found from photo circulating on social media as search continues for Sebastian Rogers‘I understand people want answers’: Sheriff’s office continues search for missing Sebastian Rogers, year after disappearanceThe FBI shared an article on Thursday detailing the night before Rogers’ was reported missing. It also shared information about the search for Rogers in the weeks and days following his disappearance. “The search consisted of about a four-and-a-half-mile radius around Sebastian’s home,” said Detective Brandon Carter from the Sumner County Sheriff’s Office. “There were roughly 2,000 searchers equipped with an app tracking their movements. The searchers could also use the app to plot things on a map that they observed while they were out searching. The total area they covered within that four-and-a-half-mile radius was equivalent to a combined 44,000 acres.”Here are instructions on how to watch WSMV4 live on various platforms.The FBI article said the search consisted of around 2,000 searchers equipped with an app tracking their movements. They covered around 44,000 acres in their search.Law enforcement also searched almost every home in Rogers’ neighborhood. They also collected video recordings from nearby homes.The article also touched on two rumors in the case that have been disproven. One being the “flashlight theory,” and the other was the person in the green hoodie.“We have followed through on every tip that has come in,” said Josh Savley, special agent in charge for the Criminal Investigation Division at the Tennessee Bureau of Investigation. “Some of those tips, we continue to examine at a deeper level, but the vast majority we have cleared as either being irrelevant or ended with no results.”The FBI is once again urging people with information on Rogers’ disappearance to come forward, saying the best way to help law enforcement in their search is to promptly share tips with SCSO, the TBI of the FBI.“If you have any information concerning the whereabouts of Sebastian Rogers, please contact the Sumner County Sheriff’s Office at 615-451-3838, or the Tennessee Bureau of Investigation at 1-800-TBI-FIND or TipsToTBI@tbi.tn.gov,“ the FBI said. ”You may also contact your local FBI office, the nearest American embassy or consulate, or you can submit a tip online at tips.fbi.gov.\"Rogers’ would be 16 now. He is 5′5″ tall and around 110 to 115 pounds when he was last seen with brown hair and eyes that look hazel or brown.The FBI is also offering a reward of up to $50,000 for information leading to Rogers’ whereabouts.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI再次呼吁提供有关塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯失踪案的线索\n这名患有自闭症的少年于2024年2月26日从其母亲位于亨德森维尔的家中失踪，此后一直未被发现。无法找到自定义嵌入内容\n作者：Kassidy Brown\n发布时间：2025年9月5日，美国中部夏令时晚上8:50\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州亨德森维尔（WSMV）——联邦调查局（FBI）再次呼吁公众提供有关塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯失踪案的线索。\n这名患有自闭症的少年于2024年2月26日从其母亲位于亨德森维尔的家中失踪，此后一直未被发现。他最后一次被看到是在亨德森维尔的斯塔福德法院街。\n相关报道：\n“我的儿子在外面的某个地方”：塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯的母亲和继父向WSMV4分享困境与希望\n儿子失踪四年后\n私家侦探称，一段新视频可能成为寻找塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯的突破口\n事实核查：随着对塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯的搜寻继续，社交媒体流传照片未带来可信线索\n“我理解人们想要答案”：失踪一年后，治安官办公室继续搜寻失踪的塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯\nFBI周四分享的一篇文章详细介绍了罗杰斯被报告失踪前一晚的情况，也分享了其失踪后数周和数日内对罗杰斯的搜寻信息。萨姆纳县治安官办公室侦探布兰登·卡特说：“搜寻范围以塞巴斯蒂安的家为中心，半径约四英里半。大约有2,000名搜寻人员配备了一款追踪其行动轨迹的应用程序。搜寻人员还可以利用该应用程序在地图上标出他们在搜寻过程中观察到的事物。在这四英里半半径范围内，他们覆盖的总面积相当于合计44,000英亩。”\n以下是在各种平台上观看WSMV4直播的说明。\nFBI文章称，约2,000名配备追踪行动轨迹应用程序的搜寻人员参与了搜寻。他们的搜寻覆盖了约44,000英亩。\n执法人员还搜查了罗杰斯所在社区几乎每一户住宅，并收集了附近住宅的视频记录。\n文章还谈及该案中两个已被证伪的传言：其一是“手电筒理论”，其二是穿绿色连帽衫的人。\n田纳西州调查局刑事调查处主管特工乔什·萨夫利说：“我们跟进了收到的每一条线索。其中一些线索，我们仍在进行更深入的审查，但绝大多数已被排除，要么与案件无关，要么没有结果。”\nFBI再次敦促掌握罗杰斯失踪信息的人挺身而出，称帮助执法部门搜寻的最佳方式是及时向SCSO、TBI或FBI提供线索。\nFBI表示：“如果您掌握任何有关塞巴斯蒂安·罗杰斯下落的信息，请致电萨姆纳县治安官办公室615-451-3838，或田纳西州调查局1-800-TBI-FIND，或发送邮件至TipsToTBI@tbi.tn.gov。您也可以联系当地FBI办公室、最近的美国大使馆或领事馆，或在tips.fbi.gov在线提交线索。”\n罗杰斯如今应为16岁。他最后一次被看到时身高5英尺5英寸，体重约110至115磅，棕色头发，眼睛看起来是淡褐色或棕色。\nFBI还悬赏最高50,000美元，奖励能帮助确定罗杰斯下落的信息。\n版权所有 © 2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-09-06T01:50:50.344000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2291","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"田纳西州参议员称FBI在1月6日调查中分析其通话记录","title_en":"TN senators among group of lawmakers who had phone records analyzed by FBI in Jan. 6 probe","summary_cn":"一群共和党参议员称，2023年美国联邦调查局在调查2021年1月6日国会骚乱事件时分析了多名议员的通话记录，包括田纳西州参议员比尔·哈格蒂和玛莎·布莱克本。参议员称FBI仅查看通话日期和时间，未分析通话内容。司法委员会主席格拉斯利批评此举侵犯宪法权利。美联社称相关文件未说明分析原因或结果。","summary_en":"A group of Republican senators said the FBI analyzed phone records of several lawmakers in 2023 as part of its investigation into the Jan. 6, 2021 Capitol riot, including Tennessee Sens. Bill Hagerty and Marsha Blackburn. The senators said only call dates and times were reviewed, not content. Judiciary Chairman Grassley called it a violation of constitutional rights. The AP reported the documents do not explain why the records were analyzed or any results.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:37:38.422454+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/10/07/tn-senators-among-group-lawmakers-who-had-phone-records-analyzed-by-fbi-jan-6-probe","content":"TN senators among group of lawmakers who had phone records analyzed by FBI in Jan. 6 probeSen. Bill Hagerty and others stated that the records analyzed by the FBI enabled investigators to view the date and time phone calls were made around the time of the Jan. 6 U.S. Capitol riot.Cannot find custom embedBy Caleb WethingtonPublished: Oct. 7, 2025 at 10:35 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON, D.C. (WSMV) - A group of Republican senators announced that in 2023, the Federal Bureau of Investigation analyzed phone records of several lawmakers as part of an investigation into the events of Jan. 6, 2021.During the Monday announcement, Tennessee Sen. Bill Hagerty and others said that the records analyzed by the FBI allowed investigators to see the date and time phone calls were made, but the content of the communications was not analyzed.Sen. Chuck Grassley of Iowa, who is the chairman of the Judiciary Committee, said that this move was a “violation of personal property and people’s rights and the law and their constitutional rights.”Below is a list of the lawmakers whose records were analyzed:Sen. Lindsey Graham of South CarolinaSen. Bill Hagerty of TennesseeSen. Josh Hawley of MissouriSen. Dan Sullivan of AlaskaSen. Tommy Tuberville of AlabamaSen. Ron Johnson of WisconsinSen. Cynthia Lummis of WyomingSen. Marsha Blackburn of TennesseeRep. Mike Kelly of PennsylvaniaHere are instructions on how to watch WSMV4 live on various platforms.Sen. Marsha Blackburn released the following statement:“The FBI under Joe Biden’s watch exercised authority that it did not have,” Blackburn said. “The Biden administration raided Mar-a-Lago, indicted President Trump, and now we know they weaponized America’s top law enforcement agency to spy on Republican U.S. Senators who support President Trump. The FBI was rotten to the core under Joe Biden and Chris Wray’s leadership, and I will not let this stand. I appreciate Director Patel and Deputy Director Bongino for launching an investigation to hold those responsible for this corruption accountable to the highest extent.”On social media, Sen. Hagerty released the following statement:“Jack Smith tracked my private communications and those of my colleagues during his witch hunt to investigate @POTUS,\" he said. “This is exactly the type of political weaponization of the federal government under Presidents Obama and Biden that Republicans and President Trump have been calling out for years. We will get to the bottom of this, but every American should be shocked to see what happened here.”The Associated Press reports that documents related to the probe do not reveal why those lawmakers’ phone records were analyzed or whether anything came from the analysis.The Associated Press contributed to this article.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"田纳西州参议员位列联邦调查局在1月6日调查中分析电话记录的议员之中\n哈格蒂参议员等人表示，联邦调查局分析的记录让调查人员能够查看1月6日美国国会大厦骚乱前后拨打电话的日期和时间。\n无法找到自定义嵌入\n凯勒布·韦瑟灵顿\n发表于：2025年10月7日中部夏令时间上午10:35\n分享\n在谷歌上添加我们\n在谷歌上添加为首选来源\n\n华盛顿特区（WSMV）——一群共和党参议员宣布，2023年，联邦调查局在调查2021年1月6日事件时分析了几名议员的电话记录。\n\n在周一的公告中，田纳西州参议员比尔·哈格蒂和其他人表示，联邦调查局分析的记录使调查人员能够看到电话拨打的日期和时间，但没有分析通信内容。\n\n担任司法委员会主席的爱荷华州参议员查克·格拉斯利说，此举是“侵犯个人财产、人民权利、法律以及他们宪法权利的行为”。\n\n以下是电话记录被分析的议员名单：\n南卡罗来纳州参议员林赛·格雷厄姆\n田纳西州参议员比尔·哈格蒂\n密苏里州参议员乔什·霍利\n阿拉斯加州参议员丹·沙利文\n阿拉巴马州参议员汤米·塔伯维尔\n威斯康星州参议员罗恩·约翰逊\n怀俄明州参议员辛西娅·卢米斯\n田纳西州参议员玛莎·布莱克本\n宾夕法尼亚州众议员迈克·凯利\n\n以下是如何在各种平台上观看WSMV4直播的说明。\n\n玛莎·布莱克本参议员发表了以下声明：\n\n布莱克本说：“在乔·拜登任内，联邦调查局行使了它并不拥有的权力。拜登政府突袭海湖庄园，起诉特朗普总统，而现在我们知道，他们把美国最高执法机构武器化，用来监视支持特朗普总统的共和党美国参议员。在乔·拜登和克里斯·雷领导下，联邦调查局腐败透顶，我不会让这种情况继续下去。我感谢帕特尔局长和邦吉诺副局长展开调查，让应对这场腐败负责的人受到最大程度的追究。”\n\n哈格蒂参议员在社交媒体上发表了以下声明：\n\n他说：“杰克·史密斯在所谓调查@POTUS的政治迫害期间追踪了我的私人通信以及我同事的通信。这正是共和党人和特朗普总统多年来一直指出的、奥巴马和拜登任内联邦政府遭到政治武器化的类型。我们会查明真相，但每个美国人都应该对这里发生的事情感到震惊。”\n\n美联社报道称，与该调查有关的文件没有说明为何分析这些议员的电话记录，也没有说明分析产生了什么结果。\n\n美联社为本文提供了报道。\n\n版权所有2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-10-07T15:35:33.473000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2147","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"纳什维尔国土安全特别工作组调查后38人被起诉","title_en":"38 charged following investigations by Nashville Homeland Security Task Force","summary_cn":"WSMV报道，在纳什维尔新成立的国土安全特别工作组新闻发布会上，官员宣布38人因多项指控被起诉，其中包括8名MS-13成员及关联人员，涉嫌毒品贩运、劫车、袭警、暴力犯罪中使用枪支及移民违法。该工作组依据第14159号行政命令设立，旨在打击犯罪卡特尔、外国帮派、跨国犯罪组织及人口走私贩运网络，由HSI、ATF、FBI等多机构参与。","summary_en":"WSMV reports that at a press conference announcing Nashville's new Homeland Security Task Force, officials said 38 people were charged on various counts, including eight MS-13 members and associates, for alleged drug trafficking, carjackings, assaulting officers, using guns in violent crimes and immigration offenses. Established by Executive Order 14159, the task force aims to eliminate criminal cartels, foreign gangs, transnational criminal organizations and human smuggling rings, involving HSI, ATF, FBI and other agencies.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:15:57.681163+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/11/06/38-charged-following-investigations-by-nashville-homeland-security-task-force","content":"38 charged following investigations by Nashville Homeland Security Task ForceThe task force is dedicated to “eliminating criminal cartels, foreign gangs, transnational criminal organizations, and human smuggling and trafficking rings” in the U.S. and beyond.Cannot find custom embedBy Caleb WethingtonPublished: Nov. 6, 2025 at 3:48 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - During a press conference to announce the work of Nashville’s new Homeland Security Task Force, officials reported the arrests of 38 people on a slew of charges.The U.S. Attorney’s Office reports that the 38 individuals charged, including eight members and associates of MS-13 (a transnational crime gang), are believed to have been involved in drug trafficking, carjackings, assaulting officers, using guns while committing violent crimes and immigration offenses.The charges are part of the Homeland Security Task Force (HSTF) established in Nashville by Executive Order 14159, Protecting the American People Against Invasion, the U.S. Attorney’s Office shared.The HSTF is dedicated to “eliminating criminal cartels, foreign gangs, transnational criminal organizations, and human smuggling and trafficking rings” in the U.S. and beyond.The Nashville HSTF involved the following:HSIATFFBIIRS Criminal InvestigationsUSPS Inspection ServiceUS MarshalsUS Secret ServiceDEAOther federal agenciesRelated Coverage:US creating Homeland Security Task Force in Nashville‘Left a trail of violence and devastation.’ DEA dismantles Nashville cell of international crime gangHere are instructions on how to watch WSMV4 live on various platforms.Below is a look at the cases being prosecuted so far through the work of the HSTF, according to the U.S. Attorney’s Office:Victor Alfonso Paez Rodriguez and Jesus Mendoza VieraBoth are allegedly unlawfully in the U.S. and are alleged to have trafficked fentanyl from Mexico into Middle TennesseeTrenell Copeland, Tabria Bowens, Cassandra Lawson, Alicia Barman, and Ashanti WilliamsAccused of trafficking fentanyl, meth and marijuana to Trousdale County Correctional FacilityDebyi BangeasAn alleged MS-13 member unlawfully present in the U.S. is accused of an armed carjacking.Kevin Jasir Contreras Arita, Jose Pena and David Dubon-EnamaradoTwo alleged MS-13 members and an alleged MS-13 associate were accused of drug trafficking, assaulting an officer and illegal re-entry in the U.S.Leonel VargasAlleged MS-13 member accused of being unlawfully present in the U.S., drug trafficking, possession of a gun and more.Anthony VargasAn alleged MS-13 associate, accused of being unlawfully present in the U.S. and caught with a gun believed to have ballistic associations with the homicide of a 14-year-old girl.U.S. v. Sandoval involves 13 defendantsIncludes an alleged MS-13 member and alleged associate charged in meth and cocaine distribution conspiracy.U.S. v. Toliver involves 12 defendantsCharged with trafficking fentanyl sourced from outside the U.S.“Crossville has experienced a spike in the number of overdose deaths linked to fentanyl. Some of those overdoses are alleged to be connected to the trafficking activities of these defendants.”This news comes on the heels of the creation of a U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) call center in Nashville, according to a contract document obtained by Reuters.According to the FBI’s website, there have been Homeland Security Task Forces created in other parts of the U.S., including Texas and Alaska.The FBI reports that these task forces will investigate transnational criminal activity:Drug trafficking Money laundering Human trafficking Alien smuggling Homicide Extortion Kidnapping; and Weapons trafficking Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"纳什维尔国土安全特别工作组调查后起诉38人\n该特别工作组致力于在美国及其他地区“消灭犯罪卡特尔、外国帮派、跨国犯罪组织以及人口走私和贩运团伙”。\n找不到自定义嵌入内容\nCaleb Wethington撰写\n发布于：2025年11月6日下午3:48（美国中部时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——在一次宣布纳什维尔新成立的国土安全特别工作组工作成果的新闻发布会上，官员报告了38人因多项罪名被捕。美国检察官办公室表示，被起诉的38人中包括8名MS-13成员及其关联人员（MS-13是一个跨国犯罪团伙），据信他们涉嫌参与毒品贩运、劫车、袭击警察、在实施暴力犯罪时使用枪支以及违反移民法等行为。美国检察官办公室称，这些指控属于根据第14159号行政命令《保护美国人民免遭入侵》在纳什维尔设立的国土安全特别工作组（HSTF）工作范围。HSTF致力于在美国及其他地区“消灭犯罪卡特尔、外国帮派、跨国犯罪组织以及人口走私和贩运团伙”。纳什维尔HSTF包括以下机构：国土安全调查局（HSI）；酒精、烟草、枪械和爆炸物管理局（ATF）；联邦调查局（FBI）；国税局刑事调查处（IRS Criminal Investigations）；美国邮政检查局；美国法警局；美国特勤局；缉毒局（DEA）；其他联邦机构\n相关新闻报道：美国在纳什维尔设立国土安全特别工作组\n“留下了暴力和破坏的痕迹。”缉毒局捣毁纳什维尔国际犯罪团伙小组\n以下是如何在各种平台观看WSMV4直播的说明。\n据美国检察官办公室称，以下是迄今通过HSTF工作提起诉讼的案件：\n维克托·阿方索·派斯·罗德里格斯和赫苏斯·门多萨·维埃拉\n两人据称非法居留在美国，并被指控将芬太尼从墨西哥贩运到田纳西州中部。\n特雷内尔·科普兰、塔布里亚·鲍恩斯、卡桑德拉·劳森、艾丽西亚·巴曼和阿什anti·威廉姆斯\n被指控向特鲁斯代尔县惩教设施贩运芬太尼、冰毒和大麻。\n黛比·班赫亚斯\n一名据称是MS-13成员、非法居留在美国的人，被指控实施持械劫车。\n凯文·贾西尔·孔特雷拉斯·阿里塔、何塞·佩尼亚和大卫·杜邦-埃纳马拉多\n两名据称是MS-13成员及一名据称是MS-13关联人员被指控贩毒、袭击警员以及非法再次入境美国。\n莱昂内尔·巴尔加斯\n据称是MS-13成员，被指控非法居留在美国、贩毒、持有枪支等。\n安东尼·巴尔加斯\n一名据称是MS-13关联人员，被指控非法居留在美国，并被发现持有一把枪，该枪据信在一名14岁女孩的凶杀案中具有弹道关联。\n美国诉桑多瓦尔案涉及13名被告\n其中包括一名据称是MS-13成员和一名据称是其关联人员，他们被控参与冰毒和可卡因分销阴谋。\n美国诉托利弗案涉及12名被告\n被控贩运来自美国境外的芬太尼。\n“克罗斯维尔与芬太尼相关的过量死亡人数激增。其中一些过量事件据称与这些被告的贩运活动有关。”\n据路透社获得的一份合同文件称，此消息发布之际，美国移民与海关执法局（ICE）正在纳什维尔设立一个呼叫中心。根据联邦调查局网站，美国其他地区也设立了国土安全特别工作组，包括得克萨斯州和阿拉斯加州。联邦调查局表示，这些特别工作组将调查跨国犯罪活动：毒品贩运；洗钱；人口贩运；偷运外国人；杀人；敲诈勒索；绑架；以及武器贩运\n版权所有 2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-11-06T21:48:46.073000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2150","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国将在纳什维尔设立国土安全特别工作组","title_en":"US creating Homeland Security Task Force in Nashville","summary_cn":"美国代理联邦检察官罗伯特·麦圭尔与联邦及地方机构领导人宣布在纳什维尔成立国土安全特别工作组，并通报中田纳西地区在毒品贩运、暴力犯罪、武器和移民违规方面的最新指控。该工作组将由国土安全调查局、ATF、FBI、陆军刑事调查部、纳什维尔警方等多机构参与，调查跨国犯罪活动。此前DEA在纳什维尔捣毁了一个MS-13团伙分支。","summary_en":"Acting U.S. Attorney Robert McGuire and federal and local leaders announced the creation of a Homeland Security Task Force in Nashville, along with updates on charges related to drug trafficking, violent crime, weapons and immigration violations in Middle Tennessee. The task force will involve Homeland Security Investigations, ATF, FBI, Army CID, MNPD and other agencies to investigate transnational criminal activity, following a DEA operation that dismantled an MS-13 cell in Nashville.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:34:30.024717+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/11/06/us-creating-homeland-security-task-force-nashville","content":"US creating Homeland Security Task Force in NashvilleThe task force will involve multiple federal and local agencies in Nashville.Cannot find custom embedBy Caleb WethingtonPublished: Nov. 6, 2025 at 11:22 AM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNEW: 38 charged following investigations by Nashville Homeland Security Task ForceNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - The U.S. is set to announce the creation of a Homeland Security Task Force in Nashville.Acting United States Attorney for the Middle District of Tennessee, Robert McGuire, and leaders from other federal and local agencies are making the announcement in Nashville on Thursday afternoon.Alongside the task force’s creation, the press conference will update the public on the latest efforts that have resulted in “charges relating to drug-trafficking, violent crime, weapons, and immigration violations” throughout Middle Tennessee, according to the U.S. Attorney’s Office.In mid-September, the Drug Enforcement Agency announced it had dismantled a cell of an international crime gang that was operating out of Nashville.Related Coverage:ICE call center planned for Nashville, report saysTHP participating in federal program to increase immigration enforcementDHS Sec. Noem condemns criticism of ICE operations in Nashville‘Left a trail of violence and devastation.’ DEA dismantles Nashville cell of international crime gangHere are instructions on how to watch WSMV4 live on various platforms.Following a nine-month investigation, a series of search warrants was executed throughout Nashville in mid-September.In total, 17 members and associates of MS-13 were arrested across three states, including Tennessee, California, and Oklahoma, according to the DEA.This news comes on the heels of the creation of a U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) call center in Nashville, according to a contract document obtained by Reuters.According to the FBI’s website, there have been Homeland Security Task Forces created in other parts of the U.S., including Texas and Alaska.The FBI reports that these task forces will investigate transnational criminal activity:Drug trafficking Money laundering Human trafficking Alien smuggling Homicide Extortion Kidnapping; and Weapons trafficking Representatives from Homeland Security Investigations, the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms, and Explosives (ATF), the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI), the Army Criminal Investigation Division, MNPD, the Cumberland County Sheriff’s Office, as well as other federal, state, and local agencies are expected to be involved with the operation.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"美国将在纳什维尔成立国土安全特别工作组\n该工作组将涉及纳什维尔的多个联邦和地方机构。\n找不到自定义嵌入\n作者：Caleb Wethington\n发布时间：2025年11月6日上午11:22（中部标准时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n最新消息：纳什维尔国土安全特别工作组调查后，38人被起诉\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——美国即将宣布在纳什维尔成立国土安全特别工作组。\n田纳西州中区代理联邦检察官Robert McGuire以及其他联邦和地方机构的负责人将于周四下午在纳什维尔宣布这一消息。\n据美国检察官办公室称，随着特别工作组的成立，新闻发布会还将向公众通报中田纳西州近期取得的成果，这些成果已促成“与贩毒、暴力犯罪、武器和移民违法行为有关的起诉”。\n9月中旬，缉毒局宣布已捣毁一个在纳什维尔活动的国际犯罪团伙分支。\n相关报道：报道称纳什维尔计划设立ICE呼叫中心\nTHP参与联邦计划以加强移民执法\n国土安全部长Noem谴责在纳什维尔开展的ICE行动所受批评\n“留下了暴力和破坏的痕迹。”缉毒局捣毁纳什维尔国际犯罪团伙分支\n以下是如何在各种平台观看WSMV4直播的说明。\n经过为期9个月的调查，9月中旬在纳什维尔各地执行了一系列搜查令。\n据缉毒局称，共有17名MS-13成员及关联人员在包括田纳西州、加利福尼亚州和俄克拉何马州在内的三个州被捕。\n据路透社获得的一份合同文件显示，此消息发布之际，美国移民与海关执法局（ICE）正在纳什维尔设立一个呼叫中心。\n根据联邦调查局网站，美国其他地区也成立了国土安全特别工作组，包括得克萨斯州和阿拉斯加州。\n联邦调查局称，这些特别工作组将调查跨国犯罪活动：\n贩毒\n洗钱\n人口贩运\n偷渡\n谋杀\n敲诈勒索\n绑架；以及\n武器贩运\n预计国土安全调查局、酒精、烟草、枪支及爆炸物管理局（ATF）、联邦调查局（FBI）、陆军刑事调查处、纳什维尔大都会警察局（MNPD）、坎伯兰县警长办公室以及其他联邦、州和地方机构的代表将参与该行动。\n版权所有2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-11-06T17:22:51.524000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2144","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部在纳什维尔启动特别工作组","title_en":"Department of Homeland Security launches task force based in Nashville","summary_cn":"WSMV报道，美国国土安全部在纳什维尔启动国土安全特别工作组，旨在打击田纳西州中部的跨国犯罪组织。代理联邦检察官Rob McGuire在新闻发布会上宣布，超过15个联邦、州和地方执法机构参与。他同时宣布，因该工作组协助的调查，38人被逮捕和起诉，其中8人与跨国帮派MS-13有关，指控涉及毒品贩运、劫车和联邦枪支犯罪。","summary_en":"WSMV reports that the U.S. Department of Homeland Security launched a Homeland Security Task Force based in Nashville to combat transnational criminal organizations in Middle Tennessee. Acting U.S. Attorney Rob McGuire announced at a press conference that more than 15 federal, state and local law enforcement agencies are involved. He also announced the arrest and indictment of 38 people due to investigations assisted by the task force, eight associated with MS-13, on charges including drug trafficking, carjacking and federal gun crimes.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:15:56.991058+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/11/07/department-homeland-security-launches-task-force-based-nashville","content":"Department of Homeland Security launches task force based in NashvilleA Homeland Security Task Force has launched in Nashville to combat drug trafficking and violent crime.A Homeland Security Task Force has launched in Nashville to combat drug trafficking and violent crime.By Braden RossPublished: Nov. 6, 2025 at 9:33 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - The Department of Homeland Security is launching a Homeland Security Task Force based in Nashville aimed at combating transnational criminal organizations in Middle Tennessee.Acting U.S. Attorney for the Middle District of Tennessee Rob McGuire made the announcement at a press conference on Thursday surrounded by representatives from some of the more than 15 federal, state and local law enforcement agencies involved in the effort.“While all of these agencies have their own areas of expertise and areas of responsibility, the idea behind the Homeland Security Task Force is to bring these resources together for the betterment of the community, to try to lower the amount of fentanyl trafficking and fentanyl overdoses, to lower the amount of gang violence, to stop the flow of illegal drugs and firearms into our communities,” McGuire said.Although Thursday’s announcement marked the official public launch of the task force, McGuire said agencies have been working under the umbrella for months now. At the press conference, he announced the arrest and indictment of 38 people due to investigations assisted by the task force. Eight of those people are associated with the transnational gang MS-13, he said. The charges ranged from drug trafficking to carjacking to federal gun charges.Agency leaders called out several of the successful investigations including one they say dismantled a fentanyl pipeline that was funneling drugs into Tennessee.“Operation We Will Rock You started when one of our local narcotics investigators noticed a spike in overdose deaths within our community,” said Cumberland County Sheriff Casey Cox. “His work led to uncovering a major drug trafficking organization operating within Middle Tennessee.”Here are instructions on how to watch WSMV4 live on various platforms.McGuire noted that several of the 38 people arrested are believed to be in the United States illegally. When asked about how immigration enforcement will fit into the task force’s duties, McGuire said they are focused mainly on drug and violent crimes.“This task force, like we’ve said, is focused entirely on combating illegal drugs, transnational criminal organizations, drug cartels, gang violence, MS-13, TDA, those kinds of groups,” said McGuire. “That’s what we’re going to be focusing on.”The announcement comes on the heels of reporting from Reuters showing U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) is planning to build an immigration enforcement call center in Nashville with a dedicated team to track down unaccompanied undocumented minors. McGuire said that effort has nothing to do with the Homeland Security Task Force.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"国土安全部在纳什维尔成立特别工作组\n一个国土安全特别工作组已在纳什维尔启动，旨在打击毒品贩运和暴力犯罪。\n一个国土安全特别工作组已在纳什维尔启动，旨在打击毒品贩运和暴力犯罪。\n作者：Braden Ross\n发布于：2025年11月6日晚上9:33（中部标准时间）\n分享\n将我们添加到Google\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——国土安全部正在成立一个以纳什维尔为基地的国土安全特别工作组，旨在打击田纳西州中部的跨国犯罪组织。\n田纳西州中区代理联邦检察官Rob McGuire于周四在新闻发布会上宣布了这一消息，发布会现场有来自参与该行动的15多个联邦、州和地方执法机构的代表。\n“虽然所有这些机构都有各自的专业领域和职责范围，但国土安全特别工作组的理念是将这些资源汇集起来，以改善社区状况，努力降低芬太尼贩运和芬太尼过量的数量，减少帮派暴力，并阻止非法毒品和枪支流入我们的社区，”McGuire说。\n尽管周四的宣布标志着该特别工作组正式公开启动，McGuire表示，各机构实际上已经在这一框架下开展工作数月。在新闻发布会上，他宣布，由于该特别工作组协助开展的调查，已有38人被逮捕并被起诉。他说，其中8人与跨国帮派MS-13有关。指控范围从毒品贩运、劫车到联邦枪支罪名不等。\n机构负责人列举了几项成功调查，其中包括一项他们称捣毁了将毒品输送至田纳西州的芬太尼供应链的行动。\n坎伯兰县警长Casey Cox说：“‘我们将震撼你’行动始于我们的一名地方缉毒调查员注意到社区内过量死亡人数激增。他的工作最终揭露了一个在田纳西州中部运营的大型毒品贩运组织。”\n以下是如何在各种平台上观看WSMV4直播的说明。\nMcGuire指出，被捕的38人中有几人据信非法滞留在美国。当被问及移民执法将如何纳入特别工作组职责时，McGuire表示，他们主要专注于毒品和暴力犯罪。\nMcGuire说：“正如我们所说，这个特别工作组完全专注于打击非法毒品、跨国犯罪组织、毒品卡特尔、帮派暴力、MS-13、TDA以及类似团体。这就是我们将关注的重点。”\n这一宣布发布之际，路透社报道称，美国移民与海关执法局（ICE）计划在纳什维尔建立一个移民执法呼叫中心，并配备专门团队追踪无人陪伴的无证未成年人。McGuire表示，该计划与国土安全特别工作组毫无关系。\n版权所有 2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-11-07T03:33:52.433000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1896","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI报告：2025年田纳西州针对儿童的暴力犯罪致82人被捕、67名受害者获救","title_en":"Violent crimes against children: 82 arrests made, 67 victims recovered in TN in 2025, FBI reports","summary_cn":"WSMV报道，美国联邦调查局发布2025年田纳西州针对儿童暴力犯罪的统计数据。FBI报告称，全年共逮捕82人，确认110名儿童受害者，其中67名儿童受害者获救。此外，共送达61份起诉书，捣毁两个针对儿童的犯罪组织，最终获得42项定罪和59项判决。","summary_en":"WSMV reports that the FBI released statistics on violent crimes against children in Tennessee for 2025. The FBI reported 82 arrests, 110 child victims identified and 67 child victims recovered throughout the year. In addition, 61 indictments were served, two crimes-against-children organizations were dismantled, resulting in 42 convictions and 59 sentences.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:36:32.727718+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2025/12/30/violent-crimes-against-children-82-arrests-made-67-victims-recovered-tn-2025-fbi-reports","content":"Violent crimes against children: 82 arrests made, 67 victims recovered in TN in 2025, FBI reportsNew data from the Federal Bureau of Investigation reveals statistics on violent crimes against children this year. Cannot find custom embedBy Caleb WethingtonPublished: Dec. 30, 2025 at 4:45 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - The Federal Bureau of Investigation has released statistics on violent crimes against children in Tennessee for 2025.Among those stats, the FBI reports that 82 people were arrested and 67 child victims were recovered throughout the year.Related: Homicide, rape and other violent crimes are down in Nashville, police saypic.twitter.com/HwyU1Kbnle— FBI Nashville (@FBI_Nashville) December 30, 2025\nBelow is a look at their stats:82 arrests made61 indictments served110 child victims identified67 child victims recoveredTwo crimes against children organizations dismantledResulting in 42 convictions and 59 sentencesCopyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"针对儿童的暴力犯罪：FBI报告称，田纳西州2025年逮捕82人，找回67名受害者\n联邦调查局的新数据披露了今年针对儿童的暴力犯罪统计数据。\n找不到自定义嵌入内容\n作者：凯莱布·韦辛顿\n发布于：2025年12月30日美国中部标准时间下午4:45\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将我们添加为首选来源\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——联邦调查局发布了田纳西州2025年针对儿童的暴力犯罪统计数据。\n在这些数据中，FBI报告称，全年共有82人被捕，67名儿童受害者被找回。\n相关报道：警方称，纳什维尔的凶杀、强奸及其他暴力犯罪正在下降\npic.twitter.com/HwyU1Kbnle——FBI纳什维尔（@FBI_Nashville）2025年12月30日\n以下为其统计数据：\n逮捕82人\n执行61份起诉书\n确认110名儿童受害者\n找回67名儿童受害者\n捣毁两个侵害儿童犯罪组织\n最终导致42项定罪和59项判刑\n版权所有2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2025-12-30T22:45:36.066000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1373","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"与肯塔基州有关联的男子因邮件与电信欺诈共谋被FBI通缉","title_en":"Man with ties to Kentucky wanted by FBI for mail, wire fraud conspiracy","summary_cn":"WSMV报道，FBI正通缉与肯塔基州有关联的34岁男子Kalpeshkumar“Kenny”Rasikbhai Patel，其涉嫌参与2017年至2021年间一项全国性诈骗计划，诱骗多人将大额现金或预付借记卡寄往美国各地地址。受害者被电话告知其个人信息或身份与犯罪活动有关。联邦逮捕令于2023年6月22日签发，他被控邮件与电信欺诈。FBI称其被视为逃犯，呼吁公众提供线索。","summary_en":"WSMV reports that the FBI is seeking Kalpeshkumar \"Kenny\" Rasikbhai Patel, 34, with ties to Kentucky, for alleged participation in a nationwide scheme between 2017 and 2021 to defraud multiple people into sending large sums of cash or prepaid debit cards to addresses across the U.S. Victims were contacted by phone and led to believe their personal information or identities were linked to criminal activity. A federal arrest warrant was issued on June 22, 2023, charging him with mail and wire fraud. The FBI considers him a fugitive and asks the public for tips.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:18:02.529919+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2026/03/18/man-with-ties-kentucky-wanted-by-fbi-mail-wire-fraud-conspiracy","content":"Man with ties to Kentucky wanted by FBI for mail, wire fraud conspiracy Kenny Patel is accused of participating in a nationwide scheme to defraud multiple people into sending large sums of money to addresses throughout the U.S.By Kassidy BrownPublished: Mar. 18, 2026 at 2:04 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLOUISVILLE, Ky. (WSMV) - A man with ties to Kentucky is wanted by the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) in connection with an investigation into mail and wire fraud conspiracy.The FBI said Kalpeshkumar “Kenny” Rasikbhai Patel, 34, is wanted for his alleged participation in a nationwide scheme to defraud multiple people into sending large sums of money, usually cash or prepaid debit cards, to addresses throughout the U.S. between 2017 and 2021.The victims were contacted by phone and led to believe their personal information or identities were associated with criminal activity.A federal arrest warrant was issued for Patel on June 22, 2023, in the U.S. District Court, Eastern District of Kentucky, after he was charged with mail and wire fraud.“Patel is considered a fugitive from justice, and any information regarding his whereabouts should be treated as significant and actionable,” the FBI said.Anyone with information regarding the investigation or Patel’s whereabouts is asked to contact your local FBI office or the nearest American Embassy or Consulate. An anonymous tip can also be submitted online.Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"与肯塔基州有关系的男子因邮件及电信欺诈共谋被FBI通缉 Kenny Patel被指控参与一项全国性骗局，诱骗多人向美国各地地址汇出大笔资金。\n作者：Kassidy Brown\n发布：2026年3月18日下午2:04（CDT）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n路易斯维尔，肯塔基州（WSMV）——一名与肯塔基州有关系的男子因涉及邮件及电信欺诈共谋的调查而被联邦调查局（FBI）通缉。\nFBI表示，34岁的Kalpeshkumar“Kenny”Rasikbhai Patel涉嫌参与一项全国性骗局，在2017年至2021年期间诱骗多人向美国各地地址汇出大笔资金，通常是现金或预付借记卡。\n受害者通过电话被联系，并被引导相信其个人信息或身份与犯罪活动有关。\n2023年6月22日，肯塔基东区美国地区法院在Patel被控邮件及电信欺诈后，对其签发了联邦逮捕令。\nFBI表示：“Patel被视为逃犯，任何有关其下落的信息都应被视为重要且可采取行动的线索。”\n任何掌握调查或Patel下落信息的人，请联系当地FBI办公室或最近的美国大使馆或领事馆。也可以在线提交匿名线索。\n版权2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2026-03-18T19:04:45.059000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1360","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI警告田纳西州家长：暴力网络组织正针对儿童","title_en":"FBI warns TN parents of ‘violent online networks’ targeting children","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局纳什维尔分局警告田纳西州家长、监护人和照护者，称“764”等暴力网络组织活动激增，正针对并剥削儿童及其他弱势群体。FBI表示，这些人员通过青少年常用网络平台接触儿童，操纵并胁迫其制作和分享极端血腥内容、儿童性虐待材料，并参与虐待动物、自残等暴力行为，随后进行勒索，迫使其从事人肉搜索、报假警、破坏财物及性剥削等犯罪活动。FBI呼吁家长了解相关手法，如有受害证据可向IC3或当地警方举报。","summary_en":"The FBI's Nashville field office warned Tennessee parents, guardians and caregivers about a surge in activity by \"764\" and other violent online networks targeting and exploiting children and vulnerable individuals. According to FBI Nashville, offenders connect with children through platforms commonly used by young people, then manipulate and coerce them into producing and sharing extreme gore content, child sexual abuse material, and engaging in animal cruelty, self-harm and other violent acts. They then extort victims into doxing, swatting, vandalism, sexual exploitation and sometimes murder. The FBI urged parents to understand these tactics and report evidence to IC3 or local police.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:17:55.914458+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2026/03/19/fbi-warns-tn-parents-violent-online-networks-targeting-children","content":"FBI warns TN parents of ‘violent online networks’ targeting childrenFBI Nashville reports that children are being targeted and exploited by individuals through online platforms.By Caleb Wethington and Jordan JamesPublished: Mar. 19, 2026 at 11:02 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - The Federal Bureau of Investigation in Nashville is warning parents, guardians and caregivers of the surge in activity of “764″ and other violent online networks targeting and exploiting children and other vulnerable individuals in Tennessee.FBI Nashville reported that children are being targeted and exploited by individuals who connect with children through online platforms commonly used by young people.“They then manipulate and coerce them into producing and sharing extreme gore content, child sexual abuse materials, and engaging in acts of animal cruelty, self-harm, and other violent acts,” a supervisory FBI special agent in Tennessee said.“Once they do this, they then extort them to conduct other criminal activities to include doxing, swatting, vandalism, online and in-person sexual exploitation of themselves or others, and eventually committing animal cruelty, self-harm, and sometimes murder.”The FBI is urging parents to understand the tactics these violent online networks are using to exploit their children.“If you have evidence your child or someone else you know may be a victim, report it to the FBI’s Internet Crime Complaint Center at ic3.gov. You can also contact FBI Nashville at 615-232-7500 or your local police department. If it’s an immediate, life-threatening emergency, dial 9-1-1.\"Copyright 2025 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI警告田纳西州家长：针对儿童的“暴力在线网络”\nFBI纳什维尔分局报告称，儿童正通过在线平台被个人盯上并遭到剥削。\n作者：Caleb Wethington 和 Jordan James\n发布：2026年3月19日中部夏令时间上午11:02\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——联邦调查局纳什维尔分局正在警告田纳西州的父母、监护人和照护者，“764”及其他暴力在线网络的活动激增，这些网络正以儿童和其他弱势个人为目标并对其进行剥削。\nFBI纳什维尔分局报告称，个人通过年轻人常用的在线平台与儿童建立联系，进而将儿童作为目标并加以剥削。\n田纳西州一名负责监督的FBI特别探员表示：“他们随后操纵并胁迫这些儿童制作和分享极端血腥内容、儿童性虐待材料，并从事虐待动物、自残及其他暴力行为。”\n“他们一旦这样做，便会勒索他们从事其他犯罪活动，包括人肉搜索、虚假报警、故意破坏、对自身或他人的线上及线下性剥削，以及最终实施虐待动物、自残，有时甚至谋杀。”\nFBI敦促家长了解这些暴力在线网络正用来剥削其子女的手段。\n“如果你有证据表明你的孩子或你认识的其他人可能是受害者，请通过ic3.gov向FBI互联网犯罪投诉中心举报。你也可以联系FBI纳什维尔分局，电话为615-232-7500，或联系当地警察部门。如果是迫在眉睫、危及生命的紧急情况，请拨打9-1-1。”\n版权所有 2025 WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2026-03-19T16:02:40.320000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-966","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长在预算听证会上与议员发生冲突","title_en":"FBI director clashes with lawmakers during budget hearing","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔在参议院拨款委员会听证会上与民主党议员发生激烈冲突。听证会旨在审议特朗普政府2027财年执法机构预算申请，但焦点集中在《大西洋月刊》关于帕特尔行为不当的报道上。帕特尔否认指控并已提起2.5亿美元诽谤诉讼。FBI申请1253万美元预算，较去年增长逾17%，用于增加3200多个职位和近1300名新特工。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel clashed with Democratic lawmakers during a Senate Appropriations Committee hearing meant to review the Trump administration's 2027 budget request for law enforcement agencies. The hearing focused on alleged misconduct reported by The Atlantic, which Patel denies and has sued over for $250 million. The FBI is requesting $12.53 million, a more than 17% increase, to add over 3,200 positions and nearly 1,300 new agents.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:35:59.175555+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2026/05/13/fbi-director-clashes-with-lawmakers-during-budget-hearing","content":"FBI director clashes with lawmakers during budget hearingBy Emma WulfhorstPublished: May 12, 2026 at 8:27 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON (Gray DC) - FBI Director Kash Patel clashed with Democratic lawmakers Tuesday during a Senate Appropriations Committee hearing that was intended to review the Trump administration’s 2027 budget request for national law enforcement agencies.The hearing focused on alleged misconduct by Patel, who denies claims from a report in The Atlantic, alleging he drinks alcohol excessively and it impacts his job performance. Last month, Patel filed a $250 million defamation lawsuit against the magazine.“This is the ultimate example of hypocrisy,” Patel said. “I will not be tarnished by baseless allegations and fraudulent statements from the media.”Maryland Democrat and ranking member Sen. Chris Van Hollen questioned Patel about the reports during heated exchanges.Patel fired back at Van Hollen, referencing a trip the senator took to El Salvador last year to meet with Kilmar Abrego Garcia, the migrant who was deported against a judge’s orders.“Unlike your baseless reports, the only person that was slinging margaritas in El Salvador on the taxpayer dollar with a convicted, gang-banging rapist was you,” Patel said to Van Hollen Tuesday. “The only person that ran up a $7,000 bar tab in Washington, D.C. at the Lobby Bar was you.”Sen. Patty Murray, (D-WA) vice chair of the Senate Appropriations Committee, also criticized Patel’s conduct.“We need somebody at this agency who’s focused on solving criminal cases, not passing out branded bourbon or jetting around the globe,” Murray said. “If you want to pass out liquor or pop bottles in a locker room, stick to podcasting. Leave law and order to people who really do care about justice and appearances.”Patel and other agency heads did field questions about their funding requests. The FBI is asking for $12.53 million, a more than 17% increase from last year, in order to add more than 3,200 positions, 24 attorneys and nearly 1,300 new agents.Copyright 2026 Gray DC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局局长在预算听证会上与议员发生冲突\n作者：艾玛·伍尔福斯特\n发布时间：2026年5月12日，CDT晚上8:27\n分享\n将我们添加到Google\n在Google上设为首选来源\n华盛顿（Gray DC）——周二，联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔在参议院拨款委员会听证会上与民主党议员发生冲突。该听证会原本旨在审议特朗普政府为国家执法机构提出的2027年预算请求。\n\n听证会重点关注有关帕特尔不当行为的指控。帕特尔否认《大西洋月刊》一篇报道中的说法，该报道称他过度饮酒并影响工作表现。上个月，帕特尔以诽谤为由起诉该杂志，索赔2.5亿美元。\n\n“这是虚伪的终极例子，”帕特尔说。“我不会被媒体毫无根据的指控和欺诈性陈述玷污。”\n\n马里兰州民主党参议员、委员会首席少数党成员克里斯·范·霍伦在激烈交锋中就这些报道质问帕特尔。\n\n帕特尔反击范·霍伦，提到这位参议员去年前往萨尔瓦多、与基尔马尔·阿布雷戈·加西亚会面的行程。加西亚是一名移民，曾在法官下令的情况下被驱逐出境。\n\n“与您那些毫无根据的报道不同，在纳税人的钱支持下、与一名被定罪的帮派强奸犯在萨尔瓦多喝玛格丽塔酒的人，只有您，”帕特尔周二对范·霍伦说。“在华盛顿特区大堂酒吧刷出7000美元酒水账单的人，也只有您。”\n\n参议院拨款委员会副主席、华盛顿州民主党参议员帕蒂·默里也批评了帕特尔的行为。\n\n“我们需要这个机构里有一个专注于侦破刑事案件的人，而不是分发带有品牌标志的波本威士忌，或乘飞机周游全球的人，”默里说。“如果你想分发酒水，或者在更衣室里开香槟，就继续做播客。把法律和秩序交给真正关心正义和形象的人。”\n\n帕特尔和其他机构负责人确实回答了有关资金申请的问题。联邦调查局申请1253万美元，比去年增加超过17%，以增加3200多个职位、24名律师和近1300名新特工。\n\n版权所有 2026 Gray DC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2026-05-13T01:27:02.601000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-901","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"黎巴嫩警方与FBI突袭纳什维尔怀特斯克里克地区一处住宅","title_en":"Lebanon Police, FBI raid residence in Whites Creek area of Nashville","summary_cn":"黎巴嫩警察局表示，周二清晨在戴维森县怀特斯克里克地区执行联邦行动。黎巴嫩警方与联邦调查局探员突袭了克拉克斯维尔公路4900街区一处住宅。截至上午7时30分，尚不清楚是否有人被捕或被拘留。行动性质不明，但现场可见特警队。报道称此为正在发展的事件。","summary_en":"The Lebanon Police Department said it was in Davidson County for a federal operation early Tuesday morning in the Whites Creek area. Lebanon Police officers and FBI agents converged on a residence in the 4900 block of Clarksville Highway. As of 7:30 a.m., it was unclear if anyone was arrested or taken into custody. The nature of the operation is unknown, but a SWAT unit was seen at the residence. This is a developing story.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:23.823835+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2026/05/26/lebanon-police-fbi-raid-residence-whites-creek-area-nashville","content":"Lebanon Police, FBI raid residence in Whites Creek area of NashvilleLebanon Police officers and the FBI executed search warrants at the home on Clarksville Highway.Lebanon detectives and FBI agents raided a large home in the Whites Creek area of Nashville.(WSMV)By Tony GarciaPublished: May 26, 2026 at 7:37 AM CDT|Updated: May 26, 2026 at 11:33 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNASHVILLE, Tenn. (WSMV) - The Lebanon Police Department says it was in Davidson County for a federal operation at a home in the Whites Creek area early Tuesday morning.Lebanon Police officers and agents with the Federal Bureau of Investigation converged on a residence in the 4900 block of Clarksville Highway.As of 7:30 a.m., it is unclear if anyone was arrested or taken into custody.The nature of the operation is unknown, but a SWAT unit was seen at the residence.This is a developing story. WSMV4 is working to gather more information.Copyright 2026 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"黎巴嫩警方和联邦调查局突袭纳什维尔怀特斯溪地区的一处住宅\n黎巴嫩警方人员和联邦调查局在克拉克斯维尔公路的一处住宅执行了搜查令。\n黎巴嫩警探和联邦调查局特工突袭了纳什维尔怀特斯溪地区的一栋大型住宅。（WSMV）\n作者：托尼·加西亚\n发布时间：2026年5月26日中部夏令时间上午7:37\n更新时间：2026年5月26日中部夏令时间上午11:33\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n田纳西州纳什维尔（WSMV）——黎巴嫩警察局表示，周二清晨，它因一项联邦行动来到戴维森县一处位于怀特斯溪地区的住宅。\n\n黎巴嫩警方人员和联邦调查局特工聚集在克拉克斯维尔公路4900号街区的一处住宅。\n\n截至上午7:30，尚不清楚是否有人被逮捕或被拘留。\n\n行动性质尚不清楚，但有人看到一支特警部队在该住宅处。\n\n这是一起正在发展的新闻。WSMV4正在努力收集更多信息。\n\n版权所有2026年WSMV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2026-05-26T12:37:30.702000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-623","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI在田纳西州中部一处房产执行清晨搜查","title_en":"FBI executes early-morning search at middle TN property","summary_cn":"FBI证实于周四上午在田纳西州士麦那执行了一份联邦法院授权的搜查令。此前WSMV4记者在珀西瓦尔街一处住宅外看到身着标识背心的联邦探员。FBI发言人表示，由于调查仍在进行，暂不提供更多细节。报道称此为持续发展中的事件。","summary_en":"The FBI confirmed it executed a federal court-authorized search warrant Thursday morning in Smyrna, Tennessee. The confirmation came after WSMV4 spotted federal agents wearing marked vests outside a house on Percival Street. An FBI spokesperson said no additional details could be provided as the investigation is ongoing. The report notes this is a developing story.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:05:05.098388+00:00","url":"https://www.wsmv.com/2026/07/09/fbi-executes-early-morning-search-middle-tn-property","content":"FBI executes early-morning search at middle TN propertyFederal agents were spotted Thursday morning outside of a house on Percival Street.By Chasity MaynardPublished: Jul. 9, 2026 at 9:42 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleSMYRNA, Tenn. (WSMV) - The Federal Bureau of Investigation has confirmed to WSMV4 they executed a search warrant Thursday morning in Smyrna. “I can confirm that the FBI executed a federal court authorized search warrant in Smyrna this morning,” an FBI spokesperson wrote in an email. “As this is an ongoing investigation, no additional details can be provided at this time.”The confirmation comes after WSMV4 reached out to ask about federal agents spotted at a house on Percival Street. The agents were seen wearing marked vests. This is a developing story. Check back for updates. Copyright 2026 WSMV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局清晨搜查田纳西州中部一处房产\n周四早晨，有人在珀西瓦尔街一栋房屋外发现联邦特工。\n作者：Chasity Maynard\n发布时间：2026年7月9日上午9:42（中部夏令时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n田纳西州斯迈纳（WSMV）——联邦调查局已向WSMV4确认，他们周四早晨在斯迈纳执行了搜查令。“我可以确认，联邦调查局今天早晨在斯迈纳执行了联邦法院授权的搜查令，”一名联邦调查局发言人在电子邮件中写道。“由于调查仍在进行，目前无法提供更多细节。”\n此前，WSMV4联系相关方面，询问在珀西瓦尔街一栋房屋外发现联邦特工一事。有人看到这些特工穿着带有标识的背心。\n这是一起正在发展中的新闻事件。请回来查看最新消息。\n版权归2026年WSMV所有。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wsmv.com","publish_time":"2026-07-09T14:42:43.447000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-375","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"印第安纳波利斯男子被列入FBI十大通缉犯名单后在密西西比州被捕","title_en":"Indianapolis man arrested in Mississippi after being added to FBI's 10 Most Wanted list | wthr.com","summary_cn":"印第安纳波利斯男子格雷戈里·亨德森二世在成为联邦逃犯近三年后，于2026年8月12日在密西西比州卢因被FBI杰克逊分局逮捕，未发生冲突。他因涉嫌参与国际贩毒和斗狗犯罪 enterprise 被起诉，8月11日刚被列入FBI十大通缉犯名单。他目前仍被联邦拘留，等待引渡回印第安纳州受审。","summary_en":"Gregory Henderson Jr. of Indianapolis was arrested without incident in Louin, Mississippi, on Aug. 12, 2026, by the FBI's Jackson field office after nearly three years as a federal fugitive. He faces charges from a multi-jurisdictional investigation into alleged international drug trafficking and an animal fighting enterprise, and was added to the FBI's Ten Most Wanted list on Aug. 11. He remains in federal custody pending extradition to Indiana.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:50:56.541661+00:00","url":"https://www.wthr.com/article/news/crime/gregory-henderson-jr-arrested-in-mississippi-after-added-fbis-10-most-wanted-list-indianapolis/531-7f7d6d61-481a-461c-baad-45a12352fefc","content":"Crime\nIndianapolis man arrested in Mississippi after being added to FBI's 10 Most Wanted list\nAfter almost three years as a federal fugitive, Gregory Henderson Jr. was arrested by the FBI in Mississippi on Aug. 12.\nTo stream 13 WTHR on your phone, you need the 13 WTHR app.\nDownload the 13 WTHR app\nMore Videos\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nAuthor: Hannah Race\nPublished: 10:01 PM EDT August 14, 2026\nUpdated: 10:01 PM EDT August 14, 2026\nINDIANAPOLIS — An Indianapolis man has been arrested in Mississippi after almost three years as a federal fugitive.\nAccording to a release by the Federal Bureau of Investigation, Gregory Henderson Jr., 46, was apprehended by members of the FBI's Jackson, Mississippi field office around 2 p.m. on Aug. 12, 2026 in Louin, Mississippi, without incident. According to the release, he made his initial appearance in federal court in Mississippi on Aug. 13.\nThis story continues below.\nMore in Crime\nISP: Man who crashed off I-65 into Fall Creek was wanted on child sex crime charges; 14-year-old girl remains in critical condition\n2 teenagers arrested following double shooting on Indy's southwest side\nMan critically injured in shooting on Indy's northeast side\nHe is still in federal custody pending further judicial proceedings and his extradition to Indiana to face prosecution.\nHenderson had been a federal fugitive since August 2023, when a federal arrest warrant was issued in the Southern District of Indiana for charges from a multi-jurisdictional investigation into an alleged international drug trafficking and an animal fighting enterprise.\n\"USDA is proud of its work with the FBI to capture and arrest this criminal who was involved in the cruel act of dog fighting in violation of the Animal Welfare Act,\" USDA Inspector General John Walk said in the release. Dog fighting is reprehensible and is often associated with other dangerous crimes like narcotics. Together with our law enforcement partners we will apply the full force of the law and bring justice to bear against those who threaten the safety of American communities.”\nHenderson was the 542nd person added to the list since it was established in 1950, the FBI said. A total of 503 people who have appeared on the list have been apprehended and many are due to tips from citizens.\nCredit: FBI\nA copy of the FBI Ten Most Wanted Fugitives poster for Gregory Henderson, Jr. from Indianapolis, Indiana.\nHenderson's arrest came a day after he was added to the FBI's 10 Most Wanted List on Aug. 11.\n“His apprehension reflects the extraordinary persistence of our investigators, the strength of our law enforcement partnerships, and the value of a public willing to come forward with information. A single tip can provide the critical piece investigators need to move an investigation forward,\" FBI Indianapolis Special Agent in Charge Timothy J. O’Malley said in the release.\nClose Ad\nBefore You Leave, Check This Out","content_cn":"犯罪\n印第安纳波利斯男子在被列入 FBI 十大通缉犯名单后于密西西比州被捕\n在作为联邦逃犯近三年后，Gregory Henderson Jr. 于 8 月 12 日被 FBI 在密西西比州逮捕。\n要在手机上观看 13 WTHR 的直播，你需要 13 WTHR 应用程序。\n下载 13 WTHR 应用程序\n更多视频\n接下来 5 秒\n此视频的示例视频标题将显示在这里\n接下来 5 秒\n此视频的示例视频标题将显示在这里\n作者：Hannah Race\n发布时间：2026 年 8 月 14 日美国东部夏令时间晚上 10:01\n更新时间：2026 年 8 月 14 日美国东部夏令时间晚上 10:01\n印第安纳波利斯——一名印第安纳波利斯男子在作为联邦逃犯近三年后，已于密西西比州被捕。\n根据联邦调查局发布的新闻稿，46 岁的 Gregory Henderson Jr. 于 2026 年 8 月 12 日下午约 2 点在密西西比州 Louin 被 FBI 密西西比州杰克逊办事处成员顺利逮捕。新闻稿称，他于 8 月 13 日首次在密西西比州联邦法院出庭。\n以下是本报道的后续内容。\n更多犯罪新闻\n印第安纳州警察：驾车从 I-65 州际公路冲入 Fall Creek 的男子因儿童性犯罪指控被通缉；14 岁女孩仍处于危急状态\n印第安纳波利斯西南部发生双重枪击案后，两名青少年被捕\n印第安纳波利斯东北部枪击案中一名男子重伤，情况危急\n他目前仍被联邦拘押，等待进一步司法程序及被引渡至印第安纳州接受起诉。\nHenderson 自 2023 年 8 月起一直是联邦逃犯；当时，印第安纳州南区就一项针对涉嫌国际贩毒及斗兽企业的多辖区调查，对他发出了联邦逮捕令。\n美国农业部监察长 John Walk 在新闻稿中表示：“美国农业部为能与 FBI 合作抓捕并逮捕这名违反《动物福利法》、参与残忍斗狗行为的犯罪分子而感到自豪。斗狗令人憎恶，并且常与毒品等其他危险犯罪有关。我们将与执法合作伙伴一道，全面运用法律的力量，使那些威胁美国社区安全的人受到正义制裁。”\nFBI 表示，Henderson 是自该名单于 1950 年设立以来第 542 位被列入其中的人。曾出现在该名单上的人员中，共有 503 人已被捕，其中许多案件得益于民众提供的线索。\n图片来源：FBI\nFBI 十大通缉逃犯海报副本：来自印第安纳州印第安纳波利斯的 Gregory Henderson, Jr.\nHenderson 被捕的前一天，即 8 月 11 日，他刚被列入 FBI 十大通缉犯名单。\nFBI 印第安纳波利斯分局特别探员负责人 Timothy J. O’Malley 在新闻稿中表示：“他的落网体现了我们调查人员非凡的坚持、执法合作伙伴关系的力量，以及公众愿意提供信息的价值。一条线索就可能提供调查人员推进调查所需的关键一环。”\n关闭广告\n离开前，看看这个","publish_source":"wthr.com","publish_time":"2026-08-14T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-397","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"“总有人知道他在哪” 印第安纳波利斯男子因涉嫌贩毒和斗狗团伙被列入FBI十大通缉犯名单","title_en":"'Someone, somewhere knows where he is' | Indianapolis man on FBI Top 10 Most Wanted list for alleged drug dealing and dog fighting ring | wthr.com","summary_cn":"FBI于2026年8月11日宣布，悬赏100万美元征集线索，以逮捕印第安纳波利斯男子格雷戈里·亨德森二世。他被指为一个与“黑帮门徒”有关联、并与锡那罗亚贩毒集团有联系的暴力社区帮派头目，涉嫌在印第安纳波利斯及中西部分销可卡因、芬太尼和冰毒，并参与导致多只狗死亡或受虐的斗狗犯罪活动。他自2023年起在逃。","summary_en":"The FBI announced on Aug. 11, 2026, a $1 million reward for information leading to the arrest of Gregory Henderson Jr. of Indianapolis. He is accused of leading a violent neighborhood-based gang associated with the Gangster Disciples and tied to the Sinaloa Cartel, allegedly distributing cocaine, fentanyl and methamphetamine in Indianapolis and the Midwest, and involvement in a dog fighting enterprise that abused and killed numerous dogs. He has been on the run since 2023.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:54:24.177893+00:00","url":"https://www.wthr.com/article/news/crime/someone-somewhere-knows-where-he-is-indianapolis-man-on-fbi-top-10-most-wanted-list-for-alleged-drug-dealing-and-dog-fighting-ring-sinaloa-cartel/531-bc6e4049-eb52-4d64-956d-31d78067967f","content":"Crime\n'Someone, somewhere knows where he is' | Indianapolis man on FBI Top 10 Most Wanted list for alleged drug dealing and dog fighting ring\nThe FBI announced the agency is offering a $1 million reward for information leading to the arrest of Gregory Henderson, Jr.\nTo stream 13 WTHR on your phone, you need the 13 WTHR app.\nDownload the 13 WTHR app\nMore Videos\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nAuthor: WTHR.com staff\nPublished: 12:07 PM EDT August 11, 2026\nUpdated: 12:07 PM EDT August 11, 2026\nINDIANAPOLIS — An Indianapolis man is now on the FBI's Top 10 Most Wanted list for allegedly being the leader of a \"violent neighborhood-based\" local gang, as well as alleged drug dealing and dog fighting.\nThe agency announced Tuesday, Aug. 11, it's offering a $1 million reward for information leading to the arrest of Gregory Henderson, Jr.\nThis story continues below.\nMore in Crime\n1 person killed, another hurt in shooting on near east side of Indianapolis\n1 person killed, another hurt in shooting on near east side of Indianapolis\n31-year-old man charged for alleged role in deadly shooting at east Indy motel\nAccording to the FBI, Henderson should be considered armed and dangerous. The gang he is allegedly a leader of is said to be associated with the Gangster Disciples and ties to the Sinaloa Cartel, according to the FBI. The agency says he has been on the run since 2023.\nHenderson is described as a black man standing at 6-feet-1-inches tall and weighing around 220 pounds with brown hair and brown eyes, the FBI said. He may also go by \"Grego,\" \"Whitey\" or \"Coree Williams\" and has ties to the following cities, according to the FBI:\nChicago, IllinoisDetroit, MichiganDayton, OhioCincinnati, OhioLouisville, KentuckyLexington, KentuckySt. Louis, Missouri\nCredit: FBI\nA 2023 photo of Gregory Henderson, Jr., who is on the FBI Top 10 Most Wanted list.\nHe is allegedly involved with distributing narcotics including cocaine, fentanyl and methamphetamine around Indianapolis and the Midwest, the FBI announced, and he was also allegedly involved in a dog fighting \"criminal enterprise\" resulting in the severe abuse and deaths of \"numerous\" dogs.\nThe FBI said Henderson's drug trafficking network is believed to get narcotics from the Sinaloa Cartel.\nHenderson currently faces a federal arrest warrant issued in September 2025 for charges including conspiracy to possess with intent to distribute and to distribute controlled substances, conspiracy to launder monetary instruments and conspiracy to engage in an animal fight venture (dogfighting).\nCredit: FBI\nA copy of the FBI Ten Most Wanted Fugitives poster for Gregory Henderson, Jr. from Indianapolis, Indiana.\n\"The FBI does not close the book on dangerous fugitives. Whether it has been three months or three years, our commitment remains the same - we will relentlessly pursue Gregory Henderosn, Jr. until he faces justice,\" FBI Indianapolis Special Agent in Charge Timothy O'Malley said in a release. \"Now we are asking the public to help us - someone, somewhere knows where he is and one tip could lead to his arrest.\"\nHenderson is one of 31 people indicted by the Southern District of Indiana in an investigation into international drug trafficking and dog fighting in central Indiana, according to the FBI.\nIf you have any information about Henderson, Jr., you're asking to contact your local FBI office or the nearest American Embassy or Consulate. You can also call the FBI at 1-800-CALL FBI (1-800-225-5324) or submit a tip online at tips.fbi.gov.\nClose Ad\nBefore You Leave, Check This Out","content_cn":"犯罪\n“有人、在某个地方知道他在哪里” | 因涉嫌经营毒品交易和斗狗团伙而被列入 FBI 十大通缉名单的印第安纳波利斯男子\nFBI 宣布悬赏 100 万美元，征集能够促成逮捕小格雷戈里·亨德森的信息。\n要在手机上观看 13 WTHR，您需要 13 WTHR 应用程序。\n下载 13 WTHR 应用程序\n更多视频\n5 秒后播放\n本视频的示例视频标题将在此处显示\n5 秒后播放\n本视频的示例视频标题将在此处显示\n作者：WTHR.com 工作人员\n发布：2026 年 8 月 11 日美国东部夏令时间下午 12:07\n更新：2026 年 8 月 11 日美国东部夏令时间下午 12:07\n印第安纳波利斯——据称领导一个“以暴力为特点、扎根社区的”地方帮派，并涉嫌贩毒和斗狗的一名印第安纳波利斯男子现已被列入 FBI 十大通缉名单。\n该机构于 8 月 11 日星期二宣布，悬赏 100 万美元，征集能够促成逮捕小格雷戈里·亨德森的信息。\n本文下方继续。\n更多犯罪新闻\n印第安纳波利斯近东区枪击案致 1 人死亡、另 1 人受伤\n印第安纳波利斯近东区枪击案致 1 人死亡、另 1 人受伤\n31 岁男子因涉嫌参与印第安纳波利斯东部一家汽车旅馆的致命枪击案而被起诉\n据 FBI 称，应将亨德森视为持械且危险人物。据 FBI 称，他据称领导的帮派与 Gangster Disciples 组织有关联，并与锡那罗亚贩毒集团有联系。该机构称，他自 2023 年以来一直在逃。\nFBI 称，亨德森是一名黑人，身高 6 英尺 1 英寸，体重约 220 磅，棕色头发和棕色眼睛。他也可能使用“Grego”“Whitey”或“Coree Williams”等名字。据 FBI 称，他与以下城市有联系：\n伊利诺伊州芝加哥；密歇根州底特律；俄亥俄州代顿；俄亥俄州辛辛那提；肯塔基州路易斯维尔；肯塔基州列克星敦；密苏里州圣路易斯\n图片来源：FBI\n2023 年拍摄的小格雷戈里·亨德森照片；他已被列入 FBI 十大通缉名单。\nFBI 宣布，他涉嫌在印第安纳波利斯及中西部地区分销包括可卡因、芬太尼和甲基苯丙胺在内的麻醉品；他还涉嫌参与一个斗狗“犯罪企业”，导致“众多”狗遭受严重虐待并死亡。\nFBI 表示，据信亨德森的贩毒网络从锡那罗亚贩毒集团获取毒品。\n亨德森目前面临一份于 2025 年 9 月签发的联邦逮捕令，指控包括共谋持有并意图分销及分销受管制物质、共谋洗钱以及共谋参与动物斗殴活动（斗狗）。\n图片来源：FBI\n一张来自印第安纳州印第安纳波利斯的小格雷戈里·亨德森 FBI 十大通缉逃犯海报副本。\n“FBI 不会对危险逃犯结案。无论已经过去三个月还是三年，我们的承诺都不会改变——我们将不懈追捕小格雷戈里·Henderosn，直到他接受法律制裁，”FBI 印第安纳波利斯办公室负责人特别探员蒂莫西·奥马利在一份声明中说。“现在我们请求公众帮助我们——有人、在某个地方知道他在哪里，一条线索就可能促成他的逮捕。”\n据 FBI 称，亨德森是印第安纳州南区在调查印第安纳州中部国际贩毒和斗狗活动时起诉的 31 人之一。\n如果您掌握有关小格雷戈里·亨德森的任何信息，请联系当地 FBI 办公室，或最近的美国大使馆或领事馆。您也可以拨打 FBI 电话 1-800-CALL FBI（1-800-225-5324），或在 tips.fbi.gov 在线提交线索。\n关闭广告\n离开前，请查看此内容","publish_source":"wthr.com","publish_time":"2026-08-11T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3091","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI亚特兰大新任负责人谈了解佐治亚州及移民执法期望","title_en":"New head of FBI Atlanta discusses getting to know Georgia, immigration enforcement expectations","summary_cn":"保罗·W·布朗被任命为FBI亚特兰大分局新任特别探员负责人，负责佐治亚州FBI行动。他在接受WTOC专访时表示，FBI在移民执法中扮演更积极角色，但仍需平衡反恐、网络安全和反间谍等职责。布朗提到FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在移民执法指令下向各地办事处增派资源，并计划走访佐治亚州全部14个卫星办公室。","summary_en":"Paul W. Brown has been appointed as the new Special Agent in Charge of the FBI Atlanta Division, overseeing FBI operations across Georgia. In an interview with WTOC, Brown said the FBI is taking a more active role in immigration enforcement while balancing counterterrorism, cyber and counterintelligence responsibilities. He noted FBI Director Kash Patel is directing more resources to field offices amid new immigration enforcement directives, and plans to visit all 14 FBI satellite offices in Georgia.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:20:49.537806+00:00","url":"https://www.wtoc.com/2025/03/05/new-head-fbi-atlanta-discusses-getting-know-georgia-immigration-enforcement-expectations","content":"New head of FBI Atlanta discusses getting to know Georgia, immigration enforcement expectationsBy Shea SchraderPublished: Mar. 5, 2025 at 2:46 PM ESTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleSAVANNAH, Ga. (WTOC) -Paul W. Brown has been appointed as the new Special Agent in charge of the FBI Atlanta division.In a market exclusive interview with WTOC, Brown called his appointment to his new role overseeing FBI operations across Georgia as the pinnacle of his career. He says he’s spent the past few days getting familiar with the Division- but he has decades of experience with the FBI.He started as a Special Agent in 2006, and since then, has worked in counterterrorism, been the Deputy Assistant Director of the Weapons of Mass Destruction Directorate, and most recently, served as the Special Agent in charge of the Mobile field office.He’s bringing all that experience with him, as he gets to know the lay of the land in Georgia.“I need to understand the work they do, and the challenges they face, and how do I get them the resources, the training, develop those partnerships to amplify the work they’re doing,” Brown says.Brown’s appointment comes in the beginning of the new Trump administration, which is directing more resources to immigration enforcement. Brown says the FBI is taking a more active role in enforcement activities, but they still have to balance out their other responsibilities.”We still have to make sure we protect the nation and Georgia from terrorist attacks. We still have to be there to respond to cyber-incidents. We still have to be there to protect our critical information technologies from counter-intelligence and nation-states. Those don’t go away. It’s just, how do we best make sure that we can accomplish all that?” Brown says.With the new administration comes new FBI Director Kash Patel.Brown says Patel has expressed that in the midst of new immigration enforcement directives, he’s pushing more resources to FBI field offices, the Atlanta field office included. The extra resources- a luxury among Department of Government Efficiency cuts.“I know there’s an emphasis on reducing federal spending and the size of the federal government, but he has really focused in on protecting the resources of the FBI and making sure we’re best enabled to carry out our important mission,” Brown says.Brown tells WTOC he will be visiting all 14 of the FBI’s satellite office in Georgia soon, including the Savannah and Statesboro offices.You can see an extended version of WTOC’s interview with Brown above.Copyright 2025 WTOC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局亚特兰大分局新负责人谈了解佐治亚州及移民执法方面的期望\n作者：Shea Schrader\n发布时间：2025年3月5日下午2:46（美国东部时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n佐治亚州萨凡纳（WTOC）——保罗·W·布朗已被任命为联邦调查局亚特兰大分局的新任特别探员主管。\n在WTOC的一次市场独家采访中，布朗称，获任负责监督联邦调查局在佐治亚州各地行动的新职位，是其职业生涯的巅峰。他说，过去几天一直在熟悉该分局，但他拥有数十年的联邦调查局工作经验。\n他于2006年开始担任特别探员，此后曾从事反恐工作，担任大规模杀伤性武器局副助理局长，最近则担任联邦调查局莫比尔外勤办公室特别探员主管。\n在逐步了解佐治亚州当地情况时，他将这些经验全部带到了新岗位上。\n布朗说：“我需要了解他们所做的工作、面临的挑战，以及如何为他们提供资源和培训，建立这些合作关系，从而放大他们正在开展的工作。”\n布朗的任命发生在特朗普新政府上台初期，该政府正向移民执法投入更多资源。布朗表示，联邦调查局正在执法活动中发挥更积极的作用，但仍必须平衡其他职责。\n布朗说：“我们仍必须确保保护国家和佐治亚州免受恐怖袭击。我们仍必须随时准备应对网络事件。我们仍必须保护关键的信息技术，防范反情报威胁和民族国家威胁。这些职责不会消失。问题只是，我们如何最好地确保能够完成所有这些任务？”\n新政府上台后，联邦调查局迎来了新局长卡什·帕特尔。\n布朗表示，帕特尔曾表达，在新的移民执法指令实施之际，他正在向联邦调查局各外勤办公室调配更多资源，其中包括亚特兰大外勤办公室。在政府效率部削减开支的背景下，这些额外资源实属难得。\n布朗说：“我知道，当前强调的是减少联邦支出和联邦政府规模，但他确实非常重视保护联邦调查局的资源，并确保我们能够最好地履行重要使命。”\n布朗告诉WTOC，他很快将访问联邦调查局在佐治亚州的全部14个卫星办公室，其中包括萨凡纳和斯泰茨伯勒办公室。\n你可以在上方观看WTOC对布朗采访的加长版。\n版权所有2025 WTOC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wtoc.com","publish_time":"2025-03-05T19:46:51.745000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2271","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI设立“数字媒体线索”网站协助南卡罗来纳州立大学枪击案调查","title_en":"FBI creates ‘digital media tips’ website to support SC State University shooting investigations","summary_cn":"据WTOC报道，美国联邦调查局（FBI）宣布设立“数字媒体线索”网站，以协助南卡罗来纳州立大学枪击案的调查。此前，南卡罗来纳州执法部门（SLED）表示正在调查2025年10月4日发生在该校校园的两起独立枪击事件。FBI表示，正在为数字媒体分析提供技术协助，并呼吁公众上传手机视频或其他多媒体记录至指定网站，非数字媒体线索可提供给SLED。","summary_en":"According to WTOC, the FBI announced the creation of a 'digital media tips' website to support investigations into shootings at South Carolina State University. Previously, the South Carolina Law Enforcement Division (SLED) said it was investigating two separate shootings on campus on October 4, 2025. The FBI said it is providing technical assistance with digital media analysis and encouraged the public to upload cell phone video or other multimedia recordings to a designated website, while non-digital media tips can be provided to SLED.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:36:15.562081+00:00","url":"https://www.wtoc.com/2025/10/09/fbi-creates-digital-media-tips-website-support-sc-state-university-shooting-investigations","content":"FBI creates ‘digital media tips’ website to support SC State University shooting investigationsBy Christopher J. TeutonPublished: Oct. 9, 2025 at 10:12 AM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLEXINGTON, S.C. (WTOC) - Just now, the FBI has announced the creation of a ‘digital media tips website’ in support of SC State University shooting investigations.Previously, WTOC reported that SLED says they are investigating two separate shootings that took place on the South Carolina State University campus on October 4, 2025.South Carolina State officials said the lockdown was lifted the morning of October 6, 2025. The university then implemented enhanced security measures at entrances, including vehicle checks and ID verifications.Today, October 9, the FBI says “law enforcement is seeking multimedia from the public in two shootings that occurred on the campus of South Carolina State University last weekend.”The FBI asks that anyone with cell phone video, “or any other multimedia recordings” of either incident is encouraged to upload media to www.fbi.gov/scstateuniversityshootings.“While these incidents remain under investigation by the South Carolina Law Enforcement Division (SLED), the FBI is providing technical assistance with digital media analysis,” the FBI says.Information about the SC State University shootings outside of digital media may be provided to SLED at 866-472-8477 or tips@sled.sc.gov.Copyright 2025 WTOC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI创建“数字媒体线索”网站，支持南卡罗来纳州立大学枪击案调查\n作者：Christopher J. Teuton\n发布于：2025年10月9日上午10:12（美国东部时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n南卡罗来纳州列克星敦（WTOC）——就在刚刚，FBI宣布创建一个“数字媒体线索网站”，以支持南卡罗来纳州立大学枪击案调查。\n\n此前，WTOC报道称，南卡罗来纳州执法部门（SLED）表示，他们正在调查2025年10月4日发生在南卡罗来纳州立大学校园内的两起独立枪击事件。\n\n南卡罗来纳州立大学官员表示，校园封锁于2025年10月6日上午解除。随后，该大学在入口处实施了加强安保措施，包括车辆检查和身份核验。\n\n今天，即10月9日，FBI表示：“执法部门正在寻求公众提供上周末发生在南卡罗来纳州立大学校园内两起枪击事件的多媒体资料。”\n\nFBI请求任何拥有其中任一事件手机视频“或任何其他多媒体录音录像”的人，将媒体上传至www.fbi.gov/scstateuniversityshootings。\n\nFBI表示：“虽然这些事件仍由南卡罗来纳州执法部门（SLED）调查，但FBI正在为数字媒体分析提供技术协助。”\n\n有关南卡罗来纳州立大学枪击案、但不属于数字媒体的信息，可通过866-472-8477或tips@sled.sc.gov提供给SLED。\n\n版权2025 WTOC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wtoc.com","publish_time":"2025-10-09T14:12:44.308000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1858","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI确认福赛斯公园泼酸袭击所用化学品","title_en":"FBI identifies chemical used in Forsyth Park acid attack","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局向WTOC证实，已确认佐治亚州萨凡纳福赛斯公园泼酸袭击事件中使用的化学物质，但目前不向公众公布该物质名称。FBI官员表示，南卡罗来纳州执法部门（SLED）协助并代为进行了检测。上月，一名女子在福赛斯公园散步时，一名男子从惠特克街附近暗处突然出现，用不明化学液体袭击她。消息人士称，该液体熔穿了受害者的衣物和耳机，造成严重烧伤。目前探员正根据已确认的物质跟进线索，案件仍在发展中。","summary_en":"The FBI confirmed to WTOC that it has identified the chemical used in the Forsyth Park acid attack in Savannah, Georgia, but is not releasing the substance's name to the public at this time. FBI officials said SLED assisted and conducted the testing on the agency's behalf. Last month, a woman walking in Forsyth Park was attacked by a man who emerged from the shadows near Whitaker Street and threw an unknown chemical substance at her. Sources said the liquid melted through her clothing and headphones, leaving severe burns. Agents are following up on leads now that the substance has been identified.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:33:00.847504+00:00","url":"https://www.wtoc.com/2026/01/09/fbi-identifies-chemical-used-forsyth-park-acid-attack","content":"FBI identifies chemical used in Forsyth Park acid attack Photos of the victim before and after an acid attack in Forsyth Park(N/A)By Shea Schrader and Christa RossPublished: Jan. 9, 2026 at 4:46 PM ESTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleSAVANNAH, Ga. (WTOC) - The FBI confirmed to WTOC that they’ve identified the chemical used in the Forsyth Park acid attack.Just last month, a woman was walking around Forsyth Park and a man hiding in the shadows near Whitaker St. suddenly came out and attacked the victim with an unknown chemical substance.Sources close to the investigation say that liquid melted through the victim’s clothing and headphones and left her with severe burns.PREVIOUS COVERAGEWoman critically injured after acid attack at Whitaker St. and W Waldburg St.Over a quarter of a million dollars raised in support of Forsyth Park acid attack victimWoman suffers severe burns in Forsyth Park acid attack; Community concernedSavannah business owner offers $25,000 reward for information in Forsyth Park acid attackFriday the FBI released to WTOC that they now know what that substance was but are not releasing the name of the substance to the public at this time. FBI officials say that SLED assisted and did the testing on behalf of the the organization.Agents are also following up on leads now that the substance has been identified.This is a developing story. Stick with WTOC as we continue to follow new developments.Copyright 2026 WTOC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI确认福赛斯公园酸袭击中使用的化学品\n福赛斯公园遭酸袭击受害者袭击前后的照片（无）\nShea Schrader和Christa Ross\n发布时间：2026年1月9日下午4:46（美国东部时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n佐治亚州萨凡纳（WTOC）——FBI向WTOC确认，他们已经确定了福赛斯公园酸袭击中使用的化学品。\n\n就在上个月，一名女子在福赛斯公园附近行走时，一名躲在惠特克街附近阴影中的男子突然出现，用一种未知化学物质袭击了受害者。\n\n接近调查的人士称，这种液体熔穿了受害者的衣物和耳机，并导致她严重烧伤。\n\n此前报道\n惠特克街与西沃尔德堡街交汇处发生酸袭击，一名女子重伤\n为福赛斯公园酸袭击受害者筹得超过25万美元\n女子在福赛斯公园酸袭击中严重烧伤；社区表示担忧\n萨凡纳企业主悬赏2.5万美元征集福赛斯公园酸袭击线索\n\n周五，FBI向WTOC表示，他们现在已经知道该物质是什么，但目前不会向公众公布该物质的名称。FBI官员称，南卡罗来纳州执法部门（SLED）协助并代表该机构进行了检测。\n\n现在该物质已经被确认，特工们也在跟进相关线索。\n\n这是一起正在发展的事件。WTOC将继续跟进最新进展，请持续关注。\n\n版权所有2026 WTOC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wtoc.com","publish_time":"2026-01-09T21:46:57.911000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-893","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI悬赏最高1万美元征集FCI杰瑟普卫星营地逃犯线索","title_en":"FBI offers reward up to $10,000 for information on escaped prisoner from FCI Jesup’s satellite camp","summary_cn":"佐治亚州杰瑟普联邦惩教所卫星营地一名囚犯阿瑟·科菲尔德于2026年5月26日失踪，美国法警局与联邦调查局等机构介入。FBI亚特兰大分局随后悬赏最高1万美元征集可导致其被捕和定罪的信息，并称其与亚特兰大都会区有关联，应视为持械且危险。科菲尔德因共谋银行欺诈和加重身份盗窃罪服刑。","summary_en":"An inmate, Arthur Cofield, was discovered missing from the satellite camp adjacent to FCI Jesup in Georgia on May 26, 2026. The U.S. Marshals Service, the FBI and other agencies were notified. FBI Atlanta later offered a reward of up to $10,000 for information leading to his capture and conviction, saying he has ties to Metro Atlanta and should be considered armed and dangerous. Cofield was serving a sentence for conspiracy to commit bank fraud and aggravated identity theft.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:07.981297+00:00","url":"https://www.wtoc.com/2026/05/27/man-discovered-missing-fci-jesups-satellite-camp","content":"FBI offers reward up to $10,000 for information on escaped prisoner from FCI Jesup’s satellite camp Officials say inmate walks away from FCI Jesup’s satellite campBy Summer SwansonPublished: May 27, 2026 at 9:33 AM EDT|Updated: Jun. 2, 2026 at 12:38 PM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJESUP, Ga. (WTOC) - [UPDATE 6/1/2026]  FBI Atlanta is offering a reward up to $10,000 for information leading to the capture and conviction of Arthur Cofield. Cofield escaped from Federal Correctional Institute Jesup on Tuesday, May 26, 2026.  He was serving an 11 year and 3-month sentence for Conspiracy to Commit Bank Fraud and Aggravated Identity Theft.  FBI Atlanta is assisting the United States Marshals Service in the case.The FBI said Cofield has ties to Metro Atlanta and that he should be considered armed and dangerous.Anyone with information concerning this case is asked to contact the FBI’s Toll-Free tipline at 1-800-CALL-FBI (1-800-225-5324), you can submit a tip online at tips.fbi.gov . or call the U.S. Marshals Service at 1-877-WANTED2 (926-8332).[ORIGINAL STORY] Tuesday afternoon at approximately 4:30 p.m., a man was discovered missing from the satellite camp adjacent to the Federal Correctional Institution (FCI) Jesup.Arthur Cofield is 34 years old with black hair, brown eyes, is 5’4” tall and weighs approximately 210 pounds. The United States Marshals Service, the Federal Bureau of Investigation, and other law enforcement agencies were notified about the missing inmate. Arthur Cofield(U. S. Department of Justice Federal Bureau of Prisons FCI)An internal investigation has been initiated. Officials said anyone with information about this individual should contact the United States Marshals Service at (912) 429-7169. Cofield was sentenced in the Northern District of Georgia to an aggregate 135-month sentence for Conspiracy to Commit Mail Fraud and Wire Fraud, Conspiracy to Commit Bank Fraud and Aggravated Identity Theft.According to the Federal Bureau of Prisons, the satellite camp at FCI Jesup is a minimum security facility.Copyright 2026 WTOC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI悬赏最高1万美元，征集有关从杰瑟普联邦惩教所卫星营逃跑囚犯的信息 官员称一名囚犯从杰瑟普联邦惩教所卫星营步行逃脱\n作者：Summer Swanson\n发布：2026年5月27日上午9:33（美国东部时间）|更新：2026年6月2日中午12:38（美国东部时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n佐治亚州杰瑟普（WTOC）——【2026年6月1日更新】亚特兰大FBI悬赏最高1万美元，征集能够促成抓捕并定罪Arthur Cofield的信息。Cofield于2026年5月26日星期二从杰瑟普联邦惩教所逃脱。他因共谋实施银行欺诈和加重身份盗窃罪，被判处11年3个月监禁。亚特兰大FBI正在协助美国法警局办理此案。\nFBI称，Cofield与亚特兰大都会区有联系，应被视为携带武器且危险。\n任何掌握此案信息的人，请拨打FBI免费举报热线1-800-CALL-FBI（1-800-225-5324），也可在线提交举报：tips.fbi.gov，或致电美国法警局：1-877-WANTED2（926-8332）。\n\n【原始报道】星期二下午约4点30分，官员发现一名男子从毗邻杰瑟普联邦惩教所（FCI）的卫星营失踪。\nArthur Cofield现年34岁，黑发、棕眼，身高5英尺4英寸，体重约210磅。美国法警局、联邦调查局及其他执法机构已获悉这名囚犯失踪。Arthur Cofield（美国司法部联邦监狱局FCI）\n一项内部调查已经启动。官员表示，任何掌握此人信息的人应联系美国法警局，电话：（912）429-7169。Cofield在佐治亚州北区被判处合计135个月监禁，罪名包括共谋实施邮件欺诈和电信欺诈、共谋实施银行欺诈以及加重身份盗窃。\n据联邦监狱局称，杰瑟普联邦惩教所的卫星营是一所最低安全级别设施。\n版权2026 WTOC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wtoc.com","publish_time":"2026-05-27T13:33:38.168000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-171","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"波特温特沃思警方行动与国土安全部刑事调查有关","title_en":"Port Wentworth police presence tied to Homeland Security criminal investigation","summary_cn":"佐治亚州波特温特沃思官员表示，9月15日晚在沃伦大道出现的大规模执法行动是国土安全调查局执行联邦搜查令的一部分，属于正在进行的联邦刑事调查，而非行政移民调查。当地警方的角色仅限于应联邦当局请求协助外围安保。联邦当局未公布搜查目标或可能指控的更多细节，调查仍在进行中。","summary_en":"Port Wentworth, Georgia, officials said a large law enforcement presence on Warren Drive on the night of Sept. 15 was part of an ongoing federal criminal investigation, with Homeland Security Investigations executing a federal search warrant. Local police assisted only with perimeter security at federal authorities' request. Officials clarified it was not an administrative immigration investigation. No further details on the search target or potential charges were released.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:30:26.481774+00:00","url":"https://www.wtoc.com/2026/09/16/large-law-enforcement-presence-including-department-homeland-security-reported-port-wentworth","content":"Port Wentworth police presence tied to Homeland Security criminal investigationCity officials say the operation was a federal criminal investigation, not an immigration matter; local police assisted with perimeter security.By Christa RossPublished: Sep. 15, 2026 at 9:50 PM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GooglePORT WENTWORTH, Ga. (WTOC) — [UPDATE 09/16/26 AT 3:35 p.m.] Heavy law enforcement activity reported Tuesday night on Warren Drive was part of an ongoing federal criminal investigation, according to Port Wentworth officials.Homeland Security Investigations executed a federal search warrant in the area Tuesday night, drawing a large presence of federal personnel and local officers.A representative for the City of Port Wentworth said the Port Wentworth Police Department’s role was limited to assisting with perimeter security at the request of federal authorities.Officials clarified the operation was a federal criminal investigation and was not an administrative immigration investigation.The matter remains under active investigation by federal authorities. No further details regarding the target of the search warrant or potential charges have been released.[ORIGINAL STORY] A large law enforcement presence, including personnel with the Department of Homeland Security, was reported Tuesday night on Warren Drive in Port Wentworth.WTOC reached out to the City of Port Wentworth and the Port Wentworth Police Department for information. Both agencies referred questions to the Department of Homeland Security.This is a developing story. WTOC is working to learn more and will provide updates as information becomes available.Copyright 2026 WTOC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"波特温特沃斯警方出现在国土安全部刑事调查现场\n市官员表示，此次行动是联邦刑事调查，而非移民事务；当地警方协助进行外围安保。\n作者：Christa Ross\n发布于：2026年9月15日，美国东部时间晚上9:50\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n佐治亚州波特温特沃斯（WTOC）——【更新：2026年9月16日下午3:35】据波特温特沃斯官员称，周二晚间在沃伦大道报告的大规模执法行动是正在进行的联邦刑事调查的一部分。\n国土安全调查局周二晚间在该地区执行了一份联邦搜查令，引来了大量联邦人员和地方警员。\n波特温特沃斯市的一名代表表示，应联邦当局要求，波特温特沃斯警察局的职责仅限于协助外围安保。\n官员澄清说，该行动是联邦刑事调查，并非行政性移民调查。\n联邦当局仍在积极调查此事。关于搜查令目标或可能提出的指控，尚未公布更多细节。\n【原始报道】周二晚间，据报波特温特沃斯沃伦大道出现大批执法人员，其中包括国土安全部人员。\nWTOC联系了波特温特沃斯市和波特温特沃斯警察局以获取信息。两家机构都将问题转交给国土安全部。\n这是一起正在发展的新闻。WTOC正努力了解更多情况，并将在信息 उपलब्ध时提供更新。\n版权所有 2026 WTOC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wtoc.com","publish_time":"2026-09-16T01:50:51.572000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-438","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"哥伦布水务公司遭网络攻击，国土安全主管称供水从未受威胁","title_en":"Columbus Water Works hit by cyberattack, Homeland Security director says water was never at risk","summary_cn":"佐治亚州哥伦布水务公司7月27日遭网络攻击，计算机系统受影响。国土安全与应急管理局局长钱斯·科比特表示，员工迅速转为手动操作并启动应急预案，公共供水从未受到威胁。联邦调查局与佐治亚州应急管理局IT团队正调查攻击来源，尚无法确定是否与其他水系统攻击有关。科比特称事件是“警钟”，预计本周内系统基本恢复。","summary_en":"Columbus Water Works in Georgia is recovering from a cyberattack that hit its computer systems on July 27. Homeland Security and EMA Director Chance Corbett said staff quickly switched to manual operations and activated their emergency plan, and the public water supply was never at risk. The FBI and Georgia Emergency Management Agency IT teams are investigating the source, which remains undetermined. Corbett called the incident a wake-up call and expects nearly all systems restored by week's end.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:56:13.175915+00:00","url":"https://www.wtvm.com/2026/08/04/columbus-water-works-hit-by-cybersecurity-attack-no-threat-public-water-supply","content":"Columbus Water Works hit by cyberattack, Homeland Security director says water was never at riskEMA director calls incident a ‘wake-up call’ as FBI and state cyber teams investigateBy Daniel EthertonPublished: Aug. 4, 2026 at 4:03 PM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleCOLUMBUS, Ga. (WTVM) - Columbus Water Works is still recovering from a cyberattack that hit its computer systems on Monday, July 27, but local emergency officials say the public’s water supply was never in danger.Homeland Security and EMA Director Chance Corbett said staff quickly switched to manual operations and activated their emergency plan after the attack was detected, preventing any disruption to water service.“There was never a threat of loss of water or any of the quality of water,” Corbett said.Investigation underwayThe FBI and Georgia Emergency Management Agency IT teams are working to trace the source of the attack. Corbett said he notified GEMA after Columbus Water Works identified the problem, triggering support from state and federal cyber teams.The source of the attack has not been determined. Corbett said he could not speculate on whether the incident is connected to reported cyberattacks on other water systems, including one in Clayton County near Atlanta where officials cited “unauthorized cyber activity” as the cause of a boil water advisory.The FBI recently issued a nationwide alert warning that malicious cyber actors are targeting devices used by water and wastewater utilities.Operations expected to be restored by end of weekCorbett said Columbus Water Works handled the incident without significant public safety impact.“Columbus Water Works did a great job. Their staff, they enacted their plan, their emergency plan. Plan went well. They did what they needed to do to manage the incident,” Corbett said.The primary disruption for staff was shifting from remote monitoring to on-site checks.“They had to go from whether they were looking at a screen to see what the flow was or what was going on… to actually having to go on site. So a little bit of an interruption for them, but again, they have a great team and they knew what to do,” Corbett said.Corbett said he expects nearly all systems to be fully restored by the end of the week. Columbus Water Works says it is continuing to harden any systems that were found to be vulnerable.A broader warningCorbett said the incident is a reminder that any system connected to the internet is a potential target.“Anybody that’s on the internet is vulnerable. We take actions to mitigate those risks… but you also have to have the plan if it does happen… how do we get past that and get back to normal?” Corbett said.Copyright 2026 WTVM. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"哥伦布供水公司遭网络攻击，国土安全主管称供水从未面临风险\nEMA主管称该事件是一次“警钟”，FBI和州网络团队正在调查\n作者：Daniel Etherton\n发布时间：2026年8月4日美国东部夏令时间下午4:03\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n佐治亚州哥伦布（WTVM）——哥伦布供水公司仍在从7月27日星期一袭击其计算机系统的一次网络攻击中恢复，但当地应急官员表示，公众供水从未处于危险之中。\n国土安全和EMA主任Chance Corbett表示，攻击被发现后，工作人员迅速转为手动操作并启动应急预案，避免了供水服务中断。\n“从未存在断水威胁，也从未存在水质威胁，”Corbett说。\n调查正在进行\nFBI和佐治亚州应急管理局IT团队正在追查攻击来源。Corbett表示，在哥伦布供水公司发现问题后，他通知了GEMA，由此启动州和联邦网络团队的支持。\n攻击来源尚未确定。Corbett表示，他无法推测该事件是否与其他供水系统据报遭遇的网络攻击有关，其中包括亚特兰大附近克莱顿县的一起事件，官员称“未经授权的网络活动”是发布煮沸饮水建议的原因。\nFBI最近发布全国警报，警告恶意网络行为者正瞄准供水和污水处理公用事业使用的设备。\n预计本周末前恢复运行\nCorbett表示，哥伦布供水公司处理此次事件时没有造成重大公共安全影响。\n“哥伦布供水公司做得非常好。他们的员工启动了他们的预案，即应急预案。预案执行得很顺利。他们采取了必要措施来处置事件，”Corbett说。\n对员工而言，主要的干扰是从远程监控转为现场检查。\n“他们不得不从通过屏幕查看流量或了解发生了什么……转为实际上必须到现场。因此这对他们来说有一点中断，但同样地，他们有一支优秀的团队，并且知道该怎么做，”Corbett说。\nCorbett表示，他预计到本周末前，几乎所有系统都将完全恢复。哥伦布供水公司表示，正继续加固任何被发现存在漏洞的系统。\n更广泛的警告\nCorbett表示，该事件提醒人们，任何连接互联网的系统都是潜在目标。\n“任何上网的人都存在脆弱性。我们会采取行动缓解这些风险……但也必须有预案，以便一旦发生这种情况……我们如何渡过难关并恢复正常？”Corbett说。\n版权所有 2026 WTVM。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wtvm.com","publish_time":"2026-08-04T20:03:23.065000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-568","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部长马林以威胁手段推动选举安全倡议","title_en":"DHS Secretary Mullin pushes election security initiative with threats","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部长Markwayne Mullin周五威胁称，若各州和选举官员不遵守特朗普政府的选举安全计划，将面临罚款、处罚和监禁。此前一天特朗普在黄金时段讲话中称美国投票机易受攻击，这些说法已被反复驳斥。马林还提出未经证实的广泛选民欺诈和数十万非法选民投票的说法。由于国会未能通过《SAVE America Act》，部分州如宾夕法尼亚州拒绝交出选民名册。众议院少数党领袖杰弗里斯质疑政府关注该阴谋论。","summary_en":"U.S. Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin threatened states and election officials Friday with fines, penalties and prison time if they do not comply with the Trump administration's election security plan. The warning came a day after President Trump said in a primetime address that U.S. voting machines are vulnerable and easily compromised, claims that have been repeatedly debunked. Mullin also made unsubstantiated claims of widespread voter fraud and hundreds of thousands of illegal voters casting ballots. With Congress failing to pass the SAVE America Act, some states such as Pennsylvania are refusing to turn over voter rolls. House Minority Leader Jeffries questioned the administration's focus on the conspiracy theory.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:48:54.538745+00:00","url":"https://www.wtvy.com/2026/07/17/dhs-secretary-mullin-pushes-election-security-initiative-with-threats","content":"DHS Secretary Mullin pushes election security initiative with threatsHomeland Security chief issues warnings as some states refuse to hand over voter rollsBy Molly MartinezPublished: Jul. 17, 2026 at 5:36 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON (Gray DC) - Secretary of Homeland Security Markwayne Mullin threatened states and election officials Friday with fines, penalties and prison time if they do not comply with the Trump administration’s election security plan.The warning came one day after President Donald Trump said in a primetime address that U.S. voting machines are vulnerable and easily compromised. These are two claims that have been repeatedly debunked.Mullin also made unsubstantiated claims of widespread voter fraud and hundreds of thousands of illegal voters casting ballots.“That should never happen again and because of President Trump’s leadership, we’re not allowing that to happen,” Mullin said.The administration’s push comes amid Congress’ failure to pass the SAVE America Act ahead of the midterms. Democrats have shown no appetite to advance the legislation.House Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries (D-N.Y.) questioned the administration’s focus on the issue.“Why does he continue to focus on a conspiracy theory related to a 2020 presidential election that every rational person in the United States of America knows he lost?” Jeffries said.Some states are already resisting the administration’s demands. Pennsylvania is among those refusing to turn over voter rolls requested by the administration.Copyright 2026 Gray DC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"国土安全部部长穆林以威胁推动选举安全倡议\n一些州拒绝交出选民名册之际，国土安全主管发出警告\n作者：Molly Martinez\n发布时间：2026年7月17日中部夏令时间下午5:36\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n华盛顿（Gray DC）——国土安全部部长马克韦恩·穆林周五威胁各州和选举官员，若不遵守特朗普政府的选举安全计划，将面临罚款、处罚和监禁。\n这一警告发布的前一天，唐纳德·特朗普总统在黄金时段讲话中称，美国投票机存在漏洞且很容易被攻破。这两项说法均已被反复证伪。\n穆林还毫无根据地声称存在广泛的选民欺诈，以及数十万非法选民投下选票。\n“这绝不应该再次发生，而且由于特朗普总统的领导，我们不会让这种事发生，”穆林说。\n政府的推动正值国会未能在中期选举前通过《拯救美国法案》之际。民主党人并未表现出推进该立法的意愿。\n众议院少数党领袖哈基姆·杰弗里斯（纽约州民主党籍）质疑政府对该议题的关注。\n“为什么他继续聚焦于一项与2020年总统选举有关的阴谋论，而美国每一个理性的人都知道他输掉了那场选举？”杰弗里斯说。\n一些州已经在抵制政府的要求。宾夕法尼亚州是拒绝交出政府要求提供的选民名册的州之一。\n版权所有 © 2026 Gray DC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wtvy.com","publish_time":"2026-07-17T22:36:23.040000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1012","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI突查弗吉尼亚州参议员办公室及附近大麻药房","title_en":"FBI raids office of Virginia State Senator, also nearby weed dispensary | wusa9.com","summary_cn":"2026年5月6日，FBI持法院授权的联邦搜查令突查弗吉尼亚州参议员L·路易丝·卢卡斯位于朴茨茅斯的办公室，并搜查其疑似共同经营的大麻药房，缉毒局协助行动。FBI称无公共安全威胁，调查仍在进行。卢卡斯尚未被起诉，州众议院议长斯科特等民主党人质疑行动政治化，共和党参议员里夫斯则称这属于FBI反腐职责。","summary_en":"On May 6, 2026, the FBI executed a court-authorized federal search warrant at the Portsmouth office of Virginia State Senator L. Louise Lucas and also searched a cannabis dispensary she apparently co-owns, with DEA assistance. The FBI said there was no threat to public safety and declined further comment. Lucas has not been charged. Democratic House Speaker Don Scott questioned the politicization of the raid, while Republican Sen. Bryce Reeves said public corruption is within the FBI's remit.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:48:00.157815+00:00","url":"https://www.wusa9.com/article/news/politics/fbi-virginia-state-senator-investigation-raid/65-35beb903-fce7-4682-a6d5-0afd44d990e6","content":"Politics\nFBI raids office of Virginia State Senator, also nearby weed dispensary\nThe FBI is executing a federal search warrant at Virginia State Senator L. Louise Lucas's office.\nTo stream WUSA9 on your phone, you need the WUSA9 app.\nDownload the WUSA9 app\nMore Videos\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nAuthor: Luke Eggleston, Matthew Torres\nPublished: 12:25 PM EDT May 6, 2026\nUpdated: 7:28 PM EDT May 6, 2026\nPORTSMOUTH, Va. — A Virginia State Senator’s office was the target of a Federal Bureau of Investigation raid on Wednesday morning.\nThe FBI told CBS News they were \"executing a court-authorized federal search warrant in Portsmouth, Va.” shortly after reports surfaced that agents were at the office of Virginia State Senator L. Louise Lucas (D-18).\nThis story continues below.\nMore in Politics\nGOP looking to secure $1 billion in funding for new White House ballroom\nSenate votes to block prediction market bets\nDC Mayoral debate wrap up\nAgents were also spotted at a cannabis dispensary that Lucas apparently co-owns near her office.\nThe Drug Enforcement Administration is assisting the FBI, a source told WUSA9.\nLucas released the following statement at 7p.m. on Wednesday:\nCredit: L. Louis Lucas\nSen. Lucas released this statement on social media at 7:01 p.m. on Wednesday after the FBI searched her office and a local cannabis business.\n\"There is no threat to public safety. This is an ongoing investigation and no further information is publicly available at this time,\" an FBI spokesperson adds.\nGov. Abigail Spanberger's office declined to comment, citing the ongoing investigation.\n“The governor is aware of today's law enforcement operation in Portsmouth. In the absence of additional details, the governor will not be commenting on a federal investigation at this time,\" her office said in a statement.\nSpanberger served as an operations officer in the Central Intelligence Agency before embarking on her career in politics.\nLucas, a Democrat, has long been an outspoken critic of President Donald Trump and was an architect in Virginia's efforts to redraw its Congressional districts to be more competitive for Democrats.\nVoters approved the newly redrawn maps in a referendum last month, although they are currently being challenged before the Virginia Supreme Court.\nSpeaker of the Virginia House of Delegates Don Scott — another Democrat — expressed shock.\n\"Lets start with this: Senator L. Louise Lucas has not been charged with anything! I am deeply concerned by today’s FBI raid,\" Scott said. \"Given the politicization of this administration — an FBI led by Kash Patel and a Justice Department run by President Donald Trump’s former personal attorney — I think people should take this with a grain of salt and allow the facts to come out before jumping to conclusions. At this point we simply do not know what this ultimately means. Right now, there is far more theatrics and speculation than actual information available to the public.\"\nLucas currently serves as the President pro tempore of the Virginia State Senate. She is also the chair of the Senate Finance and Appropriations Committee.\n\"Whether it's a Republican or a Democrat, to have something like this happen  is not a good thing and does not bode well for Virginia,\" State Sen. Bryce Reeves, R-Culpeper. \"I don't think this is a political hit at all and this is what the FBI does is public corruption.\"\nReeves, who is a member of the Senate finance committee, questions what it would mean to passing a budget.\n\"I don't think we're going to have a budget anytime soon if she's busy trying to defend herself against the federal government for whatever it is they're investigating her for,\" Reeves added.\nVirginia Senate District 18 includes parts of Chesapeake and Portsmouth.\nClose Ad\nBefore You Leave, Check This Out","content_cn":"政治\nFBI突袭弗吉尼亚州参议员办公室及附近的大麻 dispensary\nFBI正在弗吉尼亚州参议员L. Louise Lucas的办公室执行联邦搜查令。\n要在手机上观看WUSA9直播，您需要WUSA9应用程序。\n下载WUSA9应用程序\n更多视频\n5秒后播放\n此视频的示例标题将在此处显示\n5秒后播放\n此视频的示例标题将在此处显示\n作者：Luke Eggleston、Matthew Torres\n发布时间：2026年5月6日美国东部夏令时间下午12:25\n更新时间：2026年5月6日美国东部夏令时间晚上7:28\n弗吉尼亚州朴次茅斯——周三上午，一名弗吉尼亚州参议员的办公室成为联邦调查局突袭的目标。\nCBS新闻称，报道称特工出现在弗吉尼亚州参议员L. Louise Lucas（民主党，第18选区）的办公室后不久，FBI表示，他们“正在弗吉尼亚州朴次茅斯执行法院授权的联邦搜查令”。\n本文下方继续。\n更多政治新闻\n共和党寻求确保为新的白宫舞厅提供10亿美元资金\n参议院投票阻止预测市场下注\n华盛顿特区市长辩论总结\n有人还看到特工出现在Lucas办公室附近一家她似乎共同拥有的大麻 dispensary。\n一名消息人士告诉WUSA9，缉毒局正在协助FBI。\nLucas于周三晚上7点发布了以下声明：\n图片来源：L. Louis Lucas\n参议员Lucas在FBI搜查其办公室和当地一家大麻企业后，于周三晚上7:01在社交媒体上发布了这份声明。\nFBI发言人补充说：“不存在公共安全威胁。这是一项正在进行的调查，目前没有更多信息可公开。”\n州长Abigail Spanberger的办公室以调查正在进行为由拒绝置评。\n她的办公室在一份声明中说：“州长已获悉今天在朴次茅斯开展的执法行动。在没有更多细节的情况下，州长目前不会对一项联邦调查发表评论。”\nSpanberger在投身政界前曾担任中央情报局行动官员。\nLucas是一名民主党人，长期直言不讳地批评总统Donald Trump，并曾主导弗吉尼亚州重新划分国会选区、使其对民主党更具竞争力的工作。\n选民上月在公投中批准了重新划定的地图，但目前正面临弗吉尼亚州最高法院的挑战。\n弗吉尼亚州众议院议长Don Scott——另一名民主党人——表达了震惊。\nScott说：“先从这一点说起：参议员L. Louise Lucas没有被指控任何事情！我对今天的FBI突袭深感担忧。鉴于本届政府的政治化——由Kash Patel领导的FBI，以及由总统Donald Trump的前私人律师执掌的司法部——我认为人们应对此持保留态度，在仓促下结论前等待事实浮出水面。此时我们根本不知道这最终意味着什么。现在，公众可获得的戏剧性表演和猜测远多于实际信息。”\nLucas目前担任弗吉尼亚州参议院临时议长。她还担任参议院财政与拨款委员会主席。\n“无论是共和党人还是民主党人，发生这样的事情都不是好事，也不利于弗吉尼亚州，”州参议员、库尔佩珀共和党人Bryce Reeves说。“我不认为这完全是政治打击；FBI的职责就是处理公共腐败。”\n身为参议院财政委员会成员的Reeves质疑这将对通过预算意味着什么。\nReeves补充说：“如果她忙于为联邦政府调查她的任何事情进行辩护，我不认为我们很快会有预算。”\n弗吉尼亚州参议院第18选区包括切萨皮克和朴次茅斯的部分地区。\n关闭广告\n离开前，请查看这个","publish_source":"wusa9.com","publish_time":"2026-05-06T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1992","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"安德森县学前班员工接受FBI调查并被停职，学区称","title_en":"Anderson County preschool employee under FBI investigation, suspended, school system says","summary_cn":"田纳西州安德森县学校发言人证实，克林顿市安德森县Head Start学前班一名员工正接受联邦调查局调查，并已被停职。学区向家长发出通知称，FBI确认没有理由认为任何学生受到侵害，调查重点据信在校外活动。学区表示正全力配合联邦执法部门，出于谨慎决定在调查期间停职该员工，并强调学生安全始终是最高优先事项。发言人未透露该员工身份或调查细节。","summary_en":"A spokesperson for Anderson County Schools in Tennessee confirmed that an employee at Anderson County Head Start in Clinton is the subject of an FBI investigation and has been suspended. A note sent to parents said the FBI confirmed there is no reason to believe any students have been victimized, and that the investigation appears focused on activities outside school. The district said it is cooperating fully with federal law enforcement and suspended the employee out of caution while the matter is pending, stressing student safety remains its highest priority. The spokesperson did not identify the employee or provide investigation details.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:42:13.316362+00:00","url":"https://www.wvlt.tv/2025/12/10/anderson-county-preschool-employee-under-fbi-investigation-suspended-school-system-says","content":"Anderson County preschool employee under FBI investigation, suspended, school system says The employee has been suspended from the school they work at: Anderson County Head Start in Clinton. The employee has been suspended from the school they work at: Anderson County Head Start in Clinton.By Camruinn Morgan-RumseyPublished: Dec. 10, 2025 at 11:39 AM ESTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleCLINTON, Tenn. (WVLT) - An Anderson County preschool employee is the center of an FBI investigation, a spokesperson for Anderson County Schools confirmed Wednesday. That employee has also been suspended from the school they work at: Anderson County Head Start in Clinton. According to the spokesperson, Anderson County Schools sent a note to parents explaining the situation. That note said the investigation didn’t involve any children within the school itself. “The FBI confirmed there is no reason to believe any students have been victimized,” the note said. “Their investigation, as we understand it, stands as focused on activities outside of school.”The note to parents also said the school system is prioritizing student safety. “We understand this news may be upsetting and may indeed raise questions,” the note said. “Please know that the safety, wellbeing, and security of our students remains - and will always remain - our highest priority.”The spokesperson did not identify the employee or give details about the investigation. The letter to parents in full is below:We are writing to you regarding a serious matter involving an employee at the Head Start/Pre-K school location in Clinton. As Anderson County Schools was informed, this individual is currently under investigation by the Federal Bureau of Investigation (F.B.I.). As we understand it, that investigation remains ongoing, and our district is cooperating fully with federal law enforcement. Because this is an active investigation though, the district has no additional information to share at this time.But we at Anderson County Schools want to be clear: the FBI confirmed there is no reason to believe any students have been victimized. Their investigation, as we understand it, stands as focused on activities outside of school. Out of an abundance of caution, however, we made the immediate decision to suspend the employee at issue while this matter is pending. We understand this news may be upsetting and may indeed raise questions. Please know that the safety, wellbeing, and security of our students remains - and will always remain - our highest priority. If additional information becomes available and can be shared, we will provide an update as soon as possible.Thank you for your understanding and continued partnership as we work through this matter responsibly and in full coordination and cooperation with law enforcement.Anderson County SchoolsCopyright 2025 WVLT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"安德森县学前教育员工正接受联邦调查，已被停职，学区称\n该员工任职的学校：克林顿的安德森县启蒙计划。该员工任职的学校：克林顿的安德森县启蒙计划。\n作者：Camruinn Morgan-Rumsey\n发表于：2025年12月10日美国东部时间上午11:39\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n田纳西州克林顿（WVLT）——安德森县学校发言人周三证实，一名安德森县学前教育员工正处于联邦调查局调查的中心。该员工也已被其任职学校——克林顿的安德森县启蒙计划——停职。\n\n据发言人称，安德森县学校向家长发送了一份说明情况的通知。通知称，调查不涉及学校内的任何儿童。\n\n通知写道：“联邦调查局确认，没有理由相信任何学生曾遭受侵害。根据我们的了解，他们的调查重点是校外活动。”\n\n给家长的通知还称，学区将学生安全置于首要位置。\n\n通知写道：“我们理解这一消息可能令人不安，也可能确实引发疑问。请知悉，学生的安全、福祉和保障始终——并将永远——是我们的最高优先事项。”\n\n发言人没有透露该员工身份，也没有提供调查细节。以下是致家长信函的全文：\n\n我们写信是想告知您一件涉及克林顿启蒙计划/学前班学校地点一名员工的严重事项。正如安德森县学校获悉的那样，此人目前正接受联邦调查局（F.B.I.）调查。据我们了解，该调查仍在进行中，我们的学区正在与联邦执法部门充分合作。不过，由于这是一起正在进行的调查，学区目前无法提供更多信息。\n\n但安德森县学校希望明确说明：联邦调查局确认，没有理由相信任何学生曾遭受侵害。根据我们的了解，他们的调查重点是校外活动。不过，出于充分谨慎，在此事调查期间，我们立即决定暂停涉事员工的职务。\n\n我们理解这一消息可能令人不安，也可能确实引发疑问。请知悉，学生的安全、福祉和保障始终——并将永远——是我们的最高优先事项。如果有更多信息可供分享，我们将尽快提供更新。\n\n感谢您在我们以负责任的方式、并与执法部门全面协调和合作处理此事期间的理解与持续配合。\n\n安德森县学校\n\n版权所有 2025 WVLT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wvlt.tv","publish_time":"2025-12-10T16:39:25.947000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2955","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔访问克拉克斯堡CJIS部门","title_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel visits Clarksburg CJIS Division","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔于2025年4月17日访问了位于西弗吉尼亚州克拉克斯堡的刑事司法信息服务（CJIS）部门，参议员吉姆·贾斯蒂斯陪同参观。这是帕特尔自被特朗普总统任命以来首次访问该部门。克拉克斯堡CJIS为执法、国家安全与情报机构以及公众提供多种服务。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel visited the Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, West Virginia, on April 17, 2025, accompanied by Senator Jim Justice. This marked Patel's first visit to the Clarksburg CJIS Division since his appointment by President Donald Trump. The Clarksburg CJIS provides a range of services to law enforcement, national security and intelligence agencies, and the general public.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:36:22.859666+00:00","url":"https://www.wvva.com/2025/04/21/fbi-director-kash-patel-visits-clarksburg-cjis-division","content":"FBI Director Kash Patel visits Clarksburg CJIS Division kash at fbi(kash patel)By WDTV News StaffPublished: Apr. 21, 2025 at 4:24 PM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleCLARKSBURG, W.Va (WDTV) - Kash Patel, U.S FBI Director, visited the Clarksburg CJIS (Criminal Justice Information Services) Division on Thursday April 17th.Patel was joined by Senator Jim Justice as he toured the facility.This marks Patel’s first visit to the Clarksburg CJIS Division since his appointment by President Donald Trump.The Clarksburg CJIS provides a range of services to law enforcement, national security and intelligence, and the general public. Copyright 2025 WDTV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI 局长 Kash Patel 访问克拉克斯堡 CJIS 分部\nkash at fbi（kash patel）\nWDTV 新闻工作人员\n发布时间：2025 年 4 月 21 日，美国东部时间下午 4:24\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上设为首选来源\n西弗吉尼亚州克拉克斯堡（WDTV）——美国 FBI 局长 Kash Patel 于 4 月 17 日星期四访问了克拉克斯堡刑事司法信息服务（CJIS）分部。\nPatel 在参议员 Jim Justice 的陪同下参观了该设施。\n这是 Patel 获总统 Donald Trump 任命后首次访问克拉克斯堡 CJIS 分部。\n克拉克斯堡 CJIS 为执法部门、国家安全与情报机构以及公众提供一系列服务。\n版权所有 2025 WDTV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wvva.com","publish_time":"2025-04-21T20:24:02.128000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1495","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长回应劳雷尔县要求调查道格·哈勒斯死亡案的来信","title_en":"FBI director responds to Laurel County letter requesting inquiry into Doug Harless death","summary_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在肯塔基州曼彻斯特出席农村执法活动时，被问及劳雷尔县13名官员致信其与司法部、要求对道格·哈勒斯死亡案展开正式调查一事。帕特尔称对信件无个人了解，但表示FBI有既定程序，会与州和地方当局及司法部合作审查，再决定是否进一步调查。哈勒斯家人称2024年12月警方在其住所执行搜查令时开枪致其死亡，大陪审团未起诉涉事警员。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel, speaking at a rural law enforcement event in Manchester, Kentucky, was asked about a letter from 13 Laurel County officials requesting a formal inquiry into the death of Doug Harless. Patel said he had no personal knowledge of the letter but noted the FBI has a process to review such requests with state and local authorities and the Justice Department before deciding on further inquiry. Harless' family says he was shot by London Police officers serving a search warrant at his home in December 2024; a grand jury declined to indict the officers.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:52:32.225300+00:00","url":"https://www.wymt.com/2026/02/27/fbi-director-responds-laurel-county-letter-requesting-inquiry-into-doug-harless-death","content":"FBI director responds to Laurel County letter requesting inquiry into Doug Harless deathPatel visited Manchester for a rural law enforcement event; Laurel County officials have asked the FBI and DOJ to examine the caseFBI director responds to Laurel County letter requesting inquiry into Doug Harless deathBy Samantha ValentinoPublished: Feb. 27, 2026 at 6:02 PM ESTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleMANCHESTER, Ky. (WKYT) - FBI Director Kash Patel visited Manchester on Friday, joining Congressman Hal Rogers for a law enforcement appreciation luncheon and a panel discussion on rural law enforcement.The visit came after 13 Laurel County elected officials sent a three-page letter to Patel and the U.S. Department of Justice requesting a formal inquiry into the death of Doug Harless.During Patel’s visit, WKYT’s Samantha Valentino asked him whether he’d received the letter from Laurel County officials, and what it would take for the FBI to look into Harless’ case. Patel responds to letterThe meeting with law enforcement was closed to the public, but Patel took questions from reporters afterward. When asked by WKYT’s Samantha Valentino whether he had received the letter, Patel said he did not have personal knowledge of it.“I don’t have personal knowledge of the letter, but I’m sure if it was sent, it was received,” Patel said.Patel said there is a process in place for handling such requests.“What we do with any request or inquiry like that is there’s a process with the FBI to review the matter with our state and local authorities and our partners at the Department of Justice, and then they’ll make a decision on whether or not, based on the facts of the law, any sort of inquiry is further required, and we’ll look at it,” Patel said.Background on the Harless caseHarless’ family says the 63-year-old was asleep inside his Lily home when nearly a dozen London Police officers surrounded it just before midnight on Dec. 23, 2024. Kentucky State Police say London Police were there to serve a search warrant. According to officers, Harless pointed a gun at them, leading them to shoot him.A Laurel County grand jury failed to indict any of the officers involved in Harless’ death.What the letter outlinesThe letter outlines several concerns, including the possibility that officers were at the wrong home that night, that officers were not wearing body cameras, and that London Police were operating outside their typical jurisdiction. The letter also states that the Laurel County Sheriff’s Office was not notified of the operation until after shots were fired.County leaders say the decision not to indict any officers has left their community with fear and uncertainty. The letter asks the FBI and DOJ to determine whether Harless’ civil rights were violated.Community members seek federal actionJeremy Hicks, a regular at Justice for Doug protests, traveled to Manchester hoping Patel would see his sign.“Maybe a higher power can see Doug Harless’ name so we can get justice for him, accountability, transparency,” Hicks said.Hicks said he did not know Harless personally but often carries a weedeater bearing Harless’ photo. Repeated open records requests by WKYT Investigates for a copy of the warrant officers were attempting to serve the night Harless was killed have been denied. However, court records say the warrant was tied to stolen lawn equipment, including a weedeater.“Everybody will see the weedeater and associate it with justice for Doug and the wrongful death of Doug Harless,” Hicks said.Copyright 2026 WKYT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局局长回应劳雷尔县要求调查 Doug Harless 死亡事件的信件\nPatel 到访曼彻斯特参加农村执法活动；劳雷尔县官员已要求 FBI 和司法部审查此案\n联邦调查局局长回应劳雷尔县要求调查 Doug Harless 死亡事件的信件\n作者：Samantha Valentino\n发布时间：2026年2月27日美国东部时间下午6:02\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n将其添加为 Google 首选来源\n肯塔基州曼彻斯特（WKYT）——联邦调查局局长 Kash Patel 周五到访曼彻斯特，与国会议员 Hal Rogers 一同参加执法致谢午宴及农村执法专题讨论会。\n此次访问发生在劳雷尔县13名民选官员向 Patel 及美国司法部寄出一封三页信函之后；信中要求就 Doug Harless 的死亡展开正式调查。\n在 Patel 到访期间，WKYT 的 Samantha Valentino 询问他是否收到劳雷尔县官员的信，以及 FBI 需要满足什么条件才会调查 Harless 的案件。\nPatel 回应信件\n这场与执法部门的会议不对公众开放，但 Patel 随后接受了记者提问。当 WKYT 的 Samantha Valentino 问及他是否收到了该信件时，Patel 表示他对此没有个人了解。\nPatel 表示：“我对这封信没有个人了解，但我相信如果它已寄出，就已经收到。”\nPatel 称，处理此类请求已有既定程序。\nPatel 表示：“对于任何此类请求或问询，我们都会通过 FBI 的程序，与州和地方当局及司法部的合作伙伴共同审查此事；然后他们会根据法律事实决定是否需要进一步开展任何形式的调查，我们会对此进行审视。”\nHarless 案背景\nHarless 的家人表示，2024年12月23日午夜前不久，63岁的 Harless 正在他位于 Lily 的家中睡觉，近12名伦敦警察局警员包围了该住宅。肯塔基州警察称，伦敦警察当时是前往执行搜查令。警员称，Harless 用枪指向他们，导致他们向他开枪。\n劳雷尔县大陪审团未对任何涉入 Harless 死亡事件的警员提出起诉。\n信函概述的内容\n信函列出了多项担忧，包括警员当晚可能到了错误的住宅、警员未佩戴执法记录仪，以及伦敦警察局在其通常管辖范围外行动。信中还称，劳雷尔县警长办公室直到枪声响起后才获知此次行动。\n县领导人称，不起诉任何警员的决定使社区感到恐惧和不确定。信函要求 FBI 和司法部确定 Harless 的公民权利是否遭到侵犯。\n社区成员寻求联邦行动\n常参加“为 Doug 寻求正义”抗议活动的 Jeremy Hicks 前往曼彻斯特，希望 Patel 能看到他的标语。\nHicks 表示：“也许更高层的力量能看到 Doug Harless 的名字，让我们为他争取正义、问责和透明度。”\nHicks 表示，他并不认识 Harless，但经常携带一台印有 Harless 照片的割草机。WKYT Investigates 多次依据公开记录提出请求，索取警员在 Harless 遇害当晚试图执行的搜查令副本，均遭拒绝。不过，法庭记录称，该搜查令涉及被盗园艺设备，包括一台割草机。\nHicks 表示：“所有人都会看到这台割草机，并将其与为 Doug 伸张正义及 Doug Harless 的非正常死亡联系起来。”\n版权所有 2026 WKYT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wymt.com","publish_time":"2026-02-27T23:02:38.579000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-973","ktid":1001210,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001210","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"问答节目——布鲁金斯-美国企业研究所美国农村繁荣委员会","title_en":"Issues and Answers - Brookings-AEI Commission on U.S. Rural Prosperity","summary_cn":"由前参议员海蒂·海特坎普和前州长克里斯·苏努努领导的布鲁金斯-美国企业研究所美国农村繁荣委员会，将于本周在肯塔基州东部举行实地听证会，主题为“阿巴拉契亚农村的经济机遇与公民复兴”。活动在哈泽德和曼彻斯特举行。5月13日将在哈泽德社区与技术学院举办90分钟专家小组讨论，涉及就业创造、劳动力发展、人工智能和再培训等议题。","summary_en":"The Brookings-AEI Commission on U.S. Rural Prosperity, led by former Senator Heidi Heitkamp and former Governor Chris Sununu, will hold a field hearing in eastern Kentucky this week titled 'Economic Opportunity and Civic Renaissance in Rural Appalachia.' Sessions take place in Hazard and Manchester. On May 13, a 90-minute expert panel at Hazard Community and Technical College will discuss job creation, workforce development, AI, and reskilling.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:30:54.009818+00:00","url":"https://www.wymt.com/2026/05/12/issues-answers-brookings-aei-commission-us-rural-prosperity","content":"Issues and Answers - Brookings-AEI Commission on U.S. Rural ProsperityIssues and Answers - Brookings-AEI Commission on U.S. Rural ProsperityBy Steve HensleyPublished: May 12, 2026 at 3:09 AM EDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleHAZARD, Ky. (WYMT) - A bipartisan commission focused on rural prosperity will hold a field hearing in eastern Kentucky this week to discuss various issues in Appalachia.The Brookings-AEI Commission on U.S. Rural Prosperity, led by former U.S. Senator Heidi Heitkamp (D-North Dakota) and former Governor Chris Sununu (R-New Hampshire), will host a two-day event titled “Economic Opportunity and Civic Renaissance in Rural Appalachia.” The sessions will take place in Hazard and Manchester.On Wednesday, May 13, from 4:00 to 5:30 p.m., the Commission will host a 90-minute expert panel session to discuss job creation and attraction, workforce development, AI, and reskilling at Hazard Community and Technical College. Heitkamp and Sununu will moderate the discussion, which is open to the public.Former Senator Heitkamp and Former Governor Sununu are WYMT anchor/managing editor Steve Hensley’s guests on Issues and Answers.Copyright 2026 WYMT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"议题与解答——布鲁金斯学会—美国企业研究所美国农村繁荣委员会议题与解答——布鲁金斯学会—美国企业研究所美国农村繁荣委员会\n作者：Steve Hensley\n发布时间：2026年5月12日美国东部夏令时间上午3:09\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n\n肯塔基州哈泽德（WYMT）——一个关注农村繁荣的两党委员会将于本周在肯塔基州东部举行实地听证会，讨论阿巴拉契亚地区的各种议题。\n\n由前美国参议员海迪·海特坎普（民主党，北达科他州）和前州长克里斯·苏努努（共和党，新罕布什尔州）领导的布鲁金斯学会—美国企业研究所美国农村繁荣委员会，将举办一场为期两天、题为“阿巴拉契亚农村的经济机会与公民复兴”的活动。会议将在哈泽德和曼彻斯特举行。\n\n5月13日星期三下午4:00至5:30，委员会将在哈泽德社区与技术学院举办一场90分钟的专家小组会议，讨论就业岗位创造与吸引、劳动力发展、人工智能和技能再培训。海特坎普和苏努努将主持这场向公众开放的讨论。\n\n前参议员海特坎普和前州长苏努努是 WYMT 主播兼执行编辑 Steve Hensley 在《议题与解答》节目中的嘉宾。\n\n版权所有 © 2026 WYMT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"wymt.com","publish_time":"2026-05-12T07:09:54.484000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2707","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"大谷州立大学聘请FBI资深探员丹尼尔·林斯特伦担任新任警察局长","title_en":"GVSU hires FBI veteran Daniel Lindstrom as new police chief | wzzm13.com","summary_cn":"大谷州立大学宣布聘请拥有20年联邦调查局（FBI）工作经验的丹尼尔·林斯特伦担任公共安全主任兼警察局长，他将于8月上任，成为该部门56年历史上第七任局长。林斯特伦此前在洛杉矶担任FBI助理特别探员主管，负责调查、危机管理和合规监督，还曾担任FBI校园安全项目经理，为全美约3000所高校制定威胁缓解措施。他拥有威斯康星大学法学院法学学位和弗吉尼亚联邦大学教育学博士学位。","summary_en":"Grand Valley State University announced it has hired Daniel Lindstrom, a 20-year FBI veteran, as its new director of public safety and police chief following a nationwide search. Lindstrom, who will become the seventh chief in the department's 56-year history when he assumes duties in August, most recently served as assistant special agent in charge with the FBI in Los Angeles, handling investigations, crisis management and compliance oversight. He previously served as an FBI campus security program manager, developing national regulatory compliance measures and leading threat-mitigation efforts for around 3,000 higher education institutions nationwide.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:11:17.549740+00:00","url":"https://www.wzzm13.com/article/news/local/grand-valley-state-names-new-police-chief-daniel-lindstrom/69-1a1420ad-d7a2-4a7a-8207-9894cffbb378","content":"Local News\nGrand Valley State names new police chief\nGrand Valley State University names Daniel Lindstrom as its new director of public safety and police chief.\nCredit: GVSU\nDaniel Lindstrom named as new Grand Valley State University Police Chief\nAuthor: Riley Mack\nPublished: 10:12 AM EDT June 23, 2025\nUpdated: 10:12 AM EDT June 23, 2025\nALLENDALE, Mich. — Grand Valley State University announced Tuesday that it has hired Daniel Lindstrom, a 20-year FBI veteran, as its new director of public safety and police chief following a nationwide search.\nLindstrom will become the seventh chief in the department's 56-year history when he assumes his duties in August.\nHe comes to GVSU from Los Angeles, where he most recently served as assistant special agent in charge with the Federal Bureau of Investigation.\nThe new chief will oversee safety operations across all GVSU locations, including the main Valley Campus in Allendale, the City Campus in Grand Rapids and regional campuses throughout Michigan.\nLindstrom was the assistant special agent in charge during his time in the FBI. He handled investigations, crisis management and compliance oversight.\nPrior to that role, Lindstrom served as a campus security program manager with the FBI, where he developed national regulatory compliance measures for campus safety practices.\nHe led threat-mitigation efforts for around 3,000 higher education institutions nationwide and created specialized protocols and training programs designed specifically for academic environments.\n\"Special Agent Lindstrom has an extensive and varied law enforcement background with the Federal Bureau of Investigation and will bring tremendous interagency experience and perspectives to the Grand Valley Police Department,\" said Greg Sanial, GVSU's vice president for Finance and Administration.\nSanial praised Lindstrom's performance during the interview process, noting his \"thoughtful approach and professional insight.\"\nBeyond his law enforcement experience, Lindstrom holds a law degree from the University of Wisconsin Law School and an Education Doctorate from Virginia Commonwealth University.\n\"I'm honored to join Grand Valley State University as director of public safety and police chief,\" Lindstrom said in a statement. \"After a rewarding career with the Federal Bureau of Investigation, I'm excited to continue serving others and contributing to the safety and well-being of the GVSU community.\"\nLindstrom also expressed enthusiasm about relocating to the area, saying he looks forward to getting to know the greater Grand Rapids region.\nClose Ad\nTo stream 13OYS on your phone, you need the 13OYS app.\nDownload the 13OYS app\nMore Videos\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nIn Other News\nFull list of events in West Michigan this weekend\nBefore You Leave, Check This Out","content_cn":"本地新闻\n大峡谷州立大学任命新警察局长\n大峡谷州立大学任命丹尼尔·林德斯特罗姆为新任公共安全主管兼警察局长。\n图片来源：GVSU\n丹尼尔·林德斯特罗姆被任命为大峡谷州立大学新警察局长\n作者：莱利·麦克\n发布：2025年6月23日 美国东部夏令时间上午10:12\n更新：2025年6月23日 美国东部夏令时间上午10:12\n密歇根州阿伦代尔——大峡谷州立大学周二宣布，经过全国范围的遴选，聘用了拥有20年FBI资历的丹尼尔·林德斯特罗姆，担任新任公共安全主管兼警察局长。\n林德斯特罗姆将于8月上任，成为该部门56年历史上的第七任局长。\n他从洛杉矶来到GVSU，最近担任联邦调查局助理特别探员主管。\n这位新局长将监督GVSU所有地点的安全运营，包括阿伦代尔的主校区谷地校园、格兰德拉皮兹的城市校园，以及密歇根州各地的区域校区。\n林德斯特罗姆在FBI任职期间担任助理特别探员主管，负责调查、危机管理和合规监督。\n在此之前，林德斯特罗姆曾任FBI校园安全项目经理，制定了针对校园安全实践的全国监管合规措施。\n他领导了面向全国约3,000所高等教育机构的威胁缓解工作，并为学术环境专门制定了规程和培训计划。\n“林德斯特罗姆特别探员拥有在联邦调查局长期且多样的执法背景，将为大峡谷警察局带来卓越的跨机构经验与视角，”GVSU负责财务和行政事务的副校长格雷格·萨尼亚尔说。\n萨尼亚尔称赞了林德斯特罗姆在面试过程中的表现，并指出其“深思熟虑的方法和专业洞见”。\n除执法经历外，林德斯特罗姆还拥有威斯康星大学法学院的法学学位，以及弗吉尼亚联邦大学的教育学博士学位。\n“我很荣幸加入大峡谷州立大学，担任公共安全主管兼警察局长，”林德斯特罗姆在一份声明中说。“在联邦调查局度过一段收获颇丰的职业生涯后，我很高兴继续服务他人，并为GVSU社区的安全与福祉作出贡献。”\n林德斯特罗姆还表达了对搬到该地区的热情，称他期待了解大格兰德拉皮兹地区。\n关闭广告\n要在手机上观看13OYS，您需要13OYS应用程序。\n下载13OYS应用程序\n更多视频\n5秒后播放下一条\n此视频的示例标题将显示在这里\n5秒后播放下一条\n此视频的示例标题将显示在这里\n其他新闻\n本周末西密歇根州活动完整清单\n离开前，看看这个","publish_source":"wzzm13.com","publish_time":"2025-06-23T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1705","ktid":1000490,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000490","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"视频：杨参议员在CSIS活动上讨论与中国的全球技术竞争","title_en":"VIDEO: Young Discusses Global Technology Competition with China During CSIS Event - Senator Young","summary_cn":"美国印第安纳州共和党参议员托德·杨参加了战略与国际研究中心（CSIS）主办的一场活动，主题为美国技术领导力的未来。讨论涉及保障关键供应链、现代化美国工业基础以及确保美国在与中国的全球技术竞争中获胜等联邦政策。活动完整视频可通过链接观看。","summary_en":"U.S. Senator Todd Young (R-Ind.) participated in an event hosted by the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) focused on the future of American technology leadership. The discussion explored federal policies to secure critical supply chains, modernize America's industrial base, and ensure the United States wins the global technology competition with China. Full video of the event is available via a link.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:44:12.755094+00:00","url":"https://www.young.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/video-young-discusses-global-technology-competition-with-china-during-csis-event","content":"Newsroom Press Releases\nJanuary 28, 2026\nVIDEO: Young Discusses Global Technology Competition with China During CSIS Event\n**Click here or above to watch the video.**\nWASHINGTON – Today, Senator Todd Young (R-Ind.) participated in an event hosted by the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) focused on the future of American technology leadership. The discussion explored federal policies to secure critical supply chains, modernize America’s industrial base, and ensure the United States wins the global technology competition with China.\nFull video of the event is available here.\nPrint\nShare\nLike\nTweet\nPrevPrevious Article\nNext ArticleNext","content_cn":"新闻发布室新闻稿\n2026年1月28日\n视频：扬在CSIS活动期间讨论与中国的全球技术竞争\n**点击此处或上方观看视频。**\n华盛顿——今天，联邦参议员托德·扬（印第安纳州共和党人）参加了战略与国际研究中心（CSIS）主办的一场活动，活动聚焦美国技术领导地位的未来。讨论探讨了保障关键供应链、实现美国工业基础现代化，以及确保美国在与中国的全球技术竞争中获胜的联邦政策。\n活动完整视频可在此处观看。\n打印\n分享\n点赞\n推文\n上一页上一篇文章\n下一篇文章下一页","publish_source":"young.senate.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-28T22:03:42+00:00"}},{"id":"news-674","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS + Yahoo title resolution via Reader","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"身份安全能否成为CrowdStrike的主要增长引擎？","title_en":"Can Identity Security Become a Major Growth Driver for CrowdStrike? - June 30, 2026 - Zacks.com","summary_cn":"文章分析CrowdStrike身份安全业务增长潜力。Falcon Shield年度经常性收入同比增长近四倍，特权访问产品和收购的SGNL早期需求强劲。一家美国大型医疗企业以七位数交易扩展部署Falcon Next-Gen Identity和SGNL，以管控AI代理访问权限。文章还对比Palo Alto Networks和SentinelOne表现，并指出CRWD估值偏高、Zacks评级为卖出。","summary_en":"The article examines whether identity security can become a major growth driver for CrowdStrike. Falcon Shield ARR grew nearly fourfold year over year, with strong early demand for Privileged Access products and the acquired SGNL. A large U.S. healthcare company expanded its deployment with Falcon Next-Gen Identity and SGNL in a seven-figure deal to control AI agent access. It also compares Palo Alto Networks and SentinelOne, noting CRWD's premium valuation and Zacks Rank #4 (Sell).","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T05:52:54.658542+00:00","url":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/2945407/can-identity-security-become-a-major-growth-driver-for-crowdstrike","content":"Read MoreHide Full Article\nKey Takeaways CrowdStrike saw Falcon Shield ARR grow nearly fourfold year over year in Q1 fiscal 2027.CRWD's Privileged Access products and SGNL are seeing strong early demand for AI identities.A seven-figure healthcare deal added Falcon Next-Gen Identity and SGNL to secure AI agent access.\nCrowdStrike (CRWD Quick QuoteCRWD - Free Report) is expanding its identity security business as more companies deploy AI across their operations. As AI agents gain access to enterprise applications and data, companies need tools to control what these agents can access and what actions they can perform. This is creating the demand for identity security solutions.CrowdStrike is addressing this opportunity through Falcon Shield, Falcon Next-Gen Identity and SGNL, which it acquired in the first quarter of fiscal 2027. Falcon Shield’s ending annual recurring revenues (ARR) grew nearly four times year over year during the first quarter. Management also stated that its SGNL and Privileged Access products are seeing strong early demand as customers look to secure AI agents and other non-human identities.The company is already winning new business. During the first quarter, a large U.S. healthcare company expanded its deployment by purchasing Falcon Next-Gen Identity and SGNL in a seven-figure deal. The customer wanted to control what AI agents could access across the organization. SGNL's ability to allow companies to set access policies and manage permissions for both employees and AI agents in real time should further boost the demand for CRWD's identity security business.Identity security is becoming an important part of CrowdStrike's platform strategy. As customers add identity, cloud security, SIEM and endpoint security to the Falcon platform, CrowdStrike can increase spending from existing customers. Further, with more companies deploying AI across their businesses, the need to secure AI identities should continue to increase. The above-mentioned shows how identity security is becoming a key growth opportunity for CrowdStrike.The Zacks Consensus Estimate for fiscal 2027 and 2028 revenues indicates a year-over-year increase of around 23.5% and 21.6%, respectively.How Competitors Fare Against CRWDCompetitors like Palo Alto Networks (PANW Quick QuotePANW - Free Report) and SentinelOne (S Quick QuoteS - Free Report) are also gaining ground through platform expansion and AI innovation.In the third quarter of fiscal 2026, Palo Alto Networks saw robust growth in its Next-Gen Security ARR, which increased 60% year over year. The growth was driven by increased customer adoption of PANW’s advanced cybersecurity offerings, including its AI-driven XSIAM platform, SASE and software firewalls.Though comparatively a small competitor, SentinelOne posted first-quarter fiscal 2027 year-over-year growth of 23% in its ARR. The growth was fueled by the rising adoption of SentinelOne’s AI-first Singularity platform and Purple AI.CRWD’s Price Performance, Valuation and EstimatesShares of CrowdStrike have jumped 58.7% in the year-to-date period compared with the Zacks Security industry’s return of 49.8%.CRWD YTD Price Return PerformanceImage Source: Zacks Investment ResearchFrom a valuation standpoint, CrowdStrike trades at a forward price-to-sales ratio of 29.25, significantly higher than the industry’s average of 16.34. The Zacks Value Score of F also suggests that CRWD stock is overvalued.CRWD Forward 12-Month P/S RatioImage Source: Zacks Investment ResearchThe Zacks Consensus Estimate for CrowdStrike’s fiscal 2027 and 2028 earnings indicates year-over-year growth of 32.2% and 26.9%, respectively. The estimates for fiscal 2027 and 2028 have been revised upward by 8 cents and 10 cents, respectively, over the past 30 days.Image Source: Zacks Investment ResearchCrowdStrike currently carries a Zacks Rank #4 (Sell).You can see the complete list of today’s Zacks #1 Rank (Strong Buy) stocks here.","content_cn":"阅读更多隐藏完整文章\n要点 CrowdStrike 在2027财年第一季度的 Falcon Shield 年度经常性收入（ARR）同比增长近四倍。CRWD 的特权访问产品和 SGNL 对 AI 身份的早期需求强劲。一家医疗保健企业以七位数金额购买 Falcon 下一代身份和 SGNL，以保护 AI 代理访问。\n随着越来越多企业在运营中部署 AI，CrowdStrike（CRWD 快速报价 CRWD—免费报告）正在扩展其身份安全业务。随着 AI 代理获得企业应用程序和数据的访问权限，企业需要能够控制这些代理可以访问什么以及可以执行哪些操作的工具。这正在创造对身份安全解决方案的需求。CrowdStrike 通过 Falcon Shield、Falcon 下一代身份和 SGNL 应对这一机遇；SGNL 于2027财年第一季度被其收购。第一季度期间，Falcon Shield 的期末年度经常性收入（ARR）同比增长近四倍。管理层还表示，随着客户寻求保护 AI 代理和其他非人类身份，其 SGNL 和特权访问产品的早期需求强劲。公司已经赢得新业务。第一季度，一家大型美国医疗保健公司通过一项七位数金额的交易扩大部署，购买了 Falcon 下一代身份和 SGNL。该客户希望控制 AI 代理在整个组织中可以访问的内容。SGNL 能够让企业实时为员工和 AI 代理设置访问政策并管理权限，这应进一步推动对 CRWD 身份安全业务的需求。身份安全正成为 CrowdStrike 平台战略的重要组成部分。随着客户将身份、云安全、SIEM 和端点安全加入 Falcon 平台，CrowdStrike 可以增加现有客户的支出。此外，随着越来越多公司在业务中部署 AI，保护 AI 身份的需求应继续增加。上述情况表明，身份安全正成为 CrowdStrike 的关键增长机遇。Zacks 对2027财年和2028财年收入的一致预期显示，同比将分别增长约23.5%和21.6%。\n竞争对手与 CRWD 的表现\nPalo Alto Networks（PANW 快速报价 PANW—免费报告）和 SentinelOne（S 快速报价 S—免费报告）等竞争对手也通过平台扩展和 AI 创新取得进展。在2026财年第三季度，Palo Alto Networks 的下一代安全 ARR 强劲增长，同比增长60%。增长由客户对 PANW 高级网络安全产品的采用增加推动，其中包括由 AI 驱动的 XSIAM 平台、SASE 和软件防火墙。SentinelOne 虽然规模相对较小，但2027财年第一季度 ARR 同比增长23%。增长得益于客户对 SentinelOne 以 AI 为先的 Singularity 平台和 Purple AI 的采用上升。\nCRWD 的价格表现、估值和预期\nCrowdStrike 股价年初至今上涨58.7%，而 Zacks 安全行业回报率为49.8%。\nCRWD 年初至今价格回报表现\n图片来源：Zacks Investment Research\n从估值角度看，CrowdStrike 的远期市销率为29.25，显著高于行业平均的16.34。Zacks 价值评分为 F，也表明 CRWD 股票估值过高。\nCRWD 远期12个月市销率\n图片来源：Zacks Investment Research\nZacks 对 CrowdStrike 2027财年和2028财年盈利的一致预期显示，同比将分别增长32.2%和26.9%。过去30天内，2027财年和2028财年的预期分别上调了8美分和10美分。\n图片来源：Zacks Investment Research\nCrowdStrike 目前的 Zacks 排名为第4名（卖出）。\n你可以在这里查看今天 Zacks 排名第1（强力买入）股票的完整名单。","publish_source":"zacks.com","publish_time":"2026-06-30T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-321","ktid":2575920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"2575920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"霍尼韦尔技术能否在成本压力下提升利润率表现？","title_en":"Can Honeywell Technologies Boost Margin Performance Amid Cost Pressures? - August 26, 2026 - Zacks.com","summary_cn":"Zacks文章分析霍尼韦尔技术（HON）在成本压力下的利润率前景。2026年第二季度，公司销售总成本同比增7.2%至60.7亿美元，研发费用增14.2%至5.24亿美元，独立霍尼韦尔技术营业利润率下降50个基点至12.8%。但2026年6月分拆航空航天业务后，公司成为纯自动化企业，并完成仓储及生产力解决方案业务剥离，预计2026年分部利润率20.1%-20.5%，同比提升250-290个基点。文章还对比了3M和艾默生的成本与利润率表现，并指出HON股价过去一个月下跌12.2%，估值高于行业平均，Zacks评级为强力卖出。","summary_en":"Zacks analyzes Honeywell Technologies' (HON) margin outlook amid cost pressures. In Q2 2026, total cost of sales rose 7.2% year over year to $6.07 billion, R&D expenses jumped 14.2% to $524 million, and standalone Honeywell Technologies' operating margin fell 50 basis points to 12.8%. However, after separating Aerospace in June 2026, the company became a pure-play automation firm and completed divestitures of warehouse and workflow solutions and productivity solutions businesses. It expects a 2026 segment margin of 20.1%-20.5%, up 250-290 basis points year over year. The article also compares cost and margin performance with 3M and Emerson, noting HON shares fell 12.2% in the past month, trade above industry average valuation, and carry a Zacks Rank #5 (Strong Sell).","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:36:02.914497+00:00","url":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/2980526/can-honeywell-technologies-boost-margin-performance-amid-cost-pressures","content":"Read MoreHide Full Article\nKey Takeaways Honeywell Technologies' Q2 operating margin fell 50 bps to 12.8% as material and labor costs rose.Honeywell Technologies became a pure-play automation company after separating Aerospace in June 2026.HON expects a 20.1-20.5% segment margin in 2026, up 250-290 basis points year over year.\nHoneywell Technologies (HON Quick QuoteHON - Free Report) has been dealing with the adverse impacts of high operating costs and expenses. On a consolidated basis, the company’s total cost of sales, comprising the cost of products and services sold, was up 7.2% year over year to $6.07 billion in the second quarter of 2026.Research and development expenses surged 14.2% year over year to $524 million, while interest and other financial charges increased 10.3% to $363 million in the same period. HON incurred high costs and expenses related to rising direct and indirect material costs and increased labor costs. For standalone Honeywell Technologies, operating margin declined 50 basis points to 12.8% in the second quarter. Escalating expenses, if not controlled, are likely to hurt the company’s bottom line in the quarters ahead.However, with the separation of the Aerospace business, Honeywell Technologies started operating as a premier pure-play automation company in June 2026. Also, the company completed the divestiture of its warehouse and workflow solutions and productivity solutions and services businesses. These strategic initiatives, along with tailwinds from stranded costs elimination, are expected to support its margin performance and operational efficiency.For 2026, Honeywell Technologies expects a segment margin of 20.1-20.5%, indicating an increase of 250-290 basis points on a year-over-year basis.Peer’s Margin performanceAmong its major peers, 3M Company (MMM Quick QuoteMMM - Free Report) is facing cost pressure. In second-quarter 2026, its total costs increased 4.7% year over year to $3.82 billion, while the metric, as a percentage of total revenues, climbed 120 basis points to reach 58.7%. Research, development and related expenses increased 4.9% year over year to $302 million.Emerson Electric Co.’s (EMR Quick QuoteEMR - Free Report) cost of sales increased 2.7% year over year in the third quarter of fiscal 2026 (ended June 2026). Emerson’s selling, general and administrative expenses increased 6.1% year over year. Despite the increase in costs, Emerson’s adjusted segment EBITA margin improved 140 basis points to 28.5%, as price-cost actions and cost reductions offset inflationary impact.The Zacks Rundown for HONShares of Honeywell Technologies have lost 12.2% in the past month compared with the industry’s decline of 0.7%.Image Source: Zacks Investment ResearchFrom a valuation standpoint, HON is trading at a forward price-to-earnings ratio of 22.85X, above the industry average of 15.48X. HON carries a Value Score of F.Image Source: Zacks Investment ResearchThe Zacks Consensus Estimate for Honeywell Technologies’ earnings for 2026 and 2027 has declined in the past 60 days.Image Source: Zacks Investment ResearchHON stock currently carries a Zacks Rank #5 (Strong Sell).You can see the complete list of today’s Zacks #1 Rank (Strong Buy) stocks here.","content_cn":"阅读更多隐藏全文\n要点 Honeywell Technologies第二季度营业利润率下降50个基点至12.8%，原因是材料和劳动力成本上升。Honeywell Technologies于2026年6月分拆航空航天业务后，成为一家纯自动化公司。HON预计2026年分部利润率为20.1%-20.5%，同比上升250-290个基点。\nHoneywell Technologies（HON 快速报价HON—免费报告）一直受到高运营成本和费用不利影响的困扰。按合并口径计算，公司销售成本（包括已售产品和服务成本）在2026年第二季度同比增长7.2%，达到60.7亿美元。研发费用同比飙升14.2%，达到5.24亿美元；同期利息及其他财务费用增长10.3%，达到3.63亿美元。HON因直接和间接材料成本上升以及劳动力成本增加而产生了高额成本和费用。对独立运营的Honeywell Technologies而言，第二季度营业利润率下降50个基点至12.8%。如果不加以控制，不断上升的费用可能会在未来几个季度损害公司的利润。不过，随着航空航天业务分拆，Honeywell Technologies于2026年6月开始作为一家领先的纯自动化公司运营。此外，公司完成了仓储与工作流解决方案以及生产力解决方案和服务业务的剥离。这些战略举措，加上消除分拆遗留成本带来的顺风，预计将支持其利润率表现和运营效率。\nHoneywell Technologies预计2026年分部利润率为20.1%-20.5%，意味着同比上升250-290个基点。\n同行利润率表现\n在主要同行中，3M公司（MMM 快速报价MMM—免费报告）正面临成本压力。2026年第二季度，其总成本同比增加4.7%，达到38.2亿美元；该指标占总收入的比例上升120个基点，达到58.7%。研发及相关费用同比增加4.9%，达到3.02亿美元。\n艾默生电气公司（EMR 快速报价EMR—免费报告）2026财年第三季度（截至2026年6月）销售成本同比增长2.7%。艾默生的销售、一般及行政费用同比增长6.1%。尽管成本增加，艾默生调整后分部EBITA利润率仍提高140个基点至28.5%，因为价格—成本措施和成本削减抵消了通胀影响。\nZacks对HON的简评\nHoneywell Technologies股价过去一个月下跌12.2%，而行业跌幅为0.7%。图片来源：Zacks Investment Research从估值角度看，HON的远期市盈率为22.85倍，高于行业平均的15.48倍。HON的价值评分为F。图片来源：Zacks Investment Research过去60天，Zacks对Honeywell Technologies 2026年和2027年盈利的共识预期已下调。图片来源：Zacks Investment ResearchHON股票目前的Zacks评级为5级（强力卖出）。你可以在这里查看今日Zacks排名第一（强力买入）的股票完整名单。","publish_source":"zacks.com","publish_time":"2026-08-26T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-474","ktid":1056514,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056514","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"摩根大通预计7月政策会议后美联储将于12月加息","title_en":"JP Morgan sees December Fed rate hike after July policy meeting | ZAWYA","summary_cn":"据ZAWYA转载路透社报道，摩根大通在周三发布的报告中预计，在美国联邦储备委员会7月会议决定维持政策利率不变后，美联储将于12月加息25个基点。此前该机构预计美联储今年全年将按兵不动，下一次加息要到2027年下半年。报道未提及更多政策细节。","summary_en":"Citing a Reuters report carried by ZAWYA, J.P. Morgan said in a Wednesday note that it expects the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise interest rates by a quarter percentage point in December, after the central bank left policy rates unchanged at its July meeting. Previously the brokerage expected the Fed to hold rates through this year, with the next hike in the second half of 2027. No further policy details were provided.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:49:34.472124+00:00","url":"https://www.zawya.com/en/economy/jp-morgan-sees-december-fed-rate-hike-after-july-policy-meeting-414451","content":"Hong Kong. China- 02.15.2025. The name sign on an office building of J.P. Morgan, a leading American financial institution.\nImage used for illustrative purpose.\nImage courtesy: Getty Images/ Yau Ming Low\nINTEREST RATE\nCreate Bookmark\nJP Morgan sees December Fed rate hike after July policy meeting\nPrior to the meeting, the brokerage expected the Fed to keep rates on hold through this year\nJoel Jose | Reuters News\nJ.P. Morgan expects the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise interest rates by a quarter percentage point in December, following the central bank's decision to leave policy rates unchanged at its July meeting, it said in a note on Wednesday.Prior to the meeting, the brokerage expected the Fed to keep rates on hold through this year, with the next rate hike coming in the second half of 2027. (Reporting by Joel Jose in Bengaluru; Editing by Sonia Cheema)\nTopics\nINTEREST RATE\nDisclaimer: The content of this article is syndicated or provided to this website from an external third party provider. We are not responsible for, and do not control, such external websites, entities, applications or media publishers. The body of the text is provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis and has not been edited in any way. Neither we nor our affiliates guarantee the accuracy of or endorse the views or opinions expressed in this article. Read our full disclaimer policy here\n© ZAWYA 2026\nSubscribe and receive the best of ZAWYA in your inbox\nMost Read\nMost Watched\nMost Popular\nINTEREST RATE\nGCC central banks raise interest rates after US Fed rate increase\nREAL ESTATE\nAldar, Mubadala JV acquires Masdar City Square for $250mln\nCONSTRUCTION\nDubai announces 80km Fourth Corridor road project\nINVESTMENT\nAbu Dhabi's ADIA joins $703mln anchor raise for India's NSE IPO\nDEBT\nSaudi proptech Rize secures $50mln debt financing from Jadwa Investment\nFINANCIAL SERVICES\nPODCAST: How Egypt can unlock the growth it needs to reach its full potential\nFINTECH\nVIDEO: Bahrain fintech Tarabut secures $50mln from Saudi banks, investors\nMARKETS\nVIDEO: Highlights from Zawya’s inaugural GCC Capital Markets Forum\nFOOTBALL\nVIDEO: Kingdom Holding completes $224mln acquisition of 70% stake in Al Hilal Club\nINVESTMENT\nVIDEO: Saudi Aramco’s Wa’ed Ventures invests in COFE Tech ahead of IPO\nHYDROGEN\nSouth Africa: Sasol challenges scientists to unlock access to green hydrogen\nARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE\nServiceNow, Aramco Digital sign AI transformation agreement\nREAL ESTATE\nNakheel awards main construction contract worth over AED 800 million for Bay Grove Residences on Dub\nAVIATION\nBahrain International Airport wins three awards at the 2026 Skytrax World Airport Awards\nDEFENSE\nEDGE and Hanwha strengthen strategic cooperation on integrated air defence\nEXECUTIVE MOVES\nMOVE\nHSBC hunts for new finance chief: IFR","content_cn":"中国香港，2025年2月15日。美国领先金融机构摩根大通办公楼上的名称标牌。\n图片仅用于说明目的。\n图片来源：Getty Images/Yau Ming Low\n利率\n创建书签\n摩根大通预计美联储将在7月政策会议后于12月加息\n在会议召开前，该券商预计美联储今年将维持利率不变\nJoel Jose | 路透社新闻\n摩根大通周三在一份报告中表示，在美国联邦储备委员会决定于7月会议上维持政策利率不变后，该行预计美联储将在12月加息25个基点。\n在会议召开前，该券商预计美联储今年将维持利率不变，下一次加息将在2027年下半年进行。（Joel Jose在班加罗尔报道；Sonia Cheema编辑）\n主题\n利率\n免责声明：本文内容由外部第三方提供商转载或提供给本网站。我们不对这些外部网站、实体、应用程序或媒体出版商负责，也不控制它们。正文按“现状”和“可用”基础提供，未经任何方式编辑。我们及我们的关联方均不保证本文准确性，也不认可其中表达的观点或意见。请在此阅读我们的完整免责声明政策\n© ZAWYA 2026\n订阅并接收 ZAWYA 最精彩内容至您的收件箱\n阅读最多\n观看最多\n最受欢迎\n利率\n美国联邦储备委员会加息后，海湾合作委员会各国央行加息\n房地产\nAldar、Mubadala合资企业以2.5亿美元收购马斯达尔城广场\n建筑\n迪拜宣布建设80公里第四走廊道路项目\n投资\n阿布扎比投资局（ADIA）参与印度国家证券交易所IPO的7.03亿美元基石融资\n债务\n沙特房地产科技公司 Rize 获得 Jadwa Investment 提供的5000万美元债务融资\n金融服务\n播客：埃及如何释放实现全部潜力所需的增长\n金融科技\n视频：巴林金融科技公司 Tarabut 从沙特银行和投资者处获得5000万美元融资\n市场\n视频：Zawya首届海湾合作委员会资本市场论坛亮点\n足球\n视频：Kingdom Holding完成以2.24亿美元收购Al Hilal俱乐部70%股份\n投资\n视频：沙特阿美旗下 Wa’ed Ventures 在COFE Tech首次公开募股前进行投资\n氢能\n南非：Sasol向科学家发起挑战，以解锁绿色氢能获取途径\n人工智能\nServiceNow与Aramco Digital签署人工智能转型协议\n房地产\nNakheel授予Bay Grove Residences价值超过8亿阿联酋迪拉姆的主体建筑合同\n航空\n巴林国际机场在2026年Skytrax世界机场大奖中赢得三项奖项\n国防\nEDGE与Hanwha加强综合防空领域的战略合作\n高管变动\n变动\n汇丰寻找新任财务主管：国际财务报告准则","publish_source":"zawya.com","publish_time":"2026-07-30T05:08:45.787000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-452","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike警告：AI既是网络武器也是巨大攻击目标","title_en":"AI is both a cyber weapon and a massive target, CrowdStrike warns - ZDNET","summary_cn":"ZDNET报道CrowdStrike《2026年威胁狩猎报告》指出，AI既是攻击工具也是攻击面。AI代理触发的线索是人工线索的2.5倍，LLMJacking攻击曾在两分钟内发起近20万次API调用。报告还提到朝鲜相关组织Famous Chollima利用AI简历和深度伪造面试，以及2026年上半年88%的漏洞利用在PoC发布48小时内出现，建议企业保护AI凭证、强化身份验证并转向主动防御。","summary_en":"ZDNET reports on CrowdStrike's 2026 Threat Hunting Report, which says AI is both an attack tool and an attack surface. AI agent-triggered leads outnumber manual ones 2.5 to 1, and an LLMJacking campaign made nearly 200,000 API calls in two minutes. It cites DPRK-linked Famous Chollima using AI resumes and deepfake interviews, and notes 88% of exploits in H1 2026 appeared within 48 hours of PoC release, urging firms to secure AI credentials and adopt proactive defense.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:46:03.272030+00:00","url":"https://www.zdnet.com/article/ai-is-cyber-weapon-and-massive-target-crowdstrike-warns","content":"Tech > Security AI is both a cyber weapon and a massive target, CrowdStrike warns The same AI tools triggering suspicious alerts are being attacked by cybercriminals in droves.\nCharlie Osborne\nContributing Writer\nCharlie Osborne is a cybersecurity journalist and photographer who writes for ZDNET and CNET from London.… Read full bio\nCharlie Osborne\nContributing Writer\nRead full bio\nAugust 3, 2026, 5:52 pm ET\n4 min read\nElyse Betters Picaro / ZDNET\nFollow ZDNET: Add us as a preferred source on Google.\nZDNET’s key takeaways\nCrowdStrike warns AI is both a target and a weapon.\nLLMJacking made nearly 200,000 API calls in two minutes.\nMalicious AI exploits flaws faster than defenders can patch them.\nArtificial intelligence is increasingly “an adversary tool and target,” researchers said, forcing businesses to rethink their defensive strategies in light of attack signals far outstripping what cybersecurity experts can manually handle.\nAccording to CrowdStrike’s 2026 Threat Hunting Report, published on Monday, the same AI models, tools, and workflows that are giving businesses growth and productivity opportunities are being weaponized by cybercriminals in droves.\nAlso: How Google used AI agents to find and fix 1,072 Chrome security bugs – in 60 days\nAs corporate networks expand, endpoint devices are added, and new large language models (LLMs) are deployed to handle various workloads, organizations are also unwittingly creating larger “undefended” attack surfaces that can be exploited to steal data, obtain AI model access, conduct surveillance, and potentially even harvest computing power for their own ends.\nAI: The new weapon and target\n“AI is not just the tool or weapon that is being used, but it is also the attack surface,” Adam Meyers, head of threat intel at CrowdStrike, commented. “We’re seeing threat actors really adopt AI at the same speed that everybody else is.”\nCrowdStrike’s report said that the widespread adoption of artificial intelligence (much of it new and unproven) is increasing the sheer volume of signals that defenders have to sort through.\nAlso: Assume AI cybersecurity attacks are the future: 43% of companies have already experienced it\nThere are now 2.5 times as many AI agent-triggered leads for the firm’s threat hunters to examine as there are manually driven leads, which CrowdStrike said “makes it more difficult for defenders to distinguish malicious activity from expected AI-driven behavior.”\nSuspicious alerts and signals underscore AI-driven activity in the criminal world — and the rapid speeds at which attacks are now being conducted. CrowdStrike gave a number of examples, including:\nFamous Chollima: A Democratic People’s Republic of Korea (DPRK)-associated group is actively weaponizing trusted AI environments and tools to try to gain entry to companies working in cryptocurrency and the blockchain, using everything from AI-generated resumes to deepfake interviews.\nCordial Spider, Snarky Spider: These groups use vishing to exfiltrate data from SaaS apps and compromise single sign-on accounts. In one case documented by the researchers, an attack shifted from account takeover to data theft in less than five minutes.\nLLMJacking: LLMJacking occurs when a threat actor gains access to keys or credentials used to access a company’s AI models. Armed with access to these LLMs — which are typically cloud-based — threat actors can then steal data and wreak havoc, such as forcing the model to perform malicious tasks or those that demand high compute power, creating massive bills for the victim. For example, CrowdStrike said that in one campaign, the victim’s LLM was used to generate close to 200,000 API requests in two minutes, “resulting in large-scale financial and operational impact.”\nAI is mostly used by cybercriminals today to generate phishing and vishing material, payloads, and commands, streamlining their attack chains and potentially creating more convincing phishing schemes designed for initial access. Meyers said these creations are becoming more bespoke, with custom tools generated by AI and LLMs to manage different defense scenarios.\nVulnerability windows vanish: More bad news for defenders\nAnother concerning trend highlighted in the report is the shrinking window that human defenders — and their tools — have to respond between vulnerability discovery and exploitation.\nFrom January through June 2026, 88% of exploits detected by CrowdStrike were launched within 48 hours of a public proof-of-concept (PoC) code release.\nAlso: Not just OpenAI – Anthropic says Claude’s hacking spree ‘falls short of ideal behavior’\nSome threat groups, such as China’s Vault Panda and Genesis Panda, are keeping an even closer eye on new bugs: They developed working exploits for a critical vulnerability in a web application (React2Shell) within a day of disclosure.\nIn these situations, AI goes both ways. Two out of three recently disclosed LPE exploits, CopyFail and Fragnesia (Dirty Frag being the third), were discovered by AI-assisted research, and the report said “threat actors wasted no time incorporating them into active operations.”\nWhat does this mean for the enterprise and its cybersecurity teams? According to CrowdStrike, response times are going to become shorter and shorter — no doubt due in part to the weaponization of AI.\nAlso: Claude AI shared chats indexed by Google – see if your conversations were exposed\n“While this pattern predates the emergence of frontier AI models, the implementation of these systems is likely to compress vulnerability exploitation timelines by accelerating vulnerability discovery and exploit development,” the researchers said. “This could, in turn, increase the pressure on defenders already struggling to keep pace.”\nYour move\nAI can act as a shield, but as CrowdStrike’s research revealed, it can also be a weapon.\nAlso: Open weights vs. closed: An AI civil war’s afoot, and the stakes are existential\nWith the pressure caused by AI, defenders will be hard-pressed to retain control and secure the networks and endpoints they are responsible for, and so the team recommended that businesses adopt the following practices:\nSecure your AI applications and LLMs: With AI now embedded across multiple business environments, companies should enforce least-privilege principles, protect AI-related credentials, and monitor for suspicious LLM usage or cost spikes to reduce emerging business and operational risk.\nIdentity is a primary attack surface: This issue existed before AI, but now, securing and verifying identities is even more important. Organizations should enforce phishing-resistant multifactor authentication, monitor access to corporate resources, and apply least privilege to human and non-human accounts.\nTackle cross-domain blind spots and secure the software supply chain: Digital blind spots in the supply chain and in your own networks can be exploited. Telemetry, behavioral detection and analysis software, frequent patch cycles, and threat intelligence can reduce the risk of compromise.\nBe proactive: AI weaponization, moving at a speed we can’t, is now forcing organizations to shift from a reactive to a proactive security stance. Investment, threat triage, and tackling the legacy security issues that threaten today’s networks should all be handled quickly. By reducing the attack surface, you’ll give your teams the breathing space to keep up.\nShow Comments\nLog In to Comment\nLog Out\nCommunity Guidelines\nPlease accept cookies to view the comments powered by Disqus.\nCharlie Osborne\nContributing Writer\nCharlie Osborne is a cybersecurity journalist and photographer who writes for ZDNET and CNET from London. PGP Key: AF40821B\nSee full bio\nThe Latest from Charlie\nYour friend with ‘nothing to hide’ is more likely to spy on you, study shows\nThis LG TV jailbreak turns smart devices into spies, say researchers\nHow a lone attacker breached enterprise defenses at AI speed: A 10-hour play-by-play\n/ featured\nInside Linux-AI OS: I tested a distro with built-in local AI\nMy 6 favorite Microsoft Office alternatives for Linux – and why\nMy 5 favorite Linux distros for AI – and why\nRoku rolls out over 30 subscription bundles for up to 30% off, plus a new Labs feature","content_cn":"科技 > 安全\nCrowdStrike 警告：人工智能既是网络武器，也是巨大目标\n触发可疑警报的同一批 AI 工具，正遭到网络犯罪分子的成群攻击。\n\nCharlie Osborne\n特约撰稿人\nCharlie Osborne 是一名网络安全记者和摄影师，常驻伦敦，为 ZDNET 和 CNET 撰稿。……阅读完整简介\nCharlie Osborne\n特约撰稿人\n阅读完整简介\n2026 年 8 月 3 日，美国东部时间下午 5:52\n阅读用时 4 分钟\nElyse Betters Picaro / ZDNET\n关注 ZDNET：在 Google 上将我们添加为首选来源。\n\nZDNET 要点\nCrowdStrike 警告，AI 既是目标，也是武器。\nLLMJacking 在两分钟内发起了近 20 万次 API 调用。\n恶意 AI 利用漏洞的速度快于防御者修补漏洞的速度。\n\n研究人员表示，人工智能正日益成为“对手的工具和目标”，迫使企业重新思考防御策略，因为攻击信号的数量远远超出网络安全专家能够手动处理的范围。\n\n根据 CrowdStrike 于周一发布的《2026 年威胁狩猎报告》，那些为企业带来增长和生产力机会的相同 AI 模型、工具和工作流，正被网络犯罪分子成群武器化。\n\n另请阅读：Google 如何利用 AI 代理在 60 天内发现并修复 Chrome 的 1,072 个安全漏洞\n\n随着企业网络不断扩张、终端设备持续增加，以及部署新的大型语言模型（LLM）来处理各种工作负载，组织也在不知不觉中扩大了“未设防”的攻击面。这些攻击面可被利用来窃取数据、获取 AI 模型访问权限、开展监视，甚至可能为攻击者自身目的攫取计算能力。\n\nAI：新的武器与目标\n\nCrowdStrike 威胁情报负责人 Adam Meyers 评论道：“AI 不仅是被使用的工具或武器，它本身也是攻击面。我们看到，威胁行为者正在以与其他所有人相同的速度真正采用 AI。”\n\nCrowdStrike 的报告称，人工智能的广泛采用（其中许多技术都是新出现且未经验证的）正在增加防御者必须筛选的信号总量。\n\n另请阅读：假设 AI 网络安全攻击就是未来：43% 的公司已经遭遇过此类攻击\n\n目前，该公司威胁猎手需要检查的由 AI 代理触发的线索数量，是人工驱动线索的 2.5 倍。CrowdStrike 表示，这“使防御者更难将恶意活动与预期的 AI 驱动行为区分开来”。\n\n可疑警报和信号凸显了犯罪世界中的 AI 驱动活动，以及当前攻击实施的快速速度。CrowdStrike 给出了多个例子，包括：\n\nFamous Chollima：一个与朝鲜民主主义人民共和国（DPRK）有关联的团体，正积极将受信任的 AI 环境和工具武器化，试图进入从事加密货币和区块链业务的公司，手段包括使用 AI 生成的简历和深度伪造面试。\n\nCordial Spider、Snarky Spider：这些团体利用语音网络钓鱼，从 SaaS 应用中外传数据，并攻陷单点登录账户。在研究人员记录的一起案件中，攻击在不到五分钟内就从账户接管转为数据窃取。\n\nLLMJacking：当威胁行为者获得用于访问公司 AI 模型的密钥或凭据时，就会发生 LLMJacking。凭借对这些通常基于云端的 LLM 的访问权限，威胁行为者随后可以窃取数据并制造混乱，例如迫使模型执行恶意任务或那些\n需求高算力，给受害者造成巨额账单。例如，CrowdStrike表示，在一次攻击活动中，受害者的LLM在两分钟内被用于生成近20万次API请求，“造成了大规模的财务和运营影响”。\n如今，网络犯罪分子主要利用AI生成网络钓鱼和语音钓鱼材料、载荷及命令，简化攻击链，并可能制造更具迷惑性的网络钓鱼方案，以实现初始访问。Meyers表示，这些产物正变得更加定制化，攻击者利用AI和LLM生成定制工具，以应对不同的防御场景。\n漏洞窗口正在消失：防御者面临的又一坏消息\n报告强调的另一个令人担忧的趋势是，从发现漏洞到漏洞被利用之间，留给人工防御者及其工具作出响应的窗口正在缩短。\n2026年1月至6月期间，CrowdStrike检测到的漏洞利用中，有88%在公开概念验证（PoC）代码发布后的48小时内发起。\n另请阅读：不只是OpenAI——Anthropic称Claude的黑客行动“未达到理想行为”\n一些威胁组织，例如中国的Vault Panda和Genesis Panda，正更加密切地关注新漏洞：它们在一项关键的Web应用漏洞（React2Shell）披露后的一天内，就开发出了可用的漏洞利用程序。\n在这些情况下，AI发挥着双重作用。近期披露的三个LPE漏洞利用中，有两个——CopyFail和Fragnesia（第三个是Dirty Frag）——是通过AI辅助研究发现的，报告称“威胁行为者立即将其纳入了现有行动”。\n这对企业及其网络安全团队意味着什么？CrowdStrike表示，响应时间将变得越来越短——毫无疑问，部分原因在于AI的武器化。\n另请阅读：Claude AI分享的聊天记录被Google编入索引——查看你的对话是否遭到暴露\n研究人员表示：“虽然这一模式早于前沿AI模型的出现，但这些系统的应用很可能通过加速漏洞发现和漏洞利用开发，压缩漏洞利用时间线。这反过来可能会加大防御者的压力，而他们本已难以跟上步伐。”\n轮到你了\nAI可以充当盾牌，但正如CrowdStrike的研究所揭示的那样，它也可以成为武器。\n另请阅读：开放权重与闭源：一场AI内战正在展开， stakes关乎生死存亡\n由于AI带来的压力，防御者将难以保持对其负责的网络和终端的控制并确保其安全，因此该团队建议企业采取以下做法：\n保护你的AI应用和LLM：如今AI已嵌入多个业务环境，企业应执行最小权限原则，保护与AI相关的凭据，并监控可疑的LLM使用情况或成本激增，以降低新出现的业务和运营风险。\n身份是主要攻击面：这一问题在AI出现之前就已存在，但如今，保护和验证身份变得更加重要。组织应执行抗网络钓鱼的多因素身份验证，监控对企业资源的访问，并对人类和非人类账户实施最小权限。\n应对跨域盲点并保护软件供应链：供应链以及自有网络中的数字盲点可能遭到利用。遥测、基于行为的检测与分析软件、频繁的补丁周期，以及威胁\n情报可以降低遭到入侵的风险。\n积极主动：人工智能武器化的速度是我们无法企及的，这正迫使组织将安全策略从被动转向主动。投资、威胁分级，以及解决威胁当今网络的遗留安全问题，都应迅速处理。通过缩小攻击面，你将为团队争取喘息空间，以便跟上步伐。\n显示评论\n登录发表评论\n退出登录\n社区准则\n请接受 Cookie，以查看由 Disqus 提供支持的评论。\nCharlie Osborne\n特约撰稿人\nCharlie Osborne 是一名网络安全记者和摄影师，常驻伦敦，为 ZDNET 和 CNET 撰稿。PGP 密钥：AF40821B\n查看完整简介\nCharlie 的最新文章\n研究显示，你那个“没什么可隐瞒”的朋友更有可能监视你\n研究人员称，这款 LG 电视越狱会将智能设备变成间谍\n一名攻击者如何以 AI 的速度突破企业防御：10 小时逐幕回放\n/ 精选\n深入了解 Linux-AI OS：我测试了一款内置本地 AI 的发行版\n我最喜欢的 6 个 Linux Microsoft Office 替代品——以及原因\n我最喜欢的 5 个适用于 AI 的 Linux 发行版——以及原因\nRoku 推出 30 多个订阅套餐，最高优惠 30%，并新增 Labs 功能","publish_source":"zdnet.com","publish_time":"2026-08-03T17:52:06-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2009","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部发布“最恶劣”犯罪非法移民名单","title_en":"DHS Posts \"Worst of the Worst\" Criminal Illegal Migrants List | Y100.7 | Florida News","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部推出一个在线网页，公布被称为“最恶劣”的犯罪非法移民名单，包括恋童癖者、帮派成员和毒品贩运者。该网页上线时列出1万起逮捕案例，并将由国土安全部持续更新。国土安全部发表声明称，推出该网站是为了让每个美国人看到被逮捕的犯罪非法移民、他们所犯罪行以及被遣离的社区。佛罗里达州有近1200人出现在该名单上。","summary_en":"The U.S. Department of Homeland Security has unveiled an online list of the \"worst of the worst\" criminal illegal aliens, including pedophiles, gang members and drug traffickers. The new DHS webpage features 10,000 arrests upon launch and will be updated by the department. In a statement, DHS said the website was launched so every American can see the criminal illegal aliens being arrested, what crimes they committed, and which communities they were removed from. Florida has almost 1,200 people on the list.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:28:37.788025+00:00","url":"https://y100.iheart.com/featured/florida-news/content/2025-12-09-dhs-posts-worst-of-the-worst-criminal-illegal-migrants-list","content":"Florida NewsDHS Posts \"Worst of the Worst\" Criminal Illegal Migrants ListBy Karen CurtisDec 9, 2025BRADENTON, FLORIDA - OCTOBER 20: Photos of criminally charged undocumented immigrants are displayed during Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem's press conference in Bradenton, Florida, on October 20, 2025.The Secretary addressed ongoing immigration enforcement efforts and federal coordination with local authorities across the state, while praising President Donald Trump for their joint accomplishments under the \"One, Big, Beautiful Bill,\" which received congressional approval and funded expanded DHS operations. (Photo by Octavio Jones/Getty Images)Photo: Octavio Jones / Getty Images News / Getty Images(Washington, DC) -- Federal officials unveiling an online list of the\" worst of the worst\" criminal illegal aliens including pedophiles, gang members, and drug traffickers.\nThe new Department of Homeland Security webpage features 10,000 arrests upon launch and will be updated by DHS.\nDHS statement: \"Today, we launched a ‘worst of the worst’ website so every American can see for themselves the criminal illegal aliens that we are arresting, what crimes they committed, and which communities we removed them from. This holiday season, make sure to thank law enforcement officers for all they do to make America safe again.\"\nFlorida has almost 12-hundred people on the list.\nSponsored ContentSponsored Content","content_cn":"佛罗里达新闻\n国土安全部发布“最恶劣中的最恶劣”刑事非法移民名单\n作者：凯伦·柯蒂斯\n2025年12月9日\n佛罗里达州布雷登顿——2025年10月20日，国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆在佛罗里达州布雷登顿举行新闻发布会期间，展示被刑事起诉的无证移民照片。部长谈及全州持续开展的移民执法行动以及与地方当局的联邦协调，同时称赞唐纳德·特朗普总统，表扬他们在“一项伟大、美丽的大法案”下取得的共同成就；该法案获国会批准，并为扩大国土安全部行动提供资金。（照片由奥克塔维奥·琼斯/盖蒂图片社提供）\n照片：奥克塔维奥·琼斯/盖蒂图片社新闻/盖蒂图片社\n（华盛顿特区）——联邦官员公布了一份在线名单，列出“最恶劣中的最恶劣”的刑事非法外国人，包括恋童癖者、帮派成员和毒品贩子。\n国土安全部新设的网页上线时列出了10,000起逮捕记录，并将由国土安全部更新。\n国土安全部声明：“今天，我们推出了一个‘最恶劣中的最恶劣’网站，让每一位美国人都可以亲自看到我们正在逮捕哪些刑事非法外国人、他们犯下了什么罪行，以及我们将他们从哪些社区驱逐出去。在这个节日季，请务必感谢执法人员为让美国重新安全所做的一切。”\n佛罗里达州名单上有近1,200人。\n赞助内容 赞助内容","publish_source":"y100.iheart.com","publish_time":"2025-12-09T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3162","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿拉巴马州执法机构被美国国土安全部评为年度合作伙伴","title_en":"ALEA recognized by U.S. Department of Homeland Security as partner of the year - Yellowhammer News","summary_cn":"Yellowhammer News报道，阿拉巴马州执法机构（ALEA）被美国国土安全调查局（HSI）亚特兰大外勤办公室评为2024年度调查合作伙伴。颁奖仪式于2025年2月13日在亚特兰大举行，ALEA州调查局（SBI）的特工还获得2024年度调查奖，一名伯明翰地区特工被评为HSI年度特遣队官员。ALEA局长哈尔·泰勒表示与联邦机构的合作对保护社区至关重要。HSI是美国国土安全部的主要调查机构，负责调查跨国犯罪和威胁。","summary_en":"Yellowhammer News reports that the Alabama Law Enforcement Agency (ALEA) was named the 2024 Investigative Partner of the Year by Homeland Security Investigations' (HSI) Atlanta Field Office, which covers Alabama and Georgia. The ceremony was held in Atlanta on Feb. 13, 2025. In addition to Partner of the Year, SBI Special Agents in Mobile received the 2024 Investigation of the Year Award, and a Birmingham-area agent was recognized as HSI's Task Force Officer of the Year. ALEA Secretary Hal Taylor said partnerships with federal agencies are paramount to protecting communities. HSI is the principal investigative arm of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security, responsible for investigating transnational crime and threats.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:05:42.991061+00:00","url":"https://yellowhammernews.com/alea-recognized-by-u-s-department-of-homeland-security-as-partner-of-the-year","content":"News\nALEA recognized by U.S. Department of Homeland Security as partner of the year\nGrayson Everett\n—\nFebruary 17, 2025\nShare:\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\n(U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement/Flickr, YHN)\nThe Alabama Law Enforcement Agency (ALEA) was recently recognized as the 2024 Investigative Partner of the Year by Homeland Security Investigations’ (HSI) Atlanta Field Office, which is responsible for federal law enforcement in both Alabama  and Georgia.\nThis recognition was awarded to Special Agents assigned to ALEA’s State Bureau of  Investigation (SBI) during a ceremony held in Atlanta, Ga., on Thursday, Feb. 13. In addition to Partner of the Year, SBI Special Agents operating out of Mobile, received the Investigation of  the Year Award for 2024 and one Special Agent in the Birmingham area was also recognized as HSI’s Task Force Officer of the Year.\n“The partnerships we cultivate with federal agencies are paramount in our shared mission to  protect our communities,” said ALEA Secretary Hal Taylor. “It’s an honor for our team to  receive this prestigious award, and we are grateful for the strong partnership we share with Homeland Security Investigations.”\nRELATED: Law enforcement heroes recognized for lifesaving efforts at ALEA ceremony\nALEA SBI Director Chris Inabinett agreed and said, “Oftentimes, due to the sensitive nature of  the cases and the investigations our Special Agents handle, we are unable to highlight and  recognize them for their specialized and diligent work. However, these awards are a testament to the unwavering commitment and dedication of not only our Agents, but also our federal  partners.”\nHSI is the principal investigative arm of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS), responsible for investigating transnational crime and threats. HSI conducts federal criminal  investigations into the illegal movement of people, goods, money, contraband, weapons and sensitive technology into, out of and through the United States.\nALEA SBI is a prominent supporter of its federal partners and ALEA Special Agents serve on a  variety of Task Forces to include the U.S. Marshals Fugitive Task Force, DEA’s High-Intensity Drug Trafficking Areas Task Force, FBI Safe Streets Task Force and the FBI Joint Terrorism  Task Force.\nGrayson Everett is the editor in chief of Yellowhammer News. You can follow him on X @Grayson270.\nRecent in News\nALGOP affirms Jesse Battles’ ballot removal: ‘Republicans decide who appears on the Republican ballot’\nYaffee — 38 minutes ago\nAmerican Village, Mount Vernon reunite George Washington’s sleeve buttons at Presidential Sites Summit\nGrayson Everett — 1 hour ago\nRelated\n$22 million FEMA training center opens in Anniston, strengthening national first responder training\nSherri Blevins — 8 hours ago\nSearch continues for missing Wetumpka boater on Alabama River\nStaff Report — January 13, 2026\nALEA Troopers deliver teddy bears to Mobile children’s hospital for Christmas\nSherri Blevins — December 22, 2025\nALEA urges Alabamians to ‘Score Big with Safety’ this Labor Day weekend\nStaff Report — August 29, 2025\nCriminals in Montgomery point firearms at agent with Attorney General’s office\nAusten Shipley — August 27, 2025\nSecretary of State Wes Allen, ALEA engage Alabama businesses in human trafficking fight\nAusten Shipley — August 12, 2025\nNext Post\nUA Miracle Raises $223,725 for Children’s of Alabama\nBryant Welbourne — February 17, 2025","content_cn":"新闻\n\nALEA获美国国土安全部评为年度合作伙伴\n\nGrayson Everett\n—\n2025年2月17日\n分享：\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\n\n（美国移民与海关执法局/Flickr，YHN）\n\n阿拉巴马州执法机构（ALEA）近日被国土安全调查局（HSI）亚特兰大外地办事处评为2024年度调查合作伙伴。该办事处负责阿拉巴马州和佐治亚州的联邦执法工作。\n\n这一荣誉在2月13日星期四于佐治亚州亚特兰大举行的仪式上授予被分配至ALEA州调查局（SBI）的特别探员。除年度合作伙伴奖外，在莫比尔工作的SBI特别探员还获得了2024年度调查奖，伯明翰地区的一名特别探员也被评为HSI年度特遣队官员。\n\nALEA秘书长Hal Taylor说：“我们与联邦机构建立的伙伴关系，对于我们共同保护社区的使命至关重要。我们的团队能够获得这一 prestigious奖项是我们的荣幸，我们感谢与国土安全调查局之间的牢固合作关系。”\n\n相关文章：在ALEA仪式上表彰为拯救生命作出努力的执法英雄\n\nALEA SBI局长Chris Inabinett对此表示赞同，并说：“由于我们的特别探员所处理案件和调查的敏感性质，我们往往无法公开介绍并表彰他们专业且勤勉的工作。然而，这些奖项证明了不仅我们的探员，而且我们的联邦合作伙伴所表现出的坚定承诺和奉献精神。”\n\nHSI是美国国土安全部（DHS）的主要调查机构，负责调查跨国犯罪和威胁。HSI开展联邦刑事调查，查处人员、货物、资金、违禁品、武器和敏感技术非法进出美国以及经由美国流动的行为。\n\nALEA SBI是联邦合作伙伴的重要支持者，ALEA特别探员在多个特遣队中任职，包括美国法警逃犯特遣队、缉毒局高强度毒品贩运地区特遣队、FBI安全街道特遣队和FBI联合反恐特遣队。\n\nGrayson Everett是Yellowhammer News的主编。你可以在X上关注他：@Grayson270。\n\n近期新闻\n\nALGOP确认Jesse Battles被取消选票资格：“共和党人决定谁出现在共和党选票上”\nYaffee——38分钟前\n\n美国村与弗农山庄在总统遗址峰会上重新聚合乔治·华盛顿的袖扣\nGrayson Everett——1小时前\n\n相关文章\n\n安尼斯顿启用价值2,200万美元的FEMA培训中心，加强全国一线应急人员培训\nSherri Blevins——8小时前\n\n继续在阿拉巴马河搜寻失踪的Wetumpka船民\nStaff Report——2026年1月13日\n\nALEA在圣诞节向莫比尔儿童医院送泰迪熊\nSherri Blevins——2025年12月22日\n\nALEA敦促阿拉巴马州居民在本劳动节周末“安全赢得大奖”\nStaff Report——2025年8月29日\n\n蒙哥马利的犯罪分子用枪指向总检察长办公室的探员\nAusten Shipley——2025年8月27日\n\n国务卿Wes Allen与ALEA共同动员阿拉巴马州企业打击人口贩运\nAusten Shipley——2025年8月12日\n\n下一篇\n\nUA Miracle为阿拉巴马州儿童医院筹款223,725美元\nBryant Welbourne——2025年2月17日","publish_source":"yellowhammernews.com","publish_time":"2025-02-17T19:03:35+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3101","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"加强移动安全：Zimperium与CrowdStrike扩大战略合作","title_en":"Enhancing Mobile Security: Zimperium and CrowdStrike Expand Strategic Partnership","summary_cn":"Zimperium与CrowdStrike扩大战略合作，将Zimperium移动威胁防御（MTD）与CrowdStrike Falcon下一代SIEM集成。据Zimperium 2024全球移动威胁报告，82%钓鱼网站针对移动设备，移动恶意软件样本同比增长13%。集成后安全团队可在统一视图中查看包括移动端在内的所有端点威胁，实现更快检测响应与高级威胁狩猎，该集成已在CrowdStrike市场提供。","summary_en":"Zimperium and CrowdStrike have expanded their strategic partnership, integrating Zimperium's Mobile Threat Defense with CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM. According to Zimperium's 2024 Global Mobile Threat Report, 82% of phishing sites targeted mobile devices and unique mobile malware samples rose 13% year-over-year. The integration gives security teams a unified view of threats across all endpoints including mobile, enabling faster detection and response and advanced threat hunting. It is now available in the CrowdStrike Marketplace.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:28:38.813674+00:00","url":"https://zimperium.com/blog/enhancing-mobile-security-zimperium-and-crowdstrike-expand-strategic-partnership","content":"blog\nMar 04, 2025\nEnhancing Mobile Security: Zimperium and CrowdStrike Expand Strategic Partnership\nZimperium\nMobile devices have become essential to enterprise operations — and a primary target for cybercriminals. According to Zimperium’s 2024 Global Mobile Threat Report, 82% of phishing sites targeted mobile devices, while unique mobile malware samples increased by 13% year-over-year. To combat these evolving threats, Zimperium and CrowdStrike have expanded their partnership, integrating Zimperium’s Mobile Threat Defense (MTD) with CrowdStrike Falcon® Next-Gen SIEM. This integration enhances mobile threat visibility and response capabilities, strengthening enterprise security across all endpoints.\nAdvancing Enterprise Security Through Collaboration\nThis strategic partnership builds on both companies’ commitment to delivering comprehensive security solutions. By integrating Zimperium’s mobile threat intelligence into the CrowdStrike Falcon® platform, security teams gain a unified, single-pane-of-glass view of threats across all endpoints — including mobile devices. This enables seamless threat detection and analysis, and response while complementing existing security workflows.\nThe Zimperium and CrowdStrike integration delivers key benefits, including:\n“With mobile threats growing more sophisticated, enterprises need flexible and scalable detection strategies,” said David Natker, VP, Global Partners and Alliances at Zimperium. “Together, Zimperium and CrowdStrike are providing organizations with enhanced visibility and the tools necessary to respond to threats proactively and protect sensitive data.”Comprehensive Threat Visibility and Proactive Defense\nUnified Threat Visibility: A holistic view of risks across mobile and non-mobile endpoints for stronger security insights\nFaster Detection and Response: Correlate Zimperium data with broader SOC data for streamlined context-rich investigations and accelerated response.\nAdvanced Threat Hunting: Leverage high-speed search and world-class threat intelligence to detect patterns across mobile and enterprise data.\nBy combining Zimperium’s mobile threat detection with CrowdStrike’s advanced analytics, enterprises gain real-time visibility and rapid response capabilities to address emerging mobile risks effectively.\nNow Available in the CrowdStrike Marketplace\nThis integration is now available through the CrowdStrike Marketplace, providing enterprises with an easy way to deploy and operationalize mobile security within their broader cybersecurity strategy.\nMTD\nMobile Security\nApp Security\nLatest News\nMay 07, 2026\nZimperium Mobile SOC Agent: The AI Empowered Solution That Turns Every SOC Analyst Into a Mobile Security Expert\nFeb 19, 2026\nLe gouvernement français met en garde contre les menaces mobiles et recommande des mesures de défense contre ces menaces.\nFeb 19, 2026\nFrench Government Warns on Mobile Threat Landscape, Recommends Mobile Threat Defense","content_cn":"博客\n2025年3月4日\n增强移动安全：Zimperium与CrowdStrike扩大战略合作伙伴关系\nZimperium\n移动设备已成为企业运营的关键组成部分，也是网络犯罪分子的主要目标。根据Zimperium的《2024年全球移动威胁报告》，82%的钓鱼网站以移动设备为目标，而独特移动恶意软件样本数量同比增加13%。为应对这些不断演变的威胁，Zimperium和CrowdStrike扩大了合作关系，将Zimperium的移动威胁防御（MTD）与CrowdStrike Falcon®下一代SIEM整合。此整合增强了移动威胁的可见性和响应能力，从而强化企业所有端点的安全性。\n通过协作推进企业安全\n这一战略合作伙伴关系建立在两家公司致力于提供全面安全解决方案的承诺之上。通过将Zimperium的移动威胁情报整合到CrowdStrike Falcon®平台中，安全团队可获得跨所有端点（包括移动设备）的统一单一视图威胁态势。这使威胁检测、分析和响应能够无缝进行，同时补充现有安全工作流程。\nZimperium和CrowdStrike的整合带来主要优势，包括：\n“随着移动威胁变得更加复杂，企业需要灵活且可扩展的检测策略，”Zimperium全球合作伙伴与联盟副总裁David Natker表示。“Zimperium和CrowdStrike正共同为组织提供更强的可见性，以及主动响应威胁和保护敏感数据所需的工具。”\n全面威胁可见性与主动防御\n统一威胁可见性：全面了解移动和非移动端点的风险，获得更强的安全洞察\n更快的检测和响应：将Zimperium数据与更广泛的SOC数据关联，以简化具备丰富上下文的调查并加快响应。\n高级威胁狩猎：利用高速搜索和世界级威胁情报，检测移动和企业数据中的模式。\n通过结合Zimperium的移动威胁检测能力与CrowdStrike的高级分析能力，企业可获得实时可见性和快速响应能力，以有效应对新出现的移动风险。\n现已在CrowdStrike Marketplace推出\n该整合现可通过CrowdStrike Marketplace获得，使企业能够轻松在更广泛的网络安全战略中部署并实施移动安全。\nMTD\n移动安全\n应用安全\n最新新闻\n2026年5月7日\nZimperium移动SOC代理：由AI赋能的解决方案，让每位SOC分析师都成为移动安全专家\n2026年2月19日\n法国政府警告移动威胁，并建议采取针对这些威胁的防御措施。\n2026年2月19日\n法国政府警告移动威胁态势，建议采用移动威胁防御","publish_source":"zimperium.com","publish_time":"2025-03-04T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3092","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"Zimperium宣布与CrowdStrike Falcon下一代SIEM新集成以增强移动安全","title_en":"Zimperium Announces New Integration with CrowdStrike Falcon® Next-Gen SIEM to Enhance Mobile Security","summary_cn":"Zimperium宣布与CrowdStrike Falcon网络安全平台集成，将移动威胁防御平台的移动威胁情报无缝共享至CrowdStrike Falcon下一代SIEM，该集成已在CrowdStrike市场提供。集成将Zimperium移动威胁与风险取证能力同CrowdStrike AI驱动的检测响应结合，并映射至MITRE ATT&CK框架，帮助安全团队主动应对移动安全缺口、缩短事件响应时间并提升移动端点安全管理。","summary_en":"Zimperium announced an integration with the CrowdStrike Falcon cybersecurity platform, seamlessly sharing mobile threat intelligence from its Mobile Threat Defense platform to CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM, now available in the CrowdStrike Marketplace. The integration combines Zimperium's mobile threat and risk forensics with CrowdStrike's AI-driven detection and response, mapped to the MITRE ATT&CK framework, helping security teams proactively address mobile security gaps, reduce incident response times and improve mobile endpoint security management.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:28:19.115966+00:00","url":"https://zimperium.com/resources/zimperium-announces-new-integration-with-crowdstrike-falcon-next-gen-siem-to-enhance-mobile-security","content":"Mar 5, 2025, 12:00:00 AM\nZimperium Announces New Integration with CrowdStrike Falcon® Next-Gen SIEM to Enhance Mobile Security\nZimperium\nDALLAS, TX, – March 5, 2025 – Zimperium, a global leader in mobile security, today announced that it is enhancing detection and response capabilities of security teams by  integrating with the industry-leading CrowdStrike Falcon® cybersecurity platform. This new integration, now available on the CrowdStrike Marketplace, enables seamless sharing of mobile threat intelligence from Zimperium’s Mobile Threat Defense platform to CrowdStrike Falcon® Next-Gen SIEM.\nAccording to Zimperium’s 2024 Global Mobile Threat Report, 82% of phishing sites targeted mobile devices and unique malware samples increased by 13% year-over-year. As a pioneer of mobile security, Zimperium offers a comprehensive approach to securing the entire mobile ecosystem, from applications to endpoints, within a single platform.\nIntegrating Zimperium’s robust mobile threat and risk forensics with CrowdStrike’s AI-driven detection and response, all mapped to the MITRE ATT&CK framework, equips security teams to proactively address mobile security gaps, reduce incident response times, and improve mobile endpoint security management. Together, they deliver enhanced visibility across mobile endpoints and with Falcon Next-Gen SIEM, security teams can seamlessly ingest data from any security or IT source, which is enriched with Falcon platform data, threat intelligence, AI and workflow automation, providing rapid detection and response across enterprise environments.\n“We are excited to partner with CrowdStrike to deliver enhanced visibility and greater flexibility for our customers and partners,” said David Natker, VP, Global Partners and Alliances at Zimperium. “As mobile threats become increasingly sophisticated, enterprises need advanced detection strategies to safeguard sensitive data and prevent mobile attacks. This integration equips SOC teams with the tools to seamlessly monitor and respond to mobile threats, enhancing visibility and delivering unified mobile security across their environments.”\nTo learn more about the Zimperium and CrowdStrike partnership, visit https://marketplace.crowdstrike.com/partners/zimperium.\nAbout Zimperium\nZimperium is the world leader in mobile security. Purpose-built for mobile environments, Zimperium delivers unparalleled protection for mobile applications and devices. As cybercriminals adopt a mobile-first attack strategy, Zimperium’s AI-driven mobile security enables organizations to stay ahead of evolving threats including mobile-targeted phishing (mishing), malware, app vulnerabilities and compromise, as well as zero day threats. Learn more at www.zimperium.com\nPress Releases\nResources\nLatest News\nJun 10, 2026, 7:00:00 AM\nZimperium Positioned as a Leader in the SPARK Matrix TM: In- App Protection Platform, 2026 by QKS Group\nJun 9, 2026, 5:59:59 AM\nZimperium Expands UK Reach Through ABC Distribution to Address Growing Mobile Threat Landscape\nMay 6, 2026, 6:00:05 AM\nZimperium Arms Security and Fraud Teams with AI-Empowered Mobile App Response Agent to Counter Growing Mobile Attacks","content_cn":"2025年3月5日，上午12:00:00\nZimperium 宣布与 CrowdStrike Falcon® 下一代 SIEM 推出新集成，以增强移动安全\nZimperium\n得克萨斯州达拉斯，2025年3月5日——全球移动安全领导者 Zimperium 今日宣布，通过与业界领先的 CrowdStrike Falcon® 网络安全平台集成，增强安全团队的检测与响应能力。这项现已在 CrowdStrike Marketplace 上推出的新集成，使 Zimperium 移动威胁防御平台的移动威胁情报能够无缝共享至 CrowdStrike Falcon® 下一代 SIEM。\n根据 Zimperium 的《2024年全球移动威胁报告》，82% 的网络钓鱼网站以移动设备为目标，独特恶意软件样本数量同比增加了 13%。作为移动安全的先驱，Zimperium 在单一平台内提供全面方法，以保护从应用程序到端点的整个移动生态系统。\n将 Zimperium 强大的移动威胁与风险取证能力，同 CrowdStrike 由 AI 驱动的检测与响应能力相集成，并全部映射至 MITRE ATT&CK 框架，使安全团队能够主动应对移动安全漏洞、缩短事件响应时间，并改善移动端点安全管理。双方共同提供移动端点的增强可见性；借助 Falcon 下一代 SIEM，安全团队能够无缝接入来自任何安全或 IT 来源的数据，这些数据由 Falcon 平台数据、威胁情报、AI 和工作流程自动化加以丰富，从而在企业环境中实现快速检测与响应。\nZimperium 全球合作伙伴与联盟副总裁 David Natker 表示：“我们很高兴与 CrowdStrike 合作，为客户和合作伙伴提供更强的可见性和更大的灵活性。随着移动威胁日益复杂，企业需要先进的检测策略，以保护敏感数据并防范移动攻击。这项集成为 SOC 团队提供了无缝监控和响应移动威胁的工具，增强可见性，并在其环境中提供统一的移动安全。”\n如需了解更多有关 Zimperium 与 CrowdStrike 合作的信息，请访问 https://marketplace.crowdstrike.com/partners/zimperium。\n关于 Zimperium\nZimperium 是全球移动安全领导者。Zimperium 专为移动环境打造，为移动应用程序和设备提供无与伦比的保护。随着网络犯罪分子采用移动优先的攻击策略，Zimperium 由 AI 驱动的移动安全使组织能够领先于不断演变的威胁，包括针对移动设备的网络钓鱼（mishing）、恶意软件、应用漏洞和遭入侵，以及零日威胁。详见 www.zimperium.com\n新闻稿\n资源\n最新新闻\n2026年6月10日，上午7:00:00\nZimperium 在 QKS Group 的《2026 年 SPARK Matrix™：应用内保护平台》中被定位为领导者\n2026年6月9日，上午5:59:59\nZimperium 通过 ABC Distribution 扩大英国业务覆盖，以应对不断加剧的移动威胁格局\n2026年5月6日，上午6:00:05\nZimperium 为安全与反欺诈团队配备 AI 赋能的移动应用响应代理，以应对日益增多的移动攻击","publish_source":"zimperium.com","publish_time":"2025-03-05T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1267","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部拨款最新进展","title_en":"DHS Funding Update","summary_cn":"众议员沃尔伯格的电子通讯介绍国土安全部拨款争议：超过10万名国土安全部员工（含5万名运输安全管理局官员）因拨款僵局未能领到全额薪资，特朗普总统已采取行政措施让部分员工获得薪酬。沃尔伯格表示已三次投票支持两党两院的国土安全部拨款方案及清洁持续决议，以确保所有国土安全部人员获得薪酬并维持关键安全行动，同时反对削减该部门近26%预算的法案。","summary_en":"Rep. Walberg's e-newsletter discusses the Department of Homeland Security funding dispute: over 100,000 DHS workers, including 50,000 TSA officers, missed a full paycheck amid the funding impasse, and President Trump took executive action to pay many workers. Walberg says he voted three times for the bipartisan, bicameral DHS funding package and a clean continuing resolution to ensure all DHS personnel are paid and critical security operations continue, while opposing a bill that would cut nearly 26% of DHS funding.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:29:14.032522+00:00","url":"http://walberg.house.gov/media/e-newsletter-archive/dhs-funding-update","content":"Home\nMedia\nDHS Funding Update\nImage March 28, 2026 e-Newsletter ArchiveSupporting Our Homeland DefendersOver 100,000 DHS workers, including 50,000 TSA officers, have missed a full paycheck as a result of the Democrats' shutdown of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS). Fortunately, President Trump has taken executive action to get many workers paid, despite the antics coming from Democrats. Instead of supporting the House's bipartisan efforts, the Senate pushed the welfare of criminal illegal aliens above American citizens by forcing through a bill at 3 am on Friday that would defund nearly 26% of DHS, and force many workers to go without pay indefinitely. We must fully fund the Department of Homeland Security and the salaries of the men and women on the front lines. That is why I voted for a clean continuing resolution to ensure all DHS personnel are paid, and all critical security operations can continue. Three times, the House has passed the bipartisan, bicameral DHS funding package. We have passed a clean continuing resolution to get workers paid. We will not pass a bill that forces workers to go without pay indefinitely while reopening our border.Preserving the Health of the Great LakesAs a member of the Great Lakes Task Force and the Natural Resources Committee, I am dedicated to advancing efforts to address the threats facing the Great Lakes. I have been a longtime supporter of the Great Lakes Restoration Initiative (GLRI), which has been a vital tool in the protection and restoration efforts of some critical areas of concern. This week, the House passed the American Water Stewardship Act, which would reauthorize funding for several long-standing programs to maintain and improve water quality throughout the nation, including the Great Lakes Restoration Initiative. Securing Funding for New Buffalo I recently visited the Galien River Sanitary District (GRSD) Sewer Authority in New Buffalo to discuss federal funding I secured for a project to replace the authority's tertiary filter, an essential component of the water treatment process. For the past year, I've partnered with local leaders to identify important infrastructure needs across Michigan’s 5th District. With this federal funding, the GRSD Sewer Authority will be able to make critical improvements to the city’s water treatment system, ensuring harmful materials are removed from water discharged into Lake Michigan and protecting public health and safety for the millions of people who rely on this important water source.  Protecting Schools from Foreign InfluenceAs Chair of the Education and Workforce Committee, I held a hearing to examine how foreign adversaries, particularly geopolitical rivals like the Chinese Communist Party (CCP), are actively competing against our nation’s interests on the battlegrounds of our university campuses. Last year, the House passed the DETERRENT Act with a strong bipartisan vote, which would bring much-needed transparency to foreign gift reporting requirements for colleges and universities. We must ensure that academic collaboration strengthens America, not our adversaries.Honoring a Monroe County VeteranIt is a privilege to honor Sam Struth of Monroe as the Veteran of the Month for March. Sam served in the United States Army from 1975 to 1980 and has stayed actively involved in the veteran community, volunteering for Angels for Veterans and AMVETS of Monroe County. Sam also co-founded Flags O’er Veterans with Ken Moore after identifying that several local cemeteries lacked American flags honoring deceased veterans. The organization pays tribute to veterans in Monroe by raising funds to install flagpoles, American flags, lighting, and memorial plaques in cemeteries where they are laid to rest. Sam's remarkable life reflects the very best of American service.","content_cn":"主页\n媒体\n国土安全部拨款更新\n图片 2026年3月28日 电子通讯存档\n支持我们的国土防卫者\n由于民主党关闭国土安全部（DHS），超过10万名DHS工作人员（包括5万名运输安全管理局官员）未能领到一整份工资。幸运的是，尽管民主党方面不断制造闹剧，特朗普总统已采取行政行动，使许多工作人员得以获得薪酬。参议院没有支持众议院的两党努力，反而在周五凌晨3点强行通过一项法案，将近26%的DHS资金削减，并迫使许多工作人员无限期停薪，从而把犯罪的非法移民的福利置于美国公民之上。我们必须为国土安全部以及处于前线的男女工作人员的薪资提供全额资金。因此，我投票支持一项不附带条件的持续决议，以确保所有DHS人员获得薪酬，所有关键安全行动得以继续。众议院已三次通过两党、两院一致的DHS拨款方案。我们已经通过了一项不附带条件的持续决议，让工作人员获得薪酬。在重新开放边境的同时，我们不会通过一项迫使工作人员无限期停薪的法案。\n\n维护五大湖的健康\n作为五大湖特别工作组和自然资源委员会成员，我致力于推进应对五大湖所面临威胁的工作。我长期支持五大湖恢复倡议（GLRI），该倡议一直是保护和恢复若干重点关注区域的重要工具。本周，众议院通过了《美国水资源管理法》，该法将重新授权多个长期项目的资金，以维护和改善全美水质，其中包括五大湖恢复倡议。\n\n为新布法罗争取资金\n我最近访问了新布法罗的加连河卫生区（GRSD）下水道管理局，讨论我为一个项目争取到的联邦资金，该项目将更换管理局的三级过滤器，这是水处理过程中的关键部件。在过去一年里，我一直与地方领导人合作，确定密歇根州第五国会选区各地的重要基础设施需求。有了这笔联邦资金，GRSD下水道管理局将能够对该市的水处理系统进行关键改进，确保从排入密歇根湖的水中去除有害物质，并保护数百万依赖这一重要水源的人们的公共健康与安全。\n\n保护学校免受外国影响\n作为教育与劳动力委员会主席，我举行了一场听证会，审查外国对手，尤其是像中国共产党（CCP）这样的地缘政治竞争者，如何在我们的大学校园这一战场上积极与我国利益竞争。去年，众议院以强有力的两党支持票通过了《威慑法案》（DETERRENT Act），该法案将为学院和大学的外国赠款报告要求带来急需的透明度。我们必须确保学术合作能够增强美国实力，而不是增强我们的对手。\n\n向门罗县一名退伍军人致敬\n很荣幸将门罗的萨姆·斯特拉斯评为3月份的本月退伍军人。萨姆于1975年至1980年在美国陆军服役，并一直积极参与退伍军人社区活动，为退伍军人天使组织和门罗县美国退伍军人协会（AMVETS）担任志愿者。萨姆还与肯·摩尔共同创办了“退伍军人旗帜”（Flags O’er Veterans）组织，此前他们发现当地有几处墓地没有悬挂美国国旗以纪念已故退伍军人。该组织通过筹集资金，在安葬退伍军人的墓地安装旗杆、美国国旗、照明设备和纪念牌，以向门罗的退伍军人致敬。萨姆非凡的一生体现了美国服役精神中最优秀的一面。","publish_source":"walberg.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-28T12:54:25-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1486","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"沃尔伯格呼吁民主党通过关键的国土安全部拨款以应对安全担忧加剧","title_en":"Walberg Calls on Democrats to Pass Critical DHS Funding Amidst Heightened Security Concerns","summary_cn":"2026年3月2日，美国众议员蒂姆·沃尔伯格（密歇根州第五选区）发表声明，呼吁民主党结束国土安全部的停摆状态，通过该机构拨款法案。沃尔伯格称，民主党的停摆正危及国家安全，鉴于与伊朗的持续冲突及安全担忧加剧，应加强防御而非进行政治操作。背景显示，众议院拨款委员会1月19日公布了两党协商的DHS拨款法案，众议院共和党人1月22日通过该法案，但民主党2月12日在参议院投票反对，DHS于2月14日停摆，影响FEMA、海岸警卫队、特勤局和CISA等关键安全行动。","summary_en":"On March 2, 2026, Congressman Tim Walberg (MI-05) released a statement calling on Democrats to end the Department of Homeland Security shutdown by passing the agency's funding bill. Walberg said the Democratic shutdown is jeopardizing national security, and that amid the ongoing conflict with Iran and heightened security concerns, the U.S. should strengthen its defenses rather than engage in political maneuvers. Background: the House Appropriations Committee announced a bipartisan, bicameral conferenced DHS funding bill on January 19; House Republicans passed it January 22; Democrats voted against it in the Senate on February 12; DHS shut down February 14, impacting FEMA, the Coast Guard, Secret Service, CISA and other critical security operations.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:26:58.785391+00:00","url":"http://walberg.house.gov/media/press-releases/walberg-calls-democrats-pass-critical-dhs-funding-amidst-heightened-security","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nWalberg Calls on Democrats to Pass Critical DHS Funding Amidst Heightened Security Concerns\nImage March 2, 2026 Press ReleaseToday, Congressman Tim Walberg (MI-05) released the following statement calling on Democrats to end the Department of Homeland Security's shutdown by passing the funding bill for the agency. \"The Democrats' shutdown of the Department of Homeland Security is jeopardizing our national security,\" said Rep. Walberg. \"Due to the ongoing conflict with Iran and heightened security concerns, we need to strengthen our defenses rather than engage in political maneuvers that undermine our ability to protect our homeland. I urge my Democratic colleagues to quit their partisan games and instead support the bipartisan funding for DHS to ensure that the department has the necessary resources to carry out its critical mission of keeping our communities safe from any threats.\"BackgroundOn January 19, the House Appropriations Committee announced the conferenced Department of Homeland Security funding bill that was negotiated on a bipartisan, bicameral basis. On January 22, House Republicans passed this full-year funding bill for the Department of Homeland Security.Democrats voted against this previously negotiated bill in the Senate on February 12. On February 14, the Department of Homeland Security shut down, impacting FEMA, the Coast Guard, Secret Service, CISA, and other critical security operations.\nIssues:Defense and National Security","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\nWalberg呼吁民主党人在安全担忧加剧之际通过关键的国土安全部资金法案\n图片 2026年3月2日 新闻稿今天，国会议员Tim Walberg（密歇根州第五选区）发表以下声明，呼吁民主党通过该机构的拨款法案，结束国土安全部的停摆。\n“民主党对国土安全部造成的停摆正在危及我们的国家安全，”Walberg众议员表示。“鉴于与伊朗持续的冲突以及安全担忧加剧，我们需要加强防御，而不是进行削弱我们保护国土能力的政治操作。我敦促我的民主党同僚停止党派游戏，转而支持两党共同支持的国土安全部拨款，以确保该部门拥有履行关键使命、保障社区免受任何威胁所需的资源。”\n背景\n1月19日，众议院拨款委员会公布了经两党、两院协商达成的国土安全部拨款法案。1月22日，众议院共和党人通过了这项为期全年的国土安全部拨款法案。\n民主党人于2月12日在参议院投票反对这项此前协商达成的法案。2月14日，国土安全部停摆，影响了FEMA、海岸警卫队、特勤局、CISA以及其他关键安全行动。\n议题：国防与国家安全","publish_source":"walberg.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-02T14:22:59-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1304","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"沃尔伯格第三次投票支持为国土安全部拨款","title_en":"Walberg Votes for the Third Time to Fund the Department of Homeland Security","summary_cn":"美国众议员蒂姆·沃尔伯格（密歇根州第五选区）于2026年3月26日投票支持《保护国土卫士拨款法案》，该法案以218票对206票通过，旨在重新开放并全额资助美国国土安全部。这是沃尔伯格第三次投票确保边境巡逻队、运输安全管理局、海岸警卫队和特勤局等一线人员薪资。他批评国土安全部已停摆41天，危及TSA、海岸警卫队和联邦应急管理局等关键服务，并呼吁参议院民主党人支持这一两党协商的拨款法案。","summary_en":"U.S. Representative Tim Walberg (MI-05) voted on March 26, 2026, for the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act, which passed 218-206 to reopen and fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. This was Walberg's third vote to ensure full funding for frontline personnel including the Border Patrol, TSA, U.S. Coast Guard, and Secret Service. He criticized the Department's 41-day shutdown for jeopardizing essential services like TSA, the Coast Guard, and FEMA, and urged Senate Democrats to support the bipartisan funding bill.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:29:58.574520+00:00","url":"http://walberg.house.gov/media/press-releases/walberg-votes-third-time-fund-department-homeland-security","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nWalberg Votes for the Third Time to Fund the Department of Homeland Security\nImage March 26, 2026 Press ReleaseToday, Congressman Tim Walberg (MI-05) voted for the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act, which would reopen and fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. This marks the third vote by Congressman Walberg to ensure full funding for the salaries of the men and women on the front lines, including the Border Patrol, Transportation and Security Administration, U.S. Coast Guard, and Secret Service. The legislation was passed by a vote of 218-206.\"The Department of Homeland Security carries out a critical mission to ensure the safety of our communities, especially during a time of heightened global tensions and increased and evolving terror threats,\" said Rep. Walberg. \"The Department's current 41-day shutdown is jeopardizing essential services like TSA, the Coast Guard, and FEMA. My constituents, many of whom are recovering from this month's devastating tornadoes, deserve these vital services. I urge Senate Democrats to support this funding, which was negotiated in a bipartisan manner, to reopen the Department and ensure our homeland defenders are treated like the essential personnel they are, not political pawns by Democrats.\" BackgroundOn January 19, the House Appropriations Committee announced the conferenced Department of Homeland Security funding bill that was negotiated on a bipartisan, bicameral basis.On January 22, House Republicans passed this full-year funding bill for the Department of Homeland Security.Democrats voted against this previously negotiated bill in the Senate on February 12.On February 14, the Department of Homeland Security shut down, impacting FEMA, the Coast Guard, Secret Service, CISA, and other critical security operations.On March 5, House Republicans voted again to pass a full-year funding bill for the Department of Homeland Security.\nIssues:Defense and National Security","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n沃尔伯格第三次投票支持为国土安全部提供资金\n图片 2026年3月26日 新闻稿\n今天，联邦众议员蒂姆·沃尔伯格（密歇根州第05选区）投票支持《支付我们国土捍卫者薪酬法案》，该法案将使国土安全部恢复运作并获得全额资金。这是沃尔伯格众议员为确保前线男女工作人员薪资获得全额保障而进行的第三次投票，其中包括边境巡逻队、运输安全管理局、美国海岸警卫队和特勤局。该法案以218票赞成、206票反对获得通过。\n\n沃尔伯格众议员表示：“国土安全部承担着确保我们社区安全的重要使命，尤其是在全球紧张局势加剧、恐怖威胁增加且不断演变之际。该部门目前已停摆41天，正危及运输安全管理局、海岸警卫队和联邦紧急事务管理局等基本服务。我的选民，其中许多人正从本月毁灭性龙卷风中恢复，理应获得这些至关重要的服务。我敦促参议院民主党人支持这笔经两党协商达成的拨款，使该部门恢复运作，并确保我们的国土捍卫者得到与其作为必要人员相称的对待，而不是沦为民主党的政治棋子。”\n\n背景\n1月19日，众议院拨款委员会宣布了经两党、两院协商达成的国土安全部拨款法案。\n1月22日，众议院共和党人通过了这项为国土安全部提供全年资金的法案。\n2月12日，民主党人在参议院投票反对这项此前已协商达成的法案。\n2月14日，国土安全部停摆，影响联邦紧急事务管理局、海岸警卫队、特勤局、网络安全和基础设施安全局以及其他关键安全行动。\n3月5日，众议院共和党人再次投票通过了一项为国土安全部提供全年资金的法案。\n\n议题：国防与国家安全","publish_source":"walberg.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-26T15:33:18-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1029","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"多伊诉马林案——挑战国土安全部利用行政传票揭露社交媒体批评者身份","title_en":"Doe v. Mullin – Challenging DHS’s Use of Administrative Summonses to Unmask Social Media Critics - ACLU of DC","summary_cn":"美国公民自由联盟华盛顿特区分会（ACLU-DC）与北加州ACLU代表化名约翰·多伊的加拿大公民兼居民，起诉美国国土安全部。国土安全部通过仅需自身批准、无需中立法官授权的行政传票，要求谷歌等互联网服务商和社交媒体公司披露批评其做法的用户敏感信息，包括姓名、位置和在线活动数据。原告经常在X等平台批评特朗普总统和国土安全部，帖子浏览量超过10万次。案件质疑国土安全部滥用政府权力，可能将监控范围扩展至全球任何批评者。","summary_en":"The ACLU of DC and the ACLU of Northern California filed suit against the Department of Homeland Security on behalf of John Doe, a Canadian citizen and resident who criticizes President Trump and DHS on X and other platforms. DHS issued administrative summonses, requiring only its own approval rather than a neutral judge, to compel Google and other providers to disclose sensitive user information including name, location, and online activity data. The case challenges DHS's abuse of government power, warning it could enable surveillance of any critic anywhere in the world.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:20:44.025359+00:00","url":"http://www.acludc.org/cases/challenging-dhs-action-to-unmask-social-media-critics","content":"Court Cases\nDoe v. Mullin – Challenging DHS’s Use of Administrative Summonses to Unmask Social Media Critics\nFreedom of Speech and Association,\nPrivacy\nFiled:\nMay 4, 2026\nLatest Update:\nMay 4, 2026\nSummary\nThe Department of Homeland Security has ordered multiple Internet Service Providers and social media companies to disclose sensitive information about users who criticized DHS’s practices. DHS has issued these demands through administrative summonses or subpoenas, which require approval only by DHS itself and not a neutral judge.\nThis case challenges another instance of this disturbing trend. Plaintiff John Doe regularly criticizes President Trump and DHS on X and other social media platforms, with his posts collectively receiving well over 100,000 views. Now, DHS wants to obtain detailed information about Mr. Doe and his activities. The government sent an administrative summons to Google, ordering it to disclose “[a]ll records and other information” it possesses relating to the Gmail account Mr. Doe linked to his X account. DHS’s demand expressly includes Mr. Doe’s name, his location information, and data on his online activity—records that could allow the government to trace Mr. Doe’s physical movements and discern the things he reads online and the people with whom he communicates there.\nCourt cases challenging similar summonses have involved the U.S. government targeting people inside the U.S. This case represents a potentially new and troubling development, as Mr. Doe is a Canadian citizen and resident. If DHS can surveil him, it may be able to monitor any critic anywhere on the globe.\nDHS’s actions in this case are unlawful. The government can act only based on authority conveyed via the Constitution or a statute and here, the statute DHS invoked provides no basis to issue the summons. Represented by the ACLU-DC and the ACLU of Northern California, Mr. Doe brings this case to stand up to DHS’s blatant abuse of government power.\nDocuments\nLearn More About the Issues in This Case\nFreedom of Speech and Association\nPrivacy\nView All Issues\nStay Informed\nSign up to be the first to hear about how to take action.\nBy completing this form, I agree to receive occasional emails per the terms of the ACLU’s privacy statement.\nBy completing this form, I agree to receive occasional emails per the terms of the ACLU’s privacy statement.","content_cn":"法院案件\nDoe 诉 Mullin——挑战国土安全部利用行政传票揭露社交媒体批评者身份\n言论与结社自由，\n隐私\n提起日期：\n2026年5月4日\n最新更新：\n2026年5月4日\n摘要\n国土安全部已命令多家互联网服务提供商和社交媒体公司披露批评国土安全部做法的用户的敏感信息。国土安全部通过行政传唤或传票发出这些要求，而这些要求只需国土安全部本身批准，无需中立法官批准。\n本案挑战的是这一令人不安趋势的又一实例。原告约翰·多伊经常在X和其他社交媒体平台上批评特朗普总统和国土安全部，他发布的帖子总浏览量远超10万。现在，国土安全部希望获取有关多伊先生及其活动的详细信息。政府向谷歌发出行政传票，要求其披露与多伊先生关联到其X账户的Gmail账户有关的“其持有的所有记录及其他信息”。国土安全部的要求明确包括多伊先生的姓名、位置​​信息以及其在线活动数据——这些记录可能使政府能够追踪多伊先生的实际行动，并识别他在线阅读的内容以及他在网上与之交流的人。\n挑战类似传票的法院案件涉及美国政府针对美国境内人员。本案可能代表一种新的、令人担忧的发展，因为多伊先生是加拿大公民和居民。如果国土安全部能够监视他，它或许就能监控全球任何地方的批评者。\n国土安全部在本案中的行为是违法的。政府只能依据宪法或法律赋予的权力采取行动，而国土安全部援引的法律并未提供签发该传票的依据。在美国公民自由联盟哥伦比亚特区分部和美国公民自由联盟北加州分部的代理下，多伊先生提起本案，以抵制国土安全部对政府权力的公然滥用。\n文件\n进一步了解本案涉及的问题\n言论与结社自由\n隐私\n查看所有问题\n获取最新信息\n注册以第一时间了解如何采取行动。\n填写此表格即表示我同意按照美国公民自由联盟隐私声明中的条款接收不定期电子邮件。\n填写此表格即表示我同意按照美国公民自由联盟隐私声明中的条款接收不定期电子邮件。","publish_source":"acludc.org","publish_time":"2026-05-04T15:43:31+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1121","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"切斯特县监狱指挥人员完成FBI培训","title_en":"Command Staff at Chester County Prison Complete FBI Training • Chester County, PA","summary_cn":"美国宾夕法尼亚州切斯特县监狱多名指挥人员近日完成了联邦调查局（FBI）执法行政发展协会（LEEDA）三部曲领导力培训项目。该项目包含监督领导力学院、指挥领导力学院和行政领导力学院三门课程，内容涵盖道德决策、组织领导、沟通及公共安全策略等。代理典狱长布莱恩·谢勒表示，这体现了领导团队追求成长与诚信的承诺。监狱预计到2026年底将有超过25名主管完成该项目。","summary_en":"Several members of the command staff at Chester County Prison in Pennsylvania recently completed the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) Law Enforcement Executive Development Association (LEEDA) Trilogy leadership training program. The program consists of three courses: the Supervisor Leadership Institute, the Command Leadership Institute, and the Executive Leadership Institute, covering ethical decision-making, organizational leadership, communication, and public safety strategies. Acting Warden Brian Sheller said the accomplishment reflects the leadership team's dedication to growth and integrity. The prison expects more than 25 supervisors to graduate from the FBI-LEEDA program by the end of 2026.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:49:55.864774+00:00","url":"http://www.chesco.org/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/1730","content":"News Flash\nCommand Staff at Chester County Prison Complete FBI Training\nCounty News\nPosted on April 23, 2026\nSeveral members of the command staff at Chester County Prison recently completed the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) Law Enforcement Executive Development Association (LEEDA) Trilogy leadership training program.  This distinguished program comprises three comprehensive courses: the Supervisor Leadership Institute, the Command Leadership Institute, and the Executive Leadership Institute.The FBI-LEEDA Trilogy is widely recognized to be a premier leadership development series for law enforcement professionals. The curriculum focuses on critical areas such as ethical decision-making, organizational leadership, communication, and the development of effective strategies to meet the evolving challenges of public safety.“This accomplishment reflects our leadership team’s dedication to growth and to leading with integrity,” said Brian Sheller, Acting Warden.Sheller continues, “Investing in professional development ensures that we remain responsive, forward-thinking, and prepared to meet the needs of those in our care and the community we serve.”By completing all three components of the Trilogy, the command staff at Chester County Prison demonstrated a continued commitment to professional excellence, accountability, and the highest standards of service to the community.In addition to the command staff, the Trilogy program is offered to other supervisors at the Prison. By the end of 2026, the Prison expects more than 25 corporals, sergeants, lieutenants, and other supervisors to have also graduated from the FBI-LEEDA program.Chester County Prison remains committed to fostering a culture of professionalism, innovation, and service. Ongoing training and development initiatives, such as FBI-LEEDA, strengthen the organization’s ability to lead effectively, support staff, and uphold public trust.For more information about the Prison, visit chesco.org/Prison.\nRelated News\nChester County Receives $1.35 Million in State Grants\nCounty News\nPosted on September 24, 2026 | Last Updated on September 24, 2026\nChester County to Host “Night of Light” on International Overdose Awareness Day\nCounty News\nPosted on August 18, 2026\nBrian Sheller Appointed Warden of Chester County Prison\nCounty News\nPosted on August 20, 2026\nChester County’s AI-Powered Self-Service Kiosk Project Wins National Award\nCounty News\nPosted on August 13, 2026\nChester County ACEs Coalition Marks 10th Anniversary\nCounty News\nPosted on August 06, 2026","content_cn":"新闻快讯\n切斯特县监狱指挥人员完成FBI培训\n县新闻\n发布于2026年4月23日\n切斯特县监狱的数名指挥人员近期完成了联邦调查局（FBI）执法执行发展协会（LEEDA）Trilogy领导力培训项目。该卓越项目包含三门综合课程：主管领导力学院、指挥领导力学院和高管领导力学院。\nFBI-LEEDA Trilogy被广泛认为是面向执法专业人员的一流领导力发展系列课程。课程重点涵盖道德决策、组织领导力、沟通，以及制定有效战略以应对不断演变的公共安全挑战等关键领域。\n“这一成就体现了我们领导团队致力于成长以及以诚信领导的决心，”代理典狱长Brian Sheller表示。\nSheller继续说道：“投资专业发展能够确保我们保持响应力、前瞻性，并做好准备，满足受我们照护者以及我们所服务社区的需求。”\n通过完成Trilogy的全部三个组成部分，切斯特县监狱指挥人员展现出对专业卓越、问责以及为社区提供最高标准服务的持续承诺。\n除指挥人员外，Trilogy项目也向监狱内其他主管提供。预计到2026年底，将有超过25名下士、中士、中尉及其他主管也从FBI-LEEDA项目毕业。\n切斯特县监狱始终致力于培育专业、创新和服务的文化。FBI-LEEDA等持续培训和发展举措，增强了该组织有效领导、支持员工和维护公众信任的能力。\n如需了解有关监狱的更多信息，请访问chesco.org/Prison。\n相关新闻\n切斯特县获得135万美元州拨款\n县新闻\n发布于2026年9月24日 | 最后更新于2026年9月24日\n切斯特县将在国际过量用药认知日举办“光之夜”\n县新闻\n发布于2026年8月18日\nBrian Sheller被任命为切斯特县监狱典狱长\n县新闻\n发布于2026年8月20日\n切斯特县AI驱动自助服务终端项目荣获国家奖项\n县新闻\n发布于2026年8月13日\n切斯特县ACEs联盟迎来10周年\n县新闻\n发布于2026年8月06日","publish_source":"chesco.org","publish_time":"2026-04-23T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-146","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"“打击暴力犯罪”：FBI局长卡什·帕特尔称美国谋杀率创20年新低","title_en":"'Crush violent crime': FBI Director Kash Patel touts 20-year low in US murder rate","summary_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在参议院司法委员会监督听证会上表示，美国谋杀率降至20年来最低，2025年为每10万人4.1起。他援引FBI数据称，2025年整体暴力犯罪下降9.3%，为1936年以来最大年度降幅，抢劫、强奸、严重袭击和财产犯罪均有下降。帕特尔还称其任内已有10名“十大通缉犯”落网，最新一例在委内瑞拉被捕。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel told a Senate Judiciary oversight hearing that the U.S. murder rate fell to a 20-year low of 4.1 killings per 100,000 people in 2025. Citing FBI data, he said overall violent crime dropped 9.3% in 2025, the largest yearly decline since 1936, with robbery, rape, aggravated assault and property crime also down. Patel said 10 Ten Most Wanted fugitives were captured during his tenure, the latest in Venezuela.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:28:32.049620+00:00","url":"http://www.kunptv.com/news/nation-world/crush-violent-crime-fbi-director-kash-patel-tauts-20-year-low-in-us-murder-rate-president-donald-trump-homicide-killings-deaths-violent-crime-rape-sexual-assault-robbery-top-10-most-wanted-list-fugitives-true-crime","content":"'Crush violent crime': FBI Director Kash Patel touts 20-year low in US murder rateby JESSICA A. BOTELHO | The National News DeskWed, September 16, 2026 at 3:19 PMUpdated Wed, September 16, 2026 at 3:32 PM14VIEW ALL PHOTOSWASHINGTON, DC - SEPTEMBER 15: Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) Director Kash Patel testifies during a Senate Judiciary Committee hearing in the Hart Senate Office Building on September 15, 2026 in Washington, DC. The committee held the oversight hearing to examine the Federal Bureau of Investigation. (Photo by Win McNamee/Getty Images)7CommentSharetopics: FBIKash PatelMurder rateViolent crimeSenate JudiciaryTen Most WantedLaw enforcementCrime dataWASHINGTON (TNND) — FBI Director Kash Patel said the murder rate in the U.S. has fallen to a 20-year low, describing the decline as no easy effort.'Crush violent crime': FBI Director Kash Patel touts 20-year low in US murder rate (Video: CNN Newsource)Patel made the remarks on Tuesday during a Senate Judiciary Committee oversight hearing, where he pointed to FBI crime data showing the murder rate dropped to 4.1 killings per 100,000 people in 2025. He credited law enforcement agencies nationwide, as well as the Trump administration and his team at the FBI.\"This FBI has made America safer than it's ever been, and I'm proud to lead this agency,\" Patel said.\"While doing all this great work for the American people in the world, the FBI prepared for the largest influx of tourists. Between the Club World Cup, two F1 races, protected 300,000 Americans in the Olympics, and then across six America 250 events and this year's World Cup alone, we welcomed over 12 million visitors to the United States to attend these events,\" he added. \"Not one single security incident occurred at any single one of these events. No major security incidents. With our partners, this is how we keep America safe. This is what happens when we back the blue and this new FBI has been rebuilt to crush violent crime and defend the homeland.\"The FBI director also said 10 fugitives who had appeared on the bureau’s Ten \"Most Wanted Fugitives\" list were captured during his tenure, which started when President Donald Trump began his second term. Patel corrected an earlier count of nine and said the latest arrest occurred in Venezuela during the weekend.In a recently released report, the FBI said the number of murders and nonnegligent manslaughters in the U.S. declined 18.1% from 2024. Overall violent crime fell 9.3% in 2025, which is the largest year-to-year decline since the FBI began estimating national crime trends in 1936, according to the agency.The also bureau reported that robbery dropped to 18.5%, rape decreased to 7.6%, aggravated assault went down to 7.2% and property crime plunged to 12.4%.The estimates were based on reports from more than 17,000 law enforcement agencies, representing nearly 97% of the U.S. population. FBI Director Kash Patel credited cooperation among federal, state, local and Tribal agencies, while the bureau cautioned that national figures may not reflect crime trends in every community.NEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"5Timbers spend day off the field giving back to Portland community4Residents fume after newly built St. Helens waterfront vandalized6Seniors at Battle Ground Mobile Estates seek protections for mobile home parks8Winterhawks return to a revamped Veterans Memorial Coliseum for new season","content_cn":"“打击暴力犯罪”：FBI局长 Kash Patel 宣扬美国谋杀率降至20年低点\n作者：JESSICA A. BOTELHO | The National News Desk\n2026年9月16日，星期三，下午3:19\n更新于2026年9月16日，星期三，下午3:32\n14\n查看全部照片\n华盛顿特区——9月15日：2026年9月15日，联邦调查局（FBI）局长 Kash Patel 在华盛顿特区哈特参议院办公大楼举行的参议院司法委员会听证会上作证。该委员会举行监督听证会，以审查联邦调查局。（摄影：Win McNamee/Getty Images）\n7\n评论\n分享\n主题：FBI、Kash Patel、谋杀率、暴力犯罪、参议院司法委员会、十大通缉犯、执法、犯罪数据\n华盛顿（TNND）——FBI局长 Kash Patel 表示，美国谋杀率已降至20年来的低点，并称这一降幅绝非轻易取得。\n“打击暴力犯罪”：FBI局长 Kash Patel 宣扬美国谋杀率降至20年低点（视频：CNN Newsource）\nPatel 于星期二在参议院司法委员会监督听证会上发表上述言论。他指出，FBI犯罪数据显示，2025年谋杀率降至每10万人4.1起。他将此归功于全国各地的执法机构、特朗普政府以及FBI的团队。\nPatel 表示：“这届FBI让美国比以往任何时候都更安全，我为能够领导这个机构感到自豪。”\n他补充道：“在为美国人民和世界完成所有这些出色工作的同时，FBI还为规模最大的游客涌入做好了准备。在世俱杯、两场F1赛事、奥运会期间保护30万美国人，以及六场‘美国250周年’活动和仅今年的世界杯期间，我们迎接了超过1200万游客赴美参加这些活动。所有这些活动均未发生任何一起安全事件，没有重大安全事件。与我们的合作伙伴一道，这就是我们保障美国安全的方式。这就是当我们支持警察、而这个新的FBI经过重建以打击暴力犯罪并保卫国土时所发生的事情。”\nFBI局长还表示，自唐纳德·特朗普总统开始第二任期、他本人上任以来，曾出现在该局“十大通缉逃犯”名单上的10名逃犯已被捕。Patel 更正了此前的9人统计，并表示最新一次逮捕发生在周末的委内瑞拉。\nFBI在最近发布的一份报告中称，美国谋杀和非过失杀人案件数量较2024年下降18.1%。该机构表示，2025年总体暴力犯罪下降9.3%，这是自FBI于1936年开始估算全国犯罪趋势以来最大的年度降幅。\n该局还报告称，抢劫下降18.5%，强奸下降7.6%，严重攻击下降7.2%，财产犯罪大幅下降12.4%。\n这些估算基于逾17,000个执法机构的报告，覆盖近97%的美国人口。FBI局长 Kash Patel 将此归功于联邦、州、地方和部落机构之间的合作；同时，该局警告，全国数据未必反映每个社区的犯罪趋势。\n图片新闻：\n“本地”\n5\nTimbers 在非比赛日回馈波特兰社区\n4\n居民对新建的圣海伦斯滨水区遭破坏感到愤怒\n6\nBattle Ground Mobile Estates 的老年居民寻求对移动房屋公园的保护\n8\nWinterhawks 回归翻新的 Veterans Memorial Coliseum，开启新赛季","publish_source":"kunptv.com","publish_time":"2026-09-16T22:19:03+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1874","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部在明尼阿波利斯启动“史上最大移民行动”","title_en":"DHS launches 'largest immigration operation ever' in Minneapolis","summary_cn":"据美联社报道，特朗普政府启动了其称为史上最大规模的移民执法行动，向明尼阿波利斯地区部署多达2000名联邦探员和官员，部分与涉及索马里居民的欺诈指控相关。约四分之三人员来自ICE执法与遣返行动部门，行动还包括国土安全调查局探员，重点调查欺诈、人口走私和非法用工。国土安全部长诺姆在明尼阿波利斯-圣保罗地区随同ICE官员参与至少一次逮捕。DHS发言人称已在该州实施超过1000次逮捕，但以探员安全为由拒绝透露部署人数。","summary_en":"According to the Associated Press, the Trump administration launched what officials describe as the largest immigration enforcement operation ever, deploying as many as 2,000 federal agents and officers to the Minneapolis area, tied in part to fraud allegations involving Somali residents. Roughly three-quarters of personnel come from ICE's Enforcement and Removal Operations, and the operation includes Homeland Security Investigations agents focusing on fraud, human smuggling and unlawful employment. Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem accompanied ICE officers during at least one arrest in the Minneapolis-St. Paul area. A DHS spokeswoman said the agency had made more than 1,000 arrests in the state but declined to give a deployment figure, citing officer safety.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:49:47.404260+00:00","url":"http://www.minnpost.com/metro/2026/01/dhs-deploys-2000-federal-agents-to-minneapolis-area-to-carry-out-largest-immigration-operation-ever","content":"Posted inMetro\nDHS deploys 2,000 federal agents to Minneapolis area to carry out ‘largest immigration operation ever’\nThe Trump administration has launched its largest immigration enforcement operation, deploying up to 2,000 federal agents to the Minneapolis area.\nBy Rebecca Santana and Mike Balsamo, Associated Press01/06/202601/06/2026\nShare this:\nEmail a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\nEmail\nShare on Facebook (Opens in new window)\nFacebook\nShare on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\nBluesky\nShare on X (Opens in new window)\nX\nPrint (Opens in new window)\nPrint\nICE agents conduct a raid near the intersection of Pillsbury Avenue S. and W. 29th Street on Monday, Dec. 15, 2025, in Minneapolis, Minn. Credit: Ellen Schmidt/MinnPost/CatchLight Local/Report for America\nWASHINGTON (AP) — The Trump administration has launched what officials describe as the largest immigration enforcement operation ever carried out, preparing to deploy as many as 2,000 federal agents and officers to the Minneapolis area for a sweeping crackdown tied in part to allegations of fraud involving Somali residents.\nThe deployment, which began over the weekend, represents one of the largest single-city mobilizations of Department of Homeland Security personnel in years, according to a person briefed on the operation. The surge dramatically expands the federal law enforcement footprint in Minnesota amid heightened political and community tensions.\nThe person was not authorized to publicly discuss details of the operation and spoke to The Associated Press on the condition of anonymity.\nRelated: Did fewer than 30% of ICE detainees in 2025 have criminal records?\nImmigrations and Customs Enforcement Acting Director Todd Lyons said during an interview with Newsmax that the agency was carrying out its “largest immigration operation ever,” though he did not specify how many officers were involved.\nDaily Newsletter | MinnPost's top stories delivered to your inbox every weekday.\nSign up\nRoughly three-quarters of the personnel are expected to come from ICE’s Enforcement and Removal Operations, which carries out immigration arrests and deportations, the person said. The operation also includes agents from Homeland Security Investigations, ICE’s investigative arm, which typically focuses on fraud and cross-border criminal networks. HSI agents were going door-to-door in the Twin Cities area investigating allegations of fraud, human smuggling and unlawful employment practices, Lyons said.\nThe HSI agents are largely expected to concentrate on identifying suspected fraud, while deportation officers will conduct arrests of immigrants accused of violating immigration law, according to the person briefed on the operation. Specialized tactical units are also expected to be involved.\nHomeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem was also in the Minneapolis–St. Paul area and accompanied ICE officers during at least one arrest. In a video posted on the social media platform X, Noem is seen wearing a tactical vest and knit cap as agents arrest a man in St. Paul. In the video, she tells the man, whose hands are cuffed behind his back, “You will be held accountable for your crimes.”\nRelated: Rural Minnesota sheriffs frustrated by delays, pushback on ICE contracts\nThe Department of Homeland Security said in a news release that the man arrested was from Ecuador and that he was wanted in Ecuador and Connecticut on charges including murder and sexual assault.\nWhen asked how many officers and agents had been deployed to Minnesota, Homeland Security spokeswoman Tricia McLaughlin declined to provide a figure, citing officer safety. She said DHS had surged law enforcement resources to the state and had already made more than 1,000 arrests of people it described as killers, rapists, child sexual offenders and gang members.\nThe operation also includes personnel from U.S. Customs and Border Protection, including Commander Gregory Bovino, whose role in previous federal operations in other cities has drawn scrutiny from local officials and civil rights advocates, the person familiar with the deployment said.\nFederal authorities began increasing immigration arrests in the Minneapolis area late last year. Noem and FBI Director Kash Patel announced last week that federal agencies were intensifying operations in Minnesota, with an emphasis on fraud investigations.\nPresident Donald Trump has repeatedly linked his administration’s immigration crackdown in Minnesota to fraud cases involving federal nutrition and pandemic aid programs, many of which have involved defendants with roots in Somalia.\nThe person with information about the current operation cautioned that its scope and duration could shift in the coming days as it develops.\n__\nBalsamo reported from New York.\nSupport the news you rely on\nYou rely on MinnPost to report on the things that matter to you. And we depend on readers like you to help fund our work. Will you make a gift to support our work and keep articles like this one paywall-free?\nDonate now\nRelated\nTagged: Metro Area, News\nRepublish This StoryRepublish our articles for free, online or in print, under a Creative Commons license.\nClose windowRepublish this articleThis work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 International License.\n* Please read before republishing *\nWe’re happy to make this story available to republish for free under an Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives Creative Commons license as long as you follow our republishing guidelines. See our full republication guidelines for more information.\nTo republish, copy the HTML below, which includes our tracking pixel, all paragraph styles and hyperlinks, the author byline and credit to MinnPost.\nIf you have questions, email feedback@minnpost.com.\n— The EditorsDHS deploys 2,000 federal agents to Minneapolis area to carry out ‘largest immigration operation ever’\nby Associated Press, MinnPost January 6, 2026\n<h1>DHS deploys 2,000 federal agents to Minneapolis area to carry out ‘largest immigration operation ever’</h1>\n<p class=\"byline\">by Associated Press, MinnPost <br />January 6, 2026</p>\n<p>WASHINGTON (AP) — The Trump administration has launched what officials describe as the largest immigration enforcement operation ever carried out, preparing to deploy as many as 2,000 federal agents and officers to the Minneapolis area for a sweeping crackdown tied in part to&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/minnesota-fraud-immigration-enforcement-somali-76e246b70d582f1dd42f1242cf7d7a66\">allegations of fraud involving Somali residents</a>.</p>\n<p>The deployment, which began over the weekend, represents one of the largest single-city mobilizations of Department of Homeland Security personnel in years, according to a person briefed on the operation. The surge dramatically expands the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/immigration-minnesota-trump-somali-ice-4911f903e12f949334afdad9dedee878\">federal law enforcement footprint in Minnesota</a>&nbsp;amid heightened&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/immigration-minnesota-trump-somali-ice-4911f903e12f949334afdad9dedee878\">political and community tensions</a>.</p>\n<p>The person was not authorized to publicly discuss details of the operation and spoke to The Associated Press on the condition of anonymity.</p>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color\"><em>Related: <a href=\"https://www.minnpost.com/fact-briefs/2026/01/did-less-than-30-of-ice-detainees-in-2025-have-criminal-convictions-on-their-records/\">Did fewer than 30% of ICE detainees in 2025 have criminal records?</a></em></h3>\n<p>Immigrations and Customs Enforcement Acting Director Todd Lyons said during an interview with Newsmax that the agency was carrying out its “largest immigration operation ever,\" though he did not specify how many officers were involved.</p>\n<p>Roughly three-quarters of the personnel are expected to come from ICE’s Enforcement and Removal Operations, which carries out immigration arrests and deportations, the person said. The operation also includes agents from Homeland Security Investigations, ICE’s investigative arm, which typically focuses on fraud and cross-border criminal networks. HSI agents were going door-to-door in the Twin Cities area investigating allegations of fraud, human smuggling and unlawful employment practices, Lyons said.</p>\n<p>The HSI agents are largely expected to concentrate on identifying suspected fraud, while deportation officers will conduct arrests of immigrants accused of violating immigration law, according to the person briefed on the operation. Specialized tactical units are also expected to be involved.</p>\n<p>Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem was also in the Minneapolis–St. Paul area and accompanied ICE officers during at least one arrest. In a video posted on the social media platform X, Noem is seen wearing a tactical vest and knit cap as agents arrest a man in St. Paul. In the video, she tells the man, whose hands are cuffed behind his back, “You will be held accountable for your crimes.”</p>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color\"><em>Related: <a href=\"https://www.minnpost.com/greater-minnesota/2025/12/rural-minnesota-sheriffs-frustrated-by-delays-pushback-on-ice-detention-contracts-aclu/\">Rural Minnesota sheriffs frustrated by delays, pushback on ICE contracts</a></em></h3>\n<p>The Department of Homeland Security said in a news release that the man arrested was from Ecuador and that he was wanted in Ecuador and Connecticut on charges including murder and sexual assault.</p>\n<p>When asked how many officers and agents had been deployed to Minnesota, Homeland Security spokeswoman Tricia McLaughlin declined to provide a figure, citing officer safety. She said DHS had surged law enforcement resources to the state and had already made more than 1,000 arrests of people it described as killers, rapists, child sexual offenders and gang members.</p>\n<p>The operation also includes personnel from U.S. Customs and Border Protection, including Commander Gregory Bovino, whose role in previous federal operations in other cities has drawn scrutiny from local officials and civil rights advocates, the person familiar with the deployment said.</p>\n<p>Federal authorities began increasing immigration arrests in the Minneapolis area late last year. Noem and FBI Director Kash Patel&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/minnesota-fraud-immigration-enforcement-somali-76e246b70d582f1dd42f1242cf7d7a66\">announced last week that federal agencies</a>&nbsp;were intensifying operations in Minnesota, with an emphasis on&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/minneapolis-minnesota-ice-immigration-noem-fraud-investigation-5f97cefc9adf9c0d14a90762dca3cfc8\">fraud investigations</a>.</p>\n<p>President Donald Trump has repeatedly linked his administration’s immigration crackdown in Minnesota to fraud cases involving federal nutrition and pandemic aid programs, many of which have involved&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/somalia-trump-immigration-explainer-f5155ea29c22441b6507e999b574e136\">defendants with roots in Somalia</a>.</p>\n<p>The person with information about the current operation cautioned that its scope and duration could shift in the coming days as it develops.</p>\n<p>__</p>\n<p>Balsamo reported from New York.</p>\n<p>This &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;http://www.minnpost.com/metro/2026/01/dhs-deploys-2000-federal-agents-to-minneapolis-area-to-carry-out-largest-immigration-operation-ever/&quot;&gt;article&lt;/a&gt; first appeared on &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;http://www.minnpost.com&quot;&gt;MinnPost&lt;/a&gt; and is republished here under a &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/&quot;&gt;Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 International License&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;img src=&quot;https://i0.wp.com/www.minnpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/favicon.png?fit=150%2C150&quot; style=&quot;width:1em;height:1em;margin-left:10px;&quot;&gt;</p>\n&lt;img id=&quot;republication-tracker-tool-source&quot; src=&quot;http://www.minnpost.com/?republication-pixel=true&amp;post=2219313&amp;amp;ga4=3376753669&quot; style=&quot;width:1px;height:1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;script&gt; PARSELY = { autotrack: false, onload: function() { PARSELY.beacon.trackPageView({ url: &quot;http://www.minnpost.com/metro/2026/01/dhs-deploys-2000-federal-agents-to-minneapolis-area-to-carry-out-largest-immigration-operation-ever/&quot;, urlref: window.location.href }); } } &lt;/script&gt; &lt;script id=&quot;parsely-cfg&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.parsely.com/keys/minnpost.com/p.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\nCopy to Clipboard\nYour guide to the policy shaping Minnesota.\nKeep up with the politics, culture and stories shaping Minnesota with MinnPost's daily newsletter.\nSign up\nMost Read\nState Government\nWalz sales tax proposal hits consumers, while sparing business-to-business transactions\nby Matthew Blake\nCityscape\nThree things to know about St. Paul’s latest development spat, and why neighborhood organizers are right this time\nby Bill Lindeke\nMetro\nIt’s still unclear if trash will be picked up in St. Paul starting April 1\nby Winter Keefer\nEnvironment\nTrump’s critical minerals order may boost efforts to mine copper, nickel and cobalt in Minnesota\nby Ana Radelat\nFrom Other Nonprofit Media\nCrowded field emerges to replace former state Sen. Justin Eichorn\nby Chelsey Perkins, KAXE/KBXE\nMinnPost is your source for local news.\nHelp keep our independent journalism paywall-free with a donation today!\nGive Now\nThanks to our major sponsors","content_cn":"发表于 Metro\n国土安全部向明尼阿波利斯地区部署2000名联邦特工，开展“有史以来最大规模的移民行动”\n特朗普政府已启动其最大规模的移民执法行动，向明尼阿波利斯地区部署多达2000名联邦特工。\n丽贝卡·桑塔纳和迈克·巴尔萨莫，美联社，2026年1月6日\n分享：\n通过电子邮件发送链接给朋友（在新窗口中打开）\n电子邮件\n在 Facebook 上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nFacebook\n在 Bluesky 上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nBluesky\n在 X 上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nX\n打印（在新窗口中打开）\n打印\n2025年12月15日星期一，移民与海关执法局特工在明尼苏达州明尼阿波利斯市皮尔斯伯里大道南段与西29街交叉口附近进行突袭。图片来源：Ellen Schmidt/MinnPost/CatchLight Local/Report for America\n华盛顿（美联社）——特朗普政府已启动一项官员称有史以来规模最大的移民执法行动，准备向明尼阿波利斯地区部署多达2000名联邦特工和官员，对该地区展开全面打击，行动部分与涉及索马里裔居民的欺诈指控有关。\n据一名获悉行动情况的人士透露，这次部署于周末开始，是国土安全部人员多年来在单一城市进行的最大规模动员之一。随着政治和社区紧张局势加剧，这一增派行动大幅扩大了联邦执法机构在明尼苏达州的存在。\n这名人士未获授权公开讨论行动细节，并以匿名为条件向美联社透露情况。\n相关阅读：2025年被移民与海关执法局拘留者中，有犯罪记录的是否不到30%？\n移民与海关执法局代理局长托德·莱昂斯在接受 Newsmax 采访时表示，该机构正在开展其“有史以来最大规模的移民行动”，但没有说明涉及多少名官员。\n每日通讯｜每个工作日将 MinnPost 的头条故事发送到你的收件箱。\n注册\n这名人士说，预计约四分之三的人员将来自移民与海关执法局的执法与遣返行动部门，该部门负责移民逮捕和驱逐出境。此次行动还包括国土安全调查局特工，该机构是移民与海关执法局的调查部门，通常重点打击欺诈和跨境犯罪网络。莱昂斯说，国土安全调查局特工正在双城地区逐户调查欺诈、人口走私和非法雇佣行为的指控。\n据这名获悉行动情况的人士透露，国土安全调查局特工预计将主要集中于查明涉嫌欺诈的行为，而遣返官员将逮捕被指控违反移民法的移民。预计还将有专业战术部队参与其中。\n国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆也在明尼阿波利斯—圣保罗地区，并至少陪同移民与海关执法局官员参与了一次逮捕行动。在社交媒体平台 X 上发布的一段视频中，诺姆身穿战术背心、戴着针织帽，画面显示特工在圣保罗逮捕一名男子。视频中，她对这名双手被铐在身后的男子说：“你将为你的罪行负责。”\n相关阅读：明尼苏达州农村地区的警长对延误感到沮丧，推动反对移民与海关执法局合同\n国土安全部在一份新闻稿中表示，被捕男子来自厄瓜多尔，在厄瓜多尔和康涅狄格州因包括谋杀和性侵在内的指控而被通缉。\n当被问及有多少名官员和特工已经\n已部署到明尼苏达州，国土安全部发言人特里西娅·麦克劳克林以警员安全为由，拒绝提供具体人数。她说，国土安全部已向该州增派执法资源，并已逮捕1000多人，这些人被该部门描述为杀人犯、强奸犯、儿童性犯罪者和帮派成员。\n\n据一名熟悉部署情况的人士称，此次行动还包括美国海关与边境保护局人员，其中包括格雷戈里·博维诺指挥官；他在其他城市参与以往联邦行动时的角色，曾受到地方官员和民权倡导者的审查。\n\n联邦当局去年年底开始增加在明尼阿波利斯地区的移民逮捕行动。诺姆和联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔上周宣布，联邦机构正在加大在明尼苏达州的行动力度，重点开展欺诈调查。\n\n总统唐纳德·特朗普一再将其政府在明尼苏达州的移民打击行动，与涉及联邦营养援助和疫情援助项目的欺诈案件联系起来，其中许多案件涉及有索马里背景的被告。\n\n这名掌握当前行动信息的人士提醒说，随着行动推进，其规模和持续时间可能在未来几天发生变化。\n\n__\n巴尔萨莫从纽约报道。\n\n支持你所依赖的新闻\n\n你依靠 MinnPost 报道那些对你重要的事情。而我们依靠像你这样的读者来帮助资助我们的工作。你愿意捐款支持我们的工作，让像这篇文章这样的内容继续免费开放、不设付费墙吗？\n\n立即捐款\n\n相关文章\n\n标签：都会区、新闻\n\n重新发布本文重新发布我们的文章\n\n根据知识共享许可协议，免费在线或印刷发布我们的文章。\n\n关闭窗口重新发布本文\n\n本作品根据知识共享署名-禁止演绎 4.0 国际许可协议授权。\n\n* 重新发布前请阅读 *\n\n只要你遵守我们的重新发布指南，我们很乐意根据知识共享署名-非商业性-禁止演绎许可，免费提供这篇报道供重新发布。更多信息请参阅我们的完整重新发布指南。\n\n如要重新发布，请复制下面的 HTML，其中包含我们的跟踪像素、所有段落样式和超链接、作者署名以及对 MinnPost 的致谢。\n\n如有问题，请发送电子邮件至 feedback@minnpost.com。\n\n——编辑部\n国土安全部向明尼阿波利斯地区部署2000名联邦特工，执行“史上最大规模移民行动”\n\n美联社、MinnPost，2026年1月6日\n\n<h1>国土安全部向明尼阿波利斯地区部署2000名联邦特工，执行“史上最大规模移民行动”</h1>\n<p class=\"byline\">美联社、MinnPost<br />2026年1月6日</p>\n<p>华盛顿（美联社）——特朗普政府已启动一项官员称为有史以来最大规模的移民执法行动，准备向明尼阿波利斯地区部署多达2000名联邦特工和执法人员，开展大规模打击行动，部分行动与<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/minnesota-fraud-immigration-enforcement-somali-76e246b70d582f1dd42f1242cf7d7a66\">涉及索马里居民的欺诈指控</a>有关。</p>\n<p>据一名获悉行动情况的人士称，此次部署于周末开始，是国土安全部人员多年来最大规模的单一城市动员之一。此次增援大幅扩大了<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/immigration-minnesota-trump-somali-ice-4911f903e12f949334afdad9dedee878\">联邦执法力量在\n明尼苏达州</a>&nbsp;正值<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/immigration-minnesota-trump-somali-ice-4911f903e12f949334afdad9dedee878\">政治和社区紧张局势加剧</a>之际。</p>\n<p>由于未获授权公开讨论行动细节，此人以匿名为条件向美联社透露了情况。</p>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color\"><em>相关阅读：<a href=\"https://www.minnpost.com/fact-briefs/2026/01/did-less-than-30-of-ice-detainees-in-2025-have-criminal-convictions-on-their-records/\">2025年ICE被拘留者中，有犯罪记录的人是否少于30%？</a></em></h3>\n<p>移民与海关执法局代理局长托德·莱昂斯在接受Newsmax采访时表示，该机构正在开展“有史以来最大规模的移民行动”，但没有具体说明有多少名官员参与。</p>\n<p>据此人称，预计约四分之三的人员将来自ICE的执法与遣返行动部门，该部门负责执行移民逮捕和驱逐。此次行动还包括国土安全调查局的特工，该机构是ICE的调查部门，通常重点关注欺诈和跨境犯罪网络。莱昂斯说，国土安全调查局特工正在双子城地区挨家挨户调查欺诈、人口走私和非法雇佣行为的指控。</p>\n<p>据一名获悉此次行动情况的人士称，国土安全调查局特工预计将主要集中于查明涉嫌欺诈行为，而遣返官员将逮捕被指违反移民法的移民。预计特种战术部队也将参与其中。</p>\n<p>国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆也在明尼阿波利斯—圣保罗地区，并在至少一次逮捕行动中陪同ICE官员。在社交媒体平台X上发布的一段视频中，诺姆身穿战术背心、戴着针织帽，现场人员正在圣保罗逮捕一名男子。视频中，她对这名双手被铐在身后的男子说：“你将为你的罪行承担责任。”</p>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color\"><em>相关阅读：<a href=\"https://www.minnpost.com/greater-minnesota/2025/12/rural-minnesota-sheriffs-frustrated-by-delays-pushback-on-ice-detention-contracts-aclu/\">明尼苏达州农村地区警长因ICE拘留合同延误及阻力而感到沮丧</a></em></h3>\n<p>国土安全部在一份新闻稿中表示，被捕男子来自厄瓜多尔，并因涉嫌谋杀和性侵等罪名而在厄瓜多尔和康涅狄格州被通缉。</p>\n<p>当被问及有多少名官员和特工被部署到明尼苏达州时，国土安全部发言人特里西娅·麦克劳克林以官员安全为由拒绝提供数字。她说，国土安全部已向该州增派执法资源，并已逮捕超过1,000人，这些人被该部门描述为杀人犯、强奸犯、儿童性犯罪者和帮派成员。</p>\n<p>熟悉此次部署情况的人士称，此次行动还包括美国海关与边境保护局的人员，其中包括格雷戈里·博维诺指挥官。他在其他城市先前联邦行动中的角色曾受到地方官员和民权倡导者的审视。</p>\n<p>联邦当局从去年年底开始增加明尼阿波利斯地区的移民逮捕行动。诺姆和联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://apnews.com/article/minnesota-fraud-immigration-enforcement-somali-76e246b70d582f1dd42f1242cf7d7a66\">上周宣布，联邦机构</a>&nbsp;正在明尼苏达州加强行动，重点是&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/minneapolis-minnesota-ice-immigration-noem-fraud-investigation-5f97cefc9adf9c0d14a90762dca3cfc8\">欺诈调查</a>。</p>\n<p>总统唐纳德·特朗普多次将其政府在明尼苏达州的移民打击行动与涉及联邦营养援助和疫情援助项目的欺诈案件联系起来，其中许多案件涉及&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/somalia-trump-immigration-explainer-f5155ea29c22441b6507e999b574e136\">具有索马里背景的被告</a>。</p>\n<p>这名掌握当前行动信息的人士提醒说，随着行动推进，其规模和持续时间在未来几天可能会发生变化。</p>\n<p>__</p>\n<p>Balsamo从纽约报道。</p>\n<p>本文最初发表于<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.minnpost.com/metro/2026/01/dhs-deploys-2000-federal-agents-to-minneapolis-area-to-carry-out-largest-immigration-operation-ever/\">此处</a>的<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.minnpost.com\">MinnPost</a>，现依据<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/\">知识共享署名-禁止演绎4.0国际许可协议</a>转载于此。&lt;img src=&quot;https://i0.wp.com/www.minnpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/favicon.png?fit=150%2C150&quot; style=&quot;width:1em;height:1em;margin-left:10px;&quot;&gt;</p>\n&lt;img id=&quot;republication-tracker-tool-source&quot; src=&quot;http://www.minnpost.com/?republication-pixel=true&amp;post=2219313&amp;amp;ga4=3376753669&quot; style=&quot;width:1px;height:1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;script&gt; PARSELY = { autotrack: false, onload: function() { PARSELY.beacon.trackPageView({ url: &quot;http://www.minnpost.com/metro/2026/01/dhs-deploys-2000-federal-agents-to-minneapolis-area-to-carry-out-largest-immigration-operation-ever/&quot;, urlref: window.location.href }); } } &lt;/script&gt; &lt;script id=&quot;parsely-cfg&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.parsely.com/keys/minnpost.com/p.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n复制到剪贴板\n了解塑造明尼苏达州的政策。\n通过MinnPost每日新闻通讯，持续了解塑造明尼苏达州的政治、文化和故事。\n注册\n阅读最多\n州政府\n沃尔兹的销售税提案冲击消费者，却避开企业间交易\n作者：Matthew Blake\n城市景观\n关于圣保罗最新开发争端需要了解的三件事，以及为什么社区组织者这次是对的\n作者：Bill Lindeke\n都市区\n目前仍不清楚从4月1日开始圣保罗是否会收运垃圾\n作者：Winter Keefer\n环境\n特朗普的关键矿产令可能推动明尼苏达州开采铜、镍和钴的努力\n作者：Ana Radelat\n其他非营利媒体\n前州参议员Justin Eichorn的继任者竞争者众多\n作者：Chelsey Perkins，KAXE/KBXE\nMinnPost是您获取本地新闻的来源。\n今天就捐款，帮助我们保持独立新闻事业无需付费墙！\n立即捐赠\n感谢我们的主要赞助商","publish_source":"minnpost.com","publish_time":"2026-01-06T21:45:01+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3430","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"密西西比州FBI负责人庆祝与密西西比州立大学的合作","title_en":"Lead Miss. FBI agent celebrates partnership with MSU","summary_cn":"密西西比州FBI负责人、杰克逊分局特别探员主管罗伯特·艾克霍夫于11月1日访问密西西比州立大学，与校长马克·基纳姆及其他管理人员会面，重申该机构与这所赠地大学的合作关系。艾克霍夫参观了先进复合材料研究所、拉斯佩特飞行研究实验室和农业自主研究所等多个研究单位，并讨论了双方如何合作构建更强大的凝聚力。FBI局长克里斯托弗·雷于今年3月任命艾克霍夫为杰克逊分局负责人。","summary_en":"Robert Eikhoff, special agent in charge of the FBI's Jackson Field Office, visited Mississippi State University on Nov. 1 to meet with President Mark E. Keenum and other administrators, reaffirming the agency's partnership with the land-grant institution. Eikhoff toured numerous MSU research units, including the Advanced Composites Institute, Raspet Flight Research Laboratory and Agricultural Autonomy Institute, and discussed how the agency and university can work together to build a \"stronger fabric of cohesion.\" FBI Director Christopher Wray named Eikhoff special agent in charge of the Jackson bureau in March.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:42:29.380147+00:00","url":"http://www.msstate.edu/newsroom/article/2024/11/lead-miss-fbi-agent-celebrates-partnership-msu","content":"Lead Miss. FBI agent celebrates partnership with MSU\nRobert Eikhoff, special agent in charge of the FBI’s Jackson Field Office, receives a cowbell from Mississippi State President Mark E. Keenum, right, Friday [Nov. 1] after touring numerous MSU research units. (Photo by Grace Cockrell)\nContact: Carl Smith\nSTARKVILLE, Miss.—Mississippi’s lead FBI agent visited with Mississippi State President Mark E. Keenum and other university administrators Friday [Nov. 1] to reaffirm the agency’s partnership with the Magnolia State’s leading land-grant institution.\nRobert Eikhoff, special agent in charge of the FBI’s Jackson Field Office, toured numerous MSU research units, including the Advanced Composites Institute, Raspet Flight Research Laboratory and Agricultural Autonomy Institute, and discussed how the agency and university can work together to build a “stronger fabric of cohesion” for the future.\n“This has been a great opportunity for us to really share our appreciation for the partnership that we have with the school. It's uncommon to have this degree of relationship with academia, so we want to celebrate and honor that, and find pathways to have better points of collaboration,” Eikhoff said. “We recognize the importance of academia in our mission of protecting the American people and upholding the Constitution. We have existential threats that only together are we able to mitigate and hopefully disrupt and dismantle.”\nFBI Director Christopher Wray named Eikhoff special agent in charge of the Jackson bureau in March. Previously, Eikhoff served as a section chief in the Operational Technology Division at FBI Headquarters in Washington and in numerous counterterrorism-related positions.\nBefore joining the FBI, Eikhoff served in the U.S. Navy as a surface warfare officer and later worked in the credit and recruiting industries. He earned a bachelor’s degree in computer information systems from Georgia State University.\nMississippi State University is taking care of what matters. Learn more at www.msstate.edu.","content_cn":"密西西比州首席 FBI 特工庆祝与 MSU 的合作伙伴关系\nFBI 杰克逊外地办事处负责人 Robert Eikhoff 特别探员主管，在参观众多 MSU 研究单位后，于周五[11月1日]从密西西比州立大学校长 Mark E. Keenum（右）手中接过一个牛铃。（Grace Cockrell 摄）\n联系方式：Carl Smith\n密西西比州斯塔克维尔——密西西比州首席 FBI 特工于周五[11月1日]拜会密西西比州立大学校长 Mark E. Keenum 及其他大学管理人员，重申该机构与这所木兰州领先赠地大学之间的合作伙伴关系。\nFBI 杰克逊外地办事处负责人 Robert Eikhoff 特别探员主管参观了众多 MSU 研究单位，包括先进复合材料研究所、Raspet 飞行研究实验室和农业自主研究所，并讨论该机构和大学如何携手为未来构建“更强大的凝聚纽带”。\nEikhoff 表示：“这对我们而言是一次绝佳机会，让我们真正表达对与学校之间伙伴关系的感谢。与学术界拥有如此程度的关系并不常见，因此我们希望庆祝并珍视这种关系，并寻找实现更好协作的途径。我们认识到学术界在保护美国人民和维护宪法这一使命中的重要性。我们面临着只有共同努力才能缓解、并希望加以扰乱和瓦解的生存性威胁。”\nFBI 局长 Christopher Wray 于3月任命 Eikhoff 为杰克逊办事处特别探员主管。此前，Eikhoff 曾担任位于华盛顿的 FBI 总部行动技术处科长，并担任过许多与反恐相关的职位。\n加入 FBI 前，Eikhoff 曾以水面作战军官身份在美国海军服役，后来在信贷和招聘行业工作。他获得佐治亚州立大学计算机信息系统学士学位。\n密西西比州立大学致力于关照重要之事。欲了解更多信息，请访问 www.msstate.edu。","publish_source":"msstate.edu","publish_time":"2024-11-01T17:07:45-05:00"}}];
